window.UIM_SEARCH=[{"t":"How to read this guide","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s1-h","x":"This guide is written for Ultimate Ironmen from the first tick, at a comfortable pace, and it never assumes a bank. What it optimises is comfort and safety: no tick manipulation (Chapter 4's fast track is the one exception), the fewest trips, slots and risky deaths, and training that quest XP would give you later left to the quests. It is not the fewest-hours route. Its mechanics were last checked against the wiki on 23 November 2026, and its coin figures are estimates, so keep about 15% over any target before a big purchase. Comfort and safety come first because a UIM has nothing behind its inventory: one careless death or one overfull trip can cost hours of items, while a slower but safe r"},{"t":"Ground rules","p":"Chapter 1 › How to read this guide","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b1-h","x":"There is no bank. Every item lives in your inventory, your worn equipment, or one of the storages in the glossary below. A step never says \"grab from the bank\". A UIM can't deposit, withdraw or note anything at a bank. A bank booth still turns notes back into items for you (as many as your free slots hold; for an exact number, fill the other slots first or pay Phials in Rimmington 5 gp an item), which the Entrana kit in 1.3 uses to unnote its fish at the Falador east bank, but it never stores anything. Services that send items to your bank do nothing for a UIM either, so no step relies on one. Count item types, not quantities. Coins, runes, feathers, arrow shafts, noted loot and tokens each "},{"t":"Before every trip","p":"Chapter 1 › How to read this guide","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b2-h","x":"Check these before you leave a location. They are the protocol behind the rules above. Recount your inventory against the 28 slots before leaving, and again after any reward, drop or delivery. Each unstackable item takes one slot. Some rewards need free space at the moment you claim them: Misthalin Mystery's three gems are handed over only if you have three empty slots. Confirm no other deathpile is active. A second death does not restart the first pile's 60 minutes of logged-in time. Note the time you die, so you know when the pile runs out. Items from the second death last only for what is left of the first pile's hour, so a second death late in a trip can leave you minutes rather than an "},{"t":"How the steps are written","p":"Chapter 1 › How to read this guide","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b3-h","x":"Each section is split into blocks, one per stretch of the map. A block opens with a short note on what you carry through it, then its steps follow in play order. Each step is written as one continuous walkthrough: where to go, who to talk to, what to pick up, what to wear, and what to throw away the moment it has done its job. Inventory management is part of the instructions, not a separate checklist. A coin estimate closes each block; times are left out, because they depend on your pace. Read a whole step before you start it: the warnings and the drop instructions often come at the end, and some of them change what you do at the start. Each block also opens with a route card, so you can che"},{"t":"Storage glossary (Chapter 1)","p":"Chapter 1 › How to read this guide","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b4-h","x":"Storage Available from Holds Catch Inventory + equipment Start 28 slots + worn gear Everything else in this table exists to free these slots Reclaimable XP lamps (Veos) X Marks the Spot, Client of Kourend Quest XP lamps Destroy the lamp, reclaim it later from Veos. Costs nothing Tool leprechaun Any farming patch Farming tools, buckets, compost Stores tools and notes harvested herbs and saplings; won't note logs Wintertodt Reward Cart First Wintertodt game with 500+ points Up to 8,000 unclaimed rewards Loot is rolled when you search, not when you earn it Deathpile Any time Everything you carried, except unnoted food and potions; the Chronicle and rainbow scarf are destroyed 60 minutes, counte"},{"t":"Chapter 1 at a glance","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s2-h","x":"Chapter 1 has four destinations, each with a storage milestone, so the account never carries more than it needs. Section Destination UIM milestone added What changes most 1.1 Tutorial to Wintertodt Early quests, 50 Firemaking, warm clothing, long Wintertodt Wintertodt Reward Cart used as deferred storage No Entrana trip, silk money in timed batches, quest items collected only when used 1.2 Fishing and thieving Rooftops to 40 Agility, Tempoross, Trawler, barbarian fishing, blackjacking to 55 Thieving Tempoross reward pool as deferred storage; POH in Pollnivneach Coins are the only stockpile; blackjacking stops near 55 Thieving because the rogue outfit needs the 1.3 armour case 1.3 Money, ques"},{"t":"1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s3-h","x":"Section 1.1 ends with 85 Firemaking, 60 Woodcutting, 30 Construction, four warm items worn, a house in Rimmington and most of your Wintertodt loot waiting in the Reward Cart. Your standing kit through the section is small on purpose: coins, runes, knife, tinderbox, spade, hammer and a steel axe that moves to your weapon slot at 5 Attack. Everything else is picked up for the step that uses it and dropped once that step is done. The slot counts in this section include the arrow-shaft stack from Lumbridge; take one off each count if you skip the shafts."},{"t":"Tutorial Island, Lumbridge and Draynor","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b5-h","x":"This block takes you from a fresh account to a Draynor kit of about 18 items, with 15 Firemaking, around 19 Woodcutting (11 without the arrow shafts), around 7 Thieving and four quests started or finished. The kit you leave with is: coins, the air and mind rune stacks, a jug of water, one bucket, tinderbox, knife, spade, hammer, steel axe, small fishing net, air talisman, the X Marks the Spot clue, the arrow-shaft stack (if you make it) and four jugs of wine. Worn: leather boots, leather gloves, ghostspeak amulet, forestry kit, bronze sword and wooden shield. Gate in a new account; Ultimate Ironman chosen on Tutorial Island. Carry in what the tutorial leaves you, then the Lumbridge starter k"},{"t":"Set up the account on Tutorial Island","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Tutorial Island, Lumbridge and Draynor","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t9-h","x":"Pick your look. The old advice to start as a female character no longer applies, so choose whatever you like. Before you leave the island, set up two-step authentication on the account. A UIM is months of work held in one inventory with no bank behind it, and a hijacked account can be emptied in a single death. On the island, talk to Paul, the Iron Man tutor, and choose Ultimate Ironman. Do it before the Magic instructor sends you to the mainland: once you leave the island the mode can only ever be downgraded (at Adam in Lumbridge), never chosen again. Finish the rest of the tutorial normally. Paul lets you change your choice as often as you like while you are still on the island. When you a"},{"t":"Build the Lumbridge starter kit and reach 15 Firemaking","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Tutorial Island, Lumbridge and Draynor","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t10-h","x":"Take the knife and the jug that spawn in the Lumbridge Castle cellar (down the kitchen trapdoor; both are free), and fill the jug with water at the nearest sink or fountain. The jug of water is for Brother Cedric in Monk's Friend, so it rides along until Ardougne. Pick up a pair of leather boots in the same cellar and wear them; they are your feet slot until the clue hunter boots replace them. The cellar also has a bucket and a second pair of leather boots; if you have already sold or dropped the tutorial bucket, take the spare here, because the guide needs one bucket through to Gertrude's Cat. Climb to the first floor of Lumbridge Castle and talk to Duke Horacio in his bedroom to start Rune"},{"t":"Fund the Lumbridge route and start the local quests","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Tutorial Island, Lumbridge and Draynor","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t11-h","x":"Pickpocket the men around Lumbridge Castle until you hold about 250 gp. Each success gives 3 gp and 8 Thieving XP, so this takes about 85 successful pickpockets and leaves you near 7 Thieving, already past the 5 that Ardougne's baker's stall needs. The 250 gp pays for the spade, the hammer and the steel axe below with a small cushion. Pickpocketing a man in Lumbridge is also a Lumbridge & Draynor easy diary task, so your first success ticks it. A failed attempt stuns you for 4.8 seconds and deals 1 damage, so over 85 successes watch your Hitpoints and pause to regenerate rather than eat: you have no food to spare until the wines in Draynor. While you are in the courtyard, talk to Hans and as"},{"t":"Complete Misthalin Mystery and gear up in Draynor","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Tutorial Island, Lumbridge and Draynor","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t12-h","x":"Go south into the Lumbridge Swamp and complete Misthalin Mystery, which starts at the jetty there: talk to Abigale in the south-eastern corner of the swamp, near the fishing spots, and take the rowboat south of her to the island. It needs no items of your own (the bucket, tinderbox and knife it uses are found during the quest) and no combat. Two things can set you back. Read the notes in the order you find them, because each part opens only once the earlier note is read. During the first cutscene with the killer, click only the text box to continue: clicking elsewhere or pressing the space bar ends it early and puts you out of the room. It rewards an uncut ruby, emerald and sapphire, plus 60"},{"t":"The levers to Ardougne and the three Ardougne quests","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b6-h","x":"This block moves you to Ardougne and closes Clock Tower, Monk's Friend and Hazeel Cult in a single pass, then trains Woodcutting to 35. You carry the Draynor kit with about ten free slots. That is enough because Clock Tower lets you hold only one cog at a time and every other quest item here is handed in within minutes of being picked up. If you ever run short of space, finish the next hand-in instead of dropping a quest item. Gate in the Draynor kit with about ten free slots. Carry in the Draynor kit: about 18/28. Exit Clock Tower, Monk's Friend and Hazeel Cult done; 35 Woodcutting; about 2,500 gp. Carries forward nothing beyond the Draynor kit; Monk's Friend's eight law runes are dropped a"},{"t":"Take the levers to Ardougne","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The levers to Ardougne and the three Ardougne quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t14-h","x":"Ardougne holds the next three quests and most of your early money, and at this point nothing teleports you there: the Ardougne Teleport spell needs Plague City and 51 Magic. The lever chain gets you there in a couple of minutes and completes an easy Ardougne Diary task on the way, which is why the guide takes it instead of the long walk west. Open the grouping tab and use the Clan Wars minigame teleport. It drops you at the Ferox Enclave, a safe zone inside the Wilderness where players can't attack each other. In the chapel, the two Pools of Refreshment restore your Hitpoints, Prayer and run energy, cure poison, venom and disease, and reset changed stats for free (they don't restore special "},{"t":"Start Hazeel Cult and Monk's Friend","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The levers to Ardougne and the three Ardougne quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t15-h","x":"Run to the Carnillean house in the south-west of East Ardougne and talk to Ceril Carnillean to start Hazeel Cult. Walk east to the cave entrance next to the river, east of the clock tower, and talk to Clivet inside. Choose to help the cult. He gives you a bottle of poison and asks you to slip it into Ceril's food. The poison is used in a few minutes, so leave it in your inventory. Run south to the Ardougne Monastery and talk to Brother Omad to start Monk's Friend. He explains that thieves stole a child's blanket and you need to fetch it before he can hold a party. Slots: about 19/28 with the poison Done when both quests are started."},{"t":"Finish Clock Tower and Monk's Friend","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The levers to Ardougne and the three Ardougne quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t16-h","x":"Walk to the clock tower south of Ardougne and talk to Brother Kojo to start Clock Tower. Four cogs, one of each colour, are hidden in the dungeon under the tower and in the tunnels around it, and each one goes on the spindle of its own colour, on a different floor of the tower's central column. The game lets you hold only one cog at a time, whatever its colour, so you can't gather them all and fit them in one climb. The order below fits each cog before fetching the next and threads the Monk's Friend errands into the walks between them, so the blanket, the jug of water and the log are each handed in minutes after you pick them up. White cog. Climb down the ladder in the middle room of the tow"},{"t":"Finish Hazeel Cult","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The levers to Ardougne and the three Ardougne quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t17-h","x":"Walk back to the Carnillean house, in the south-western corner of East Ardougne, and go down to the basement and use the poison on the range. The family dog, Scruffy, eats the meal instead of Ceril; Clivet accepts that as proof of your loyalty anyway. Go upstairs and talk to Ceril, then return to Clivet in the cave. He gives you Hazeel's mark and tells you to reach the hideout by redirecting the sewers. Turn the five sewer valves around the river south of East Ardougne in this order: Valve 1, north of the cave entrance: turn LEFT. Valve 2, at the southern end of the bridge by the Carnillean house: turn RIGHT. Valve 3, north-east of Valve 2 across the bridge: turn RIGHT. Valve 4, back across "},{"t":"Train to 35 Woodcutting","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The levers to Ardougne and the three Ardougne quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t18-h","x":"Train Woodcutting next to the Carnillean house or any spot near Ardougne with normal and oak trees. Chop a normal log and burn it on the spot, over and over, until 15 Woodcutting, then switch to oaks (if the arrow shafts already took you past 15, start on oaks straight away) and keep chopping and burning each log immediately. One free slot is all this needs. If no oaks are close to the house, there are clusters of them inside East Ardougne, east of the market. An oak gives several logs before it falls, after about 27 seconds of chopping, so you don't need to change trees after every log. Stop at 35 Woodcutting, which is 22,406 XP. Starting from about 19 Woodcutting and with Monk's Friend's 2"},{"t":"Ardougne money and the first warm clothing","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b7-h","x":"This block takes your coin stack from about 2,500 to about 7,500 gp, gets you to 20+ Thieving, completes Sheep Herder and puts the first two Wintertodt warm items on your body. Before you start, drop any empty wine jugs; from here your food is cakes from the stall. Gate in 5 Thieving for the cake stall; 20 Thieving for silk; 100 gp for Sheep Herder. Carry in the Ardougne kit with five cakes, three slots kept for Sheep Herder: up to 28/28. Exit 20+ Thieving; Sheep Herder done; the clue hunter gloves and boots worn; about 7,500 gp. Carries forward two warm items for Wintertodt. The money comes from three sources: Sheep Herder's 3,100 gp reward, the silk stall, and the cake stall's diary task o"},{"t":"Restore, check pets, and steal cakes to 20 Thieving","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Ardougne money and the first warm clothing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t20-h","x":"Start with two free Ardougne easy diary tasks. Switch Thick Skin on for a moment so you are below full Prayer (the task only counts then), pray at the altar in the East Ardougne church to restore it, then walk to the pet shop and right-click Probita to check your insured pets. Both tasks need nothing but the walk, which is why they come first. Go to the baker's stall in the market and steal cakes. Your Lumbridge pickpocketing and Hazeel Cult's 1,500 Thieving XP have already put you past the 5 Thieving the stall needs, and the first successful cake completes another Ardougne easy diary task. Each steal gives 16 XP; keep going until 20 Thieving (4,470 XP). If the baker or a guard spots you mid"},{"t":"Fill the first silk load","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Ardougne money and the first warm clothing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t21-h","x":"At 20 Thieving, move to the silk stall and steal until only three slots are free (Sheep Herder needs them); with your kit and five cakes, that is about seven pieces. To make the load worth the wait, drop the cakes for this load only and steal another five, which takes you to about twelve pieces. The stall gives 24 Thieving XP per steal. Ardougne Market has two silk stalls. The south-west one has fewer guards around it, and the owner of the north-east one isn't nearby. Guards and Knights of Ardougne can catch you; the hero and the paladin in the market do nothing unless your combat level is near theirs. Then leave the stall alone completely. From your last theft, the silk merchant remembers y"},{"t":"Complete Sheep Herder during the first wait","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Ardougne money and the first warm clothing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t22-h","x":"Walk to East Ardougne church and talk to Councillor Halgrive outside it, in the graveyard just south of the church, to start Sheep Herder, with at least three free slots: the quest hands you the poisoned sheep feed, and Doctor Orbon the plague jacket and trousers. Then talk to Doctor Orbon inside the church and pay him 100 gp for the plague jacket and plague trousers. Wear both; worn items take no slots, so the silk can stay in your inventory. The wiki says the plague jacket has gloves built in and takes yours off, so they land in your bag: drop the leather gloves, because the clue hunter gloves replace them in the next step and you need that slot for the cattleprod's swap and the sheep bone"},{"t":"Dig up the clue hunter gloves and boots","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Ardougne money and the first warm clothing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t23-h","x":"On your way back south, stop at the oak tree south-west of the Fishing Guild, just north of East Ardougne, and dig next to it with your spade. This is the dig from the Week 1 Crack the Clue map, and it needs nothing but the spade. You get the clue hunter gloves and clue hunter boots. Wear both and drop the leather gloves and leather boots they replace. These are warm items one and two for Wintertodt, and from now on they stay in your gloves and feet slots. If your inventory is completely full of silk, drop one piece before digging, then put the gloves and boots on immediately; they never need a free slot for longer than a click. If a piece is ever destroyed, dig at the same oak again to get "},{"t":"Sell the silk and run the remaining loads","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Ardougne money and the first warm clothing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t24-h","x":"By the time you're back in the market, the ten minutes have passed. Talk to the silk merchant and choose to sell. Offer 120 gp per piece; he counters with 50. Answer with 60 and he buys every piece of silk in your inventory at once. The first 60 gp sale completes another Ardougne easy diary task. Keep to that order. Other answers end the haggle at 20, 40 or 50 gp a piece, and only a sale at 60 gp counts for the diary. Steal and sell two more loads the same way, and fill its ten-minute wait with whatever you like near the market: a few more cake steals, or walking to the docks to check the boat. Steal a new load only after the current one is sold, so the inventory never overflows. Three loads"},{"t":"Brimhaven and Witchaven: Tribal Totem and Sea Slug","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b8-h","x":"This block completes Sea Slug and collects the tribal totem, and you leave it holding exactly one new long-term item: a raw sardine for Gertrude's Cat. You need about six free slots at any moment here, which your five cakes and the Ardougne kit leave you. Gate in 30 Firemaking for Sea Slug; 21 Thieving for the mansion stairs; about six free slots. Carry in the Ardougne kit and five cakes: about 18/28. Exit Sea Slug done; the tribal totem collected; a raw sardine for Gertrude's Cat; about 7,500 gp. Carries forward the totem (Tribal Totem), the sardine (Gertrude's Cat). Don't stock up on this trip on soda ash, buckets of sand, a cake tin, a glassblowing pipe, two fishing rods, a fly fishing ro"},{"t":"Start Tribal Totem in Brimhaven","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Brimhaven and Witchaven: Tribal Totem and Sea Slug","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t26-h","x":"Walk to the Ardougne docks and take Captain Barnaby's boat to Brimhaven for 30 gp. On the Brimhaven docks, buy one swamp paste from the Trader Stan's crew member. That single swamp paste is for Sea Slug; Holgart takes it from you within the hour. Check the name before you pay: Holgart wants swamp paste, not swamp tar, and the tar does nothing for his boat. Walk north into the Shrimp and Parrot and talk to Kangai Mau to start Tribal Totem. He wants his tribe's totem back from Lord Handelmort's mansion in Ardougne. Tell him you are in search of adventure, then agree to get it back. Take the boat straight back to Ardougne (30 gp). Done when Tribal Totem is started. Coins: about 7,400 gp · Slots"},{"t":"Complete Sea Slug and fish for the diary","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Brimhaven and Witchaven: Tribal Totem and Sea Slug","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t27-h","x":"Walk east from Ardougne to Witchaven. Sea Slug needs 30 Firemaking, which your oak burning has already given you. Talk to Caroline on the coast just north of the village to start Sea Slug. Holgart stands next to her: give him the swamp paste so that he can repair his boat and row you out to the fishing platform. From then on you can right-click him and choose Travel. On the platform, talk to Bailey in the small room in the south-west corner and pick up the broken glass from its floor, then the damp sticks in the north-east corner. Don't pick up any of the sea slugs on the floor, because each one hurts you for 3 damage. Climb the ladder beside the sticks, enter the west cabin, past the crane,"},{"t":"Collect the totem from Handelmort Mansion","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Brimhaven and Witchaven: Tribal Totem and Sea Slug","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t28-h","x":"Back in East Ardougne, go to the G.P.D.T. depot south of the eastern bank. Investigate the north-easternmost crate to take its address label, which is addressed to Lord Handelmort's mansion. Use that label on the crate two tiles south of it, which holds Wizard Cromperty's experimental teleport block, then ask a G.P.D.T. employee when the crate will be delivered. Walk to Wizard Cromperty's house north-east of the market and ask him to teleport you: ask what he has invented, ask to be teleported and confirm. You land next to his block, which is now inside the mansion. Go west two doors and open the combination lock with the code K-U-R-T; if the game says the combination is incorrect, enter it "},{"t":"The Lumbridge loop","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b9-h","x":"This loop closes Tribal Totem, Sheep Shearer and The Restless Ghost, brings X Marks the Spot to its last stop, and gives you the Chronicle and your third warm item. You start it holding the totem and the sardine on top of the Ardougne kit, and you finish it holding only two items you didn't have before: the Chronicle and the research package. Gate in the totem and the sardine on top of the Ardougne kit. Carry in the kit, totem and sardine: about 19/28. Exit Tribal Totem, Sheep Shearer and The Restless Ghost done; X Marks the Spot at its last stop; the Chronicle; the third warm item; about 6,510 gp. Carries forward the casket and onion, the empty bucket, the sardine. The order matters for the"},{"t":"Complete Tribal Totem and return to Lumbridge","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The Lumbridge loop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t30-h","x":"Take the boat from Ardougne to Brimhaven (30 gp) and give the totem to Kangai Mau in the Shrimp and Parrot to complete Tribal Totem. The reward is 1,775 Thieving XP and five swordfish. Keep the swordfish as your food from here to Varrock and drop your remaining cakes now: Sheep Shearer needs the slots. Cast Lumbridge Home Teleport from the standard spellbook. It has a 30-minute cooldown, so note the time: if it is ready again when you finish at the Wizards' Tower, you can use it a second time for the return to the graveyard. Done when Tribal Totem is complete. Coins: about 7,470 gp · Slots: about 18/28 · Requirements: none"},{"t":"Talk to the ghost and make the castle dig","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The Lumbridge loop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t31-h","x":"With the ghostspeak amulet still on, walk to the small building in the Lumbridge graveyard, open the coffin and talk to the ghost for The Restless Ghost. The building stands in the south-east corner of the graveyard, next to the chapel where Father Aereck started the quest. He tells you that his skull was stolen and is at the Wizards' Tower. Without the amulet you would only hear \"wooo\", which is why it has stayed in your neck slot until now. If you have lost the amulet, Father Urhney in his house on the west side of the Lumbridge Swamp gives you another. Walk round to the back exit of Lumbridge Castle, next to the kitchen. Stand one tile south-west of the large crate outside the door and di"},{"t":"Complete Sheep Shearer in two halves","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The Lumbridge loop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t32-h","x":"Run north to Fred the Farmer's house and talk to him to start Sheep Shearer. He hands you a pair of shears if you don't have any. Enter the sheep pen on the east side of his house and shear as many sheep as your free slots allow (about nine); skinny sheep have already been shorn, so click the woolly ones. Watch for rams, the horned ones: they can't be shorn and a misclick attacks them, so set your attack option to hidden if you keep hitting them. A sheep sometimes runs off as you shear; keep clicking, and a shorn sheep grows its wool back after a minute. Carry the wool to Lumbridge Castle and climb to the spinning wheel on the first floor (second floor US). It is in the bedroom at the south "},{"t":"Make the Draynor digs and visit Diango","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The Lumbridge loop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t33-h","x":"Run west to Draynor Village with the orb. It works like a hot-and-cold clue, warming as you get closer. The dig spot is north-west of the Draynor jail, south of the wheat field near Leela: stand four tiles north of the bush there and dig for the next clue. The jail guards are aggressive to low-level players, so keep your distance from the jail itself. That clue is a cipher, ESBZOPS QJH QFO, which decodes to DRAYNOR PIG PEN. Walk to the pig pen just north of the market, next to Martin the Master Gardener, stand in the centre and dig for the ancient casket. The casket goes to Veos in Port Sarim in the next block. In Draynor market, visit Diango's toy shop. Buy the Chronicle for 300 gp and four"},{"t":"Collect the research package and the skull","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The Lumbridge loop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t34-h","x":"Walk south from Draynor across the bridge to the Wizards' Tower and climb down to the basement. The ladder is in the room beside the tower's entrance. The ground and first floors are a multi-combat area with level 9 wizards, so don't stop to fight on the way in; the basement itself is not multi-combat. Talk to Archmage Sedridor and give him the air talisman for Rune Mysteries; he hands you a research package in exchange. Keep it. Aubury takes it in Varrock and gives you research notes back in the same slot, and those notes stay with you until Rune Mysteries is finished at this tower in section 1.3. It is the one deliberate long carry in this section, and it saves you a whole trip to the towe"},{"t":"Complete The Restless Ghost","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › The Lumbridge loop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t35-h","x":"If Home Teleport is off cooldown, cast it; otherwise run back east through Draynor to Lumbridge, a two-minute run. Walk into the graveyard building and use the skull on the coffin to complete The Restless Ghost, for 1,125 Prayer XP. It is one of the requirements for Nature Spirit, so finishing it here keeps 1.3's Morytania trip open. Take off the ghostspeak amulet, put the rainbow scarf back on, and drop the amulet. You leave Lumbridge with the kit, the Chronicle, the research package, the ancient casket, the onion, the raw sardine, the empty bucket and your food. Everything else from this loop has already been handed in. Done when The Restless Ghost is complete. Coins: about 6,510 gp · Slot"},{"t":"Port Sarim, Karamja, Rimmington and Falador","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b10-h","x":"This block completes X Marks the Spot and Witch's Potion, takes Pirate's Treasure to its last stage and starts two quests that continue in Varrock. You arrive with the casket, onion, sardine and empty bucket on top of the kit and the Chronicle. On Karamja the banana crate is filled one banana at a time, so a single free slot is enough there. Gate in the casket, onion, sardine and empty bucket; one free slot for the bananas. Carry in the kit and the Chronicle: about 20/28. Exit X Marks the Spot and Witch's Potion done; Pirate's Treasure at its last stage; A Porcine of Interest and The Knight's Sword started; about 6,640 gp. Carries forward the Pirate's Treasure key. Every Witch's Potion ingre"},{"t":"Start A Porcine of Interest and finish X Marks the Spot","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Port Sarim, Karamja, Rimmington and Falador","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t37-h","x":"On your way out of Draynor, read the notice board in the village to start A Porcine of Interest. The board stands behind Fortunato's Wine Shop. The quest continues with Sarah at the Falador farm at the end of this block, so starting it here saves a walk later. Its later stages need a rope and a fight with a level 37 sourhog, so leave them for the Draynor block later in this chapter that finishes it. Walk south to Port Sarim and find Veos on the northernmost dock, outside the Rusty Anchor. Give him the ancient casket to complete X Marks the Spot, for 200 gp, a quest point, an antique lamp worth 300 XP and a beginner scroll box. Destroy the antique lamp: Veos keeps destroyed quest lamps and ha"},{"t":"Get the rum for Pirate's Treasure","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Port Sarim, Karamja, Rimmington and Falador","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t38-h","x":"Talk to Redbeard Frank on the Port Sarim docks to start Pirate's Treasure. He wants Karamjan rum, which the customs officers confiscate if they find it on you when you sail back, so the rum has to be smuggled. He stands in front of the same northern dock as Veos, outside the Rusty Anchor. Take the boat from the Port Sarim docks to Musa Point on Karamja (30 gp). The sailors for Karamja are on the south docks; the monks there sail to Entrana instead, so don't board with them. Walk into the Karamja Spirits bar and buy one Karamjan rum from Zembo (30 gp). From this moment, don't teleport until Frank has the rum: any teleport breaks the bottle, and that includes a random event that moves you. The"},{"t":"Collect the Witch's Potion ingredients and finish it in Rimmington","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Port Sarim, Karamja, Rimmington and Falador","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t39-h","x":"While you're in Wydin's, buy one raw beef. It costs 1 gp, and he stocks only one at a time; if another player has just bought it, wait a minute for the shop to restock. Walk into Betty's magic shop and buy one eye of newt. That costs 3 gp. You already have the onion from Fred's farm. Walk west to Rimmington and talk to Hetty in her house to start Witch's Potion. Her house is in the south-east of the village. She wants an onion, burnt meat, an eye of newt and a rat's tail. Cook the beef on the range in the house next to the Rimmington general store, and cook the result again until it burns. Kill a rat near Hetty's house and pick up its tail. The small rats in the archery shop just west of her"},{"t":"Progress A Porcine of Interest and start The Knight's Sword","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Port Sarim, Karamja, Rimmington and Falador","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t40-h","x":"Walk north to Sarah's farm shop, south of Falador, and talk to Sarah for A Porcine of Interest. While you're there, open her shop with Trade and close it without buying anything: browsing Sarah's farm shop is a task in the easy Falador diary, which Chapter 2 claims. Next, use your empty bucket on the dairy cow in the farm's pen to fill it with milk. The bucket of milk is for Gertrude's cat in the Lumber Yard. The farm has only the one dairy cow, so if another player is milking it, wait a moment rather than walking to Lumbridge for another. The tool leprechaun next to the Falador allotment patch here is the first storage you'll use in 1.3, when farming starts. Nothing in this section farms, s"},{"t":"Varrock: quest starts, 5 Attack, Aubury and Old Man Yarlo","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b11-h","x":"Varrock is a talking block. Almost every stop is a dialogue that starts or advances a quest you continue later in this section, and the only items you gain are the saw, the seasoned sardine, one beer and three waxwood logs. The research package goes to Aubury and comes back as research notes in the same slot. The Chronicle's teleport lands you at the Champions' Guild, just south-west of the city, so run west to east and finish at Old Man Yarlo's house next to the east gate, where the next block starts. Gate in the research package; The Knight's Sword started with the Squire in Falador (end of the previous block); 5 Attack (trained here) for the steel axe. Carry in the kit: about 19/28. Exit "},{"t":"Start Gertrude's Cat and the square quests","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varrock: quest starts, 5 Attack, Aubury and Old Man Yarlo","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t42-h","x":"Teleport with the Chronicle and run west to Gertrude's house to start Gertrude's Cat. Her cat Fluffs has gone missing, and her sons know where. Pick a few doogle leaves from the bushes outside her house, use one on your raw sardine to make a seasoned sardine, and drop the spare leaves. The bushes grow just south of the house. Run into Varrock square. Talk to Gertrude's sons, Shilop and Wilough, and pay them the small coin fee they ask; they tell you Fluffs is hiding in the Lumber Yard north-east of the city. The fee is 100 gp. In the same square, talk to Romeo to start Romeo & Juliet; he wants a message carried to Juliet, which you do on your way back through the west of the city in the Lumb"},{"t":"Advance The Knight's Sword, start Priest in Peril and Daddy's Home","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varrock: quest starts, 5 Attack, Aubury and Old Man Yarlo","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t43-h","x":"Walk north into Varrock Palace. In the library on the ground floor, talk to Reldo for The Knight's Sword (the Squire in the White Knights' Castle, at the end of the previous block, started it and sent you here). The library is the northernmost room on that floor. He tells you about the Imcando dwarves and sends you to Thurgo south of Port Sarim, whom you visit in section 1.2 together with the Falador park dig for Pirate's Treasure. Thurgo wants a redberry pie before he helps, which is why 1.2 bakes one before that visit. On the same floor, in the south-east of the palace, talk to King Roald to start Priest in Peril. It continues at the Paterdomus temple on the way into Morytania in 1.3, so t"},{"t":"Train 5 Attack and wield the steel axe","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varrock: quest starts, 5 Attack, Aubury and Old Man Yarlo","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t44-h","x":"Train Attack from 1 to 5 on anything that can't hurt you, such as a training dummy, a chicken or a low-level goblin, using the accurate style on your bronze sword. 5 Attack is 388 XP and takes a few minutes. At 5 Attack, wield the steel axe. From now on the axe lives in your weapon slot and never takes an inventory space again, which matters most at Wintertodt, where every free slot is a root you can carry. Drop the bronze sword. Keep the wooden shield on; the steel axe is one-handed. Slots: about 19/28 · Requirements: 5 Attack to wield the steel axe Done when you are 5 Attack with the steel axe wielded."},{"t":"Visit Aubury, the Blue Moon Inn and Dimintheis","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varrock: quest starts, 5 Attack, Aubury and Old Man Yarlo","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t45-h","x":"Walk to Aubury's Rune Shop in south-east Varrock and give Aubury the research package. The shop is just south of the east bank. Keep talking until he offers you a cup of tea and accept it: it fully restores your run energy. He gives you the research notes for Sedridor. They take the package's old slot and stay with you until section 1.3. They go back to Sedridor in 1.3, on the same trip that buys the Chronicle back from Diango, and that hand-in completes Rune Mysteries and frees the slot. UIM risk Like the package, the notes can only be destroyed, not dropped, and Aubury hands out new ones if they are lost. Don't buy a stack of mind, air, water, earth and fire runes here. Nothing in this sec"},{"t":"Prepare Old Man Yarlo's house","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varrock: quest starts, 5 Attack, Aubury and Old Man Yarlo","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t46-h","x":"Walk to Old Man Yarlo's house in south-east Varrock, south-west of Aubury's shop, and talk to him for Daddy's Home. Inside, remove the old broken furniture the quest marks for removal, then talk to Yarlo again. The carpet only shows its remove option on a right-click. The quest plays short cutscenes here; if you click away from one, you have to watch it again. Search the crates in the north-western corner of his kitchen for three waxwood logs. Keep them: the sawmill operator turns them into waxwood planks for free in the next block. The waxwood bed can't be built without those planks, so don't leave the house without the logs. Done when you hold the waxwood logs and beer. What this block del"},{"t":"Varlamore teaks, the Lumber Yard, Daddy's Home and your first Construction","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b12-h","x":"This block takes Firemaking from about 37 to 50, finishes Gertrude's Cat and Daddy's Home, and gives you a house and 10 Construction for Tower of Life. It is also the tightest moment of the section: Daddy's Home needs 18 unstackable materials in your inventory at once. This block makes room in two ways. It drops the knife and tinderbox after the teaks, because Wintertodt's crates hand out free ones. And it builds at Old Man Yarlo's before completing Gertrude's Cat, whose rewards would otherwise land in the same slots. Gate in Children of the Sun; 35 Woodcutting for teaks; a hammer and saw; 28 free slots for the Daddy's Home materials. Carry in the kit, then Daddy's Home's 18 unstackable mate"},{"t":"Complete the Lily Pad quest","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varlamore teaks, the Lumber Yard, Daddy's Home and your first Construction","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t48-h","x":"Run out of Varrock's east gate to Regulus Cento and ask him to take you to Varlamore by quetzal; Children of the Sun, which you finished in the square, is what unlocked it. He stands just outside the gate. You land at Civitas illa Fortis. Travel south and start and complete The Ribbiting Tale of a Lily Pad Labour Dispute. It is a short quest that needs 15 Woodcutting and nothing you aren't already carrying, and it gives 2,000 Woodcutting XP. It starts with Marcellus, by the hardwood tree patch at the Locus Oasis; the blue frogs you deal with sit just north of the teak grove in the middle of the oasis. The quest needs an axe, and your steel axe does. When the frogs ask you to sabotage a lily "},{"t":"Burn teaks to 50 Firemaking","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varlamore teaks, the Lumber Yard, Daddy's Home and your first Construction","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t49-h","x":"Hop to a Forestry world (444 is the usual one) and chop teak logs at the teak trees near the quest area, lighting each log on the spot. Teaks need 35 Woodcutting, which you reached in Ardougne. Each teak gives 105 Firemaking XP and 85 Woodcutting XP, and Forestry events add bonus Woodcutting XP and anima-infused bark, which goes straight into your worn forestry kit. The six teak trees just east of the Locus Oasis are the main group here, and they are close to the quetzal landing. Events can spawn on any world, but on the dedicated worlds more players share them, and world 444 has a friends chat where players call events out. Events only spawn when someone chopping there has a forestry kit, w"},{"t":"Find Fluffs in the Lumber Yard","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varlamore teaks, the Lumber Yard, Daddy's Home and your first Construction","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t50-h","x":"Take the quetzal back to Varrock and walk to the Lumber Yard north-east of the city. Squeeze in through the broken fence and climb the ladder to Fluffs. The broken fence is on the yard's south side, and the ladder stands in the middle of the yard; Fluffs is on the first floor. Give her the bucket of milk, then the seasoned sardine. She still won't leave, because her kittens are missing: search the crates on the ground floor of the yard until the kitten lands in your inventory, then climb back up and use it on Fluffs. Check the crates that show a yellow \"Mew!\": the sound moves from crate to crate, but the kitten stays in one, so keep trying different crates rather than the same one. If the se"},{"t":"Buy the Daddy's Home materials at the sawmill","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varlamore teaks, the Lumber Yard, Daddy's Home and your first Construction","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t51-h","x":"Chop ten normal logs from the trees around the Lumber Yard. Give them to the sawmill operator to make ten planks, at 100 gp each. He stands along the yard's south wall. Give him the three waxwood logs too: because he knows Old Man Yarlo, he turns them into waxwood planks for free. From the same operator, buy five bolts of cloth at 650 gp each and a stack of about a hundred steel nails. Daddy's Home needs at least 16 nails, and some bend while you build, so the spare ones are cheap insurance. The nails cost 3 gp each. Use normal logs only: the quest's furniture takes plain planks, and oak, teak or mahogany planks won't work. You now hold 10 planks, 3 waxwood planks and 5 bolts of cloth on top"},{"t":"Complete Daddy's Home","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varlamore teaks, the Lumber Yard, Daddy's Home and your first Construction","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t52-h","x":"Walk to Old Man Yarlo's house in south-east Varrock. Build the five pieces of furniture where the translucent outlines stand, using the hammer and saw: the carpet, with 3 bolts of cloth; two wooden stools, with 2 planks and 4 nails in total; two wooden tables, with 6 planks and 8 nails in total; the wooden chair, with 2 planks and 2 nails; the waxwood bed, with the 3 waxwood planks and 2 bolts of cloth. Building them gives 544 Construction XP. Talk to Yarlo, then walk to Marlo in the estate agent's house in north-east Varrock to complete Daddy's Home, for another 400 XP. Since the 3 November 2026 update it counts as a full quest and gives a quest point. 944 Construction XP puts a fresh accou"},{"t":"Finish Gertrude's Cat and push Romeo & Juliet","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varlamore teaks, the Lumber Yard, Daddy's Home and your first Construction","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t53-h","x":"With the furniture built and the materials gone, run west to Gertrude's house to complete Gertrude's Cat. She gives you a kitten, a chocolate cake and a stew. Drop the kitten so it follows you instead of taking a slot, and feed it a fish or some milk whenever it says it's hungry, or it eventually runs away. Eat or drop the cake and stew; both can be made again when A Tail of Two Cats and The Queen of Thieves ask for them. A kitten needs attention as well as food. It warns you when it gets hungry, roughly 24 minutes after its last meal, and runs off if you ignore it for about six minutes more; it also complains when it is lonely, and stroking it settles it again. A kitten that runs away is go"},{"t":"Build to 10 Construction in your house","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Varlamore teaks, the Lumber Yard, Daddy's Home and your first Construction","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t54-h","x":"Open Marlo's crate. Its materials come out noted, so they cost one slot per type, and the house teleports and Falador teleport stack. Break one house teleport to arrive in your new house in Rimmington. Tower of Life needs 10 Construction, which is 1,154 XP, and it can't be boosted. You are at 944. Leave the house through the portal and walk to Phials in Rimmington, next to the house portal, and unnote six planks and six bolts of cloth; that fills your inventory to the last slot. Go back in and build torn curtains in your parlour's curtain space (3 planks, 3 bolts of cloth and 3 of the crate's mithril nails), then remove them and build them again. Each build gives 132 XP, which takes you to a"},{"t":"Tower of Life, Kourend and Wintertodt","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b13-h","x":"The last block gives you four more Construction levels from Tower of Life, takes Client of Kourend to its last stage, puts on your fourth warm item, and ends with the long Wintertodt session that closes the section. Tower of Life is the last inventory squeeze: its machines are built from parts you collect one machine at a time, about nine to eleven slots each. Before you take the Fishing Trawler teleport, make sure you have that much room. Gate in 10 Construction (not boostable) for Tower of Life; 50 Firemaking and four warm items for Wintertodt. Carry in the Tower of Life items, then about 12/28 at Wintertodt. Exit Tower of Life done; Client of Kourend at its last stage; the clue hunter gar"},{"t":"Complete Tower of Life","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Tower of Life, Kourend and Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t56-h","x":"Use the Fishing Trawler minigame teleport to reach Port Khazard and walk north to the Tower of Life. Talk to the builders outside to start Tower of Life. The quest needs 10 Construction, which you just reached, and it can't be boosted. Inside, you wear the builder's costume for the quest, so move your clue hunter boots into your inventory when the costume's boots go on. The tower has three broken machines; the parts come from the crates in the tower. The pressure machine is repaired by turning its wheels and pulling its levers in a fixed sequence and the cage by fitting bars of the right sizes side by side, so keep the wiki's steps open for both. Get the costume before you go in: the hard ha"},{"t":"Sail to Kourend and start Client of Kourend","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Tower of Life, Kourend and Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t57-h","x":"Break a house teleport and walk east from Rimmington to the Port Sarim docks, about a minute. Buy one feather at Gerrant's Fishy Business on the way (neither shop near Veos in Piscarilius sells one). Talk to Veos and ask him to take you to Port Piscarilius in Great Kourend. In Piscarilius, talk to Veos again to start Client of Kourend. He gives you an enchanted scroll; use the feather on it to make the enchanted quill, which writes a reference for each of Kourend's five houses. Veos waits on the same northern dock by the Rusty Anchor where you gave him the casket. A stripy or coloured feather also makes the quill, but a magic gold feather doesn't. Slots: about 18/28 with the scroll · Require"},{"t":"Visit the five houses","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Tower of Life, Kourend and Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t58-h","x":"Talk to the general store owner in each of the five Kourend houses about Veos and write what they tell you on the scroll: Leenz, in the Port Piscarilius general store, a few steps from Veos. Horace, in the Hosidius general store. Jennifer, in the Shayzien general store. Munty, in the Lovakengj general store. Regath, in the Arceuus general store. Use the Lovakengj minecart network to move between the houses instead of running across the whole continent. While you're in Shayzien, do one lap of the Shayzien agility course for the Kourend & Kebos diary. Port Piscarilius has its own station, so you can start riding from there. Each minecart ride costs 20 gp until you complete The Forsaken Tower, "},{"t":"Dig up the clue hunter garb","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Tower of Life, Kourend and Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t59-h","x":"Take the minecart to the Shayzien East station. Just north of the station there is a spot with two rocks; stand on it and dig with the spade for the clue hunter garb. Wear it. With the clue hunter gloves and boots and the rainbow scarf you now wear the four warm items Wintertodt asks for, and none of them costs an inventory slot. The garb goes in your body slot. If you ever destroy or lose it, dig on the same spot to get it again. Four is also the most that count: four warm items give the largest cut in the cold damage you take, and each one speeds up how fast your warmth recovers. Enter with fewer and the game warns you at the door. Take the minecart to the Northern Tundras station and walk"},{"t":"Train at Wintertodt","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Tower of Life, Kourend and Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t60-h","x":"Walk through the Doors of Dinh. The crates beside the entrance hand out a knife, a tinderbox, a hammer and a bronze axe, but only to players who aren't already carrying one; that is why you dropped your knife and tinderbox after the teaks. Take a knife and a tinderbox. Take one unfinished rejuvenation potion from the crates too, pick a bruma herb from the sprouting roots on the east or west side of the prison, and combine them into a rejuvenation potion. If you haven't done Druidic Ritual, Brew'ma at the entrance combines them for you. At this point you haven't, because Druidic Ritual comes in 1.2, so Brew'ma is your route for now. Play a calm single-world game. Chop bruma roots with your wi"},{"t":"Claim the Reward Cart in batches","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.1: Tutorial Island up to and including Wintertodt › Tower of Life, Kourend and Wintertodt","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t61-h","x":"Don't search the Reward Cart while you're still training. It holds up to 8,000 unclaimed rewards, and each reward's loot is rolled at the moment you search, using your levels at that moment. For a UIM, that turns the cart into a storage unit whose contents improve as you level. The cart stands just outside the bank in the Wintertodt camp. Coins are about one roll in five, at 2,000 to 4,999 gp each, so they average roughly 700 gp per roll. Going from 50 to 85 Firemaking earns about 450 rolls if you fletch kindling (about 230 games of 500 points; nearer 300 rolls on roots alone). Every roll count in this guide is an estimate, because drops vary per account, so each batch below is sized by what"},{"t":"End of section 1.1","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s4-h","x":"You leave Wintertodt with 85 Firemaking, 60 Woodcutting, 30 Construction, about 102,000 gp and roughly two-thirds of your estimated Wintertodt rolls still unclaimed in the cart. Section 1.2 starts right here at the camp, so you don't need to travel before it begins. Skill Level Note Firemaking 85 Higher if you stayed Woodcutting 60+ Required before cart batch 1 Construction 30+ Daddy's Home and Tower of Life take you to 14; brazier repairs do the rest Thieving about 24 Cakes, silk, Tribal Totem and Tower of Life Fletching varies From kindling; section 1.2 tops it up to 46 if needed Attack 5 Enough to wield the steel axe Where your things are Storage Contents Worn Clue hunter garb, gloves and"},{"t":"1.2: Some fishing and thieving","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s5-h","x":"Section 1.2 takes you from the Wintertodt camp to about 56 Fishing from Tempoross, 46 Fletching, about 53 Agility from the early rooftops and barbarian fishing, about 55 Thieving and a coin stack for section 1.3, with seventeen more quests completed on the way. Two things stand out. First, the rogue outfit moves to 1.3: the Rogues' Den maze needs an empty inventory and nothing worn, and the wiki's UIM advice is to collect it once your house has an armour case to put each piece in. Second, blackjacking therefore stops around 55 Thieving here and resumes, with double loot, in 1.3. Tempoross becomes your third deferred storage after Wintertodt's Reward Cart and Veos's lamps. Its reward pool hol"},{"t":"Leaving Kourend","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b14-h","x":"You start 1.2 at the Wintertodt camp with about 13 items: coins, research notes, spade, hammer, saw, knife, tinderbox, the arrow shafts, the house and Falador teleports, 5 noted steel bars, 10 noted oak planks and 2 noted iron ore, with the Chronicle worn. This block finishes Client of Kourend, takes Thieving from about 24 to 41 on the Hosidius fruit stalls, and picks up the one Kourend item the next blocks need: raw rat meat for Druidic Ritual. Gate in the Dark Altar visit; 25 Thieving for the fruit stalls. Carry in about 13 items from Wintertodt: about 13 to 16/28. Exit Client of Kourend done; Thieving trained on the fruit stalls; the rat meat collected and the saltpetre diary task done; a"},{"t":"Finish Client of Kourend","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Leaving Kourend","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t65-h","x":"Take the minecart from the Northern Tundras to the Port Piscarilius station (20 gp a ride) and walk to Veos on the Piscarilius docks. The fare stays at 20 gp until you complete The Forsaken Tower, after which every ride is free, so budget a few rides through this block. The orb shattered into broken glass when you activated it, so just talk to him and finish the dialogue to complete Client of Kourend. Veos claims at first that he hasn't seen you since he brought you to Kourend; keep talking, because his client takes over his voice and hands you the reward before letting him go. It rewards 1 quest point, two antique lamps of 500 XP each, the Kourend Castle Teleport spell and Kharedst's memoir"},{"t":"Train Thieving on the Hosidius fruit stalls","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Leaving Kourend","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t66-h","x":"Take the minecart to Hosidius and walk to the building just east of the market square (north of two magic trees), where two unguarded fruit stalls stand next to each other. Use these two and not the four stalls in the square itself: level 44 guard dogs watch the square, and they attack anyone they see stealing. The stalls need 25 Thieving, which Wintertodt's camp left you just short of or at, depending on your silk count; if you're below 25, steal a few cakes from the Kourend Castle courtyard bakery first. The bakery stall needs only 5 Thieving and gives 16 XP a cake, so a short session there covers the gap. Steal from the two stalls in turn. Each successful steal gives 28.5 Thieving XP and "},{"t":"Collect the rat meat, dig saltpetre and visit the estate agent","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Leaving Kourend","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t67-h","x":"Walk north of Hosidius town square and kill a giant rat for its raw rat meat. That is one of the four raw meats Druidic Ritual needs in Taverley; the other three are bought or killed near Falador, so this is the only one you carry across the sea. The rats there are level 6 and aggressive, so expect one to attack you as you arrive, and every Kourend giant rat drops raw rat meat. Take nothing else from the rat. UIM risk The meat is the one item from this block that rides all the way to Taverley, so don't drop it by accident when you trim the kit in Port Sarim; if you lose it, the giant rats north of the Port Sarim chapel drop another. Walk to the five saltpetre deposits north-east of the Woodc"},{"t":"Port Sarim, Rimmington and Falador","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b15-h","x":"This block is the main shopping stop of the section. It finishes Pirate's Treasure, moves your house to Pollnivneach, and gathers every ingredient the four Taverley quests in the next block need. The ingredients are what make it tight: by the time you leave Falador you hold about 26 items, and the next block hands them in one quest at a time until Doric's Quest, the hungriest of the four, has the twelve slots it needs. Gate in a spade; about 75,000 gp for runes, feathers, ingredients and the house move. Carry in the trimmed kit, then every Taverley ingredient: about 26/28 by Falador. Exit Pirate's Treasure done; the house moved to Pollnivneach; every ingredient for the four Taverley quests h"},{"t":"Trim the Wintertodt kit","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Port Sarim, Rimmington and Falador","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t69-h","x":"Before you buy anything, make room. Drop the saw: nothing before 1.3 builds furniture, and the saw that spawns in the Varrock estate agent's house is free whenever you want it back. Drop the tinderbox; Tempoross and the Trawler provide their own fires, and the general stores sell one for a coin. Drop the 10 noted oak planks too. Don't keep them for 1.3: the Tempoross reward pool and the Varrock sawmill both give oak planks right when 1.3 needs them, and in between they'd cost a slot through the whole section. Eat your strange fruit when your run energy is low and drop the rest. Keep the 5 noted steel bars. They are the five clockworks for your first bird houses in 1.4, and you can't smelt st"},{"t":"Buy runes, feathers and the quest ingredients in Port Sarim","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Port Sarim, Rimmington and Falador","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t70-h","x":"Veos drops you on the Port Sarim docks. You don't have a rune pouch yet, so every rune type costs a slot, and this guide buys only four types. In Betty's magic shop, in the north-west corner of the town, buy about 500 air, 1,000 water, 1,000 mind and 150 chaos runes as single runes, for about 22,500 gp, most of it the chaos runes. Betty keeps 5,000 of each elemental and mind rune but only 250 chaos runes at 90 gp each, so if another player has just bought her out, hop worlds rather than wait for the restock. That is Water Strike now and Water Bolt at 23 Magic, the spells the experiments, warlords and Feud fighters ahead are weakest to, with enough margin to train Magic as you quest. Water St"},{"t":"Pick the onions in Rimmington","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Port Sarim, Rimmington and Falador","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t71-h","x":"Walk west to Rimmington and pick two onions from the field just north of the village. With the three redberries, they let Aggie make the yellow and red dyes that combine into orange for Goblin Diplomacy. The field has 15 onions and each one regrows about 30 seconds after it is picked, so even on a busy world you won't wait long. Slots: about 24/28 Done when you hold the onions."},{"t":"Finish Pirate's Treasure and buy the woad leaves","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Port Sarim, Rimmington and Falador","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t72-h","x":"Walk north to Falador and into the park. Dig at the spot the Blue Moon Inn message described to complete Pirate's Treasure. The spot is near the statue of Saradomin in the middle of the park: look for the patch of dirt that roughly forms an X, stand in its centre and dig. A gardener attacks you the moment you dig; he is level 4, so kill him with a couple of Water Strikes and dig again. You can't dig again while he is alive; if you would rather not fight, walk out of the park until he despawns and then come back to the same spot. The casket holds coins, a gold ring and an emerald. Keep the coins and drop the ring and the emerald: you have no slots to spare, and the Al Kharid gem trader sells "},{"t":"Move your house to Pollnivneach","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Port Sarim, Rimmington and Falador","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t73-h","x":"Talk to the Falador estate agent and pay 7,500 gp to move your house to Pollnivneach. From now on every house teleport tablet from Marlo's crate drops you in the desert town where you blackjack, a few steps from the bandits and from the bar that sells their food. It turns the tablets you already carry into free trips to your training spot. The move needs 20 Construction, which your Wintertodt repairs passed long ago, and boosts can't be used for it. The town itself has no desert heat, so arriving by tablet costs you no water, while the magic carpet from the Shantay Pass would cost 200 gp every trip. Don't take the Knight's Sword portrait now: you pass back through Falador on the way to Thurg"},{"t":"Draynor dyes and the Taverley quests","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b16-h","x":"This block completes Goblin Diplomacy, Druidic Ritual, Witch's House and Doric's Quest, unlocks Herblore, and starts Fishing Contest and Below Ice Mountain. It is built as a chain of hand-ins. You arrive with about 26 slots filled, and the order below makes each quest return the space the next one needs: Aggie turns seven ingredients into two dyes, Druidic Ritual eats four raw meats, Witch's House the cheese, Goblin Diplomacy the dyes, and that leaves Doric's Quest exactly the twelve slots it needs for its ores. Gate in the kit and every ingredient (about 26 slots); Water Strike (5 Magic); 16 quest points for Below Ice Mountain. Carry in the ingredients, used in the order below: about 26/28 "},{"t":"Have Aggie make the dyes","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Draynor dyes and the Taverley quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t75-h","x":"Walk south-east from Falador to Draynor Village and find Aggie in her house, at the end of a short dead-end road that branches off the east road through the village. Use each set of ingredients on her rather than going through her dialogue: the two onions for yellow dye, the three redberries for red dye and the two woad leaves for blue dye, 5 gp each. Mix the red and yellow dyes together into orange. Mix them with each other and not on a goblin mail: red dye used on a yellow mail, or yellow on a red one, gives you a red or yellow mail, not an orange one. You now hold an orange dye and a blue dye in place of seven ingredients. Done when you hold the dyes. Coins: about 70,400 gp · Slots: about"},{"t":"Rooftops to 30: Draynor and Al Kharid","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Draynor dyes and the Taverley quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t76-h","x":"Most of 1.2 is on foot, and run energy is what runs out first. Before you go north for the bear, put an hour and a half into the rooftop courses: Draynor to 20 Agility, then Al Kharid to 30. Varrock's course takes you to 40 in the next block, and the marks of grace you collect on all three go towards the graceful outfit in 1.3. The Draynor course starts at the rough wall next to the wheat field north of Draynor's bank. Since the May 2024 update it has no Agility requirement and none of its obstacles can fail. A lap is 120 XP and takes about 43 seconds, roughly 10,000 XP an hour, so 1 to 20 Agility (4,470 XP) is about 37 laps, or half an hour. Each lap ends when you climb down a crate off Ned"},{"t":"Kill a bear for its meat","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Draynor dyes and the Taverley quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t77-h","x":"Walk back north through Falador and out of its north gate. North of Falador, where the path meets the trees, there are bears; kill one from behind the trees so it can't reach you. These are the four black bears outside the Mind Altar ruins, east of Goblin Village and short of Ice Mountain. A black bear is level 19, hits no more than 3 and isn't aggressive, so you pick the one you fight. Use Water Strike from a spot it can't path to, then take the raw bear meat. That is the fourth Druidic Ritual meat. Every black bear drops one, so if a second player takes the kill from you, wait for the respawn rather than look elsewhere. Slots: about 23/28 · Requirements: Water Strike (5 Magic) Done when yo"},{"t":"Complete Druidic Ritual","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Draynor dyes and the Taverley quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t78-h","x":"Walk west into Taverley and north to the stone circle, and talk to Kaqemeex to start Druidic Ritual. He sends you to Sanfew, upstairs in the house south of the circle, who asks for four raw meats dipped in the Cauldron of Thunder. Sanfew's house is the large octagonal Herblore shop in the south of the village, marked with a herb icon on the minimap; tell him you were sent to help. The cauldron is in Taverley Dungeon, whose ladder is just south of the village. Head north past the skeletons to the gate on the dungeon's east side, flanked by the two suits of armour. The skeletons on the way are level 22 and 25, so keep running and don't stop to fight them. Two suits of armour come to life when "},{"t":"Complete Witch's House","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Draynor dyes and the Taverley quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t79-h","x":"Talk to the boy by the hedges near Taverley's eastern entrance to start Witch's House; his ball is locked in the witch's shed. Find the key hidden by the house's front door and let yourself in. Walk west and then north around the hedge to reach the door, and search the pot just north of it for the key. Go down to the basement. With your gloves on, open the gate; any gloves work, including your clue hunter gloves, and the boxes in the basement give leather gloves if you have none. The ladder down is in the northern room. Search the cupboard behind the gate for a magnet. Go back upstairs to the small room on the south side, drop your cheese there and use the magnet on the mouse the moment it a"},{"t":"Complete Goblin Diplomacy","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Draynor dyes and the Taverley quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t80-h","x":"Walk to Goblin Village, north of Falador and east of Taverley, and talk to the two goblin generals to start Goblin Diplomacy. They argue about the colour of their armour and want three goblin mails to choose from. Collect three goblin mails in the village; goblins there drop them, and three named crates in the village each hold one. One crate is behind the generals' hut, one inside the western hut between the small square hut and the generals' hut, and one up a ladder near the village gate. Use the orange dye on one goblin mail and the blue dye on another. Leave the third one plain: if you dye it by mistake, its crate won't give you another, and you'd have to kill goblins until one drops a m"},{"t":"Complete Doric's Quest","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Draynor dyes and the Taverley quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t81-h","x":"On your way to Doric, stop at the Falador west bank and unnote your noted iron ore at a bank booth into two ore; that is the one thing a UIM may still do at a bank. Walk north to Doric's hut and talk to him to start Doric's Quest. His hut is the small house at the crossroads north of Falador, east of the Taverley gate and south of Goblin Village. He wants 6 clay, 4 copper ore and 2 iron ore, all at once and unnoted, and gives you a bronze pickaxe to mine them. He asks for plain clay, not soft clay, so don't wet it. Walk east to the Dwarven Mine and climb down. From Doric's hut, go east and then north up the path onto Ice Mountain; the ladder down is among the buildings and dwarves on the mou"},{"t":"Start Fishing Contest and Below Ice Mountain","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Draynor dyes and the Taverley quests","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t82-h","x":"Walk north from Taverley to Austri at the eastern entrance of the White Wolf Mountain tunnel and talk to him to start Fishing Contest. He gives you a fishing pass, which you take to Hemenster in the Catherby block. The quest needs 10 Fishing to start and it can't be boosted; Sea Slug's 7,175 Fishing XP already took you well past it. The pass is the only item this start adds, and it rides with you until the contest itself. Finally, walk back south-east toward Ice Mountain and talk to Willow to start Below Ice Mountain. She stands on the path south of Ice Mountain, north-east of Falador and just south of the Dwarven Mine entrance you used for Doric. It needs 16 quest points to start, which you"},{"t":"Varrock and Varlamore","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b17-h","x":"This block puts a staff of air in your weapon slot, completes Shield of Arrav and starts Ethically Acquired Antiquities, which needs Shield of Arrav finished first. You arrive with about 17 items and leave with about 20, the two iron bars included: the staff swaps your air runes for the steel axe in the inventory, and the only new carry is a pie dish for Thurgo's redberry pie. Gate in a partner from the other gang for Shield of Arrav; Children of the Sun and 25 Thieving for Ethically Acquired Antiquities. Carry in about 17/28. Exit a staff of air wielded; 40 Agility from the Varrock rooftops; Shield of Arrav done; Ethically Acquired Antiquities started; about 69,700 gp. Carries forward the p"},{"t":"Wield a staff of air","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Varrock and Varlamore","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t84-h","x":"The Chronicle drops you at the Champions' Guild. Walk into Varrock to Zaff's Superior Staffs and buy a staff of air. Wield it: it supplies unlimited air runes for every Strike and Bolt spell, so you can drop your air rune stack straight away. The steel axe moves into your inventory, so the swap costs nothing. The staff costs 1,500 gp and Zaff keeps only two in stock, so if both are gone, hop worlds rather than wait for the restock. Done when you wield a staff of air. Coins: about 69,100 gp · Slots: about 17/28 · Requirements: none"},{"t":"Varrock rooftops to 40","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Varrock and Varlamore","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t85-h","x":"Before the palace, train on the Varrock Rooftop Course to 40 Agility. Climb the rough wall on the east side of the Varrock General Store to start. It needs 30 Agility and gives about 270 XP a lap of about 1 minute 10 seconds, roughly 14,000 XP and 8 to 11 marks of grace an hour. The clothes line (3 to 8 damage) and one wall (2 to 5) can fail; as in Al Kharid, wait out low Hitpoints rather than carry food. 30 to 40 is about 23,900 XP, roughly 88 laps or just under two hours, and you should finish with around 30 marks. Each lap ends with a jump off the house south of Lowe's Archery Emporium, and your first full lap completes a Varrock medium diary task. 40 Agility is also what the Canifis cour"},{"t":"Pick up the pie dish","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Varrock and Varlamore","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t86-h","x":"In Varrock Palace, take the pie dish from the kitchen. It is for the redberry pie that buys Thurgo's help with The Knight's Sword in the next block. While you're in the palace, talk to Reldo and ask about quests to start Shield of Arrav; read the book he points you to and talk to him again. Reldo is in the northernmost room of the palace library, and the book is a blue-and-white one on the top shelf of the bookcase east of the short bookcases in the middle of the room. Slots: about 18/28 Done when you hold the pie dish."},{"t":"Complete Shield of Arrav with a partner","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Varrock and Varlamore","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t87-h","x":"Shield of Arrav needs two players, one in each of two gangs, who swap a key and some crossbows. Join the clan chat \"osrs soa\" and ask for a partner from the other gang. Join the Black Arm Gang, because Phoenix players looking for a Black Arm partner are more common, so you find one faster. Black Arm Gang. Talk to Charlie the Tramp next to Varrock's southern entrance, at the end of the alley to the Black Arm hideout, then go in and talk to Katrine. She wants two Phoenix crossbows from the Phoenix weapon store. Get the weapon store key from your Phoenix partner, kill the Weaponsmaster inside with Water Strike, and take two Phoenix crossbows to Katrine, who makes you a gang member. The weapon s"},{"t":"Start Ethically Acquired Antiquities in Varlamore","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Varrock and Varlamore","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t88-h","x":"Ethically Acquired Antiquities needs Children of the Sun, Shield of Arrav and 25 Thieving, all of which you now have. Run out of Varrock's east gate to Regulus Cento and take the quetzal to Civitas illa Fortis. The quest needs no items and has no fights, and its quest items come and go within a few steps of each other. In the Grand Museum in the north of the city, inspect the empty display case in the north-east corner to start Ethically Acquired Antiquities, then talk to Curator Herminius in the middle of the museum about it. Investigate the tools behind the case, inspect the case again, ask the visitors in the museum, talk to Curator Herminius once more, and then ask Regulus Cento at the l"},{"t":"Iron bars, Thurgo and The Knight's Sword","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b18-h","x":"This block completes The Knight's Sword and Ethically Acquired Antiquities. The Knight's Sword alone takes Smithing from 1 to 29, which is what lets you start Sleeping Giants in the desert next. You arrive in Varrock with about 20 items including the two iron bars from Varlamore, pick up the pie ingredients, the portrait and the blurite ore in that order, and hand each in within the same trip. Nothing new leaves the block with you. Gate in two iron bars; 10 Cooking for the pie; 10 Mining for blurite. Carry in about 20 to 22/28. Exit The Knight's Sword and Ethically Acquired Antiquities done; Smithing about 29; about 25,000 gp. Carries forward nothing new. The one real danger is the Asgarnia "},{"t":"Check your two iron bars","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Iron bars, Thurgo and The Knight's Sword","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t90-h","x":"The Knight's Sword needs two iron bars, and you can't smelt iron until 15 Smithing. You collected two iron bars in Varlamore at the end of the previous block, from the spawns upstairs in the Shields of Mistrock and on the Sunset Coast. The only Wilderness iron bar spawn is north-west of Ferox Enclave, so don't fetch one there: a UIM death in the Wilderness hands everything to the killer. Slots: about 20/28 · Requirements: none Done when you hold two iron bars."},{"t":"Bake the redberry pie","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Iron bars, Thurgo and The Knight's Sword","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t91-h","x":"Break the Falador teleport tablet from Marlo's crate and walk south to Port Sarim. Before anything else, pick up the Port Sarim leads for Ethically Acquired Antiquities, since you're here anyway: on the southernmost dock, talk to Trader Stan or one of his crewmembers about the grey-haired man with the case. They tell you he headed north looking for runes. In Betty's magic shop, talk to Betty, read the note she gives you, and destroy it once read. Have a free slot when you talk to her, because she hands you the note during the conversation; the note is what tells you the man wanted the runes for a Varrock Teleport, which is why the trail now leads to the Varrock Museum. While you're at her co"},{"t":"Bribe Thurgo and take the portrait","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Iron bars, Thurgo and The Knight's Sword","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t92-h","x":"Walk south-west from Port Sarim to Mudskipper Point and find Thurgo in his hut. His hut is on the west side of the hill south of Port Sarim, with an anvil beside it. Give him the redberry pie, then ask him about the sword. He can make one, but needs a picture of it to copy. That conversation is what makes the squire tell you about the portrait, so walk north to Falador now and talk to the squire in the White Knights' Castle courtyard. Climb the ladder on the east side of the castle to the first floor, walk west and climb the staircase. From the courtyard that means going east through three doors to the ladder, then west through a door and an open doorway to the staircase. Sir Vyvin's bedroom"},{"t":"Mine the blurite and complete The Knight's Sword","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Iron bars, Thurgo and The Knight's Sword","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t93-h","x":"The trapdoor into the Asgarnia Ice Dungeon is on the hill just east of Thurgo's hut. Climb down with full Hitpoints. Follow the dungeon until you reach the icy area with the ice warriors and ice giants, and keep moving along the southern wall to the blurite rocks. Every monster in this dungeon is aggressive, including the level 26 pirates you meet first: from the ladder, run north until you reach them, take the first corridor east and enter the large icy room. The blurite rocks are at its south-eastern end, beside the entrance to the skeletal wyvern area, and standing directly in front of that entrance is a safespot from which you can mine without the giants and warriors reaching you. Mine o"},{"t":"Recover the diadem and finish Ethically Acquired Antiquities","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Iron bars, Thurgo and The Knight's Sword","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t94-h","x":"From Falador, teleport to Varrock with the Chronicle. Walk to the Varrock Museum. Pickpocket Curator Haig Halen for the storeroom key. Following the wiki's order, tell him first that you are looking for Xerna's Diadem; he acts suspicious and refuses to help, and then you take the key from him. Open the storeroom on the ground floor and search the single unstacked crate inside for Xerna's Diadem. The storeroom is in the north-east of the museum, directly under the stairs to the first floor. Confront Haig with it; the dialogue has a shame meter, and you keep pressing him until he agrees to return the diadem. Options that call him a thief or criticise his museum usually raise the meter, and som"},{"t":"Al Kharid and the desert","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b19-h","x":"This block completes The Feud and Tourist Trap, starts Prince Ali Rescue, and gets your first blackjacking session in Pollnivneach, to 55 Thieving. The Feud's 15,000 Thieving XP is the biggest single jump of the section, and its oak blackjack is what unlocks blackjacking at all. Gate in 10 Fletching and 20 Smithing for Tourist Trap; 30 Thieving for The Feud; 45 Thieving and a blackjack for bandits. Carry in about 18 to 22/28, 26 for a moment at the mining camp gate; wines while blackjacking. Exit Prince Ali Rescue started; Tourist Trap and The Feud done; 55 Thieving; about 125,000 gp. Carries forward the willow blackjack. One quest from the desert trip moves out of this section: Sleeping Gia"},{"t":"Start Prince Ali Rescue","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Al Kharid and the desert","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t96-h","x":"Walk south from Varrock to the Al Kharid toll gate and pay the 10 gp to pass. In the palace, talk to Hassan to start Prince Ali Rescue, then talk to Osman just outside. Hassan is in the palace's southern chamber; ask him whether he needs help, and he sends you to Osman, who waits outside the northern side of the palace. He lists what the rescue needs; you collect it in 1.4, so this is a dialogue stop that saves a later walk. The collecting happens in 1.4's Lumbridge and Draynor block, where you also smelt the bronze key yourself: since January 2026 Osman no longer makes it for you. Done when Prince Ali Rescue is started. Coins: about 25,000 gp · Slots: about 18/28 · Requirements: none"},{"t":"Prepare for the desert at the Shantay Pass","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Al Kharid and the desert","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t97-h","x":"Walk south to the Shantay Pass. From Shantay's shop, buy a desert shirt, desert robe and desert boots and wear all three. They replace the clue hunter garb and boots, which you drop: Wintertodt is behind you, and both are dug up again for free if you ever want them. Destroy the rainbow scarf too, for the same reason: it has no stats, its only job was warm clothing for Wintertodt, and if you ever want it back Diango sells another for 120 gp and Gilbert, in the flower field south-east of Barbarian Village, gives one free. Then buy one full waterskin, one Shantay pass and three bronze bars: one for Tourist Trap's prototype dart and two spares, because the dart tip can fail. One waterskin and on"},{"t":"Complete Tourist Trap","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Al Kharid and the desert","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t98-h","x":"Talk to Irena at the Shantay Pass to start Tourist Trap. Her daughter Ana is being held at the Desert Mining Camp, and the quest needs 10 Fletching and 20 Smithing, both of which you have. Show a Shantay pass to the guard and cross into the desert. The quest's main fight is the Mercenary Captain at the mining camp gate. He can be safespotted with Water Strike or Water Bolt (Oziris has a video of the spot). He is level 47, and the order matters: talk to him first and finish his whole dialogue, because attacking him before it ends teleports you away, hurts you and costs you your water. The dialogue itself ends by starting the fight. The wiki's safespot uses one of his mercenaries: wait until o"},{"t":"Complete The Feud","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Al Kharid and the desert","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t99-h","x":"Back in Al Kharid, talk to Ali Morrisane in the market to start The Feud; it needs 30 Thieving, which you passed in Hosidius. Buy a Kharidian headpiece and a fake beard from him and combine them into a desert disguise. Pick up an empty bucket for the camel dung step if you don't have one. The disguise doesn't have to be worn all the time; you put it on for the mayor's villa later. Break a house teleport tablet: your house is now in Pollnivneach, so the portal drops you at the start of the quest. Buy three beers from Ali the Barman (2 gp each) and use them on Drunken Ali to get information, then work through the gangs. Drunken Ali is in the bar in the south-east of town; finish each conversat"},{"t":"Blackjack bandits to 55 Thieving","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Al Kharid and the desert","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t100-h","x":"The Feud has taken you to about 45 Thieving, which is enough for the bearded Pollnivnian bandits (45 to 55). Wield the willow blackjack. Lure a bandit into a quiet corner, knock it out, then pickpocket it twice while it's unconscious; repeat. If a knock-out fails, the bandit turns aggressive: try the knock-out again at once, or, with a full inventory, select Pickpocket on it, which steals nothing but resets its aggression (if it attacks anyway, unequip the blackjack and knock it out to stop the attacks). The bearded bandits wander the north of town, between the general store and the rug merchant. The wiki's luring spot is Ali the Dyer's house in the north: it is small, other bandits can't se"},{"t":"Catherby, Seers and Hemenster","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b20-h","x":"This block takes Fishing to 35, the level Tempoross needs, finishes Fletching to 46, and completes Murder Mystery and Fishing Contest. It is a low-risk, low-slot block: drop your remaining wines before you leave Pollnivneach, and the quest items here come and go within the same short walk. Fly fishing is the backbone, and both quests are threaded into the fishing rather than done as separate trips. Fishing Contest is already started: Austri gave you the fishing pass in the Taverley block, so the pass is the only thing it brings in. Nothing in this chapter needs Murder Mystery, but Chapter 2 does, for Recipe for Disaster's Lumbridge Guide and for King's Ransom, and this walk passes the mansio"},{"t":"Travel to Catherby and finish 46 Fletching","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Catherby, Seers and Hemenster","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t102-h","x":"Use the Fishing Trawler minigame teleport to reach Port Khazard and charter a ship to Catherby. The trader crew stand on the Port Khazard docks, and the ship drops you in the harbour south of Catherby; Hickton's Archery Emporium is in the centre of the town, a short walk north. In Hickton's Archery Emporium, buy steel arrowtips. If you made arrow shafts in Lumbridge, add a feather to each shaft to make headless arrows as you walk, then add a steel arrowtip to each headless arrow. Both actions work in batches of 15, and steel arrows need 30 Fletching, which you already have. Each steel arrow is about 6 Fletching XP (1 for the headless arrow, 5 for the tip). From about 32 Fletching, 46 (67,983"},{"t":"Collect the Fishing Contest supplies","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Catherby, Seers and Hemenster","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t103-h","x":"Walk west to Seers' Village. Take the garlic from the table in the house south-west of the Seers' Village bank. Walk west to McGrubor's Wood, which lies west of Seers' Village and north of Hemenster, and squeeze through the loose railing on its northern edge. The main entrance is closed to you (a forester stands in it and the southern gate is locked), so the railing is the only way in: the loose section sits immediately north-east of the small building set into the northern fence. The guard dogs inside are level 44 and aggressive, and they attack anyone who gets close, so move straight to the red vines west of the fairy ring, near the western fence. You dropped your wines in Pollnivneach and"},{"t":"Fly fish to 35 and complete Murder Mystery","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Catherby, Seers and Hemenster","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t104-h","x":"Fly fish with your rod and feathers at the river just north of the Seers' Village bank. Trout give 50 XP and need 20 Fishing; from 30 you also catch salmon at 70 XP. Drop every fish as it lands. Cooking comes from barbarian fishing later at no slot cost, so there's no reason to carry raw fish here. Between inventories, do Murder Mystery at the Sinclair Mansion just north of the fishing spot. You need an empty pot: buy one for 1 gp at Arhein's General Goods on the Catherby pier before you walk over. Arhein's is on the docks where your charter landed, so buy the pot as you arrive rather than walking back from Seers'. The mansion stands north of Camelot Castle. Talk to the guard at the gate and"},{"t":"Complete Fishing Contest at Hemenster","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Catherby, Seers and Hemenster","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t105-h","x":"Walk south-west from Seers' Village to Hemenster, west of the Ranging Guild. In the house opposite the entrance, buy a fishing rod from Grandpa Jack for 5 gp. Show your fishing pass to Morris at the gate and walk in. Morris lets you in only with the pass, so keep it until you are through the gate. Put the garlic into the third pipe from the gate on the south wall of the northern building. Do this before you pay: the Sinister Stranger, who is fishing at the spot by the pipes, complains about the smell once the contest starts and swaps places with you. Pay Bonzo the 5 gp entry fee, then fish at the spot by the pipes using the red vine worms. You catch a giant carp, the winning fish, and Bonzo "},{"t":"Tempoross to 56 Fishing","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b21-h","x":"This block trains Fishing from 35 to 56 at Tempoross and banks a large stack of reward permits in its reward pool. Tempoross suits a UIM almost perfectly. The crates on the docks supply the harpoons, ropes, buckets and hammers the fight uses, so you arrive with an empty-ish inventory and leave with nothing new in it. It is also safe in the way a UIM cares about most: Tempoross's attacks deal no damage, and the only things the cove can take from you are its own tools and the harpoonfish you are holding, so nothing from your kit is ever at risk here. The reward pool is the third deferred storage of the chapter: it holds up to 8,000 permits, and each reward is rolled at the moment you collect i"},{"t":"Travel to the Ruins of Unkah","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Tempoross to 56 Fishing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t107-h","x":"Cast Lumbridge Home Teleport, walk east through the Al Kharid toll gate (10 gp) and south through the town to Ferryman Sathwood, just south of the Al Kharid bank. He ferries you to the Ruins of Unkah and the Sea Spirit dock. Talk to Captain Pudi on the dock the first time for an outline of the fight. The boat out to the fight leaves from the sea spirit dock on the west side of the ruins. Slots: about 17/28 · Requirements: 35 Fishing Done when you are at Tempoross."},{"t":"Fight Tempoross on a mass world","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Tempoross to 56 Fishing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t108-h","x":"Join a Tempoross mass world, where a full boat makes the fight fast and forgiving. The wiki lists worlds 341 (UK), 422 (US west) and 463 (Germany) as the official Tempoross worlds. Take a harpoon, a rope, a bucket and a hammer from the crates as the round starts; they belong to the minigame and stay behind when you leave. Get off the boat quickly at the start; the wiki's tip is to click far west on the minimap. Each round, harpoon raw harpoonfish at the fishing spots on your side of the island, cook them at the shrine, and load them into the cannon. On a mass world, load only the cannon nearest the ship's entrance, as the wiki advises. Below 85 Fishing the wiki's standard rhythm is to catch "},{"t":"Fishing Trawler and the angler's outfit","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b22-h","x":"This block collects the four-piece angler's outfit, which adds 2.5% Fishing XP for the whole barbarian fishing grind that follows and is the base of the spirit angler's outfit later. It is the most passive block of the section. The full set takes about 48 games on average, so plan it for a relaxed evening. Gate in 15 Fishing. Carry in about 19/28 with the slave robes. Exit the four-piece angler's outfit. Carries forward the angler's outfit (into the armour case in 1.3). You need only two tools beyond your core kit: the steel axe and the hammer you already carry. An axe and a hammer let you skip swamp paste entirely, which saves a purchase and a slot. The axe has to be an ordinary one (a bles"},{"t":"Play Fishing Trawler","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Fishing Trawler and the angler's outfit","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t110-h","x":"Use the Fishing Trawler minigame teleport to reach Port Khazard; Fishing Trawler needs 15 Fishing. Board the trawler with your axe and hammer. A game takes about 6.5 minutes with docking and cutscenes, 5 of them trawling. The wiki lists worlds 315 (US west) and 370 (US east) as the official Trawler worlds. During a game, the boat springs leaks and tentacles grab the railings. Chop the tentacles with your axe and repair the broken railings with your hammer, staying close to the railings and clicking quickly, because the other players compete for them. If you want extra activity, bail water with a bailing bucket; an ordinary bucket doesn't work, but you can search the crates on the trawler's d"},{"t":"Waterfall, Fight Arena and Tree Gnome Village","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b23-h","x":"This block completes three combat quests south and west of Ardougne. Together they give about 37,000 Attack XP and 13,750 Strength XP, which takes Attack to around 40 and Strength to around 30, plus the 15 Strength that barbarian fishing needs and the spirit tree network. Every fight is safespotted with Water Strike or Water Bolt from your staff of air, so you never melee anything here. The order follows the geography and the item chain: Lady Servil stands at the corner of the Tree Gnome Village maze, the dungeon under that maze holds Glarial's pebble, and the Waterfall Quest can't start its tomb step without the pebble, so it comes last. Gate in safespots for every fight; 5 free slots for t"},{"t":"Prepare in East Ardougne","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Waterfall, Fight Arena and Tree Gnome Village","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t112-h","x":"From Port Khazard, walk north to East Ardougne. At Aemad's Adventuring Supplies, buy one rope for the Waterfall. That rope is the only new item this block needs from a shop. Swap your angler's outfit back into the inventory and put the slave robes on, or keep wearing the angler pieces; neither set matters for these fights. The head and body pieces of whichever set you wear come off for Fight Arena's Khazard armour, and everything worn goes on the table for Glarial's Tomb, which bans armour. Slots: about 17/28 · Requirements: none Done when your kit for the three quests is ready."},{"t":"Complete Fight Arena","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Waterfall, Fight Arena and Tree Gnome Village","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t113-h","x":"Walk south-west of the Ardougne Monastery to Lady Servil, by the north-east corner of the Tree Gnome Village maze, and talk to her to start Fight Arena. Search the chest in the most north-eastern house of the Khazard camp for the Khazard helmet and armour, and wear both; your current helmet and body piece go into the inventory for the duration. The camp is the group of buildings south of the monastery, and the prison is south of the camp. The guards let you into the prison only while you wear the armour, and they won't speak to you inside if you take it off, so keep both pieces on until the fights are over. Your other slots don't matter, so your staff stays wielded. Talk to Sammy Servil in h"},{"t":"Complete Tree Gnome Village and get Glarial's pebble","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Waterfall, Fight Arena and Tree Gnome Village","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t114-h","x":"Walk into the Tree Gnome Village maze and follow it to the centre, then talk to King Bolren to start Tree Gnome Village. Elkoy leads you back out. Chop six normal logs near the maze with your steel axe; they are the quest's only item. Walk north to the battlefield and talk to Commander Montai, in red, at the south-west edge of the battlefield south of the river. Give him the six logs, then talk to him again. Find the three tracker gnomes on the battlefield and ask each one for his coordinate. The first is north-west of the Khazard stronghold, by its largest north-western building; the second is locked in a prison cell in the north-eastern building; the third wanders outside its south-west co"},{"t":"Complete the Waterfall Quest","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Waterfall, Fight Arena and Tree Gnome Village","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t115-h","x":"Walk north-west to Almera's house above Baxtorian Falls and talk to her to start Waterfall Quest. Take the raft down to Hudon on the rock in the river and talk to him; you wash ashore. Go through every line of Hudon's dialogue before you leave him: if you cut it short, the book you need next doesn't appear. From his island, swim south and you wash up near a large building with a fisherman outside. In Hadley's house nearby, read the book on Baxtorian, which tells you about Glarial's tomb. The book is upstairs, in the southernmost bookcase on the eastern wall. Read it and then close it. Glarial's tomb is east of Hadley's house. You may not take weapons, armour, runes, fletching items or a loot"},{"t":"Barbarian fishing and Death on the Isle","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b24-h","x":"This block is the long grind of the section: barbarian fishing from about 43 to about 53 Agility, which also takes Fishing into the 70s, Strength up, and Cooking past 43 if you cut-eat. It is UIM-friendly in the best way. It needs only Otto's heavy rod, your feather stack and your knife, everything you catch is cut or dropped on the spot, and nothing leaves the grotto with you. Death on the Isle comes first, as soon as you have the rod: the rooftops and Tourist Trap's lamps have already taken you past its 32 Agility, and its 7,500 Agility XP and 10,000 Thieving XP are worth taking as early as possible. Gate in 48 Fishing, 15 Agility and 15 Strength; 32 Agility, 34 Thieving and Children of th"},{"t":"Unlock barbarian fishing with Otto","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Barbarian fishing and Death on the Isle","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t117-h","x":"Walk from Port Khazard or Seers' Village to the Barbarian Outpost first and do the Barbarian Assault tutorial with Captain Cain: the minigame teleport only works once that tutorial is complete or you have chosen to skip it, and this chapter uses it twice (the barcrawl start and the walk to Rellekka). The teleport lands at the Barbarian Outpost and shares the 20-minute minigame cooldown. Then walk to Otto's Grotto, by the river above Baxtorian Falls. Talk to Otto Godblessed and ask about barbarian training, then choose fishing. In the dialogue, answer \"You think so?\" to begin the training, then ask \"What can I learn about the use of a fishing rod?\" for the fishing part. Barbarian fishing need"},{"t":"Complete Death on the Isle","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Barbarian fishing and Death on the Isle","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t118-h","x":"Death on the Isle needs 32 Agility and 34 Thieving, neither boostable, plus Children of the Sun. Use the Fishing Trawler minigame teleport to reach Port Khazard and charter a ship to Aldarin. Leave the barbarian rod in your inventory for the trip; it is one slot, and Otto's bed gives you another if you lose it. Talk to Patzi by the entrance to Villa Lucens to start Death on the Isle. The quest is a murder mystery: you get into the villa in a servant's uniform from the house just west of the Aldarin General Store (reached through its southern window), investigate the cellar, pickpocket the suspects for their notes, and search the backstage crate, costume rack and bookshelf before accusing the"},{"t":"Barbarian fish to about 53 Agility","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Barbarian fishing and Death on the Isle","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t119-h","x":"Walk from Port Khazard or Seers' Village back to Otto's spots and fish the leaping fish spots outside the grotto with your feathers as bait, wearing the angler's outfit for 2.5% more Fishing XP. Each catch gives Fishing XP plus a little Agility and Strength XP. From 48 Fishing you catch leaping trout; from 58 Fishing, 30 Agility and 30 Strength you catch leaping salmon; and from 70 Fishing, 45 Agility and 45 Strength leaping sturgeon, each worth more Agility than the last. Cut-eat every fish: use your knife on it to cut it open. Only some cuts give roe or caviar (the chance rises with your Cooking level), which you eat straight away for Cooking XP, and then sometimes fish offcuts. Each cut g"},{"t":"Back to Pollnivneach","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b25-h","x":"The section closes where your house now stands. Death on the Isle has left Thieving at about 55 after the first blackjacking session, so there is no second session here. This block just returns you to your house in Pollnivneach and explains where your rune pouch comes from, because Last Man Standing, where most players get one, isn't the best way for a UIM. Gate in Death on the Isle done. Carry in about 22/28. Exit you are home in Pollnivneach, about 67,000 gp. Carries forward the plan for the rune pouch (1.3)."},{"t":"Return to Pollnivneach","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.2: Some fishing and thieving › Back to Pollnivneach","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t121-h","x":"Break a house teleport tablet and walk out of your portal in Pollnivneach. Pollnivneach is a town, so the desert heat doesn't drain you inside it; put the slave robes back on only for the walks outside, and move the angler's outfit into your inventory. Wield the willow blackjack. 1.3 opens right here with a short blackjacking session that pays for the costume room and the planks, so the blackjack goes straight back to work. You are at 55 Thieving. From here, every level you train without the rogue outfit earns half the coins it could, and the outfit comes in 1.3 with your armour case. Drop the empty wine jugs. Done when you are home in Pollnivneach. Coins: about 67,000 gp · Slots: about 22/2"},{"t":"End of section 1.2","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s6-h","x":"You finish 1.2 in Pollnivneach with about 56 Fishing from Tempoross pushed into the 70s by barbarian fishing, about 53 Agility and about 30 marks of grace, 55 Thieving, 46 Fletching, about 67,000 gp and seventeen more quests done. Three deferred storages now hold your future loot: the Wintertodt Reward Cart, the Tempoross reward pool and Veos's lamps. 1.3 starts from this exact spot: a short blackjacking session pays for the house, and the Tempoross pool is collected straight after it, so nothing has to move before you begin. Skill Level Note Fishing about 72 Tempoross to 56, then barbarian fishing Agility about 53 Draynor, Al Kharid and Varrock rooftops, Tourist Trap lamps, Death on the Isl"},{"t":"1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s7-h","x":"This is the longest section of the chapter and the one where the account stops feeling like an early UIM. It builds four things the rest of the guide leans on, in this order: your first permanent storage (a costume room with an armour case, at 46 Construction), the rogue outfit, about 1.4 million gp of blackjacking money, and a rune pouch and Bones to Peaches from the Mage Training Arena. Around those it completes seventeen quests in regional sweeps, from The Dig Site to Bone Voyage, which opens Fossil Island. Each sweep finishes the quests it starts: a quest whose items would ride for weeks waits for 1.4 instead, so this section's inventory never relies on room it doesn't have. Nothing here"},{"t":"Funding the house","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b26-h","x":"You start 1.3 where 1.2 ended: in Pollnivneach, at 55 Thieving, with about 67,000 gp. The costume room (50,000 gp), the kitchen (5,000), about 680 sawmill oak planks (about 170,000) and two house moves in the next two blocks cost about 240,000 gp in total, so this short session pays for them. It is the only blackjacking you do without the rogue outfit, and it stops the moment the house is paid for. Gate in 55 Thieving for unbearded bandits. Carry in the 1.2 kit and wines: about 18/28 plus wines. Exit about 265,000 gp. Carries forward the coins for the costume room, kitchen, planks and two house moves. Your kit for the next three blocks is the 1.2 kit minus two items: drop the steel arrows (n"},{"t":"Blackjack to 265,000 gp","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Funding the house","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t125-h","x":"At 55 Thieving the bearded bandits are no longer the best target. Move to the unbearded Pollnivnian bandits in the north of the town, between the general store and the rug merchant; the cycle is the same as before (knock out, pickpocket twice, retry the knock-out at once if one fails). Buy wine from Faisal the Barman as you need it and drop each empty jug immediately. The unbearded bandits carry steel scimitars instead of blackjacks, and each successful pickpocket on a knocked-out one pays 50 coins and 84.3 Thieving XP. Lure one into an empty house where no other bandit can see it. Ali the Dyer's small house in the north of the town is the usual spot, and its ladder lets you reset a bandit t"},{"t":"Planks from the Tempoross pool","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b27-h","x":"Every permit you earned at Tempoross in 1.2 is still in the reward pool, and the pool rolls its loot at your Fishing level when you collect. At about 72 Fishing the fish band is salmon, tuna, lobster, bass and swordfish, and the non-fish table includes noted planks, noted oak planks and steel nails. About 200 permits give roughly 220 planks, 125 oak planks and 1,000 nails, about 14,000 Construction XP for the next block at no cost; the rolls are random, so buy sawmill planks for any shortfall. Gate in the Tempoross permits in the pool; about 72 Fishing. Carry in about 24/28 with the plank, nail, swordfish and seaweed stacks and the saw. Exit the pool collected; a saw; about 275,000 gp. Carri"},{"t":"Collect the reward pool","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Planks from the Tempoross pool","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t127-h","x":"The pool is not at Tempoross Cove itself: it sits on the Sea Spirit dock just west of the Ruins of Unkah, where you boarded the ship in 1.2, and no minigame teleport goes there. From Pollnivneach, take the magic carpet back to the Shantay Pass (200 gp until Rogue Trader is started later in this section, which halves the fare), walk north through Al Kharid to Ferryman Sathwood just south of the bank, and let him ferry you to the Ruins of Unkah, as you did in 1.2. Searching the pool needs a small or big fishing net in your inventory: take the free small net from the Spirit Angler and drop it after the last search: nothing else in this section fishes. Before you search, make sure you have at le"},{"t":"Pick up a saw on the way to Kourend","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Planks from the Tempoross pool","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t128-h","x":"You dropped your saw in 1.2. Break a Chronicle card to land at the Champions' Guild, walk north to the estate agent's house in north-east Varrock and take the saw that spawns inside. Cast Lumbridge Home Teleport and walk west through Draynor to Port Sarim, where Veos sails you to Port Piscarilius. While you're at the dock, claim your destroyed X Marks the Spot lamp from Veos and use it on Herblore. The Chronicle drops you just outside the guild, and the spawn is free, which is why the guide fetches the saw here instead of paying for one: the sawmill operator in the Woodcutting Guild sells saws for 13 gp, so if someone has taken the Varrock spawn, buy one there instead of waiting. You took th"},{"t":"Construction to 46 in Hosidius","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b28-h","x":"This block takes Construction from about 30 to 46 and builds a costume room with an oak armour case. It is the most important UIM investment in Chapter 1. The armour case holds full sets of skilling and minigame outfits; for a UIM it accepts pieces one at a time and only gives them back once the set is complete, which is exactly how the Rogues' Den hands them out. The wiki's own advice for UIMs doing the Rogues' Den is a Taverley house with an armour case, and that is the plan. Gate in 33 Construction for oak larders, 42 for the costume room, 46 for the oak armour case; the pool planks. Carry in the plank stacks and food: about 24/28. Exit 46 Construction; 52 Cooking from the mess hall; the "},{"t":"Move the house and claim the Kourend lamps","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Construction to 46 in Hosidius","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t130-h","x":"On the Port Piscarilius dock, claim the two Client of Kourend lamps from Veos and use them on Herblore too. Walk south to Hosidius and pay the estate agent 8,750 gp to move your house to Hosidius. The two lamps are worth 500 XP each. The Hosidius move needs 25 Construction and can't be boosted; you passed 30 in 1.1, so it is open to you, and you have already visited Kourend, which the agent also checks. Done when the house is in Hosidius and the lamps are used."},{"t":"Cooking to 52 at the Hosidius mess hall","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Construction to 46 in Hosidius","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t131-h","x":"You are in Hosidius with about 43 Cooking, and two later steps need more: the raw swordfish from the Tempoross pool, your food for the rest of the section, need 45 to cook, and the botanical pie for Eadgar's Ruse in 1.4 needs 52. The mess hall just south of Kingstown is the UIM way to close that gap, because the wiki says it needs no gathered materials: the flour, potatoes, meat and the dishes and bowls all come from its cupboards and tables, and it no longer needs Kourend favour. Make servery stews (25 Cooking, about 168 XP each, about 60,000 to 69,000 XP an hour at lower levels by the wiki's estimate) with your free slots, serve them, and repeat until 52, about 73,000 XP or a little over a"},{"t":"Spend the pool planks first","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Construction to 46 in Hosidius","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t132-h","x":"Unnote 24 oak planks at a bank booth. Marlo's five house tablets are used up by now, so walk into the Hosidius house portal instead (it is a short walk), build a kitchen (5,000 gp, level 5) next to the parlour, and build an oak larder in it (level 33, 8 oak planks, 480 XP). Remove it and build it again until the planks run out, then fetch the next 24. When the oak planks are gone, build wooden bookcases in the parlour from the regular planks and steel nails (4 planks and 4 nails each, 115 XP) the same way. Keep the noted stacks noted between trips and unnote only what fits in your free slots. Done when the pool planks are used."},{"t":"Oak larders from the Woodcutting Guild","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Construction to 46 in Hosidius","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t133-h","x":"When the pool's planks are used up, the rest comes from oak logs. Wield the steel axe in place of the blackjack and fill every free slot with oak logs: about nine at first, because the noted stacks, saw, hammer and coins stay with you, and about fourteen once the angler's outfit is in the armour case. Give the logs to the sawmill operator in the Woodcutting Guild for oak planks (250 gp each), run to the house portal, go in and build larders with every set of eight planks. Run back from the portal and repeat. This is the slowest stretch of the chapter, roughly 70 trips and two to three hours of play; nothing here is dangerous, so put a podcast on. The guild needs 60 Woodcutting to enter, whic"},{"t":"Move the house to Taverley","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Construction to 46 in Hosidius","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t134-h","x":"Before you spend the pool planks, set aside four planks and eighteen oak planks and keep them noted: the planks wait for the Observatory and Mountain Daughter in 1.4, and the oak planks go into your magic wardrobe later in this section (four), and the workshop's crafting table (four) and the Museum Camp on Fossil Island (ten) at the start of 1.4. Noted, they are two slots; unnote them at a bank booth right before each build. When the larders are done, drop the steel nails and the saw: the saw that spawns in the Varrock estate agent's house is free when the wardrobe needs one. At Vannah's farm shop in Hosidius, buy a compost pack (2,000 gp), a rake and a seed dibber, open the pack, and leave "},{"t":"The rogue outfit","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b29-h","x":"The Rogues' Den maze needs an empty inventory and nothing worn, and each successful run ends at a wall safe that gives a Rogue's equipment crate, from which you choose any one piece of the set (or a rogue kit). Because you choose, there are no duplicates, but a failed lockpick at the safe gives nothing, so the set takes at least five successful runs. This block uses the section's first planned death to empty your inventory for about an hour, stores each piece in the Taverley armour case as it arrives, and collects everything at the end. Gate in 50 Agility and 50 Thieving; an empty inventory and nothing worn (a Falador Castle deathpile). Carry in nothing for the maze; then about 24/28. Exit t"},{"t":"Planned death: Falador Castle","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The rogue outfit","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t136-h","x":"Sail back to Port Sarim with Veos and walk north to Falador. Don't use a minigame teleport on the way: you need one the moment you respawn, and they share a 20-minute cooldown. In the courtyard of Falador Castle, take off your staff, turn auto-retaliate off and attack a White Knight. Let it kill you. Keep any fish you carry noted: the wiki says unnoted food disappears from a deathpile and doesn't say whether raw fish count, so the guide never risks it. Note the time. The wiki lists Falador Castle as a deathpile spot: the White Knights don't wander, nothing else there is aggressive, and the castle is a two-minute walk from Taverley. Your whole inventory drops where you die, hidden from everyo"},{"t":"Five or more maze runs","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The rogue outfit","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t137-h","x":"You respawn in Lumbridge with nothing. Use the Burthorpe Games Room minigame teleport, which needs no items, and walk to the Toad and Chicken pub. The trapdoor behind the bar leads to the Rogues' Den; you meet its 50 Agility and 50 Thieving requirement. Talk to Brian O'Richard at the entrance first: he has to introduce the maze before your first run. Run the maze. It is a fixed obstacle course of traps, ledges, pressure plates and doors to pick. At the end, crack one of the wall safes; which safe you pick makes no difference. Open the Rogue's equipment crate it gives and choose a piece you don't have yet. Each run also gives 12 Agility and Thieving XP per level drained. Walk out of the den a"},{"t":"Collect the deathpile","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The rogue outfit","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t138-h","x":"Walk from Taverley to Falador Castle and pick everything up except the spade and the clue hunter gloves: nothing in this section digs, and the rogue gloves, and later the graceful gloves, take your hands slot. Check the clock as you go: from your death to here should take about 40 minutes. If you are running late, skip the safe and go straight to the pile. While you're in Falador in the rogue outfit, pickpocket a Falador guard once for the diary, and do one lap of the Falador rooftop course for the diary as well. The guard is a medium Falador task and needs 40 Thieving; the rooftop lap is a hard task and needs 50 Agility. You meet both with room to spare, and the rogue outfit doubles whateve"},{"t":"A pickaxe and soft clay","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The rogue outfit","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t139-h","x":"The next part of the section needs a pickaxe. Walk to the Dwarven Mine and buy an adamant pickaxe from Nurmof (it needs 31 Mining to use, which The Dig Site gives you later) and a bronze pickaxe for 1 gp to mine the clay with now; a rune pickaxe costs ten times as much and mines nothing here faster that matters for a UIM. Walk south to Rimmington, mine four clay, buy a bucket at the general store and make four soft clay at the well, then drop the bronze pickaxe and the bucket. The Golem needs the clay. Nurmof's shop is in the north-west corner of the Dwarven Mine, down the alley with the anvil south-west of the north entrance. The adamant pickaxe costs 3,200 gp, and he keeps only two in stoc"},{"t":"Rune Mysteries and the road to Pollnivneach","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b30-h","x":"Rogue Trader, the miniquest that opens Ali Morrisane's rune shop, needs Rune Mysteries finished, and Ali has to send you to Aubury himself. This block finishes Rune Mysteries on the way south, gets Ali's first dialogue, starts The Golem at Uzer with the soft clay you just made, and runs the main blackjacking session in the rogue outfit. Gate in The Feud, Rune Mysteries and Gertrude's Cat for Rogue Trader; 20 Crafting and 25 Thieving for The Golem; 65 Thieving for Menaphite thugs. Carry in about 23/28. Exit Rune Mysteries done; Rogue Trader and The Golem started; about 910,000 gp after blackjacking. Carries forward the coins for Ali's runes."},{"t":"Rune Mysteries","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Rune Mysteries and the road to Pollnivneach","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t141-h","x":"Walk from Rimmington to Port Sarim and on to Draynor, buy the Chronicle back from Diango in the market for 300 gp (its teleport charges come back with it) and twelve teleport cards (1,800 gp), one for each Chronicle teleport from here to the end of the chapter, and continue to the Wizards' Tower, and give the research notes to Sedridor in the basement to complete Rune Mysteries (since November 2026 it also pays 500 Runecraft XP). That frees the slot the notes have held since 1.1. The tower is south of Draynor; climb down the ladder to find Sedridor. Completing the quest also lets Aubury teleport you to the rune essence mine, which is how you collect Drezel's 50 essence for Priest in Peril in"},{"t":"Start Rogue Trader","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Rune Mysteries and the road to Pollnivneach","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t142-h","x":"Pay the 10 gp toll at the Al Kharid gate and talk to Ali Morrisane, east of the gem trader, to start Rogue Trader. He sends you to Aubury in Varrock; you go there in the block after next, when you have the money to buy what Ali sells. When he asks, choose the option asking what's in it for you: starting Rogue Trader halves the magic carpet fare from 200 to 100 gp, which matters with the carpet rides between the Shantay Pass, Uzer and Pollnivneach over the next few blocks. Done when Rogue Trader is started."},{"t":"The Golem","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Rune Mysteries and the road to Pollnivneach","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t143-h","x":"Buy a Shantay pass at the Shantay Pass, along with the three desert clothes and a few waterskins if you dropped them, go through the gate and walk east across the desert to the Ruins of Uzer. The carpet to Uzer only opens once The Golem is complete, and there is no carpet from Pollnivneach. Talk to the clay golem to start The Golem and use your four soft clay on it to repair it. Ask how to open the portal, read the letter outside the temple, then go down the stairs behind the golem, and take the strange implement from the north-western room; the black mushroom by the stairs waits until you finish the quest here, since the wiki's quick guide grinds it only at the end. The quest then sends you"},{"t":"Blackjack to 910,000 gp","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Rune Mysteries and the road to Pollnivneach","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t144-h","x":"Walk back to the Shantay Pass and take the carpet to Pollnivneach. Drop the desert clothes and waterskins there (the Shantay Pass sells fresh ones next time), wear the full rogue outfit and blackjack the Menaphite thugs at the southern end of town; you already have the 65 Thieving they need. With the full set, every successful pickpocket pays double. Each successful pickpocket on a thug pays 60 coins and 137.5 Thieving XP, so with the full set you collect 120 coins a time. The thugs are level 55 and not aggressive until you fail a knock-out. If one does turn on you, knock it out again straight away, which resets its aggression; if that fails, get it stuck on an object in the room and knock i"},{"t":"Ali Morrisane's runes","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b31-h","x":"The Mage Training Arena burns a lot of runes, and Ali Morrisane in Al Kharid sells nature, law, cosmic and chaos runes one step from the arena. Buying them in the Mage Arena bank in level 54 Wilderness would mean carrying 800,000 gp through the worst place in the game for a UIM, because a Wilderness death converts what you carry for the killer. Ali's stock per world is small, so this block is a long hop, but nothing in it can kill you. Gate in Rogue Trader's rune section. Carry in about 20/28 with the three new rune stacks and two spare staves. Exit the runes for the Mage Training Arena bought; a few hundred gp left. Carries forward the rune stacks (the arena)."},{"t":"Aubury, Zaff and the way back","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Ali Morrisane's runes","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t146-h","x":"From Pollnivneach, take the carpet to the Shantay Pass and walk north to Al Kharid. Break a Chronicle card and walk into Varrock. Talk to Aubury in his rune shop about Ali's business proposal. While you're there, buy about 1,000 water runes from his stock. Walk to Zaff's staff shop and buy a staff of earth and a staff of fire; with the staff of air you already wear, they cover every elemental rune the arena needs. Aubury's shop is in south-east Varrock, where you first took him the research package in 1.1. The water runes do more than the arena: they are the Water Bolt runes for Sir Mordred and the outlaws later in the section, which is why they go in the rune pouch when you get it. Walk out"},{"t":"Open the casket and buy","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Ali Morrisane's runes","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t147-h","x":"Talk to Ali again and ask to see his runes. Choose to examine the lock on the large casket and solve the runedoku; solving it once unlocks Ali's standard stock of non-elemental runes for good. Buy every nature, law and cosmic rune he has, hop worlds, and repeat. The chaos runes wait until after the arena, when you have the money for them. Only the examine option works on the large casket: forcing it or picking the lock always fails, and each failure drains a few levels of Strength and Agility or Thieving. The runedoku is a grid of runes in which no rune may repeat in any row, column or 3x3 block. Ali's prices never rise as his stock falls, so clearing all 100 of a rune costs the same per run"},{"t":"Spend down before the arena","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Ali Morrisane's runes","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t148-h","x":"The Alchemist's Playground doesn't let you bring coins in, and the only coin store a UIM can use this early is the Last Man Standing coffer in the Ferox Enclave (see the storage glossary), a detour that isn't worth it for the few coins you would keep here; Nightmare Zone's coffer needs five of its quests. Plan the last purchases so you walk into the arena with only a few hundred gp; anything left over you spend on extra nature runes or drop at the door. The ban covers coin pouches too, so make sure none are left over from blackjacking. Done when a few hundred gp remain. Coins: a few hundred gp · Slots: about 20/28 with the new rune stacks and two spare staves · Requirements: Rogue Trader (ru"},{"t":"The Mage Training Arena","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b32-h","x":"This block earns Bones to Peaches and a rune pouch from the Rewards Guardian. Since August 2025 the rune pouch is sold there for 150 Telekinetic, 150 Graveyard, 1,500 Enchantment and 200 Alchemist pizazz points, so a UIM no longer needs a Last Man Standing win for it. Together with Bones to Peaches (200, 200, 2,000 and 300) and one mud rune (1, 1, 15 and 1 points; a 1.4 quest uses it), your targets are: Gate in 21 Magic for Low Alchemy, 33 for Telekinetic Grab, 15 for Bones to Bananas, 60 to cast Bones to Peaches. Carry in the arena runes and staves: about 22/28 with a few hundred coins. Exit the rune pouch and Bones to Peaches; about 5,000 gp. Carries forward the rune pouch (core kit). Room"},{"t":"Inventory for the arena","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The Mage Training Arena","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t150-h","x":"Before you go in, drop the steel axe (Bob in Lumbridge sells another for 200 gp when you next need one) and the mind runes. What stays is: hammer, knife, adamant pickaxe, costume needle, the noted steel bars, the willow blackjack, the swordfish and seaweed stacks, the plank and oak plank stacks, the marks of grace, the Golem's strange implement, your rune stacks (nature, law, cosmic, chaos and water) and the two spare staves, with the staff of air and the Chronicle worn. With the few hundred coins that is 20 slots, which leaves eight free for the first three rooms. Keep the staff of fire until the Enchanting Chamber is done if you are below 57 Magic there (Lvl-3 Enchant takes fire runes); at"},{"t":"Alchemist's Playground","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The Mage Training Arena","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t151-h","x":"Wield the staff of fire. Low Alchemy needs 21 Magic and High Alchemy 55; switch as soon as you can for the extra Magic XP: the coins, and so the points, are the same either way. Alchemise only the item the board marks as free or worth 30 coins, deposit the coins in the chute whenever you hold a few hundred, and stop at 501 points. The board's values and the item positions change once a minute, so search the cupboards for the marked item and alchemise as many as you can before the change. Every 100 coins you deposit is one point and pays 10 coins back to you, which is where the 5,000 gp in this block's coin line comes from. Done when your Alchemist points are earned."},{"t":"Enchanting Chamber","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The Mage Training Arena","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t152-h","x":"Wield the staff of earth for Lvl-4 Enchant (57 Magic, the target), or the staff of fire for Lvl-3 if you are below 57. Cast the highest Enchant spell your Magic allows (a Wizard's mind bomb boosts you early, but nothing near the arena sells one, so buy it at the Rising Sun in Falador or another Asgarnian pub before you come) on the shapes the room shows as bonus, and drop the shapes you don't enchant. Dragonstones that spawn are worth double. Deposit the orbs in the hole in the middle for the extra runes, and stop at 3,515 points. Each enchant is worth as many points as the spell's level, and every tenth shape counts double, so Enchant Level 4 earns twice what Enchant Level 2 does for the sa"},{"t":"Telekinetic Theatre","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The Mage Training Arena","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t153-h","x":"Wield the staff of air. Each maze is a statue you move with Telekinetic Grab (33 Magic, one law rune per cast) until it rests on the target square; every fifth maze in a row pays 10 law runes and 1,000 Magic XP back. Stop at 351 points. Each solved maze is worth 2 points and 250 Magic XP, and the fifth in a row adds a bonus of 8 points and refills your run energy. Done when your Telekinetic points are earned."},{"t":"Creature Graveyard, the rune pouch and Bones to Peaches","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The Mage Training Arena","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t154-h","x":"Wield the staff of earth again. Grab bones from the piles, cast Bones to Bananas, and deposit the fruit in the chutes; every 16 fruit is a point, and the bones that fall from the ceiling hurt, so eat a banana when you need to. The falling bones hit for 2 and can be dodged by stepping off the tile they land on. You can't bring bananas or peaches into the room, so the bananas you eat are ones you have just made, at 2 Hitpoints each. Each point also earns one bonus rune (water, earth, nature, death or blood), paid when you leave the room. This is the only room where you can take damage, so keep an eye on your Hitpoints between casts. At 150 Graveyard points, go upstairs and buy the rune pouch f"},{"t":"The second blackjacking session","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b33-h","x":"You leave the arena with about 5,000 gp from the Alchemist's Playground and the rest of the section still to buy: Excalibur's replacement fee, a rune sword, quest items, sawmill planks, shop food, the Hosidius move back to Kourend and the Rellekka move. This session funds all of it plus a buffer for 1.4. Gate in 65 Thieving; the rogue outfit. Carry in the core kit: about 18/28. Exit about 600,000 gp after the chaos runes. Carries forward the coins for the rest of 1.3. Take the carpet from the Shantay Pass to Pollnivneach, wear the rogue outfit and blackjack the Menaphite thugs at the southern end of town to 630,000 gp. You reach it at about 80 Thieving, and blackjacking pauses there until th"},{"t":"The Barbarian Outpost, the Gnome Stronghold and Merlin's Crystal","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b34-h","x":"This block starts four things in Kandarin that cost nothing to carry: Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl, Dwarf Cannon, The Grand Tree and Merlin's Crystal. Merlin's Crystal starts here because its next steps, the Lady of the Lake in Taverley and the beggar in Port Sarim, sit on later routes; its ritual and Excalibur come back to Camelot near the end of the section. The only new carries are the barcrawl card, which is stamped bar by bar through Chapter 2, and the greenman's ale for the Lumbridge cook. Gate in 45 Magic for Camelot Teleport. Carry in about 23/28 with the barcrawl card and the ale. Exit Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl, Dwarf Cannon, The Grand Tree and Merlin's Crystal started; the greenman'"},{"t":"The barcrawl and Rasolo","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The Barbarian Outpost, the Gnome Stronghold and Merlin's Crystal","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t157-h","x":"Use the Barbarian Assault minigame teleport and talk to the barbarian guard by the agility course entrance to start Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl. The barcrawl card is one slot until the last stamp in Chapter 2. Each bar charges a few coins for its drink, and some drinks drain stats for a short while. Never drop the card: if you lose it, the barcrawl starts again from the first bar. A few drinks also take Hitpoints rather than stats, the worst being the Heart Stopper in Ardougne's Flying Horse Inn, which can take 20 to 30 percent of your health, so drink those with your Hitpoints high. The finished barcrawl opens the Barbarian Outpost agility course, which a Kandarin medium diary task and later"},{"t":"Dwarf Cannon and The Grand Tree","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The Barbarian Outpost, the Gnome Stronghold and Merlin's Crystal","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t158-h","x":"Talk to Captain Lawgof at the dwarven camp to start Dwarf Cannon, and follow it, repairing the railings with your hammer and the railings he gives you, until he asks you to find Lollk. That part of the quest waits for Chapter 1.4, when it comes back on the Ardougne route. The camp is between the coal trucks and the Fishing Guild. There are six bent railings; with your hammer and his railings in your inventory, use Inspect on each one to fix it (using the hammer on the railing does nothing). A failed attempt costs a point or two of Hitpoints or briefly lowers your Strength or Crafting, so keep trying. Then check the watchtower to the south for Gilob, bring his remains back to Lawgof, and he s"},{"t":"Merlin's Crystal to Morgan Le Faye","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The Barbarian Outpost, the Gnome Stronghold and Merlin's Crystal","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t159-h","x":"Teleport to Camelot and talk to King Arthur to start Merlin's Crystal. Talk to Sir Gawain and Sir Lancelot, then walk to Catherby and hide in Arhein's crate to reach Keep Le Faye. Inside, climb to Sir Mordred (level 39). Fight him with Water Bolt (water runes from the pouch, air from your staff, and chaos runes); a melee player can flinch him, but magic can't flinch. When he is nearly dead, Morgan Le Faye stops the fight and tells you how to free Merlin. The next step is Excalibur, from the Lady of the Lake in Taverley, and it waits until you pass Port Sarim with a loaf of bread for the beggar. Don't kill a giant bat here: the bat bones are for the black candle ritual at the end of the secti"},{"t":"Varrock: A Ruff Situation, The Dig Site and Priest in Peril","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b35-h","x":"This block completes A Ruff Situation and The Dig Site, takes Priest in Peril to its essence step, collects The Golem's statuette and fills your kudos. The Dig Site's reward is the turning point for Mining, 15,300 XP, which is what lets you mine coal and essence later in the section. Nothing you pick up here outlives the next block except two gold bars and one charcoal. Gate in 10 Agility, 10 Herblore and 25 Thieving for The Dig Site; 15 Crafting for A Ruff Situation. Carry in the core kit, the Jatix items, the barcrawl card and the ale: about 23/28. Exit A Ruff Situation and The Dig Site done; Priest in Peril at its essence step; Demon Slayer and Dragon Slayer I started; about 95 kudos; the"},{"t":"Varrock","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Varrock: A Ruff Situation, The Dig Site and Priest in Peril","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t161-h","x":"The Chronicle lands you at the Champions' Guild. Talk to the Guildmaster to start Dragon Slayer I; the map pieces and Crandor are Chapter 2. Don't buy the rune sword yet: the Temple Guardian below is flinched with your adamant pickaxe, which you can wield at 30 Attack (31 Mining to mine with it), and the sword is bought when the Black Knight Titan needs it. In Varrock, buy the barcrawl drink in the Blue Moon Inn, do one lap of the Varrock rooftop course for the diary, and buy a tinderbox and a bucket at the general store (The Dig Site needs the tinderbox, Priest in Peril the bucket). Steal a cup of tea from the tea stall in east Varrock; the Digsite's panning guide wants it. The Blue Moon's "},{"t":"A Ruff Situation","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Varrock: A Ruff Situation, The Dig Site and Priest in Peril","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t162-h","x":"Buy a fur from Baraek and pick a grain from any wheat field. Walk out to the Dog Shelter south-west of Edgeville Monastery and talk to Talia (twice) to start A Ruff Situation, then follow it back to Gertrude in west Varrock. When the quest asks for a stuffed dog, use the grain on the fur with your costume needle in your inventory. The last step is a fight with two outlaws (levels 22 and 23); Water Bolt handles both. The quest needs 15 Crafting. The costume needle stands in for a needle and thread, which is one more reason it stays in the core kit. The stray dog leads you from Gertrude's to a house west of the clothes shop, then through the bank to the field north of the Cooks' Guild, where P"},{"t":"The Dig Site and Priest in Peril","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Varrock: A Ruff Situation, The Dig Site and Priest in Peril","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t163-h","x":"Walk east to the Digsite and start The Dig Site by talking to the examiner, who sends you back to the curator for a letter of recommendation. Find Elissa in the north-eastern corner of the site for The Golem and read Varmen's notes on the south-eastern bookshelf in the Exam Centre; she sends you to the museum. The examiner is in the Exam Centre at the south of the site. Fail the first exam on purpose: the students around the site give you the answers in return for small favours (a teddy from a bush north of the centre, a special cup from panning, and an animal skull from pickpocketing the workmen), and you have to talk to each student twice. Walk to the Paterdomus temple north-east of the Di"},{"t":"Kudos","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Varrock: A Ruff Situation, The Dig Site and Priest in Peril","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t164-h","x":"Keep the Level 3 certificate from The Dig Site and don't hand it to the curator yet: he takes it in exchange for a free drink, the fruit blast for the Lumbridge cook, and the wiki says the certificate is used up then and can't be got back, so you give it to him on the way to the cook, after the desert. Go down to the basement and take the natural history quiz with Orlando Smith: 2 kudos per display, 28 in all, plus 1,000 Slayer and 1,000 Hunter XP. Upstairs, tell Historian Minas about your completed quests for their kudos. Leave Shield of Arrav for later: its antique lamp from Minas (1,000 XP) needs 20 in the chosen skill, and your Herblore is about 18 here. Tell Minas about it on the Demon "},{"t":"The desert: The Golem, your ring of dueling and 43 Mining","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b36-h","x":"This block completes The Golem, makes your ring of dueling, and trains Mining from about 35 to 43 on sandstone. It also makes the molten glass the workshop's crafting table needs and the silver sickle for Nature Spirit, so that nothing for them has to be bought later where it isn't sold. Gate in 20 Crafting and 25 Thieving for The Golem; 27 Crafting and 27 Magic for the ring of dueling; 35 Mining for sandstone (iron ore first). Carry in 28/28 with the Level 3 certificate; 24/28 after the Al Kharid stop. Exit The Golem done; a ring of dueling worn; 43 Mining; a molten glass and a silver sickle; about 570,000 gp. Carries forward the molten glass (the workshop's crafting table), the silver sick"},{"t":"The Golem","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The desert: The Golem, your ring of dueling and 43 Mining","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t166-h","x":"Walk to Al Kharid and make room before you buy anything. Sell the spare gold bar at the general store and drop the tinderbox (the Lumbridge general store sells another for 1 gp when the next block needs one). Then make the ring of dueling now rather than after the quest: buy one cut emerald from the gem trader and a ring mould from Dommik's crafting shop, make an emerald ring at the furnace from the other gold bar and the emerald (27 Crafting), cast Enchant Level 2 on it for a ring of dueling and wear it. Drop the ring mould and the cosmic runes: nothing else in this section enchants. Buy a papyrus from Ali Morrisane (10 gp). At the Shantay Pass, buy a Shantay pass, a desert shirt, robe and "},{"t":"Al Kharid: the ring of dueling and the silver sickle","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The desert: The Golem, your ring of dueling and 43 Mining","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t167-h","x":"Ride the Uzer carpet to the Shantay Pass and walk to Al Kharid. Your ring of dueling is already on your finger from the start of this block. At Dommik's crafting shop buy a sickle mould. Mine one silver ore in the Al Kharid mine. At the Al Kharid furnace, smelt the silver ore and cast it into a silver sickle with the sickle mould (18 Crafting); Nature Spirit blesses it in the next-but-one block. Drop the mould. The blessing happens in the pool in the nature spirit's grotto once Nature Spirit is done. From here on you wear the ring of dueling. Its Castle Wars teleport is next to the Observatory, and its Ferox Enclave teleport is a UIM's best friend: the enclave's pool restores run energy and "},{"t":"Sandstone to 43 Mining","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › The desert: The Golem, your ring of dueling and 43 Mining","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t168-h","x":"Mine an iron ore in the Al Kharid mine for the diary and drop it, then keep mining iron until you reach 35 Mining (about 140 ores, dropped as you go: The Dig Site and the information clerk leave you at about 31): the sandstone needs it. Do one lap of the Al Kharid rooftop course for the diary. Take the carpet from the Shantay Pass to Pollnivneach and walk to the quarry; bring your adamant pickaxe and four or five waterskins, since the quarry is in the desert heat (the Shantay guards at the Ruins of Unkah, just south of the quarry, sell full waterskins if you run short). Mine sandstone and grind it in Drew's grinder as you go, rather than dropping it; the grinder keeps the sand for you. Stop "},{"t":"Lumbridge and Draynor: Recipe for Disaster, Lost City and Vampyre Slayer","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b37-h","x":"This block starts Recipe for Disaster with all four of the cook's ingredients in one hand-in, completes Cook's Assistant, The Ides of Milk and Vampyre Slayer, starts Lost City, and picks up the ghostspeak amulet Nature Spirit needs next. The three Varrock items it uses are collected at the start of the block, not carried from the Digsite. Gate in 10 Cooking for Recipe for Disaster. Carry in about 21/28, then the stake, the rotten tomato and the fruit blast: about 24/28. Exit Cook's Assistant, The Ides of Milk and Vampyre Slayer done; Recipe for Disaster and its first three subquests started; Lost City started; the ghostspeak amulet; about 560,000 gp. Carries forward the ghostspeak amulet (Na"},{"t":"Varrock errands","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Lumbridge and Draynor: Recipe for Disaster, Lost City and Vampyre Slayer","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t170-h","x":"Break a Chronicle card. In Varrock, buy a beer in the Blue Moon Inn and give it to Dr Harlow for the stake Vampyre Slayer needs, buy a rotten tomato (1 gp) at the Pelters' Veg Stall by the pillory cages for the Lumbridge cook, and claim the free drink from the Varrock Museum curator with your Level 3 certificate: it is a fruit blast, and a fruit blast with ashes added is the dirty blast the cook asks for. The beer costs 2 gp. Dr Harlow sits in the Blue Moon Inn, so you can buy and hand it over without moving. The wiki warns that a premade fruit blast won't work for the cook; the curator's fruit blast is one of the sources it lists. UIM risk When the curator takes your certificate, pick the f"},{"t":"Recipe for Disaster begins","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Lumbridge and Draynor: Recipe for Disaster, Lost City and Vampyre Slayer","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t171-h","x":"Cast Lumbridge Home Teleport. Buy a steel axe from Bob and a tinderbox from the general store (1 gp), chop a log, and burn it with the tinderbox for ashes; add the ashes to the fruit blast for the dirty blast. Complete Cook's Assistant (an egg from the chicken farm, a bucket of milk from the dairy cow and a pot of flour from the windmill); hand each ingredient to the cook as you get it, so they never take three slots at once. Talk to the cook again to start Recipe for Disaster: he wants an eye of newt, a greenman's ale, a rotten tomato and a dirty blast, and you give him all four now. The Culinaromancer's Chest in the cellar is now open to you; buy one spice from it for the goblin generals' "},{"t":"The Ides of Milk, Lost City and the ghostspeak amulet","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Lumbridge and Draynor: Recipe for Disaster, Lost City and Vampyre Slayer","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t172-h","x":"Cassius, by the pond south of the windmill, starts The Ides of Milk. Gillie then gives a cowbell amulet and a 1,000 XP lamp for any combat skill: use the lamp on Prayer and drop the amulet. UIM risk Its bull, Brutus, is fought in an instance: his melee can't kill you during the quest, but his specials can and ignore protection prayers, so step two tiles sideways (or one back) when he snorts and two tiles sideways when he growls and charges, and leave by the south-west gate if it goes badly. Before the fight, the quest walks you between Gillie Groats in the cow field, her father Seth by the chicken coop (search the shelves on his house's southern wall for The Groats Principles) and Duke Horac"},{"t":"Vampyre Slayer","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Lumbridge and Draynor: Recipe for Disaster, Lost City and Vampyre Slayer","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t173-h","x":"Walk west to Draynor. Talk to Morgan in his house to start Vampyre Slayer and take the garlic from the cupboard upstairs. Walk north to Draynor Manor and kill Count Draynor in the basement with the stake and your hammer in your inventory and the garlic on you; the quest gives 3 quest points and 4,825 Attack XP. Pickpocket Martin the Master Gardener in the market for the Lumbridge & Draynor diary. Morgan's house is just north of Ned's. In the manor, take the large staircase on the east side down and open the coffin in the middle of the room to wake the Count. The garlic weakens him only when melee combat starts, and he regenerates far faster than most monsters; if the fight drags on he return"},{"t":"Priest in Peril, Morytania and the graceful outfit","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b38-h","x":"This block finishes Priest in Peril, opens Morytania, completes Nature Spirit, turns your marks of grace into the full graceful outfit on the Canifis Rooftop Course, and finishes with Shades of Mort'ton, once the marks and the saw no longer take slots. Priest in Peril has to come first, because Nature Spirit, Shades of Mort'ton and the Canifis course all require it. It has the section's only unplanned danger: Mort Myre and Mort'ton can kill you, and for a UIM that means a deathpile in a swamp. Take your best food, keep your Hitpoints high, and leave if a fight turns. Gate in 15 Herblore, 20 Crafting and 5 Firemaking for Shades of Mort'ton; 18 Crafting for Nature Spirit's sickle; 40 Agility f"},{"t":"Fifty essence, a few at a time","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Priest in Peril, Morytania and the graceful outfit","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t175-h","x":"Break a Chronicle card and walk north to the Varrock estate agent's house in north-east Varrock: take the saw that spawns inside, for the magic wardrobe at the end of this block. Priest in Peril's Drezel wants 50 essence, and he accepts them in batches, so you never need 50 free slots. He takes rune and pure essence alike, as long as it is unnoted. Have Aubury teleport you to the rune essence mine; at 43 Mining you get pure essence. Fill your free slots (about six), leave through the portal, walk east to the Paterdomus temple and hand them over, and repeat until Drezel has all 50, which completes Priest in Peril. It takes about eight short trips. The reward includes a wolfbane dagger. Drop i"},{"t":"Nature Spirit","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Priest in Peril, Morytania and the graceful outfit","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t176-h","x":"Talk to Drezel to start Nature Spirit, and walk through the temple's back door into Morytania. He hands you three meat pies and three apple pies meant for Filliman; you never actually give them to him, so eat them whenever you need to. Enter the swamp through its gate: the wiki notes that Filliman doesn't appear if you come in another way. Head south along the western river to the Grotto Tree, on an island reached by jumping a broken bridge. The jump can fail for 1 to 7 damage, so never take it on low Hitpoints. In Mort Myre, do the quest with the ghostspeak amulet, the silver sickle you cast in Al Kharid and the druid pouch it gives you. The swamp itself takes 3 Hitpoints from you every two"},{"t":"Canifis rooftops and the graceful outfit","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Priest in Peril, Morytania and the graceful outfit","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t177-h","x":"The Canifis Rooftop Course starts in Canifis and needs 40 Agility and Priest in Peril. You climb the tall tree just north of the Canifis bank and finish by jumping down off the north side of the bank, so each lap ends a few steps from the next one's start. A lap is 240 XP and takes about 44 seconds, roughly 19,700 XP an hour at best, and gives about 16 to 18 marks an hour: Canifis spawns a mark twice as often as most courses, and unlike the others its rate doesn't drop once you are 20 levels above it. You need 260 marks for the whole set and bring about 30, so this is about 230 more: roughly 13 to 14 hours of laps, which take you from about 53 to about 62 Agility. Your first lap also complet"},{"t":"Shades of Mort'ton","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Priest in Peril, Morytania and the graceful outfit","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t178-h","x":"Break a Chronicle card and walk east through the Paterdomus temple and south to Mort'ton. Do Shades of Mort'ton there. The town has about 25 aggressive loar shades wandering its streets, so arrive with full Hitpoints. Do the whole quest on the world you are on. The wiki mentions world 377, the official Shades world, only as optional help for the temple repair, where other players speed it up; you don't need it, and it also warns that building materials can cost much more there because players buy them up. You have no herbs at this point (the Reward Cart's herbs come in 1.4), and you don't need to leave Morytania for them: search the smashed table in the south-westernmost house in Mort'ton fo"},{"t":"Taverley, Port Sarim and the Goblin Village: Excalibur and the slop","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b39-h","x":"This block gets Excalibur back for Merlin's Crystal, makes the goblin generals' slop and hands it in, and bakes Rohak's dwarven rock cake. Every ingredient is bought or caught on the loop it is used on, so the peak is the rock cake's eight items just before Rohak. Gate in Merlin's Crystal at its Excalibur step; the charcoal and spice; 33 Magic for Telekinetic Grab. Carry in about 19/28, 20 with the vial. Exit Excalibur; Freeing the Goblin generals done; the rock cake (handed in on the Lumbridge stop of the next block); the wine of Zamorak diary task; about 545,000 gp. Carries forward Excalibur (Merlin's Crystal, then the Black Knight Titan), the rock cake (the Mountain Dwarf), the vial (Bone"},{"t":"The Lady of the Lake and the willows","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Taverley, Port Sarim and the Goblin Village: Excalibur and the slop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t180-h","x":"Cast Teleport to House to Taverley. At Jatix's Herblore Shop, buy one vial for Bone Voyage's Potion of Sealegs at the end of the section (nothing nearer the barge sells one). Talk to the Lady of the Lake, on the lake peninsula south of the Taverley balloon, for Merlin's Crystal. She wants you to help a beggar before she returns Excalibur; that happens in Port Sarim. The Falador diary's willow task (chop and burn a willow log) waits for a visit when you carry an axe. Walk north to the Chaos Temple and cast Telekinetic Grab on the wine of Zamorak inside for the diary; it is a medium Falador task. Casting the spell turns the monks on the ground floor aggressive, so cast from where you can walk "},{"t":"Port Sarim: Excalibur","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Taverley, Port Sarim and the Goblin Village: Excalibur and the slop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t181-h","x":"Walk south through Falador. In the park, buy two woad leaves from Wyson (offer 20 gp to get two at once) for the blue dye. In the Rising Sun Inn, stamp the barcrawl card and pay Emily 200 gp to learn how to make Asgoldian ale; the ales themselves come later, right before Rohak. In Port Sarim, buy two pots of flour at Wydin's food store, an orange at Trader Stan's on the dock and a fishing bait at Gerrant's. In Rimmington, buy a bucket at the general store and fill it at the well, make two bread doughs from the flour and water, and bake them on the range in the house next to the general store. Walk back to Port Sarim and give a bread to the beggar outside Grum's gold shop for Merlin's Crystal"},{"t":"The goblin generals' slop","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Taverley, Port Sarim and the Goblin Village: Excalibur and the slop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t182-h","x":"Walk north to Draynor and use the two woad leaves on Aggie for a blue dye (5 gp). Walk north to the Goblin Village and climb down the ladder in the building just south of the generals. Give Mudknuckles the charcoal, then make the ingredients: slice the orange with your knife and dye the slices blue, use the spice on the fishing bait, and use the bucket of water on the bread. The charcoal makes his cauldron explode in a short cutscene; it is part of the quest and does you no harm. Only blue, black, green or purple dye works on the slices; red, yellow, orange and pink don't. Talk to Mudknuckles again for the slop of compromise. Cast Lumbridge Home Teleport and give the slop to the goblin gener"},{"t":"Rohak's rock cake","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Taverley, Port Sarim and the Goblin Village: Excalibur and the slop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t183-h","x":"Cast Falador Teleport and buy four Asgarnian ales in the Rising Sun Inn (or collect them free at the Toad and Chicken in Burthorpe, next to the tunnel), and use a coin on each to make Asgoldian ale. With the cake ingredients that is your fullest moment of the section, about 27 slots. Walk into the dwarven tunnel under White Wolf Mountain from Taverley. Give Rohak, the old dwarf, Asgoldian ales until he agrees to bake a dwarven rock cake, then talk to him three times; finish every dialogue, or you'll need new ales. Hand the ales over one after another without stopping: if he sobers up before the cake, you need more, and four is all you carry. Pay him 100 gp and give him the ingredients; he pu"},{"t":"Varrock, Lumbridge and Camelot: Merlin's Crystal and Elemental Workshop I","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b40-h","x":"This block finishes Merlin's Crystal and Elemental Workshop I, frees the Mountain Dwarf with the rock cake, starts Holy Grail, and clears the Seers' Village diary stops on the way. The black candle, the bat bones and the thread are all made or bought within a few minutes of being used. Gate in Excalibur and the rock cake; 20 Attack for Holy Grail; 30 Mining for coal. Carry in about 20/28. Exit Merlin's Crystal, Freeing the Mountain Dwarf and Elemental Workshop I done; Holy Grail started; three Seers' Village diary tasks; the rune sword; about 520,000 gp. Carries forward Excalibur and the rune sword (the Black Knight Titan), the holy table napkin (Holy Grail)."},{"t":"Varrock and Lumbridge","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Varrock, Lumbridge and Camelot: Merlin's Crystal and Elemental Workshop I","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t185-h","x":"Break a Chronicle card. In the Champions' Guild, buy a rune sword (not the longsword) from Scavvo: it is your melee weapon from the Black Knight Titan until well into Chapter 2. Walk into Varrock, buy one thread from the Fancy Clothes Store (Elemental Workshop I's bellows), and read the inscription on the altar in the Zamorak temple in south-east Varrock: the words go on the black candle ritual. Tell Historian Minas about Priest in Peril and Vampyre Slayer for their kudos. Cast Lumbridge Home Teleport and give the rock cake to the frozen dwarf in the castle dining room to complete Freeing the Mountain Dwarf (1 quest point, 1,000 Slayer and 1,000 Cooking XP). Done when you hold the rune sword"},{"t":"Merlin's Crystal","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Varrock, Lumbridge and Camelot: Merlin's Crystal and Elemental Workshop I","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t186-h","x":"Teleport to Camelot and walk to Catherby. Pick up the insect repellent from the table in Perdu's house, north of the Catherby bank, buy a bucket at the general store, and fill it with wax at the beehives in the enclosure at Catherby. Use the repellent on a hive before you take the wax. The candle maker turns the bucket of wax into a black candle; drop the repellent. He lives in the house west of the Catherby bank, and you have to ask him about black candles before he takes the wax. Hide in Arhein's crate again to reach Keep Le Faye and kill a giant bat for its bat bones, then leave the way you came. The giant bats fly around outside the keep, beyond its ground-floor doors, and the crates in "},{"t":"Elemental Workshop I and Seers' Village","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Varrock, Lumbridge and Camelot: Merlin's Crystal and Elemental Workshop I","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t187-h","x":"Cross the log shortcut to the Coal Trucks and mine four coal (one of them also counts for the diary). In Seers' Village, start Elemental Workshop I from the bookcase in the house just south-west of the bank and follow it into the workshop, using your knife, hammer and thread: the costume needle works on the workshop's bellows only if you carry real thread. The bookcase gives a battered book; cut it with your knife for the key, which leaves a slashed book. Keep that slashed book: the shield can't be made without it, and if the workbench still refuses, the wiki's fix is to destroy the book and take a new one from the bookcase. The key opens the odd-looking wall in the northern building with th"},{"t":"Entrana, Lost City, Demon Slayer and the Black Knight Titan","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b41-h","x":"This block makes the section's second planned death so you can visit Entrana with nothing it bans, then finishes Lost City, Demon Slayer and Holy Grail's Black Knight Titan in one sweep south. Entrana's monks search you before the boat leaves and turn away most weapons and armour with combat bonuses, and that includes your staff, rune sword, Excalibur and pickaxe. Runes, a knife and food are allowed, and so are most jewellery, gloves and boots. Rather than check every item you own against the wiki's list, the guide takes a short kit that is plainly allowed. Gate in 31 Crafting and 36 Woodcutting for Lost City; Rune Mysteries for Enter the Abyss; a Falador Castle deathpile for Entrana. Carry "},{"t":"Planned death: Falador Castle again","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Entrana, Lost City, Demon Slayer and the Black Knight Titan","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t189-h","x":"In Port Sarim, buy about 300 air runes and about 200 fire runes from Betty, because your staff of air can't come to Entrana and the tree spirit there is weak to fire. Make sure your rune pouch still holds law, nature and water runes, which with the air runes cast Falador Teleport, carry the chaos runes loose for Fire Bolt, keep your raw fish noted, and walk to Falador Castle. Don't cook food before a planned death: the wiki's UIM guide warns that un-noted food and potions disappear from a deathpile. This death destroys the Chronicle, as every death does; you buy it back in Draynor later in this block, and nothing before then uses it. Take off everything, attack a White Knight with auto-retal"},{"t":"Entrana","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Entrana, Lost City, Demon Slayer and the Black Knight Titan","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t190-h","x":"Walk to Port Sarim and take the monks' boat to Entrana. Talk to the High Priest for Holy Grail. He is in the island's church; after him, an old crone appears and tells you the Fisher King is in trouble, which points you to the magic whistles later in this block. The dungeon is in the north-west of the island: walk east around the church and north over the bridge, and the cave monk stands just west of it. Talk to him and climb down. Your Prayer drops to almost 0 inside and there is no way back up the ladder, so you leave by teleport (the magic door to the east leads to level 32 Wilderness; don't use it). Kill level 25 zombies until one drops a bronze axe (50/128 a kill); the mushrooms against"},{"t":"Lost City","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Entrana, Lost City, Demon Slayer and the Black Knight Titan","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t191-h","x":"Cast Lumbridge Home Teleport. Use your knife on a dramen branch to make a dramen staff (31 Crafting). Walk to the shed in the Lumbridge Swamp, wield the staff and walk in to reach Zanaris and complete Lost City: 3 quest points, 1,500 Woodcutting and 1,500 Crafting XP. The shed is in the middle of the swamp; you open its door with the staff wielded. Lost City also lets you buy and wield the dragon longsword and dragon dagger from 60 Attack, and the dramen staff is your key to the fairy rings from 1.4 on. Wield your staff of air again and drop the leftover air and fire runes. Done when Lost City is complete."},{"t":"Demon Slayer and the magic whistles","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Entrana, Lost City, Demon Slayer and the Black Knight Titan","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t192-h","x":"Wizard Traiborn wants 25 bones for his part of Demon Slayer, and he takes them in batches, so a UIM never carries all 25. Walk to the Wizards' Tower and talk to Traiborn in the tower to agree to help. He is on the first floor; ask him whether he has any keys knocking around. Walk to the chicken farm north-west of Lumbridge, kill chickens for as many bones as you have free slots (about five), and walk back to hand them in; five trips do it. He gives you the first of the three silver keys. If you die while you hold his key, he wants another 25 bones, so take no risks until all three keys are with Sir Prysin. Walk north to Draynor. In the market, buy the Chronicle back from Diango for 300 gp (i"},{"t":"Karamja and the Black Knight Titan","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Entrana, Lost City, Demon Slayer and the Black Knight Titan","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t193-h","x":"Cast Falador Teleport, walk to Port Sarim and charter a ship to Brimhaven. Stamp the barcrawl card in the Dead Man's Chest. Take the rope swing to Moss Giant Island and back for the Karamja diary. At the gold rocks on Karamja's north-west peninsula (the North Brimhaven mine), mine a gold ore for the diary and drop it. The scorpions around the mine are poisonous, so don't linger among them. Blow a magic whistle under the guard tower just north of them to reach the Fisher Realm's entrance for Holy Grail, and fight the Black Knight Titan (level 120) with your rune sword. He has 142 Hitpoints, hits with crush for up to 15 and never moves from his tile, and his Magic and Ranged defence are so hig"},{"t":"Rellekka: the Fremennik Trials, Peer the Seer and Koschei","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b42-h","x":"This block takes the Fremennik Trials as far as they go before Olaf's lyre and Manni's keg, which wait for 1.4, and clears the Fremennik diary tasks that don't need the Trials finished. It has the section's third planned death, because Peer the Seer's task needs an empty inventory and nothing worn, and because Koschei's arena bans weapons, armour and runes. The trial items come and go in Rellekka itself. Gate in a planned death at the Rellekka rock crabs. Carry in about 23/28. Exit the Fremennik Trials up to the lyre and keg; the Fremennik diary tasks that don't need the Trials finished; about 485,000 gp. Carries forward nothing new."},{"t":"The Fremennik Trials","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Rellekka: the Fremennik Trials, Peer the Seer and Koschei","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t195-h","x":"Use the Barbarian Assault minigame teleport and walk north to Rellekka. Talk to Brundt in the longhall to start The Fremennik Trials, then follow the wiki quick guide's order for the votes that don't need Peer, Koschei, Olaf or Manni: each trial hands you a single-use item that goes straight to the next person, so hand each over before you take the next. Olaf's lyre needs 40 Woodcutting for the swaying tree's branch, 40 Crafting to cut it and 25 Fletching to string it with golden wool, and Manni's vote needs a low alcohol keg from Seers' Village, so both wait for 1.4, along with Lalli's golden fleece for the lyre (he trades it for a stew that needs Askeladden's pet rock). UIM risk Sigmund's "},{"t":"Planned death: the Rellekka rock crabs","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Rellekka: the Fremennik Trials, Peer the Seer and Koschei","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t196-h","x":"Make sure you have a knife and the dramen branch somewhere you can pick them out of a pile; you don't need food for Koschei (see below). Walk to the rock crabs on the coast north of Rellekka, take everything off, turn auto-retaliate off, and stand among the rocks until the crabs wake. The death destroys the Chronicle; you buy it back in Draynor at the start of the next block, before you next need it. Each crab hits for 1 at most, every 2.4 seconds, but several at once wear down an unarmoured player within a few minutes. They turn tolerant after ten minutes; if they stop attacking, walk about halfway back towards the village entrance to reset them and come back. You respawn in Lumbridge. Use "},{"t":"Peer the Seer and Koschei","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Rellekka: the Fremennik Trials, Peer the Seer and Koschei","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t197-h","x":"With nothing worn and nothing in your inventory, do Peer the Seer's task in his house for his vote. For other accounts Peer offers to bank everything you hold; a UIM has no bank for him to use, which is why the pile comes first. His riddle's answer is one of Mind, Tree, Life, Fire, Time or Wind. Inside, search the south-west cupboard (bucket), the unicorn head (red disk), the bull head (wooden disk), the southern chest (jug) and the northern bookcase (red herring). Use the red herring on the range and the sticky red goop on the wooden disk, go down the east trapdoor and put both red disks on the abstract mural; upstairs, fill the bucket at the tap and pour between the bucket and the jug unti"},{"t":"The Fremennik diary","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Rellekka: the Fremennik Trials, Peer the Seer and Koschei","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t198-h","x":"For the Fremennik diary, take Jarvald's boat to Waterbirth Island and pick up five snape grass (you can pick one up and drop it again). Until the Trials are complete, Jarvald charges 1,000 gp for the trip. Three other Rellekka tasks look as if they belong here but need The Fremennik Trials completed, not just started: browsing Yrsa's Accoutrements (her shoe store is gone; browsing the clothes shop counts), stealing from the fish stall (medium, 42 Thieving) and mining coal in the Rellekka mine (medium, 30 Mining). They wait for 1.4, straight after the Trials end. The tiara task and the oak log wait for a visit when you carry a tiara mould and an axe. The tiara has to be made from scratch in R"},{"t":"Bone Voyage","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b43-h","x":"This block completes Bone Voyage, which opens Fossil Island, and moves your house to Hosidius, where 1.4 starts. Its items are a chain: the sawmill proposal becomes the agreement, and the lucky charm and the Potion of Sealegs go to the barge crew the same hour you make them. The Museum Camp, the bird houses and the Reward Cart's herb batch open 1.4, once this block's long carries are gone. Gate in 100 kudos and The Dig Site for Bone Voyage; the grimy marrentill and the vial. Carry in about 22/28. Exit Bone Voyage done; the house in Hosidius; about 455,000 gp. Carries forward nothing new."},{"t":"Varrock and Kourend","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Bone Voyage","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t200-h","x":"Cast Falador Teleport and walk to Draynor: buy the Chronicle back from Diango in the market (the Rellekka death destroyed it), then break a Chronicle card. In the Varrock Museum, talk to Curator Haig Halen to start Bone Voyage (it needs 100 kudos and The Dig Site; your quests have taken you past 100). Go to the barge foreman north of the Digsite, and take the sawmill proposal he sends you for from the sawmill operator at the Lumber Yard east of Varrock. The foreman needs redwood planks for the barge, and the proposal and the agreement are what get them cut. Cast Falador Teleport and walk south to Port Sarim. Ask Veos to take you to Port Piscarilius. Walk to the Woodcutting Guild in Hosidius,"},{"t":"The barge and the Potion of Sealegs","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.3: Money, quests and the road to Fossil Island › Bone Voyage","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t201-h","x":"Break a Chronicle card, walk to the Lumber Yard and give the Varrock sawmill operator the sawmill agreement, then go to the barge north of the Digsite, board it and talk to the Lead Navigator. He calls the voyage cursed and won't sail until his crew feels safe. He sends you to the Rusty Anchor Inn in Port Sarim: cast Falador Teleport and walk south to talk to Jack Seagull (\"Ever made any cursed voyages?\"), who suggests a lucky charm, while Ahab cuts in with a Potion of Sealegs. Stamp the barcrawl card in the Rusty Anchor while you're there. Break a Chronicle card and take the quetzal from Regulus Cento to Civitas illa Fortis; buy two vodka at The Flaming Arrow, which the wiki lists among vod"},{"t":"End of section 1.3","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s8-h","x":"You finish 1.3 on Fossil Island's barge landing with Bone Voyage done, about 80 Thieving, 46 Construction, 43 Mining, about 60 Magic, a rune pouch, Bones to Peaches, a costume room holding the rogue and angler outfits, the full graceful outfit and about 62 Agility from Canifis, and about 455,000 gp. The Museum Camp, the bird houses and the Reward Cart's herb batch open 1.4, which starts in Hosidius, where your house now stands. Before you leave the island, check that the chaos runes and the mud rune are still in your inventory: 1.4's first block uses both. Skill Level Note Thieving about 80 Blackjacking stops here until the end of 1.4 Construction 46 Pool planks plus oak larders in Hosidius "},{"t":"1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s9-h","x":"This section is a long questing loop that ends with 62 Farming from the Tithe Farm, Desert Treasure and 43 Prayer, with blackjacking paying for Chapter 2. The rest doesn't: Herblore comes first. Eadgar's Ruse and the herb potions want Herblore before the Tithe Farm's seed box exists, so the Reward Cart's remaining rolls are split: its herbs now (batch 2), everything else after the Tithe Farm (batch 3). The earth orbs are gone. They need 1,600 molten glass, a looting bag and repeated Wilderness deaths, the three things a UIM handles worst. Chapter 2's money comes from blackjacking Menaphite thugs from about 80 to 85 Thieving in the rogue outfit instead, a level target that the wiki's rates tu"},{"t":"The Grand Tree and The Eyes of Glouphrie","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b44-h","x":"Section 1.3 left you on Fossil Island with the chaos runes and the mud rune from the Mage Training Arena still in your bag. Both are for this block, so it comes first: The Grand Tree's black demon is a Fire Bolt fight, and The Eyes of Glouphrie needs the mud rune, which no shop sells. Doing them now means neither stack is carried through the section. The Grand Tree also opens the gnome gliders, which Chapter 2 uses. Gate in 25 Agility for The Grand Tree; The Grand Tree, 5 Construction and 46 Magic for The Eyes of Glouphrie; 35 Magic for Fire Bolt. Carry in about 20/28. Exit The Grand Tree and The Eyes of Glouphrie done; the gnome gliders open; about 452,000 gp; about 18/28. Carries forward n"},{"t":"Taverley and Varrock","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › The Grand Tree and The Eyes of Glouphrie","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t205-h","x":"Take the barge back to the Digsite. Drop the costume needle: its last job in this chapter, the diary coif, is sewn later with a plain needle. Cast Falador Teleport, walk to Taverley and buy a pestle and mortar at Jatix's Herblore Shop. Cast Varrock Teleport, buy about 200 fire runes and, if your chaos stack is under 150, more chaos runes from Aubury, and take the spirit tree at the Grand Exchange to the Tree Gnome Stronghold. Done when you are in the Stronghold with the pestle and mortar and the runes."},{"t":"The Grand Tree","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › The Grand Tree and The Eyes of Glouphrie","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t206-h","x":"Talk to King Narnode Shareen at the foot of the Grand Tree with two free slots: he gives you the translation book and the bark sample again. Hazelmere lives on the peninsula east of Yanille, and the fairy rings are not open yet, so use the ring of dueling's Castle Wars teleport, walk east through Yanille and on to his house. He takes the bark sample and gives you a scroll. Cast Varrock Teleport, ride the spirit tree back and follow the wiki's steps: Give the king Hazelmere's message, then talk to Glough in his tree house south-east of the Grand Tree, and let him have you arrested. Talk to Charlie on the top floor of the Grand Tree until the conversation ends, then search the cupboard in Glou"},{"t":"The Eyes of Glouphrie","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › The Grand Tree and The Eyes of Glouphrie","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t207-h","x":"Talk to Brimstail in his cave in the south-west of the Stronghold to start The Eyes of Glouphrie, inspect the singing bowl in the west of the cave, try Oaknock's machine to the north and talk to Brimstail again. He sends you to Hazelmere: ring of dueling to Castle Wars and the same walk as before. Watch the cutscenes upstairs until you receive the violet pentagon. Let his dialogue run to the very end: the wiki warns that skipping part of it leaves him unable to be understood later in the quest. The quest also wants a saw, an oak log and a maple log, and this is the moment to get them. Cast Camelot Teleport and chop one maple log in Seers' Village. Cast Varrock Teleport, walk to the Lumber Ya"},{"t":"Fossil Island and the Hosidius workshop","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b45-h","x":"Take the barge from the Digsite back to Fossil Island. This block opens the island's mushtrees, builds the workshop that turns your steel bars into clockworks, trains Herblore on the Reward Cart's first herbs, starts the compost line, and places your first four bird houses. It is a block of building and processing, so it starts with your kit at its lightest. Gate in Bone Voyage; 22 Mining for volcanic ash; 25 Construction for the crafting table 2; 8 Crafting for clockworks and 5 for bird houses; 22 Herblore for compost potions; 25 Thieving for the fruit stall and 38 for master farmers. Carry in about 18/28. Exit the mushtrees; a workshop with a crafting table 2; 27 Herblore; the compost line"},{"t":"Fossil Island","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Fossil Island and the Hosidius workshop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t209-h","x":"In the Museum Camp's general store, buy a chisel (1 gp) and an empty bucket pack (650 gp), and open the pack: it gives 100 noted buckets in one slot. The camp is just east of the barge landing. Climb the House on the Hill and use its mushtree once, then walk to the Verdant Valley mushtree (south of the camp) and the Mushroom Meadow one (north-west of the Mushroom Forest) and try each: a mushtree only works once you've found it. The Sticky Swamp one, inside the Tar Swamp, isn't needed. Reaching it takes an axe and a rake to clear the way, and a level 132 tar monster lives in that swamp. Mine about 150 volcanic ash at the volcano in the north-east (22 Mining). It stacks, and it is the \"ash\" in"},{"t":"The workshop","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Fossil Island and the Hosidius workshop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t210-h","x":"Talk to Lord Kandur Hosidius in his house to start The Depths of Despair (18 Agility), and to Chief Farmer Phabelle at the vinery as he asks; the quest's library and cave steps come in the Kourend blocks. At the Hosidius allotment just north of your house, hand the noted buckets to the tool leprechaun, who stores them, and fill the compost bin with 15 compostable items (weeds from the patches, or produce from the Hosidius stalls); close it so it rots while you work. Walk to the Woodcutting Guild. In Perry's Chop-chop Shop by the entrance, buy a rune axe (41 Woodcutting to use): you dropped your steel axe in 1.3, and from here the bird house logs, Mountain Daughter, Sleeping Giants and 70 Woo"},{"t":"Herblore from the Reward Cart, batch 2","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Fossil Island and the Hosidius workshop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t211-h","x":"Eadgar's Ruse needs 31 Herblore (a botanical pie boosts 4). You are at about 22. Walk to the Wintertodt camp, search the Reward Cart until you hold about 60 grimy harralander and one grimy ranarr (the number of searches that takes is an estimate and varies per account; it is the largest use of the cart's remaining rolls); drop everything else, including the other herbs and the seeds, which come back in batch 3 once you have the seed box. The ranarr is for Eadgar's Ruse's troll potion: the potion made from it needs 30 Herblore and the troll potion 31, so you make both later with the botanical pie. Back in Hosidius, buy vials of water from Horace's general store and make compost potions: unnot"},{"t":"Ultracompost","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Fossil Island and the Hosidius workshop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t212-h","x":"When the bin has rotted, open it and use the compost potion on it for supercompost, then use 25 volcanic ash on it for ultracompost. Take buckets back from the leprechaun a few at a time (he returns them unnoted), fill them from the bin and store the ultracompost with him, until the bin is empty. Drop the rest of the ash and the empty potion vial: the bird runs pass the volcano whenever you need more ash, and you make the next compost potion when the next batch starts. Done when the ultracompost is with the leprechaun."},{"t":"Clockworks, bird houses and seeds","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Fossil Island and the Hosidius workshop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t213-h","x":"Walk to the Woodcutting Guild, unnote your steel bars at the bank chest (you get one per free slot, so five with room to spare) and drop one: four clockworks are all the bird runs need, because dismantling a full bird house gives its clockwork back. Chop four logs from the guild's normal trees. Teleport to your house and make the four clockworks at the crafting table (8 Crafting, one steel bar each). You are about 9 Hunter from the museum quiz, so your first houses are regular ones (5 Hunter, 5 Crafting); oak needs 14 Hunter. Use a clockwork on each log with the hammer and chisel in your inventory to make four bird houses. Then pickpocket the two master farmers in Hosidius (38 Thieving) unti"},{"t":"The first bird run","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Fossil Island and the Hosidius workshop","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t214-h","x":"Break a Chronicle card, walk east through Varrock and take the barge north of the Digsite to Fossil Island. Set the four houses at the four sites: two in the Verdant Valley, one in the Mushroom Forest (west of the ancient shroom, just north of the Mushroom Meadow mushtree) and one at the Tar Swamp entrance (don't go into the swamp). Each takes ten low-level seeds or five high-level ones, and seed types can be mixed; drop any low-level seeds left over (keep the barley), because the next runs' seeds come from the Draynor seed market. A house fills in about 50 minutes (10 birds at most); dismantling it returns the clockwork, and emptying it early loses the house, the seeds and the loot. Birds a"},{"t":"Burthorpe: Death Plateau and Troll Stronghold","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b46-h","x":"This block does both troll quests in one go, frees Eadgar and opens the Troll Stronghold's secret south entrance for Eadgar's Ruse later. On the way north it finishes Sir Percival's part of Holy Grail, and on the way out of Port Sarim it collects what the next two blocks need: the iron bars, the clay for Prince Ali's key and a redberry for the skin paste. The two quests go in this order because Troll Stronghold can't start until Death Plateau is complete, and Death Plateau's reward is the right to buy climbing boots from Tenzing: Troll Stronghold's route climbs rocks that need those boots and 15 Agility. Gate in 43 Magic for Superheat Item; Death Plateau and 15 Agility for Troll Stronghold; "},{"t":"Port Sarim, Rimmington and the Goblin Village","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Burthorpe: Death Plateau and Troll Stronghold","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t216-h","x":"From Falador, walk south to Port Sarim. At Gerrant's Fishy Business buy a fly fishing rod and about 50 feathers (Death Plateau's ten trout), and at Wydin's food store one redberry for Prince Ali's skin paste. In the Rimmington mine, mine two iron ores and one clay, and cast Superheat Item on both ores (43 Magic, four fire runes and one nature rune each): one bar is for Dunstan's spiked boots, the other for the Museum Camp's bank chest. Superheat never fails, where a normal furnace smelts iron ore into a bar only half the time. The spell works only on unnoted ore in your inventory, and each cast gives 53 Magic XP on top of the Smithing XP a furnace would give for the bar. Keep the clay unwork"},{"t":"Death Plateau","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Burthorpe: Death Plateau and Troll Stronghold","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t217-h","x":"Walk on to Burthorpe and talk to Denulth in the Imperial Guard camp to start Death Plateau, and follow it: win the gamble with Harold in the Toad and Chicken (bets must be over 60 gp, and a 101 gp bet bankrupts him at once), find the combination for the stone balls, and get the secret way from Tenzing the Sherpa. Tenzing wants ten unnoted bread, ten unnoted cooked trout and the spiked boots Dunstan makes from a pair of climbing boots, Denulth's certificate and an iron bar (Tenzing sells climbing boots for 12 gp: buy one pair for Dunstan and one to wear), and the wiki is explicit that all 21 items go in one go: a UIM needs 21 free slots for the hand-in. Denulth's tent is south of the Games Ro"},{"t":"Troll Stronghold","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Burthorpe: Death Plateau and Troll Stronghold","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t218-h","x":"Talk to Denulth again to start Troll Stronghold. Beat Dad (level 101) in the arena with your rune sword and best food, stopping when he yields (magic from the gate is a safespot), and leave by the north gate; run past the thrower trolls. Inside the Stronghold, kill a Troll General (max hit 38; safespot behind the counter with magic or ranged) for the prison key. In the prison, the two sleeping guards Berry and Twig (level 71) hold the cell keys: pickpocket them with 30 Thieving, or kill them through the cell doors. Free both Eadgar and Godric, leave by the secret exit and climb the south-east rocks, and report to Dunstan in Burthorpe to complete the quest (1 quest point, 2,000 Agility XP and"},{"t":"Lumbridge, Draynor and Varrock: Prince Ali Rescue, The Lost Tribe and Fairytale I","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b47-h","x":"This block builds the Museum Camp, completes Prince Ali Rescue and Romeo & Juliet, takes The Lost Tribe as far as the goblin emotes, starts Fairytale I with two of its five farmers and plants Forgettable Tale's barley. Prince Ali's rescue takes eight slots at the end, so the camp comes first, while its planks and bar are still in your bag, and the rescue items are collected in the order below and used the same hour. Gate in 29 Construction for the camp's loom; Goblin Diplomacy, Rune Mysteries, 13 Agility, 13 Thieving and 17 Mining for The Lost Tribe; Lost City, Nature Spirit, Priest in Peril and The Restless Ghost for Fairytale I. Carry in about 22/28. Exit the Museum Camp built; Prince Ali "},{"t":"The Museum Camp","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Lumbridge, Draynor and Varrock: Prince Ali Rescue, The Lost Tribe and Fairytale I","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t220-h","x":"Teleport to Varrock. At the Lumber Yard east of the city, buy 25 steel nails from the sawmill operator, and at Varrock East Bank unnote oak planks, which comes out as many as you have free slots, so take the two you need first and let the rest stay noted. Take the barge north of the Digsite to Fossil Island, and build the camp's structures with your hammer, in this order, so the oak planks never pile up in your bag: The bank chest (21 Construction): the two oak planks, the iron bar and five nails. For a UIM it is the island's unnoting point, and from now on it unnotes the log stacks for your bird houses. The well (22): unnote two oak planks at the new chest (it gives as many as fit, so drop "},{"t":"Prince Ali's rescue items","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Lumbridge, Draynor and Varrock: Prince Ali Rescue, The Lost Tribe and Fairytale I","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t221-h","x":"In Varrock, buy a pink skirt from Thessalia's Fine Clothes. Walk to Lumbridge, buy a bucket at the general store, take a pot of flour from the Culinaromancer's Chest in the castle basement, chop a log and burn it for ashes, and mine one copper and one tin ore in the Lumbridge Swamp's eastern mine; smelt them into a bronze bar at the Lumbridge furnace. Walk to Draynor. Fill the bucket at a well and use it on your clay for soft clay, fill it again, and in Aggie's house use the redberry, ashes, pot of flour and bucket of water on her for skin paste; drop the bucket. In the jailhouse east of the bank, talk to Lady Keli until she lets you take a key print with the soft clay. Walk back to the Lumb"},{"t":"Prince Ali Rescue","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Lumbridge, Draynor and Varrock: Prince Ali Rescue, The Lost Tribe and Fairytale I","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t222-h","x":"In Draynor, talk to Leela south of the wheat field. In the jailhouse, give Joe the three beers, use the rope on Lady Keli, open the cell door with the bronze key, and give Prince Ali the wig, skin paste and pink skirt. Walk east through Lumbridge, go on to Al Kharid (the toll gate is free from now on). Report to Chancellor Hassan in the palace to complete Prince Ali Rescue (3 quest points and 700 gp). If Leela doesn't tell you to deal with the guard, the wig is still white: dye it before you go in. Offer Joe the beers until he is drunk, and only then tie up Keli. Hassan is in the palace's southern chamber, and the reward also gives 500 Smithing and 500 Crafting XP. Don't craft the diary coif"},{"t":"The Lost Tribe and the botanical pie","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Lumbridge, Draynor and Varrock: Prince Ali Rescue, The Lost Tribe and Fairytale I","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t223-h","x":"Walk back to Lumbridge. Talk to Sigmund on the castle's upper floor to start The Lost Tribe, ask the Duke, the cook, Hans, Father Aereck and Bob about the cellar until one of them mentions the goblin (the cook does), and tell the Duke. At the swamp east of the castle, buy a candle from the candle seller (1,000 gp: the nearest shop candle is in Catherby, and a candle isn't worth a separate trip). Go down the kitchen trapdoor, mine through the rubble (17 Mining) and squeeze through (13 Agility), light the candle with your tinderbox, and take the brooch about ten steps in; come back the same way, because straying off the route can make the gas explode a naked flame. Show the brooch to the Duke."},{"t":"Fairytale I, the barley and the seeds","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Lumbridge, Draynor and Varrock: Prince Ali Rescue, The Lost Tribe and Fairytale I","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t224-h","x":"In Draynor, talk to Martin the Master Gardener by the pig pen to start Fairytale I - Growing Pains (never pickpocket him: it blocks him for 10 minutes). At Olivia's seed stall in the market, buy about 200 potato seeds for your next bird runs; they stack in one slot. Buy the Chronicle back from Diango in the market too (300 gp, its charges come back with it): the Death Plateau death destroyed it, and Fairytale I's grotto exit below uses it. Walk to the hops patch north of Lumbridge. Talk to Vasquen, the first of the five farmers Fairytale I asks you to consult, then take the rake, seed dibber and compost from the tool leprechaun, rake the patch, add the compost and plant the four barley seeds"},{"t":"Varrock: Romeo & Juliet, Reldo and Dreven","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Lumbridge, Draynor and Varrock: Prince Ali Rescue, The Lost Tribe and Fairytale I","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t225-h","x":"Pick two cadava berries from the bushes south-east of Varrock. Give them to the Apothecary in south-west Varrock for a cadava potion, give it to Juliet in her house west of the square, and tell Romeo in the square to complete Romeo & Juliet (5 quest points). The bushes are just west of the south-east Varrock mine, and the Apothecary's shop, with the purple potion icon, is west of the sword shop. Choose to talk about something else when he greets you. Don't drink the cadava potion yourself: it knocks you out for a moment. The reward also includes an antique lamp worth 500 XP in a skill of your choice; rub it straight away so it doesn't take a slot. In the palace library, show Reldo the brooch"},{"t":"Falador, the Goblin Village and the Lost Tribe","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b48-h","x":"Cast Falador Teleport. This block consults Fairytale I's last three farmers, starts Eadgar's Ruse, takes Fairytale I into Zanaris and finishes The Lost Tribe. It also buys the pestle and mortar and the vial that The Shadow of the Storm needs two blocks from now, because Taverley is the last place on the route that sells them. Gate in 31 Herblore (boostable), Druidic Ritual and Troll Stronghold for Eadgar's Ruse; the goblin emotes for The Lost Tribe's end. Carry in about 20/28. Exit Eadgar's Ruse started; The Lost Tribe done and Death to the Dorgeshuun started; Fairytale I at Zandar Horfyre; the ghostspeak amulet worn; about 411,000 gp; about 21/28. Carries forward the symptoms list (Zandar H"},{"t":"Falador and Taverley: three farmers and Eadgar's Ruse","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Falador, the Goblin Village and the Lost Tribe","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t227-h","x":"Talk to Elstan at the allotment south of Falador and to Heskel at the tree patch in Falador Park: your third and fourth Fairytale I farmers. Walk to Taverley and talk to Alain at the tree patch, your fifth. At Jatix's Herblore Shop buy a pestle and mortar and one vial. Elstan's allotment is through the cabbage field on the farm south of the city. Eat half of the botanical pie for the Herblore boost (27 + 4 is 31) and talk to Sanfew upstairs in Taverley to start Eadgar's Ruse. Keep the other half for the troll potion. Walk to the Goblin Village and talk to the two generals for The Lost Tribe, mediating between them until you learn the goblin emotes. Sanfew is on the first floor above Jatix's "},{"t":"Draynor and Zanaris","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Falador, the Goblin Village and the Lost Tribe","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t228-h","x":"Cast Falador Teleport and walk south-east to Draynor. Tell Martin the Master Gardener what the five farmers said. Walk on to the shed in the Lumbridge Swamp, wield your dramen staff and enter Zanaris. Talk to the Fairy Godfather in the throne room, then to Fairy Nuff north of the bank for the symptoms list. Wield your staff of air again and leave. Fairytale I's next step is Zandar Horfyre in the Dark Wizards' Tower, at the start of the next block. Ask the Godfather where the queen is, and he names Fairy Nuff, whose room is in the north-west of the city, north of the bank. While you're in the swamp, walk to Father Urhney's hut and ask him for a ghostspeak amulet, and wear it: you lost yours w"},{"t":"The end of The Lost Tribe","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Falador, the Goblin Village and the Lost Tribe","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t229-h","x":"Go down the Lumbridge Castle kitchen trapdoor, light your candle and follow the cave route the wiki maps to Mistag, staying on it (clicking the minimap auto-paths) because the swamp gas can explode a naked flame. Perform the Goblin Bow in front of Mistag and ask him to show you out. Then follow the wiki's last steps: tell the Duke, who won't believe you; pickpocket Sigmund for his key and open his chest in the next room; pick the lock on the H.A.M. hideout's trapdoor north-west of the castle and take the silverware from the crate south of the ladder; give it to the Duke for the peace treaty; and follow Kazgar from the cellar to Mistag with the treaty to complete The Lost Tribe (1 quest point"},{"t":"Fairytale I's magic secateurs","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b49-h","x":"This block takes Fairytale I from the symptoms list to the magic secateurs. It is kept short on purpose: the three items the quest asks for are random, and you carry them into Morytania with nothing else on top of your kit. Gate in Fairytale I at Zandar Horfyre; the ghostspeak amulet. Carry in about 21/28. Exit the magic secateurs; the Falador diary's haircut and pump tasks; about 410,000 gp; about 21/28. Carries forward the magic secateurs (Tanglefoot), a spade stored with the tool leprechaun, the pestle and mortar and vial (The Shadow of the Storm)."},{"t":"Falador, Zandar and the Draynor skull","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Fairytale I's magic secateurs","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t231-h","x":"Teleport to Falador. Get a haircut from the hairdresser, and buy a bucket at the general store, fill it at the pump north of the west bank and drop it, both for the diary. Climb over the western Falador wall and take the symptoms list to Zandar Horfyre at the top of the Dark Wizards' Tower. Walk back round to Sarah's Farming Shop at the farm south of Falador and buy a spade. Walk east to Draynor Manor and dig on the grave north of the building, inside the fence, for the Draynor skull. Hand the spade to the tool leprechaun at the manor's belladonna patch: he keeps one for you, and any leprechaun gives it back, which is how a UIM owns a spade without carrying it. Zandar reads the list and send"},{"t":"The three items","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Fairytale I's magic secateurs","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t232-h","x":"The items are random. Notes for the hard ones: A clean avantoe or irit: the Reward Cart's remaining rolls drop both grimy, and Zahur in Nardah cleans a grimy herb for a fee; the Sorceress's Garden is the other source. A clean snapdragon: buy one for 10 vouchers at the Brimhaven Agility Arena. A nature talisman: the wiki's UIM advice of 50 abyssal pearls at Guardians of the Rift needs Temple of the Eye first, and the Abyss needs Enter the Abyss, both of which come later in this section. If your list has the talisman, check the wiki's talisman page for the monsters that drop it near you before anything else: this is the one item that can hold the block up. White berries: the Lava Isle spawn is"},{"t":"The nature grotto","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Fairytale I's magic secateurs","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t233-h","x":"Use the Shades of Mort'ton minigame teleport and walk north-west through Mort Myre to the nature grotto, killing a snail on the way for thin snail meat and its shell; step back out of the swamp and craft the shell into a snelm with your chisel there for the diary, because the task only counts a snelm made in Morytania outside Mort Myre; drop both. With the ghostspeak amulet on, give the Nature Spirit the three items for the magic secateurs. The grotto is deep in the swamp, north-west of Mort'ton, and the last stretch is a jump across a broken bridge to the cave entrance. The spirit enchants your secateurs into the magic secateurs, and only they can hurt the Tanglefoot. Break a Chronicle card"},{"t":"Al Kharid: Sleeping Giants and The Shadow of the Storm","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b50-h","x":"This block does two desert quests from one base. Sleeping Giants needs 20 empty slots when you search Kovac's crate, so it gets a planned death of its own right next to the Giants' Plateau; The Shadow of the Storm follows from the same spot. Sleeping Giants' 6,000 Smithing XP is also the first of the three quest rewards that carry you to the 40 Smithing the gold bars need later. Gate in 15 Smithing for Sleeping Giants; The Golem, Demon Slayer and 30 Crafting for The Shadow of the Storm; 33 quest points for the Champions' Guild; a planned death in the Al Kharid mine. Carry in about 21/28. Exit Sleeping Giants and The Shadow of the Storm done; about 404,000 gp; about 19/28. Carries forward not"},{"t":"Varrock: the black items, nails and oak logs","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Al Kharid: Sleeping Giants and The Shadow of the Storm","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t235-h","x":"Evil Dave only lets you into the demon's lair in at least three accepted black items, worn at once, and two of them are sold where the Chronicle put you. Upstairs in the Champions' Guild, buy a black full helm (1,372 gp) and black platelegs (2,496 gp) at Valaine's Shop of Champions. Walk into Varrock and buy a priest gown top at Thessalia's Fine Clothes. Do a bird run from the Digsite barge if the houses are ready. Then walk to the Lumber Yard north-east of the city, buy ten steel nails from the sawmill operator and chop three oak logs from the oaks around the yard. Your bag is now full, at 28, and that is fine for the next two minutes: use your ring of dueling's Emir's Arena teleport and wa"},{"t":"Planned death: the Al Kharid mine","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Al Kharid: Sleeping Giants and The Shadow of the Storm","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t236-h","x":"Take off everything you wear and let the scorpions in the mine kill you (level 14; it takes a few minutes with no armour on). The death destroys the Chronicle: you buy it back at Diango's for 300 gp when you reach Draynor two blocks from now, and its charges come back with it. Nothing until then needs its teleport. You respawn in Lumbridge with nothing. Walk to Fred the Farmer's house north of the castle, take the shears from the table inside and shear one sheep: Kovac wants one piece of wool, and a ball of wool does not work. Drop the shears. Walk east through the Al Kharid gate and north to your pile, and pick up only the hammer, the chisel, the ten nails and the three oak logs. The hammer"},{"t":"Sleeping Giants","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Al Kharid: Sleeping Giants and The Shadow of the Storm","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t237-h","x":"Talk to Kovac on the Giants' Plateau, just east of the mine, to start Sleeping Giants. Inside the foundry, repair the polishing wheel, the grindstone and the trip hammer with the logs, the wool and the nails, talk to Kovac twice, then search the crate: this is the step that needs 20 empty slots, and you now have 26. Put each crate item into the crucible separately, set the moulds Kovac names at the mould jig, pour the metal, and cool the preform with a bucket of water from the pile by the waterfall (your hands must be empty to pick it up). Then work it as Kovac describes: heat it in the lava until it is red and use the trip hammer until the progress bar is yellow; cool it to almost green and"},{"t":"The evil disguise","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Al Kharid: Sleeping Giants and The Shadow of the Storm","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t238-h","x":"Talk to Father Reen, south of the Al Kharid bank, to start The Shadow of the Storm. The wiki's quest page says he hands you a Silverlight if you don't have one, and you dropped yours after Delrith; if he doesn't, Sir Prysin in Varrock Palace sells a replacement for 500 gp. Mine one silver ore in the Al Kharid mine and smelt it at the furnace: it becomes the demonic sigil. Take only one Silverlight into the ruins. Evil Dave won't let you join the ritual while you carry a dyed and an undyed Silverlight together, and dyeing one deletes any other Silverlight in your bag. Cast Teleport to House and put all six graceful pieces in the magic wardrobe, the gloves, boots and cape included: a UIM can o"},{"t":"The Shadow of the Storm","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Al Kharid: Sleeping Giants and The Shadow of the Storm","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t239-h","x":"Follow the wiki's steps: Talk to Father Badden at the ruins, pick a black mushroom by the dungeon entrance, grind it into your vial with the pestle and mortar and use the black dye on Silverlight. Drop the pestle and mortar and the empty vial. Go down into the ruins, tell Evil Dave you want to join, and enter the portal. Denath gives you an incantation that is different for every player: write it down. Take the strange implement in the lair, ask Jennifer for the demonic sigil mould, and talk to Matthew about Josef's book. Outside, ask the clay golem what happened (before you search anything), then search the four kilns around Uzer until one gives you the demonic tome. Ride the carpet back to"},{"t":"Creature of Fenkenstrain","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b51-h","x":"This block does the whole of Creature of Fenkenstrain, which Garden of Tranquillity needs later. The quest fills your bag with body parts in the Experiment Cave, so for this one trip you shed four cheap things and buy three of them back afterwards. Its reward, the ring of charos, is the ring the first Garden of Tranquillity block turns into the ring of charos (a) at the Wise Old Man's house. Gate in Priest in Peril and The Restless Ghost; 20 Crafting and 25 Thieving; 43 Magic for Superheat Item; the ghostspeak amulet. Carry in about 19/28. Exit Creature of Fenkenstrain done, with the ring of charos; about 385,000 gp; about 20/28. Carries forward the ring of charos (Garden of Tranquillity), c"},{"t":"Varrock: the wires, the silver bar and the runes","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Creature of Fenkenstrain","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t241-h","x":"At the Hosidius allotment north of your house, hand the magic secateurs to the tool leprechaun and take the spade from him. Cast Varrock Teleport. Do a bird run if the houses are ready and drop what is left of the potato seeds afterwards; Draynor's seed market is in the next block. Buy about 200 chaos runes from Aubury: with your fire runes and the staff of air they are Fire Bolt, your safespot spell from here to the end of the section. Mine one silver ore in the mine south-west of Varrock and cast Superheat Item on it for a silver bar. In the mine south-east of Varrock, mine three copper and three tin ores and superheat each pair into a bronze bar, then smith three bronze wires at the anvil"},{"t":"Canifis and the castle","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Creature of Fenkenstrain","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t242-h","x":"Walk east through Paterdomus to Canifis. Read the signpost in the centre of the village to start Creature of Fenkenstrain. At the Canifis general store buy a needle and five thread (a costume needle would not have worked), and buy the pickled brain from the table in the Hair of the Dog for 50 gp. If the signpost says you don't meet the requirements, go to Dr Fenkenstrain anyway: he still offers you the job. In Fenkenstrain's Castle, north-east of the village, talk to Dr Fenkenstrain and choose the braindead and grave-digging answers. Upstairs, read The Joy of Grave Digging in the west bookcase and Handy Maggot Avoidance Techniques in the east one: they hold the marble and obsidian amulets, w"},{"t":"The graves and the Experiment Cave","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Creature of Fenkenstrain","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t243-h","x":"Dig at the cross-shaped grave marker in the Haunted Woods, south-east of the castle, for the decapitated head, and use the pickled brain on it; the vampyres here are level 61 to 72, so don't stand around. Head north out of the woods, use the star amulet on the easternmost memorial and push it to enter the Experiment Cave; drop the amulet once you're in. The grave is Ed Lestwit's, south-east of fairy ring ALQ, and the right memorial is the one with an indent in it. Kill a level 51 Experiment for the cavern key, with Fire Bolt and your swordfish. Follow the north-western path to the end, search the chest and climb the ladder, then dig up the three graves for the torso, arms and legs. Drop the "},{"t":"The lightning conductor","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Creature of Fenkenstrain","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t244-h","x":"With the ghostspeak amulet on, talk to the Gardener Ghost for the shed key. Search the cupboard in the shed for the garden brush, take three canes from the pile beside the shed, and attach them to the brush with the three bronze wires. Upstairs, use the extended brush on the western fireplace for the conductor mould. The ghost is behind the castle, the canes are east of the shed, and attaching them needs 20 Crafting. Use the brush on the middle of the fireplace, not on its surround, or nothing happens. The conductor is cast from the mould and your silver bar at a furnace, and the nearest you can use is Lumbridge's: cast Lumbridge Home Teleport, cast the conductor at the furnace north of the "},{"t":"Back through Varrock","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Creature of Fenkenstrain","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t245-h","x":"Walk back to Varrock. Buy a hammer, a chisel and a tinderbox at the general store, and pick three redberries from the bushes by the mine south-east of the city: they are the pie Thurgo wants in The Giant Dwarf. Walk south to Lumbridge for the next block. Done when you hold the tools and the redberries. Coins: about 385,000 gp after the chaos runes · Slots: about 20/28 at the end; about 27/28 at the peak, at the three graves · Requirements: 20 Crafting and 25 Thieving for Creature of Fenkenstrain; 43 Magic for Superheat Item; 4 Smithing for bronze wire Wiki references Creature of Fenkenstrain Bronze wire Needle Ring of charos Superheat Item"},{"t":"Zanaris and Draynor: Fairytale I, the fairy rings and A Porcine of Interest","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b52-h","x":"This block completes Fairytale I and A Porcine of Interest and opens the fairy rings with the first steps of Fairytale II. It also bakes the redberry pie Thurgo wants in The Giant Dwarf, because Lumbridge is the last range and pie dish on the way there. Gate in the magic secateurs; Lost City and Nature Spirit for Fairytale II. Carry in about 20/28. Exit Fairytale I and A Porcine of Interest done; the fairy rings open; the Chronicle bought back; about 388,000 gp; about 23/28. Carries forward the redberry pie (Thurgo), the magic secateurs and three jute seeds (the next block's first stops), potato seeds."},{"t":"Lumbridge: the secateurs and the redberry pie","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Zanaris and Draynor: Fairytale I, the fairy rings and A Porcine of Interest","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t247-h","x":"At the hops patch north of Lumbridge, where your barley is growing, take the magic secateurs back from the tool leprechaun. Leave the barley in the ground: grown hops don't die, and Forgettable Tale's brew is made much later in this section. In the castle basement, take a pie dish and a pot of flour from the Culinaromancer's Chest. In the kitchen, fill a jug at the sink (the chest sells jugs), make pastry dough and a pie shell, add the redberries and bake the redberry pie on the range (10 Cooking). Drop the jug and the empty pot. Done when you hold the magic secateurs and the redberry pie."},{"t":"Fairytale I","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Zanaris and Draynor: Fairytale I, the fairy rings and A Porcine of Interest","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t248-h","x":"Walk to the shed in the Lumbridge Swamp, wield the dramen staff and enter Zanaris. Wield the magic secateurs, squeeze through the gap towards the cosmic altar (using the low-level Agility shortcut once is a diary task) and kill Tanglefoot, which only the secateurs can hurt. Pick up the queen's secateurs and give them to the Fairy Godfather to complete Fairytale I - Growing Pains: 2 quest points, 3,500 Farming, 2,000 Attack and 1,000 Magic XP, and the magic secateurs are yours to keep. Head south-west from the entrance, past the two Agility shortcuts, to the ruins around the cosmic altar. The lower shortcut, the 46 Agility jutting wall, is the Lumbridge & Draynor hard diary task, and failing "},{"t":"Draynor: the Chronicle, the seeds and A Porcine of Interest","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Zanaris and Draynor: Fairytale I, the fairy rings and A Porcine of Interest","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t249-h","x":"Walk to Draynor. Buy the Chronicle back from Diango for 300 gp and wear it; it keeps the charges it had. At Olivia's seed stall buy about 200 potato seeds for the bird runs and three jute seeds for a diary task in the next block, and buy a rope from Ned. Talk to Martin the Master Gardener by the pig pen to start Fairytale II - Cure a Queen, and again in the market. He needs five minutes before the next step, which is the time A Porcine of Interest takes. The wait counts logged-in time only, so stay logged in while you do the sourhog. For A Porcine of Interest, walk to the crossroads north of the village, follow the cabbages and carrots north-east to the strange hole, use the rope on it and c"},{"t":"Fairytale II until the rings open","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Zanaris and Draynor: Fairytale I, the fairy rings and A Porcine of Interest","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t250-h","x":"Talk to Martin again. In Zanaris, pick up Nuff's certificate from the floor of Fairy Nuff's grotto north of the bank and study it, read the Rune Temple sign just south of the cosmic altar, talk to the Fairy Godfather in the throne room, then to the Co-ordinator just north of it, which unlocks the fairy rings, and to Fairy Fixit by the ring. Drop the certificate. The rest of the quest needs 57 Herblore and waits for a later chapter. Both the certificate and the sign matter: the wiki says that without the sign read, the later ring sequence to the queen only tells you to investigate further. Ask the Godfather both of his questions and agree to come back once you've found the queen. From the Co-"},{"t":"The fairy ring tour: Holy Grail, Jungle Potion and Tai Bwo Wannai","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b53-h","x":"With the dramen staff wielded, this block uses the rings for a string of diary tasks, finishes Holy Grail, does Jungle Potion and the Tai Bwo Wannai cleanup, and starts three quests. The Karamja stop used to come much later; it is here because its fairy ring is the cheapest way in, and because Jiminua's store sells the antipoison the Kourend blocks need. Gate in the fairy rings; 13 Farming for jute; 3 Herblore for Jungle Potion; 20 Farming for The Garden of Death. Carry in about 23/28. Exit Holy Grail and Jungle Potion done; Tai Bwo Wannai Trio, The Garden of Death and Olaf's Quest started; 100% Tai Bwo Wannai favour; about 388,000 gp; about 22/28. Carries forward the redberry pie (Thurgo), "},{"t":"Holy Grail and the Kandarin rings","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › The fairy ring tour: Holy Grail, Jungle Potion and Tai Bwo Wannai","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t252-h","x":"Visit in order: CIR, for the diary. It lands you in the Kebos Lowlands south of Mount Karuulm, and using it is a Kourend & Kebos medium diary task. BJR, the Fisher Realm: cross the bridge, go up through the castle and take the Holy Grail. Sir Percival took your whistle in Burthorpe's block, so the ring is your way in. Percival is the king now and you don't fight the Black Knight Titan again; the grail is reached by the staircase at the castle's east end and the ladder above it. ALS, McGrubor's Wood, for the diary. Walk out to the hops patch north of the wood, take the rake and seed dibber from the tool leprechaun, plant the three jute seeds for the diary, and hand him the rake, the dibber an"},{"t":"Karamja: Jungle Potion and Tai Bwo Wannai","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › The fairy ring tour: Holy Grail, Jungle Potion and Tai Bwo Wannai","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t253-h","x":"Take ring CKR and walk north to Tai Bwo Wannai. At Jiminua's Jungle Store, north-west of the village, buy two antipoisons, a machete and a spade. Talk to Trufitus in his house to start Jungle Potion. He wants five herbs one at a time, each cleaned and shown to him before he names the next: Snake weed, from the marshy jungle vines south-west of the village. A search can take one to five minutes, depending on your Herblore, so keep searching. Ardrigal, from the palm trees north-east of Trufitus, past the harpie bug swarms. The palms are on a peninsula just south of the Agility shortcut, and the swarms there are level 46. Sito foil, from the scorched earth directly south of the village. The tri"},{"t":"The Garden of Death and Olaf's Quest","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › The fairy ring tour: Holy Grail, Jungle Potion and Tai Bwo Wannai","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t254-h","x":"Take ring BLS. Start The Garden of Death (20 Farming, not boostable) by searching the tent at the campsite south of the lizardman settlement, and explore the cave below until you have enough words to be sent to Lake Molch. The lizardmen on the way poison, which is the first use of your antipoison; sip it, don't finish it. The tent gives you Kasonde's journal, and the cave is down the hole beside the camp. Search the numbered stone table for the first tablet, then the other tables, the vase and the eastern chest for the carvings and phrases that translate its words; once the tablet points north to an island, the only one it can mean is on Lake Molch, which the Kourend blocks visit. You can't "},{"t":"Keldagrim and the mountains: The Giant Dwarf, Mountain Daughter and Eadgar's Ruse","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b54-h","x":"This block completes The Giant Dwarf and Mountain Daughter and takes Eadgar's Ruse to the parrot. The Giant Dwarf's 2,500 Smithing XP is the second of the three quest rewards on the way to 40 Smithing, and Forgettable Tale of a Drunken Dwarf, which it unlocks, is done whole in the Blast Furnace block later. The Giant Dwarf also opens the Keldagrim minecarts, and Mountain Daughter uses them for its trip to White Wolf Mountain, which is why the two quests share a block in that order. Gate in 12 Crafting, 16 Firemaking, 14 Thieving and 33 Magic for The Giant Dwarf; 20 Agility for Mountain Daughter; 43 Magic for Superheat Item; an Eadgar's Ruse already started. Carry in about 22/28. Exit The Gia"},{"t":"The Giant Dwarf: the axe and Thurgo","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Keldagrim and the mountains: The Giant Dwarf, Mountain Daughter and Eadgar's Ruse","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t256-h","x":"Enter the cave east of Rellekka and talk to the Dwarven Boatman to start The Giant Dwarf; finish the conversation with Commander Veldaban when you arrive, and talk to Blasidar the sculptor on the east side of the city, south of the kebab shop. He needs clothes, boots and an axe for his statue, and the order below keeps your bag under 27. Inside the entrance, carry on east past the statues; the passage south leads to the foot of Trollweiss Mountain instead. Talk to the Dwarven Boatman, not the Ferryman: his ride is free, and it ends with the boat hitting the king's statue and you under arrest at the Black Guard headquarters, which is how you meet Veldaban. Blasidar's house is across the bridg"},{"t":"The Giant Dwarf: the clothes, the boots and the Consortium","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Keldagrim and the mountains: The Giant Dwarf, Mountain Daughter and Eadgar's Ruse","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t257-h","x":"Ask Vermundi in the eastern market for special clothes. In the library in the north-east of West Keldagrim, ask the librarian about King Alvis's clothes and climb a bookcase for the book on costumes (the ladder needs you under 30 kg, which graceful takes care of). Buy one coal from Ordan (67 gp), put the coal and the log into Vermundi's spinning machine, light it with your tinderbox and pay her 200 gp for the exquisite clothes. Give Vermundi the book first: she can't make the clothes without a picture of them. If lighting the machine fails, light it again. Talk to Saro at the anvil south-west of the bank. In Dromund's house north of the bank, take the left boot while he isn't looking, then c"},{"t":"Mountain Daughter","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Keldagrim and the mountains: The Giant Dwarf, Mountain Daughter and Eadgar's Ruse","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t258-h","x":"At Gunslik's Assorted Items in the West Consortium building, buy a rope (23 gp) and a pair of leather gloves (7 gp), and unnote one plank at the Keldagrim bank. Leave the city and walk to the Mountain Camp east of Rellekka: take the path north past the guard and use the rope on the boulder to get round the rockslide. Talk to Hamal the Chieftain to start Mountain Daughter, then follow the wiki's parts: Dig mud from the pond south of Hamal's tent and take a pole from north of it (the dramen staff doesn't work as one). Go north along the lake, use the mud on the tall tree and climb it, pole-vault over the rock clump, lay the plank on the flat stones and listen to the shining pool. Use the plank"},{"t":"Eadgar and Burntmeat","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Keldagrim and the mountains: The Giant Dwarf, Mountain Daughter and Eadgar's Ruse","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t259-h","x":"Use the Burthorpe Games Room minigame teleport and buy a pair of climbing boots from Tenzing (12 gp); wear them with the graceful boots in your bag. Take Death Plateau's secret way up to Trollheim and talk to Eadgar in his cave at the top about goutweed. Go down into the Troll Stronghold, talk to Burntmeat in the kitchen at the south end of the middle floor, and return to Eadgar, who now wants a parrot. That is the Ardougne zoo's job in the farming tour later. Eadgar's cave is the unmarked one on the south side of Trollheim's summit; he is only there because you freed him in Troll Stronghold. Burntmeat is one of the troll cooks, and he trades what he knows about goutweed for a human to put i"},{"t":"Kourend I: Port Piscarilius, Shayzien, Lovakengj and Arceuus","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b55-h","x":"Kourend is split into three blocks. This one buys back the tools Mountain Daughter cost you, sails to Port Piscarilius and starts four of the five Kourend quests. Whenever you need the minecart network, the Wintertodt camp's station is the hub. Gate in 16 Strength and 10 Mining for Tale of the Righteous; 20 Thieving and 25 Cooking for The Queen of Thieves; 18 Agility for The Depths of Despair; 12 Hunter for The Ascent of Arceuus. Carry in about 18/28. Exit The Queen of Thieves, Tale of the Righteous, The Forsaken Tower and The Ascent of Arceuus started; the Arceuus spellbook; about 378,000 gp; about 25/28. Carries forward Kharedst's memoirs, the letter (The Queen of Thieves), earth runes (th"},{"t":"Varrock and Port Sarim","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Kourend I: Port Piscarilius, Shayzien, Lovakengj and Arceuus","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t261-h","x":"The Chronicle put you outside the Champions' Guild. In Varrock, buy a hammer, a chisel and a tinderbox at the general store, and a shortbow and a few bronze arrows at Lowe's Archery Emporium: one puzzle in Tale of the Righteous has to be hit with ranged, and you own no ranged weapon yet. Do a bird run from the Digsite barge. Use up your potato seeds on it and drop the rest: there is no bird run from Kourend, and the master farmers in Hosidius refill the stack when you are back there. The bow is for one moment only. Pagida's puzzle wants a magic hit, a melee hit and a ranged hit in the same visit, and fists don't count as the melee hit, so the shortbow joins your Fire Bolt runes and the rune "},{"t":"Port Piscarilius, Shayzien and Lovakengj","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Kourend I: Port Piscarilius, Shayzien, Lovakengj and Arceuus","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t262-h","x":"Start The Queen of Thieves with Tomas Lawry outside the bank (20 Thieving, not boostable). Buy a piece of meat and a raw potato at Kenelme's Wares and a bowl at the general store, fill the bowl at the sink in Robert O'Reilly's house, cook the stew (25 Cooking) and give it to him. He sends you through the manhole into the Warrens: kill Conrad King on the dock for Devan Rutter, then speak to the Queen of Thieves, who sends you to Kingstown. Everything for the stew is a few steps from Tomas. Kenelme's Wares is the house directly west of him, Leenz's General Supplies is the general store, and Robert lives in the building directly south of him. In Robert's house, fill the bowl at the sink and add"},{"t":"Arceuus and Kingstown","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Kourend I: Port Piscarilius, Shayzien, Lovakengj and Arceuus","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t263-h","x":"In Arceuus, talk to Galana in the library for The Depths of Despair, which you started in Hosidius at the top of this section, and find and read The Varlamore Envoy for it. Hand a book in at the library for the diary, putting the XP on Magic. Talk to Mori to start The Ascent of Arceuus. Galana is on the library's ground floor, in its north-eastern section. The Varlamore Envoy sits on a different shelf for each player, and every square of bookcase is its own shelf, so search them one at a time in the area she names. If you log out before you find it, ask her again, because the book can move. Reading it is not optional: until you have, the Crabclaw Caves refuse you entry, and they are where Ko"},{"t":"Kourend II: the Forsaken Tower, Mount Karuulm and Getting Ahead","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b56-h","x":"Gate in 30 Crafting and 26 Construction for Getting Ahead (neither boostable); 20 Fishing for the trout; 49 Agility for the boulder leap. Carry in about 25/28. Exit Getting Ahead done; The Forsaken Tower and The Ascent of Arceuus advanced; back on the standard spellbook; about 381,000 gp; about 23/28. Carries forward Kharedst's memoirs, the letter, the antipoison."},{"t":"The Forsaken Tower and Mount Karuulm","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Kourend II: the Forsaken Tower, Mount Karuulm and Getting Ahead","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t265-h","x":"Take the minecart to the Wintertodt camp and progress The Forsaken Tower. Its puzzles: start the steam generator and align the power grid as the wiki's image shows; for the furnace, end with 4 gallons of coolant in the 5-gallon jug and pour it into the coolant west of the furnace before you light it; for the potion, read the old notes to find the cleansing fluid (its position differs per player, and a wrong one hits for 25 or more and poisons, so log out before advancing the dialogue if unsure); for the altar, move the discs W to E, W to C, E to C, W to E, C to W, C to E, W to E, W to C, E to C, E to W, C to W, E to C, W to E, W to C, E to C, then take Dinh's hammer to Undor. At the camp, te"},{"t":"Getting Ahead","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Kourend II: the Forsaken Tower, Mount Karuulm and Getting Ahead","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t266-h","x":"Do Getting Ahead at the farm south of the Farming Guild. Everything it needs is on the farm, so collect each thing only when its step comes; the last step is the fullest your bag gets in Kourend, at 28. Gordon is outside and Mary is inside the house; Gordon pays nothing until you prove the beast is dead, and no other trophy convinces him. Talk to Gordon, then to Mary in the main building. Take the pot of flour from upstairs in the house and use it on the southern gate beside the cow pen. Follow the flour trail south over the bridge and west to the cave at the Kebos Lowlands mine, and kill the Headless Beast (level 82) with Fire Bolt and cooked swordfish. Mine one clay at the mine and pick up"},{"t":"Back to the standard spellbook","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Kourend II: the Forsaken Tower, Mount Karuulm and Getting Ahead","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t267-h","x":"Cast the Arceuus home teleport to the Dark Altar and progress The Ascent of Arceuus there, then talk to Tyss next to the altar to switch back to the standard spellbook. Take the boulder leap shortcut in the Arceuus essence mine (49 Agility) for the diary. The Arceuus home teleport needs no runes but can only be cast once every 30 minutes, and combat interrupts it. Switching back costs nothing. You go back because your Falador, Camelot and Varrock teleports for the rest of the chapter are standard spells. Done when you are on the standard spellbook. Coins: about 381,000 gp · Slots: about 23/28 at the end; 28/28 at the peak, mounting the head · Requirements: 30 Crafting and 26 Construction for"},{"t":"Kourend III: the five Kourend quests completed","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b57-h","x":"Gate in each quest's requirements; 30 Crafting and 30 Construction for the crane. Carry in about 23/28. Exit The Depths of Despair, The Queen of Thieves, The Forsaken Tower, Tale of the Righteous, The Garden of Death and The Ascent of Arceuus done; about 400,000 gp; about 21/28. Carries forward a fresh stack of bird house seeds, a raw shark (Olaf's lyre)."},{"t":"Hosidius and Port Piscarilius","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Kourend III: the five Kourend quests completed","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t269-h","x":"Teleport to your house in Hosidius and refill the compost bin to the north with 15 compostable items. At the Woodcutting Guild's sawmill operator buy about 50 steel nails for the crane. In the Crabclaw Caves south of Hosidius, kill a sand crab with magic for the diary, kill the Sand Snake that guards the Royal Accord, take the accord to Lord Kandur Hosidius and complete The Depths of Despair. The Crabclaw Caves entrance is south of the Woodcutting Guild; don't confuse it with Crabclaw Isle. Inside, go east, south through a crevice and over the stepping stones and rocks, which is the part the 18 Agility is for. The Sand Snake is level 36, hits no more than 3 and is weak to magic, so Fire Bolt"},{"t":"The Forsaken Tower and Tale of the Righteous","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Kourend III: the five Kourend quests completed","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t270-h","x":"In Arceuus, buy a rope at Regath's Wares (25 gp). Take the minecart to Lovakengj and complete The Forsaken Tower. Tell Phileas Rimor in Shayzien what you found in the archive, then in the Shayzien encampment talk to Lord Shayzien until he gives permission for the Mount Quidamortem expedition. At Mount Quidamortem, continue Tale of the Righteous until you've spoken to Duffy and Gnosi at the unstable altar, and talk to the Mountain Guide to unlock the quick route. You fight the Corrupt Lizardman in the red cave, and the lizardmen on the way poison: this is what the rope, the pickaxe, the swordfish and the rest of the antipoison are for. Leave the cave, take the minecart back to Shayzien, and r"},{"t":"The Garden of Death and The Ascent of Arceuus","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Kourend III: the five Kourend quests completed","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t271-h","x":"Walk west to Lake Molch and take the boat to the island; the diary's bluegill needs 43 Fishing and 35 Hunter, so it waits until your bird runs are further on. Continue The Garden of Death on the island and at Xeric's Shrine, then use Kharedst's memoirs to teleport to Shayzien, run south and complete The Garden of Death at the Ruins of Morra. From Shayzien, the lake's east dock is to the north-west, near the Giant Pit. The quest's dungeons block teleports, so climb out before you use the memoirs. Lizardmen on this route have a poisonous ranged attack, and lizardman brutes and mountain trolls are about too, so keep the antipoison handy. At the Ruins of Morra, go down the hole in front of the l"},{"t":"Seeds for the bird runs","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Kourend III: the five Kourend quests completed","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t272-h","x":"Drop Kharedst's memoirs and what is left of the antipoison: the book's teleports have done their diary work, Veos hands out another copy whenever you want one, and it would cost a slot for the rest of the chapter. Teleport to your house and pickpocket the two Hosidius master farmers until you have about 150 low-level seeds of one or two types, dropping the other types as they come. The next block's bird runs use them. Done when you hold the seeds. Coins: about 400,000 gp with the quest rewards · Slots: about 21/28 at the end; about 27/28 at the crane · Requirements: as each quest lists; 30 Crafting and 30 Construction for the crane Wiki references The Depths of Despair The Queen of Thieves T"},{"t":"70 Woodcutting and the log basket","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b58-h","x":"Gate in 35 Woodcutting for teaks; the Soul Wars minigame teleport. Carry in about 21/28. Exit 70 Woodcutting; the log basket; the beaten book for Elemental Workshop II; about 400,000 gp; about 23/28. Carries forward the log basket, the beaten book, the raw shark (Olaf's lyre)."},{"t":"Woodcutting to 70","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › 70 Woodcutting and the log basket","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t274-h","x":"Train Woodcutting to 70 on the teaks north of Soul Wars, which the Soul Wars minigame teleport puts you next to (2-tick teaks are faster, but that is tick manipulation, so it is optional), or on a Forestry world if you want more Forestry rewards. Drop the logs as you go. Wear your graceful and keep a little cooked swordfish for the events. There are three teaks on the island, each log worth 85 XP. The wiki lists the Forestry worlds as 388, 398, 434, 444, 487 and 510, and they are where you work on the bark below. The UIM part of this block is the log basket. It costs 5,000 anima-infused bark from Forestry events plus 300 oak and 300 willow logs: deposit the logs into the Friendly Forester's "},{"t":"Bird runs and the beaten book","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › 70 Woodcutting and the log basket","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t275-h","x":"Keep doing bird runs through this block, with the best logs your Hunter allows in the basket. On the last one, buy a tinderbox at the Varrock general store if Getting Ahead cost you yours, and walk from the barge to the Exam Centre south of the Digsite: search the bookcases in its library (the wiki puts the beaten book in the most north-eastern of the south-eastern bookcases), read the beaten book and the scroll inside it, drop the scroll and keep the book. It starts Elemental Workshop II in the next block. Reading the scroll is what later lets you search the workshop's machinery for the key, which is why you read it before dropping it. The book itself has to be in your bag at the very end o"},{"t":"Rellekka and Seers' Village: The Fremennik Trials, Dwarf Cannon and Elemental Workshop II","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b59-h","x":"Section 1.3 left The Fremennik Trials with Olaf's lyre and Manni's keg. This block finishes them, takes Dwarf Cannon to its last errand and does Elemental Workshop II, whose 7,500 Smithing XP is the third quest reward on the way to 40 Smithing. Elemental Workshop II comes before the lyre on purpose: its 7,500 Crafting XP is what lifts your Crafting to the 40 the lyre needs. Gate in 40 Crafting (reached through Elemental Workshop II's 7,500 Crafting XP, so do that step first), 25 Fletching and 40 Woodcutting for the lyre; 20 Magic, 30 Smithing and Elemental Workshop I for Elemental Workshop II; 20 Agility for the Coal Trucks log. Carry in about 23/28. Exit The Fremennik Trials and Elemental W"},{"t":"Dwarf Cannon at the Coal Trucks","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Rellekka and Seers' Village: The Fremennik Trials, Dwarf Cannon and Elemental Workshop II","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t277-h","x":"Cast Camelot Teleport and cross the log west of Seers' Village to the Coal Trucks. For Dwarf Cannon, which Captain Lawgof started for you in 1.3: repair the six bent railings on the west and south sides of his fence with your hammer and talk to him; take the dwarf remains from the top of the tower south of the gate and talk to him again; find Lollk in the cave at the south-east corner of the Fishing Guild (the north-westernmost room, the northernmost crate by the east wall) and report back; and repair the cannon with the toolkit he gives you: the pliers on the safety switch, the hook tool on the spring and the tooth tool on the gear. Finish the conversation. He now sends you to Nulodion, whi"},{"t":"Elemental Workshop II","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Rellekka and Seers' Village: The Fremennik Trials, Dwarf Cannon and Elemental Workshop II","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t278-h","x":"Drop the chisel: the workshop fills your bag with parts, and Varrock sells it again in the next block. Keep the tinderbox for the Trials' strange object later in this block, and drop it there. The quest needs two elemental bars, and each takes one elemental ore and four coal at the workshop's furnace. So make them one at a time: mine four coal at the Coal Trucks, walk to the anvil building in Seers' Village, go through the odd-looking wall and down the stairs (the battered key from Elemental Workshop I opens the way; if you no longer have it, search the bookcase in the house south-west of the bank for the battered book again and cut the key out with your knife), mine the Elemental Rock in th"},{"t":"The branch and the golden fleece","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Rellekka and Seers' Village: The Fremennik Trials, Dwarf Cannon and Elemental Workshop II","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t279-h","x":"From Seers' Village, walk to the fairy ring in McGrubor's Wood (ALS), take it to DKS and walk to Rellekka. Chop a branch from the Swaying tree east of the village entrance. Talk to Lalli, south-east of the tree, and ask about the other human; get the pet rock from Askeladden outside the longhall; pick a cabbage, a potato and an onion from the patch in the village's south-east corner; give Lalli the pet rock, put the three vegetables and the rock into his stew, and talk to him again for the golden fleece. With the four stew items you are at 28 for a minute. The branch needs 40 Woodcutting and an ordinary axe; a blessed axe won't cut it. Lalli only mentions the other human once you have spoken"},{"t":"Olaf's concert and Manni's keg","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Rellekka and Seers' Village: The Fremennik Trials, Dwarf Cannon and Elemental Workshop II","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t280-h","x":"Walk to the fairy ring in McGrubor's Wood (ALS) and take it to DKS. Walk to the bridge on the road south of the village, where the council workman stands; from its northern end, walk a little west to the narrow path that heads south into the water by the large rib cage, and use the raw shark on the strange altar south-west of Rellekka with the lyre in your inventory to enchant it. The spirit there, Fossegrimen, takes one raw shark, manta ray or sea turtle per lyre, which is why the shark from Port Piscarilius was carried this far. In the longhall, buy two beers. Challenge Manni the Reveller to a drinking contest with one of them and lose. Give the other to the council workman at the bridge s"},{"t":"Eadgar's Ruse","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b60-h","x":"This block finishes Eadgar's Ruse in one visit to the trolls. Its last hand-in is seventeen items (ten grain, five raw chickens, a log and a robe), so it uses a planned death on the Death Plateau path. Finishing it here also frees the two slots the ranarr and the pie half have held since the start of the section. Gate in Eadgar's Ruse at the parrot; 27 Herblore and the botanical pie half; a planned death on the Death Plateau path. Carry in about 19/28. Exit Eadgar's Ruse done; about 34 Herblore; about 398,000 gp; about 19/28. Carries forward nothing new. The Chronicle is destroyed by the death and bought back in Draynor at the start of the next block."},{"t":"Varrock, the Stronghold and the parrot","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Eadgar's Ruse","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t282-h","x":"Break a Chronicle card. In Varrock, buy a chisel and a tinderbox at the general store, and about 100 more chaos runes from Aubury if your stack is under 150. Do a bird run. Take the spirit tree at the Grand Exchange to the Tree Gnome Stronghold and buy a vodka and a pineapple from Heckel Funch on the Grand Tree's first floor. Take the spirit tree on to the Battlefield of Khazard and walk north to the Ardougne zoo. Talk to Parroty Pete and ask him both questions. Slice the pineapple into chunks with your knife, use the vodka on the chunks for alco-chunks, and use them on the aviary hatch on the west side of the parrot cage. Never drop the parrot: it flies away. Parroty Pete is by the northern"},{"t":"Taverley and the climb","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Eadgar's Ruse","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t283-h","x":"Cast Falador Teleport and walk to Taverley. At Jatix's buy a pestle and mortar and a vial, and fill the vial at the fountain. Chop two logs. Walk to Burthorpe, buy climbing boots from Tenzing (12 gp) and wear them, and take the secret way up to Trollheim. You are at about 27 here. Talk to Eadgar about the fake man. Run north down both flights of stairs into the Troll Stronghold and use the parrot on the rack north of the cells, then return to Eadgar. Find the troll thistle in the grass patches by his cave entrance (it is small and grass-coloured, and only one patch has it at a time), light one log and dry the thistle on the fire, and grind it with the pestle and mortar. If you can't spot the"},{"t":"Planned death: the Death Plateau path","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Eadgar's Ruse","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t284-h","x":"Go back down the secret way to Tenzing's house and walk round to the main path that the Imperial Guard watches, where the trolls on the plateau throw rocks at anyone who walks up. Take off everything except the climbing boots and let them kill you; the pile forms on the path, which you can reach again without boots. The death destroys the Chronicle. In Lumbridge, use the Burthorpe Games Room minigame teleport. In Taverley, get the dirty robe from Tegid, south-east of the herblore shop, and pick ten grain in the field south-west of him. Walk to your pile and take only the climbing boots, your coins and your rune sword. Kill five chickens at Tenzing's house for five raw chickens. Climb to Eadg"},{"t":"Garden of Tranquillity I: the farming tour","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b61-h","x":"Garden of Tranquillity sends you round the farmers of Gielinor with three crops that each take 20 to 40 minutes to grow, so this block plants all three first and fills the waiting time with Plague City. Everything the quest plants or digs with lives with the tool leprechaun, not in your bag. Gate in 25 Farming (not boostable), Creature of Fenkenstrain, Priest in Peril and The Restless Ghost for Garden of Tranquillity; the ring of charos; the fairy rings. Carry in about 20/28. Exit the delphinium, snowdrop and orchid seeds; Plague City done; about 395,000 gp; about 27/28. Carries forward the three seed types, two plant cures, a pure essence, a filled plant pot, the watering can, a fishing rod"},{"t":"Varrock and Draynor","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Garden of Tranquillity I: the farming tour","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t286-h","x":"Cast Varrock Teleport and talk to Queen Ellamaria in the palace garden to start Garden of Tranquillity. Do a bird run. Cast Lumbridge Home Teleport and walk to Draynor: buy the Chronicle back from Diango (300 gp) and wear it, and at Olivia's seed stall buy two marigold seeds, six cabbage seeds and six onion seeds, which the wiki's ironman note confirms she sells. With the ring of charos on, talk to the Wise Old Man in his house. He quizzes you: answer \"Show them a range of colours\", \"Take his generous gift\", \"It's absolutely…\", \"Put on the silly helmet and jump\", \"You of course\", \"Ask me nicely\" and \"No, especially\", and he turns the ring into a ring of charos (a). From now on, use the Charm"},{"t":"Falador and Port Sarim","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Garden of Tranquillity I: the farming tour","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t287-h","x":"Walk to the farm south of Falador. At Sarah's Farming Shop buy a watering can, a gardening trowel, a spade and two plant cures. Talk to Elstan at the allotment, take a bucket of ultracompost and the rake and seed dibber from the tool leprechaun, compost the flower patch and plant a marigold seed. Hand the leprechaun the spade and the tools you aren't using; from here on he carries the rake, dibber, spade, trowel and watering can for you, and every patch on this tour has one. Walk south to Port Sarim and buy a chocolate bar at Wydin's food store, then west past the Crafting Guild to the snape grass spawn on the coast and pick one. They are two of the three ingredients of Plague City's hangove"},{"t":"Catherby","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Garden of Tranquillity I: the farming tour","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t288-h","x":"Cast Camelot Teleport and walk to Catherby. Talk to Dantaera at the allotment: she sends you for a white tree shoot, which is the next block. At Vanessa's farming shop buy a plant pot, take the trowel from the leprechaun and fill the pot with soil at the allotment; it is for the white tree. Take the watering can too and keep it for the same job. Buy a fishing rod at Harry's Fishing Shop (5 gp); it fishes your ring out of a well in the next block. Done when you hold a filled plant pot, the watering can and the fishing rod."},{"t":"Ardougne: the cabbages and Plague City","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Garden of Tranquillity I: the farming tour","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t289-h","x":"Walk west to the fairy ring in McGrubor's Wood, picking one sprig of dwellberries from the spawn in the wood on the way, and take ring ALS to BIS, the Ardougne zoo. Stamp the barcrawl card at the Flying Horse Inn. North of the city, talk to Kragen at the allotment, compost both allotment patches and plant three cabbage seeds in each. Use an empty bucket from the leprechaun on the dairy cow beside the farm, grind the chocolate bar with your knife, and add the chocolate dust and then the snape grass to the bucket of milk: that is the hangover cure. Take the magic secateurs back from the leprechaun here. Add the dust and the grass by using one item on the other: a left-click on the chocolate ba"},{"t":"Lyra's onions, the marigolds and the willows","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Garden of Tranquillity I: the farming tour","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t290-h","x":"Take ring BIS to ALQ and walk to the allotment west of Port Phasmatys. Talk to Lyra, compost both patches and plant three onion seeds in each. While they grow, cast Falador Teleport. At the farm south of the city, pick your marigolds and give them to Elstan for the delphinium seeds. Cast Camelot Teleport, walk to ring ALS and return to ALQ. Harvest the onions, talk to Lyra for the orchid seeds and drop the onions. Hand the leprechaun everything he stores. Done when you hold the delphinium, snowdrop and orchid seeds. Coins: about 395,000 gp · Slots: about 27/28 at the end and in Ardougne · Requirements: 25 Farming for Garden of Tranquillity; none for Plague City Wiki references Garden of Tran"},{"t":"Garden of Tranquillity II: the vines, the roses and the white tree","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b62-h","x":"This block collects the last three plants and finishes the quest. It runs west to east, Burthorpe to Edgeville to Ice Mountain to Varrock, and your bag is at its fullest of the whole section just before the planting, so nothing else is added to it. Gate in the three seed types, two plant cures, an essence, a filled plant pot, the watering can, the fishing rod and the magic secateurs. Carry in about 27/28. Exit Garden of Tranquillity done; about 395,000 gp; about 20/28. Carries forward the ring of charos (a), worn in place of the ring of dueling whenever a charter or a fee is involved."},{"t":"Burthorpe: the vines","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Garden of Tranquillity II: the vines, the roses and the white tree","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t292-h","x":"Use the Burthorpe Games Room minigame teleport. Talk to Bernald in the garden behind the Toad and Chicken and use one plant cure on his vines; it doesn't work. Walk to Taverley and ask Alain at the tree patch about a stronger cure, and buy a pestle and mortar at Jatix's. Use your hammer on the essence for rune shards and the pestle and mortar on the shards for rune dust, add the dust to the second plant cure, and use the strong plant cure on the vines. Bernald gives you the vine seeds. Drop the pestle and mortar. With Alain, use the plain answers: a Charm option makes him refuse to help. The essence you mined in Ardougne is what becomes the rune dust here. Done when you hold the vine seeds."},{"t":"Edgeville: the roses","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Garden of Tranquillity II: the vines, the roses and the white tree","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t293-h","x":"Cast Camelot Teleport, walk to ring ALS and take it to DKR, east of Edgeville; walk west to the Edgeville Monastery. Talk to Brother Althric in the garden. Throw the ring of charos (a) down the well in Edgeville as he asks, take four seeds each from the red, pink and white rose bushes in the monastery garden, and fish the ring back out of the well with the fishing rod. Drop the rod. Throw the ring only when Althric asks for it. Once it is in the well, nothing but your own fishing rod gets it back; an oily or barbarian rod won't do. If the ring is destroyed some other way, Dr Fenkenstrain can be pickpocketed for a replacement. Done when you hold the three kinds of rose seed and wear the ring "},{"t":"Ice Mountain: the white tree","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Garden of Tranquillity II: the vines, the roses and the white tree","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t294-h","x":"Walk west past Barbarian Village to Ice Mountain. Use the magic secateurs on the white tree in the north of the mountain for a shoot, plant it in your filled plant pot and water it with the watering can you kept from the last leprechaun. Drop the can. Done when you hold the white tree sapling."},{"t":"Varrock: the statues and the garden","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Garden of Tranquillity II: the vines, the roses and the white tree","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t295-h","x":"Cast Varrock Teleport. Ask Queen Ellamaria about the statues for a trolley. The wiki's steps: at Lumbridge Castle use the trolley on the king's statue, push it east over the bridge and place it on the garden's eastern plinth; at Falador square use the trolley on the Saradomin statue, push it north through the gate and place it on the southern plinth. Do each without teleporting once the statue is on the trolley and without stopping for more than five minutes, or the statue resets. Walk to Lumbridge and Falador for them: this is twenty minutes of pushing. If the five minutes run out, the statue is taken back to where it stood and you need a new trolley from Ellamaria. A random event that tele"},{"t":"Edgeville and Ice Mountain: Enter the Abyss, the Wilderness tasks and Dwarf Cannon","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b63-h","x":"This block does A Soul's Bane, finishes Enter the Abyss, does three Wilderness diary tasks from one planned deathpile, clears the Stronghold of Security and completes Dwarf Cannon. Below Ice Mountain, Black Knights' Fortress and Dragon Slayer I's Oracle used to be here: the first two are Chapter 2's now, and the Oracle is in the chapter's last block, so that no map piece is carried. Gate in Enter the Abyss started; 5 Runecraft for water runes, 9 for earth runes; 31 Prayer for the monastery's upper floor; a planned death at the Edgeville Monastery. Carry in about 20/28. Exit A Soul's Bane, Enter the Abyss and Dwarf Cannon done; the Abyss and team cape diary tasks done; the Stronghold of Secur"},{"t":"A Soul's Bane and Enter the Abyss","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Edgeville and Ice Mountain: Enter the Abyss, the Wilderness tasks and Dwarf Cannon","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t297-h","x":"In Varrock, do a bird run. A Soul's Bane starts with a rope used on the rift, and you hold none now, so back at the Digsite pickpocket the workmen (25 Thieving) until one gives you a rope, about one try in eleven, and drop the brushes, buckets, gloves and spades that come with it. Then walk to the rift south-east of the Digsite for A Soul's Bane: in Anger use the rack's sword on unicorns, spear on bears, mace on giant rats and battleaxe on goblins; in Fear search the holes clockwise, never the same one twice; in Confusion find the beast that takes damage; in Hopelessness kill each creature three times, then finish the dialogue before you attack Tolna's three heads. Re-enter the rift afterwar"},{"t":"The Stronghold of Security","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Edgeville and Ice Mountain: Enter the Abyss, the Wilderness tasks and Dwarf Cannon","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t298-h","x":"Walk west towards Barbarian Village. In the Edgeville Dungeon on the way, take a Slayer task from Vannaka and squeeze through the obstacle pipe into the sewers (51 Agility), both for the diary; at the canoe station by the river, make a waka canoe for the diary (57 Woodcutting) without riding it. Enter the Stronghold of Security and clear all four floors, then perform the four emotes for the diary. The reward chests that teach the emotes only open with two-factor authentication on your account. Keep the 10,000 gp and drop the boots. The entrance is in the middle of the Barbarian Village mine. Each room has two sets of doors with a safe space between them, and the second door can ask an accoun"},{"t":"Planned death: the Edgeville Monastery","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Edgeville and Ice Mountain: Enter the Abyss, the Wilderness tasks and Dwarf Cannon","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t299-h","x":"Walk north to the Edgeville Monastery. The wiki lists its Kharid scorpion as a UIM deathpile spot: it sits on the upper floor, which Abbot Langley opens at 31 Prayer, and Holy Grail and Mountain Daughter put you well past that. Take off everything and keep trying to pick the scorpion up: each attempt stings you for 3. The death destroys the Chronicle. The sting isn't poisonous and protection prayers don't reduce it, so it is a steady, predictable way down that doesn't need your gloves off. You respawn in Lumbridge with nothing. Use the Soul Wars minigame teleport and the portal back to Edgeville, and pick up from the pile only your pickaxe, one pure essence and 50 gp. Done when your pile is "},{"t":"Three diary tasks in the Wilderness","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Edgeville and Ice Mountain: Enter the Abyss, the Wilderness tasks and Dwarf Cannon","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t300-h","x":"Walk north into the Wilderness. Buy a team cape from Richard and put it on once you are inside the Wilderness, which is what the diary counts. Mine an iron ore near the Mage of Zamorak, then have him teleport you into the Abyss. Leave through the water rift and craft the essence into water runes for the diary. Leave through the altar's portal, walk back to the pile for the second essence, and repeat through the earth rift for the earth runes task. If anything goes wrong past the ditch, all you lose is a pickaxe. The Mage of Zamorak stands by the South Wilderness mine. His teleport drains your Prayer to 0 and skulls you, and the Abyss's outer ring is a multicombat area full of aggressive crea"},{"t":"Dwarf Cannon","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Edgeville and Ice Mountain: Enter the Abyss, the Wilderness tasks and Dwarf Cannon","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t301-h","x":"Walk west to Ice Mountain and talk to Nulodion at the Dwarven Black Guard camp on its south side for the ammo mould and the instruction notes. He is in the camp's western building. Cast Camelot Teleport, cross the log to the Coal Trucks and give both to Captain Lawgof to complete Dwarf Cannon: 1 quest point and 750 Crafting XP. Done when Dwarf Cannon is complete. Coins: about 405,000 gp with the Stronghold's reward · Slots: about 20/28 · Requirements: 5 and 9 Runecraft for the two Abyss tasks; 31 Prayer for the monastery's upper floor Wiki references Enter the Abyss Stronghold of Security Abyss Wilderness Diary Dwarf Cannon Ultimate Ironman Guide/Item Management"},{"t":"Keldagrim: Forgettable Tale and 40 Smithing","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b64-h","x":"Forgettable Tale of a Drunken Dwarf is two waits of fifteen to twenty minutes with a Blast Furnace next door, so this block does the whole quest and uses the waits to smelt the last stretch to 40 Smithing, the level your gold bars need in the Al Kharid block. Gate in The Giant Dwarf, Fishing Contest, 22 Cooking and 17 Farming for Forgettable Tale; 30 Smithing for steel bars. Carry in about 22/28 with the barley malt. Exit Forgettable Tale done; 40 Smithing; about 335,000 gp; about 20/28. Carries forward nothing new."},{"t":"Lumbridge: the barley malt","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Keldagrim: Forgettable Tale and 40 Smithing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t303-h","x":"Cast Lumbridge Home Teleport. At the hops patch north of the castle, pick two barley from the plants you left in the Lumbridge block, take the seed dibber from the leprechaun and keep it, and cook the two barley into barley malt on the castle range. Keldagrim has no range, which is why the malt is made here. Keldagrim has no tool leprechaun either, which is why the dibber comes with you. Done when you hold two barley malt and the seed dibber."},{"t":"The four kelda seeds","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Keldagrim: Forgettable Tale and 40 Smithing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t304-h","x":"Use the Blast Furnace minigame teleport. Talk to Commander Veldaban at the Black Guard headquarters west of the bank to start Forgettable Tale of a Drunken Dwarf. He takes you to the Drunken Dwarf's house in East Keldagrim: buy two beers at the Laughing Miner just south of it and give him one. He wants kelda stout instead, and gives you the first kelda seed. The other three: The Rowdy Dwarf, who circles the Laughing Miner, wants a random item. Ask again after a few minutes until it is one you can make on the spot: ashes (burn a log) or the broken glass on the floor of the Drunken Dwarf's house. Gauss, in the King's Axe Inn south of the west bank: toast with him using your second beer, which "},{"t":"The hops, the furnace and the brew","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Keldagrim: Forgettable Tale and 40 Smithing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t305-h","x":"At the hops patch in front of the palace in West Keldagrim, ask Rind the gardener for permission, weed the patch with the rake he gives you and plant the seeds with your dibber. They take 15 to 20 minutes, and logging out resets the timer. Use that wait at the Blast Furnace. You should be about 39 Smithing after Sleeping Giants, The Giant Dwarf, The Forsaken Tower and Elemental Workshop II. Pay the foreman (2,500 gp per 10 minutes below 60 Smithing; the ring of charos (a) halves it) and put about 50,000 gp in the coffer, which pays the dwarves while you are in the room; you take back what is left. Buy iron ore and coal from Ordan in equal numbers, as many pairs as your free slots allow, put "},{"t":"The Red Axe tunnel","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Keldagrim: Forgettable Tale and 40 Smithing","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t306-h","x":"Drink your beer for an empty beer glass, turn the valve behind the vat's barrel and fill the glass. Give the kelda stout to the Drunken Dwarf and ask about the Red Axe. Talk to the southernmost cart conductor about the closed tunnel, then to the director of the company you joined in The Giant Dwarf, upstairs in the market, and ride the southernmost cart with both hands empty and two free slots. The director has to have the boards taken down first, which is why you visit him. If you log out in the tunnel you are put back in the city, but your progress is kept. Rooms 1, 3 and 5 are cart-track puzzles: take square stones from the box and set the junctions so the cart follows the path the room s"},{"t":"The Tithe Farm to 62 Farming and Reward Cart batch 3","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b65-h","x":"Do the Tithe Farm until 62 Farming. Its points buy the seed box and the auto-weed unlock (the herb sack needs 58 Herblore, which you don't have yet, so keep the last 250 points unspent; Chapter 2 buys the sack once your Herblore reaches 58). Watch the inventory here: carrying 15 watering cans would eat it. Buy Gricoller's can with your first 200 points (it holds 1,000 charges against a watering can's 8), use the 20x5 layout (no stamina potions needed), and keep only the seed dibber, spade, the can and the seeds while you farm; the leprechaun by the farm hands you the dibber and spade. Points come at 1 per 3 fruit plus 2 per full sack of 100 (100 fruit is 35 points), so the can, auto-weed, se"},{"t":"Knives, Ranged and Imp Catcher","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b66-h","x":"Gate in 50 Thieving and 50 Agility for the Rogues' Den; none for Imp Catcher. Carry in about 24/28. Exit Imp Catcher done; 43 Ranged; a stack of throwing knives; about 323,000 gp; about 25/28. Carries forward the knives (Temple of Ikov and Watchtower). Use the Burthorpe Games Room minigame teleport, go down into the Rogues' Den under the Toad and Chicken and buy knives from Martin Thwait, hopping worlds for more (15 bronze, 10 iron and 5 steel a world, a few hundred in total). Knives stack, so this is one of the few big buys that suits a UIM. Two later quests depend on them: the Fire Warrior in Temple of Ikov and Gorad in Watchtower are both fights this guide does with thrown knives. Wield t"},{"t":"Al Kharid: jewellery and blackjacking to 85 Thieving","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b67-h","x":"This block makes the few pieces of jewellery a UIM keeps, and then earns Chapter 2's money. Gate in 40 Smithing for gold bars; 38 Crafting for the diary coif; 27 Crafting and 27 Magic for the rings of dueling; 65 Thieving and the full rogue outfit for blackjacking. Carry in about 25/28. Exit two fresh rings of dueling and a games necklace; 85 Thieving; about 1,420,000 gp; about 27/28, which the end of the next block brings down. Carries forward the Chapter 2 money."},{"t":"Jewellery","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Al Kharid: jewellery and blackjacking to 85 Thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t310-h","x":"Jewellery doesn't stack, so make what you will use and no more. Start with the diary coif, which needs 38 Crafting (Elemental Workshop II and the Trials have given you that): kill a cow in the pen east of the river and have Ellis the tanner turn the cowhide into soft leather (1 gp), buy a needle and a thread at Dommik's Crafting Store, and craft a coif back inside the Lumbridge cow pen from the leather menu; the diary wants a coif, not a cowl, and this is a Lumbridge & Draynor medium task. Drop the coif, the needle and the thread before you buy any gems. Use the last charge of your ring of dueling to the Emir's Arena. In the Al Kharid mine, mine three gold ores and smelt them at the furnace."},{"t":"Blackjacking","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Al Kharid: jewellery and blackjacking to 85 Thieving","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t311-h","x":"Earth orbs charged at the Wilderness obelisk would pay for Chapter 2, but a UIM drops the orbs, and on the wiki's numbers stealing artefacts in Port Piscarilius can't replace them as money: each delivery pays only 500 to 1,000 coins. Blackjacking Menaphite thugs is better on both counts: about 233,000 XP an hour at 80 Thieving with wines, and the wiki puts blackjacking from 45 to 91 at about 5,000,000 coins with the full rogue outfit, roughly 0.86 gp per XP. So this step has a level target, not a coin target: blackjack Menaphite thugs from about 80 to 85 Thieving. That is about 1,270,000 XP (3,258,594 for 85 against 1,986,068 for 80), about five and a half hours, and at the wiki's rate it br"},{"t":"43 Prayer","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b68-h","x":"The usual way to 43 Prayer is to kill about 70 green dragons in the Wilderness with Water Bolt and offer the bones at the Chaos Temple (church) altar, which saves half of them. For a UIM there are two ways to do it. Gate in 23 Magic for Water Bolt (Wilderness method); none for the Ectofuntus route. Carry in about 27/28; a deathpile at the Edgeville Monastery for the first method, which is also what makes the full bag harmless. Exit 43 Prayer; the anti-dragon shield (worn) and one set of dragon bones; the hammer, chisel, knife and fire runes left behind; about 1,415,000 gp; about 24/28. Carries forward the anti-dragon shield (Watchtower, then Elvarg in Chapter 2), one set of dragon bones (Wat"},{"t":"The Wilderness, with deathpiles (faster)","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › 43 Prayer","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t313-h","x":"First cast Lumbridge Home Teleport and ask Duke Horacio in the castle for an anti-dragon shield, then use the Soul Wars minigame teleport and its portal to Edgeville. The shield can only be worn once Dragon Slayer I is started, which you did at the Champions' Guild in 1.3. It cuts a green dragon's breath by roughly four-fifths, so wear it on every trip. Each trip starts with a planned death at the Edgeville Monastery's scorpion, as in the Abyss block. From the pile, take only: the anti-dragon shield, your staff of air, the rune pouch (it holds the water runes), the chaos runes, your noted raw swordfish and the ring of dueling. Cooked food doesn't survive a deathpile, so unnote a few fish at "},{"t":"The Isle of Souls and the Ectofuntus (no Wilderness)","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › 43 Prayer","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t314-h","x":"The second way is to safespot the blue dragons in the Isle of Souls Dungeon, which is slower because they're tankier, and offer the bones at the Ectofuntus for four times their burying XP. The dungeon's entrance is on the east side of the island; the Soul Wars minigame teleport and a run north-east gets you there. The blue dragons are in the third of its four rooms, counting anti-clockwise from the entrance, and the wiki's safespot is the cove beside the adamantite rocks. The Ectofuntus needs no quest, and Ghosts Ahoy (for the ectophial) can wait for Chapter 2 if you arrive in Port Phasmatys by charter ship, which the wiki says skips the two ecto-token fee at the town's barrier. The Ectofunt"},{"t":"Ardougne and Yanille: Biohazard, Watchtower and the Observatory","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b69-h","x":"My Arm's Big Adventure used to be in this block. It needs seven unnoted buckets of supercompost carried to a troll roof on top of your kit, so it moves to Chapter 2, next to Making Friends with My Arm, which needs it. Gate in Plague City for Biohazard; 14 Magic, 15 Thieving, 25 Agility, 14 Herblore and 40 Mining for Watchtower; 40 Smithing and 43 Magic to superheat Watchtower's gold bar; the dragon bones and the anti-dragon shield. Carry in about 24/28; about 23/28 once the log basket is in the magic wardrobe with the graceful outfit. Exit Biohazard, Watchtower and Observatory Quest done; Underground Pass started; the bird snare; about 1,420,000 gp; about 23/28. Carries forward the bird snar"},{"t":"Biohazard","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Ardougne and Yanille: Biohazard, Watchtower and the Observatory","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t316-h","x":"Biohazard has you wear a gas mask, a medical gown and a priest gown top and bottom, and with the graceful outfit on, each would push a graceful piece into your bag. So cast Teleport to House first and put all six graceful pieces in the magic wardrobe, together with the log basket, which the wiki lists as magic wardrobe storage and which nothing needs before the next block. That leaves the five free slots this quest fills twice, at the Chemist and at the Dancing Donkey Inn. Then use the ring of dueling to Castle Wars, walk east to Yanille, unnote three planks at the bank and walk back to the professor in the reception room north of Castle Wars. Talk to him to start Observatory Quest, and agai"},{"t":"The Observatory","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Ardougne and Yanille: Biohazard, Watchtower and the Observatory","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t317-h","x":"Walk south to the professor in the reception room north of Castle Wars. He already has the planks: give him the bronze bar and then the molten glass, one conversation each. Check that he has taken all three items before you go underground, or you repeat the dungeon. Go down into the dungeon on the hill to the east and search the chests for the goblin kitchen key; the antipoison that respawns in the chest north-east of the stairs covers the spiders. The key is often in the south-easternmost chest but moves around, a level 31 poisonous spider can jump out of a chest, and you must read the dialogue to the end after the right chest or the key isn't given. Prod the sleeping guard at the kitchen g"},{"t":"Watchtower","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Ardougne and Yanille: Biohazard, Watchtower and the Observatory","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t318-h","x":"In Yanille's Dragon Inn, stamp the barcrawl card. At Aleck's Hunter Emporium, which also counts for the diary, buy a bird snare (6 gp) for the next block. Spotted kebbits are caught by falconry, so you need no noose wand. The shop is just east of the inn, and viewing its stock is the easy Ardougne Diary task. Do the whole of Watchtower, starting with the Watchtower Wizard on the tower's top floor (the trellis outside needs 18 Agility). The wiki's list is 20 gp, a gold bar, a tinderbox, a pickaxe, dragon bones (baby dragon bones don't work), two ropes, a guam leaf and a vial of water, a pestle and mortar, bat bones, jangerberries, a light source, a death rune (it turns up during the quest) an"},{"t":"Hunter to 46","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b70-h","x":"Bird runs should have taken you to 42 Hunter. Gate in 42 Hunter; the bird snare from Aleck's; 500 coins for Matthias's falcon. Carry in about 23/28; about 25/28 once the log basket, hammer and chisel are back and the bird snare is gone. Exit 46 Hunter; the cerulean twitch and essence impling diary tasks; about 1,420,000 gp; about 25/28. Carries forward nothing new. Start by taking back what Biohazard made you leave. Cast Teleport to House and take the log basket out of the magic wardrobe. Then walk to the fairy ring you prefer (Camelot Teleport and ALS is the standing route) and take ring DKS first: catch a cerulean twitch with the bird snare for the Fremennik diary, then drop the snare and "},{"t":"Temple of Ikov","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b71-h","x":"Winelda, deep in the temple, takes 20 unnoted limpwurt roots, which means 20 free slots at the moment you unnote them. That is a deathpile quest for a UIM, and it uses the Falador Castle pile you know from 1.3. Gate in 42 Thieving; 20 noted limpwurt roots; a thrown weapon; 51 Magic for Ardougne Teleport; a Falador Castle deathpile. Carry in from the pile only: the roots, the knives, the rune pouch, coins, a candle, the tinderbox, a knife and food. Exit Temple of Ikov done; the Kandarin diary steps; about 1,420,000 gp; about 24/28. Carries forward nothing new. Cast Camelot Teleport and buy a candle at the candle shop in Catherby, and a knife (15 gp) from the trader on the charter ship at the "},{"t":"Desert Treasure","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b72-h","x":"Gate in 53 Thieving, 50 Firemaking, 50 Magic and 10 Slayer; The Dig Site, Temple of Ikov, The Tourist Trap, Troll Stronghold, Priest in Peril and Waterfall Quest; 30 Smithing for steel bars. Carry in about 24/28. Exit Desert Treasure done (the Ancient spellbook unlocked, not switched on); about 1,420,000 gp; about 22/28. Carries forward the ring of visibility."},{"t":"Eblis's list, made in Al Kharid","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Desert Treasure","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t322-h","x":"Talk to the Archaeologist at the Bedabin Camp to start Desert Treasure and run his errand to Terry Balando at the Digsite's Exam Centre and back. Eblis, east of the Bandit Camp, then wants 12 magic logs, 6 steel bars, 6 molten glass, ashes, charcoal, a blood rune and bones. The wiki says an Ultimate Ironman can deliver these in several trips by using each item on him, so no deathpile is needed: make them in Al Kharid and carry them out in two loads. The Archaeologist is Asgarnia Smith; when you bring back Terry's translation and he offers you the book, choose \"Don't read book\" and then agree to help. Before Eblis talks about the diamonds, buy a drink from the Bandit Camp's bartender for 650 "},{"t":"The four diamonds","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Desert Treasure","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t323-h","x":"Then do the rest of the quest with the wiki's list: a silver bar, garlic powder, spice, a cake or chocolate bar, spiked boots, climbing boots, a facemask (200 gp from any Slayer master), a tinderbox and lockpicks. Buy each where its diamond needs it. The UIM notes: Blood: the silver pot made for Dessous has to be blessed by the High Priest on Entrana, and Entrana bans weapons and armour. Make it a Falador Castle deathpile trip like the earlier ones, and take only the silver pot and your coins from the pile. Dessous is best met with Protect from Melee, and his combined magic and ranged attack always hits double 5s, so keep your Hitpoints above 16. Catch a swamp lizard on the way for the Moryt"},{"t":"Varlamore and Arceuus: the last loose ends","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b73-h","x":"The chapter ends without making Paddewwa tablets or charging earth orbs with repeated Wilderness deaths. Gate in each quest's requirements. Carry in about 22/28. Exit Twilight's Promise and Scrambled! done; Bear Your Soul started; about 1,420,000 gp; about 23/28. Carries forward the damaged soul bearer (2.1). Teleport to Varrock and take the quetzal to Civitas illa Fortis; do Twilight's Promise, which needs two combat styles (magic and melee). From now on your tree runs can include the Kastori fruit tree and calquat patches. Take the quetzal to Tal Teklan and, with your 46 Construction (it also wants 36 Cooking and 35 Smithing, which you have), do Scrambled!. Twilight's Promise starts with E"},{"t":"Port Sarim: Dragon Slayer I's map and ship, and The Corsair Curse","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b74-h","x":"Chapter 2 opens on Crandor, so the chapter's last block collects Dragon Slayer I's three map pieces in one loop, joins them into a single map, and repairs the ship. Done here, the map is one slot for one block; done where the old route had it, the pieces were three slots for half the section. Gate in Dragon Slayer I started (32 quest points); 33 Magic for Telekinetic Grab or 10,000 gp for the goblin's piece. Carry in about 23/28. Exit the Crandor map; the Lady Lumbridge bought and repaired; The Corsair Curse done; about 1,415,000 gp; about 24/28. Carries forward the Crandor map and the anti-dragon shield (Elvarg, in Chapter 2's first block)."},{"t":"The Oracle's door","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Port Sarim: Dragon Slayer I's map and ship, and The Corsair Curse","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t326-h","x":"Break a Chronicle card and ask the Guildmaster in the Champions' Guild for the maze key again. Collect the four things the Dwarven Mine's magic door wants, in the order you pass them: a silk from the silk stall in Ardougne market or the Al Kharid silk trader, an unfired bowl spun at the Barbarian Village pottery wheel from a soft clay (mine the clay south-west of Varrock and wet it with a jug of water), a wizard's mind bomb from the Rising Sun Inn in Falador, and a lobster pot from Gerrant's in Port Sarim. Ask the Oracle on Ice Mountain about the map (\"I seek a piece of the map to the island of Crandor\"), go down into the Dwarven Mine and use the four items, one at a time, on the magic door "},{"t":"Melzar's Maze and Wormbrain","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Port Sarim: Dragon Slayer I's map and ship, and The Corsair Curse","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t327-h","x":"Walk to Rimmington and go through Melzar's Maze with the maze key, your rune sword, Fire Bolt and cooked swordfish: each floor's key comes from one marked monster (a rat with a longer tail, a ghost without a cape, a skeleton with a round shield, then a zombie, Melzar the Mad and a lesser demon you can safespot from beside the magenta door). Open the chest at the end for the second piece and drop the keys. The maze is the building north-west of Rimmington. The lesser demon is weak to water spells, so Water Bolt from your rune pouch works there; the wiki's ranged and magic safespot is one square to the right of the magenta door as you face north. In the Port Sarim jail, Wormbrain the goblin ha"},{"t":"The Lady Lumbridge and The Corsair Curse","p":"Chapter 1 › 1.4: 62 Farming, Desert Treasure and the Chapter 2 money › Port Sarim: Dragon Slayer I's map and ship, and The Corsair Curse","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-t328-h","x":"Buy the Lady Lumbridge from Klarense on the Port Sarim docks for 2,000 gp. Repair the hull below decks with three planks, unnoted at the nearest bank or bought new, 90 steel nails from a sawmill operator, and your hammer. Ned in Draynor captains her in Chapter 2. Klarense is on the second dock from the south. Below decks, click the hole three times. Talk to Captain Tock at the crossroads north of Port Sarim to start The Corsair Curse, sail with him from Rimmington's western dock to Corsair Cove, and follow the wiki's short investigation: it needs a spade and a tinderbox, and ends with Ithoi the Navigator (level 35) upstairs in his hut. Report back to Tock to complete it for 2 quest points. T"},{"t":"End of Chapter 1","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s10-h","x":"You finish Chapter 1 with about 1.42 million gp, a house in Hosidius with a costume room and a workshop, a rune pouch, a seed box, a log basket, 250 Tithe Farm points held back for the herb sack, farming contracts running, Desert Treasure done (the Ancient spellbook is unlocked but not switched on, so you finish on the standard spellbook), Twilight's Promise and Scrambled! behind you, and the Crandor map in your bag. Your end-of-chapter stats: Skill Level Notes Thieving 85 From blackjacking Construction 46 Crafting about 46 Quest XP; Chapter 2's glassblowing takes it past 50 Magic about 63 Prayer 43 Ranged 43+ Hunter 46 Farming 62+ Woodcutting 70 Firemaking 85+ Herblore about 34 Jungle Potio"},{"t":"Verification and sources","p":"Chapter 1","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-s11-h","x":""},{"t":"Verified against the wiki","p":"Chapter 1 › Verification and sources","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b75-h","x":"[x] Section 1.1, checked on the wiki (6 Nov 2026). Marlo's crate (25 planks, 10 oak planks, 8 bolts of cloth and 5 steel bars, all noted; 50 mithril nails; 5 house tabs and a Falador tab). Daddy's Home's 544 + 400 Construction XP, which is level 8, not 9. Torn curtains at 132 XP. Monk's Friend, Sheep Herder (now also 1,000 Hunter XP), Tribal Totem (1,775 Thieving XP, 5 swordfish) and Witch's Potion rewards. Tower of Life needs no gloves; its rewards are 1,000 Construction, 500 Crafting and 500 Thieving XP. Sea Slug's and Tribal Totem's steps were rewritten from the wiki's quick guides. The Reward Cart's coin roll (2,000–4,999, 5/25), kindling's 0.6 × Fletching level XP, Diango's prices (Chro"},{"t":"Sources","p":"Chapter 1 › Verification and sources","u":"chapter-1.html#ch1-b76-h","x":"Ultimate Ironman Mode — bank, death and Wilderness rules Ultimate Ironman Guide — choosing the mode on Tutorial Island Item Management — deathpiles, tables, drops, deathbanks Looting bag — filling and emptying rules for UIMs Reward Cart — 8,000-reward cap and Big-search Crate (Wintertodt) — free tools only if you carry none Silk merchant and silk theft timer — 60 gp haggle, 1,000-tick memory Sheep Shearer transcript — wool handed in parts Daddy's Home — items, Marlo's crate, free house, 3 November 2026 change Clue hunter garb — dig spot in Shayzien Reward pool (Tempoross) — 8,000-permit cap, rolled at collection Rogues' Den and Ultimate Ironman Guide/Minigames — empty-inventory maze, armour "},{"t":"Where Chapter 1 left you","p":"Chapter 2","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-s1-h","x":"You start with about 1.42 million gp from blackjacking to 85 Thieving, 46 Construction, about 46 Crafting, a house in Hosidius with a costume room, workshop, armour case and a magic wardrobe for the graceful outfit you wear, about 62 Agility, a rune pouch, Bones to Peaches, a seed box and log basket, 250 unspent Tithe Farm points kept for the herb sack (it needs 58 Herblore, so you buy it later in this chapter), farming contracts running, Desert Treasure done (the Ancient spellbook is unlocked but not switched on, so you are on the standard book). The coin lines below start from that 1.42 million. The extra 150,000 gp over the 1.27 million this chapter was first planned on replaces about thr"},{"t":"What changes for a UIM","p":"Chapter 2","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-s2-h","x":"No servants for planks. The wiki's UIM Construction guide is explicit: a UIM can't send a servant to the bank or the sawmill. Oak-larder and teak-plank butler sessions are replaced by Mahogany Homes contracts, which also earn the plank sack. Falador becomes your respawn. Recruitment Drive gives the Gaze of Saradomin, so from section 2.1 onwards you respawn in Falador. The Falador Castle deathpile you used three times in Chapter 1 is now next to your respawn point, which makes every later planned death a short walk. The cargo hold is narrow storage. The 18 February 2026 update removed the UIM restrictions on the Sailing cargo hold, but it only accepts certain items: salvage, cargo crates, cha"},{"t":"Chapter 2 at a glance","p":"Chapter 2","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-s3-h","x":"Section Main goals What changes for a UIM 2.1 Quests and combat Construction 62, about forty quests, Sailing to 39, Dagannoth Rex for a berserker ring, Slayer Mahogany Homes for Construction; Falador respawn and three planned deathpiles (Recruitment Drive, Entrana, the Varrock essence errand); shop-bought Myreque kit; Blast Furnace gold bars alched at the dispenser; blackjacking top-ups for money 2.2 Barbarian fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre Long skilling and Prayer block, Sepulchre for Agility Cargo hold for Sailing supplies and fish only; cut gems and stackable offcuts instead of noted items; Enlightened Journey from two Falador deathpiles; green dragons from an Edgeville"},{"t":"2.1: Quests and combat","p":"Chapter 2","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-s4-h","x":"Section 2.1 is the longest questing stretch of the guide: Dragon Slayer I, Underground Pass, Heroes' Quest, One Small Favour, Monkey Madness I, the Myreque quests and about thirty more, then the first Sailing levels, a berserker ring from Dagannoth Rex and Slayer to 40. For a UIM it opens differently. The first steps are Mahogany Homes, which gives the Construction and the plank sack a UIM needs for the rest of the game. Planned deaths are written into the blocks that need them. The first is for Recruitment Drive, which needs an empty inventory and nothing worn: the Falador Castle deathpile handles it, and after that quest your respawn is Falador, so every later planned death is a short walk"},{"t":"Mahogany Homes to the plank sack","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b1-h","x":"A UIM can't send a servant to the bank or the sawmill, so all the Construction here comes from Mahogany Homes. You start at 46 Construction from Chapter 1 and finish this block with the plank sack and 62 Construction. Gate in Chapter 1 finished; 46 Construction; on the standard spellbook; three steel bars in hand. Carry in the core kit plus a hammer, a saw, your axe, the log basket and three steel bars; about 15 free slots for a contract's planks. Exit 62 Construction and the plank sack in your core kit; the costume room's oak and teak storage tiers; about 760,000 gp; about 14/28. Carries forward the plank sack (to the end of the guide). The wiki's point values set the plan. Novice contracts"},{"t":"Take the first contract and do Novice contracts to 50","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Mahogany Homes to the plank sack","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t6-h","x":"Teleport to Falador and talk to Amy, south of Falador Park. Only your first contract has to come from her, because she signs you up; after that, Marlo in Varrock, Ellie in East Ardougne and Angelo in Hosidius hand them out too. Choose Novice, which needs 20 Construction and so is well within your 46. A contract can't be cancelled, so finish each one before taking the next. Work the Novice contracts from Hosidius, where your house already stands, and take them from Angelo. A contract can send you to any of the four towns (Falador, Varrock, East Ardougne or Hosidius), so teleport to whichever town it names. A Falador contract sends you to the south-east of the city, a Varrock one to the north-"},{"t":"Adept contracts to the plank sack","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Mahogany Homes to the plank sack","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t7-h","x":"From 50, take Adept contracts. Teak planks are the cost: the sawmill charges 500 gp per teak plank. The wiki's Mahogany Homes averages for an Adept contract are about 3,260 XP, completion bonus included, and 287.9 XP per teak plank, so about 11 planks a contract. Teak at 500 gp a plank makes gold, not time, the limit here, which is why the coin line drops across this block. From your 54 Novice points, 350 points is about 74 Adept contracts: about 840 teak planks, roughly 420,000 gp, and about 241,000 XP, which carries you from 50 to 62 by the time you own the sack. The wiki's UIM Construction guide points to the Avium Savannah teaks for this: they are far from a sawmill, which is exactly wha"},{"t":"Build the costume room's cheap storage tiers","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Mahogany Homes to the plank sack","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t8-h","x":"At 62 Construction the lower tiers of the costume room's storage furniture are in reach and cost almost nothing, so build them now instead of waiting for the full upgrade in 2.3. They give the capes, costumes, mage sets and clue rewards you pick up in 2.1 and 2.2 a home until then. Build these in the costume room of your Hosidius house with the hammer and saw. Each upgrade is built from the tier before it: Piece Construction Planks Holds Treasure chest (oak) 48 2 oak Beginner and easy clue rewards Toy box (oak) 50 2 oak Holiday toys Cape rack (oak) 54 4 oak Every cape except Capes of Accomplishment Magic wardrobe (carved oak, then teak) 51, then 60 6 oak, then 4 teak 21 mage sets, up from th"},{"t":"Combat to 50 Attack at the sand crabs","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b2-h","x":"Chapter 1 trains Attack only through quest rewards, so you start 2.1 at about 46 Attack, and Iban's staff (Underground Pass) and the ancient staff (the sandstone block) both need 50. Train it now, while your house is still in Hosidius. Defence doesn't need training here: Holy Grail (15,300 XP), Nature Spirit and The Fremennik Trials leave you at about 33, which covers the initiate armour's 20, and Dragon Slayer I's 18,650 Defence XP takes you to 40 for the green d'hide body and the rune platelegs. If you are a little short when you buy the body, finish on these crabs on the defensive style. Gate in the plank sack bought and 62 Construction; the rune sword (40 Attack); the house in Hosidius. "},{"t":"Sand crabs on the Hosidius coast","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Combat to 50 Attack at the sand crabs","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t10-h","x":"Sand crabs (level 15, 60 Hitpoints, max hit 1, one attack every 2.4 seconds) line the southern coast of Hosidius, a short walk from your house. Until something wakes them they look like harmless sandy rocks and stay off the minimap, then attack as you walk past. The wiki rates them as AFK training: stand among a cluster and they attack you. After about ten minutes they stop being aggressive; walk away until you are about a minimap's width off, come back, and they attack again. An altar near the Hosidius crabs lets you top up Prayer on the walk, though you don't need it here. Avoid Crabclaw Isle (10,000 coins and often full); the Avium Savannah crabs in Varlamore are a quieter alternative. Sk"},{"t":"Dragon Slayer I, Crandor and the first lamps","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b3-h","x":"This block finishes Dragon Slayer I, takes two Karamja medium tasks on Crandor, collects an easy diary lamp and kills the two Karamja monsters whose bones Rag and Bone Man I needs. It sits here because the quest's 18,650 Defence XP is what lifts you to 40 for the green d'hide body and the rune platelegs, because the two Karamja medium tasks on Crandor need the quest started, and because the Chronicle charges bought in it are the teleport network the rest of the chapter leans on. Gate in 32 quest points; 40 Ranged for the green d'hide body, and 40 Defence, which the quest's own Defence XP gives you; the plank sack; the Lady Lumbridge already repaired with Klarense in Chapter 1. Carry in the c"},{"t":"Collect the lamps and buy Chronicle cards","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Dragon Slayer I, Crandor and the first lamps","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t12-h","x":"Teleport to Lumbridge and claim the Lumbridge & Draynor easy diary reward from Mikasi, east of the castle courtyard, and put its lamp on Herblore straight away, so it never takes a slot. The lamp gives 2,500 XP and works only on a skill at level 30 or above, which Herblore is; it is the skill you want because the herb sack later needs 58. The Kandarin easy reward waits for Harry's pet fish at the end of 2.1, so skip Camelot for now. Run to Draynor, recruit Ned for Dragon Slayer I (his house is in the east of the village), and buy 100 teleport cards from Diango, who runs the toy store in Draynor, at 150 gp each; he stocks exactly 100, so one visit covers it. Buy the Chronicle back from him fi"},{"t":"Crandor and Elvarg","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Dragon Slayer I, Crandor and the first lamps","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t13-h","x":"Board the Lady Lumbridge at Port Sarim, talk to Ned and agree to sail, giving him the map when he asks. Kill a giant bat on the island for Rag and Bone Man I's giant bat wing: Chapter 1 started the quest with the Odd Old Man, and the wiki lists giant bats on Crandor and in the Karamja dungeon below it. Rag and Bone Man II's moss giant waits for the Varrock Sewers, because that quest starts only after Rag and Bone Man I. Walk down to Elvarg's lair, climb back up the rope to Crandor once for the diary, then return and kill Elvarg behind the anti-dragon shield. The diary task needs only that Dragon Slayer I has been started, and the wiki's quick guide has you enter the hole at the top of the vo"},{"t":"Finish Dragon Slayer I and take a Slayer task","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Dragon Slayer I, Crandor and the first lamps","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t14-h","x":"Use the Soul Wars minigame teleport and step through the portal to Edgeville, as in Chapter 1, and talk to Oziach, who lives just north-west of the village, to complete Dragon Slayer I. Buy a green d'hide body from his shop (10,140 gp; he holds two) and wear it. Then get a task from Vannaka, and do it in full; Slayer rewards later in this section start from these points. Drop the Crandor map leftovers, the head and any spare quest items before you leave Edgeville. Done when Dragon Slayer I is complete, the green d'hide body is worn and Vannaka's task is finished. Coins: about 740,000 gp · Slots: about 23/28 for Crandor, 20/28 after · Requirements: 32 quest points for Dragon Slayer I; the wik"},{"t":"Rag and Bone Man I, Below Ice Mountain and Black Knights' Fortress","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b4-h","x":"Dragon Slayer I ends in Edgeville, which is where all three of these continue. None needs more than a few slots at once in this order: Below Ice Mountain's recruits first, Black Knights' Fortress while you are in Falador for Burntof, then Rag and Bone Man I's bones from Draynor to Varrock, each dropped into a pot of vinegar the moment it falls. Chapter 1 started Rag and Bone Man I and Below Ice Mountain and left the rest here. Gate in Rag and Bone Man I and Below Ice Mountain started in Chapter 1; the giant bat wing, the monkey paw and the bread from the Dragon Slayer I block; 12 quest points for Black Knights' Fortress; 10 Mining (boostable) for Camdozaal's pillars. Carry in the core kit an"},{"t":"Edgeville and Barbarian Village: Below Ice Mountain's recruits","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Rag and Bone Man I, Below Ice Mountain and Black Knights' Fortress","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t16-h","x":"Talk to Marley by the yew trees in Edgeville, in the ruins south of the bank. The wiki says he has to come first, or the cook won't give you the sandwich recipe. He was banned from the Blue Moon Inn and the cook won't make him another sandwich, so you bring one yourself. Walk south to Barbarian Village. Talk to Checkal near the pottery oven building, then to Atlas in the Long Hall, and finish his training; take a cooked meat and a beer from the tables there. Go back to Checkal and use the Flex emote when he asks; the training cutscene is what unlocks it. Buy a bronze med helm at Peksa's Helmet Shop in the village (24 gp) for Black Knights' Fortress. Teleport to Varrock and ask the cook in th"},{"t":"Falador: Burntof, Black Knights' Fortress and Camdozaal","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Rag and Bone Man I, Below Ice Mountain and Black Knights' Fortress","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t17-h","x":"Teleport to Falador. Upstairs in the western tower of the White Knights' Castle (the second floor, in UK numbering), talk to Sir Amik Varze to start Black Knights' Fortress. Buy an iron chainbody at Wayne's Chains in the south of the city (210 gp) and pick a cabbage at the farm south of Falador; the wiki says a cabbage from Draynor Manor doesn't work, and another from the same farm replaces one you lose. In the Rising Sun Inn, give Burntof the beer from the Long Hall (Emily or Kaylee sell one for 3 gp if you drank it) and play his rock-paper-scissors game; any choice works. Wear the bronze med helm and the iron chainbody, walk to the fortress north of Falador and follow the wiki's route: the"},{"t":"Rag and Bone Man I","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Rag and Bone Man I, Below Ice Mountain and Black Knights' Fortress","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t18-h","x":"The wiki's list is eight bones, eight pots, eight jugs of vinegar, eight logs and a tinderbox. Make the pots of vinegar first, so that each bone goes into one as it drops and the eight never take more than eight slots. Every bone is a guaranteed drop from its monster, and the wiki warns that emptying a bone from its vinegar loses it, so don't click Empty on a pot you have filled: Teleport to Lumbridge and buy eight pots at the general store north of the castle (1 gp each). Walk west to Draynor. Fortunato's Wine Shop, in the marketplace just west of the bank, sells jugs of vinegar for 1 gp, and only while Rag and Bone Man I or II is running (talk to him and mention the Odd Old Man first): buy"},{"t":"Underground Pass, the gold leaf and your house tablets","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b5-h","x":"Requirements It comes here because the staff needs the 50 Attack from the crabs, because the lectern's tablets become your travel for every herb and tree run afterwards, and because Iban's staff is the weapon the Haunted Mine and Dagannoth Rex later ask for. This block covers the house furniture and the next quests. It completes Underground Pass and upgrades Iban's staff, starts Between a Rock..., builds the mahogany eagle lectern and makes about a hundred teleport-to-house tablets. It is the most expensive block of the section: 200,000 gp for the staff upgrade and 130,000 gp for the gold leaf. Check your stack before you start; if you're under about 450,000 gp, do the blackjacking top-up fi"},{"t":"Move the house and build the kitchen and menagerie","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Underground Pass, the gold leaf and your house tablets","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t20-h","x":"With the plank sack filled from your next sawmill trip, pay an estate agent to move your house to Rellekka, as you did in 1.3; it puts you next to Keldagrim and Trollheim for the next two blocks. In the house, build a menagerie with a pet house, so a cat can live there between the quests that need one instead of following you everywhere. In the kitchen, which Chapter 1's larder training already built, build the pieces the lectern block's tea needs: oak shelves 2 for the kettle, teapot and porcelain cup, a pump and drain for water and a stove to boil the kettle. The wiki's tea page says the stove has to be a built range or oven and not a firepit, and that making the tea takes 20 Cooking. Leav"},{"t":"Complete Underground Pass","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Underground Pass, the gold leaf and your house tablets","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t21-h","x":"Requirements Underground Pass: 25 Ranged. You started Underground Pass with King Lathas in 1.4. The wiki's item list is two ropes (you lose one each time you fall from the rope swing), a bow with 1 to 5 non-poisoned metal-tipped arrows (crossbows, broad arrows and ogre arrows don't work; the two ropes are the ones from Ned; Chapter 1 dropped its bow and steel arrows, so buy a shortbow and ten iron arrows at Lowe's Archery Emporium in Varrock first, and keep the bow and the spare arrows: Horror from the Deep uses up an arrow and Regicide needs a bow and arrows), and a spade; a plank is picked up inside, and the quest hands you its other items as you go. Bring a dozen pieces of food and two pr"},{"t":"Start Between a Rock... and buy the gold leaf","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Underground Pass, the gold leaf and your house tablets","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t22-h","x":"Go to Rellekka (a house tablet if you have one left from Marlo's crate, otherwise the Fremennik route you used in 1.3), leave the house through the portal and walk to the Keldagrim cave entrance (the crack between the two dwarf statues). Take the ferryman across the River Kelda and talk to Dondakan on the rock to start Between a Rock... and continue until it sends you to Rolad. Bring a few coins for the ferry (2 gp a crossing). In Keldagrim, buy one gold leaf from the Stonemason in the south-west of the city for 130,000 gp. Buy silk at the clothes stall only when the quest that uses it is next. Done when Between a Rock... has sent you to Rolad and the gold leaf is in your inventory."},{"t":"Build the lectern and make house tablets","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Underground Pass, the gold leaf and your house tablets","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t23-h","x":"Requirements The mahogany eagle lectern needs 67 Construction, boostable, two mahogany planks and the gold leaf. From a base of 62, a cup of tea made in a porcelain cup at your kitchen shelves (+2) and a crystal saw (+3) reach 67. Tea items vanish when you leave the house, so brew the tea right before you build. Chapter 1 dropped its crystal saw after The Eyes of Glouphrie, so collect a new one first: take the spirit tree from the Grand Exchange to the Tree Gnome Stronghold, ask Brimstail in his cave in the south-west of the Stronghold for a crystal saw seed, and use the seed on the singing bowl in the same cave. The wiki says that costs nothing, gives 28 charges and spends a charge only whe"},{"t":"Rolad and Falador: Recruitment Drive and Wanted!","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b6-h","x":"This block reads the dwarven lore for Between a Rock..., finishes Recruitment Drive, starts Heroes' Quest and Wanted!, and makes Falador your respawn point. It has the section's first planned death, for Recruitment Drive. Troll Romance used to open this block; it now has its own block after Animal Magnetism's magnet, where its sled materials are picked up on the way. One step moves later for a UIM: the ice gloves. The wiki gives the way into the Ice Queen's lair as the rockslide on White Wolf Mountain, which needs 50 Mining, and you have about 43. They come after the sandstone block, where Mining passes 50. Gate in Black Knights' Fortress (done two blocks ago) and Druidic Ritual; 32 quest po"},{"t":"Read the dwarven lore","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Rolad and Falador: Recruitment Drive and Wanted!","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t25-h","x":"Teleport to Falador and walk out to the dwarven camp at the Ice Mountain mine entrance, in the foothills north of the road between Falador and Barbarian Village. Talk to Rolad in the eastern house and continue Between a Rock... until Rolad asks for three book pages from the Dwarven Mine behind the camp. Click through all of his dialogue before you leave, because the pages do not appear if you cut it short. Take one from the scorpions in the south-east of the mine (level 14; it can take several kills, and the wiki suggests changing worlds if none drops it), search a mine cart along the tracks for the second and get the third by mining clay, copper, tin or iron. The pages can come in any order"},{"t":"Recruitment Drive with the Falador Castle deathpile","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Rolad and Falador: Recruitment Drive and Wanted!","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t26-h","x":"Recruitment Drive needs an empty inventory and nothing worn, and the wiki's UIM note says exactly that. With no bank, the only way to empty a bag full of quest gear is to leave it on the ground, so in the Falador Castle courtyard take off everything and die to a White Knight, as in Chapter 1. Everything lands in a deathpile there, which lasts 60 minutes of logged-in time, and that clock keeps running while you do the quest, so go straight through it. You respawn in Lumbridge with nothing; walk back to Falador, climb the stairs on the west side of White Knights' Castle to the second floor and talk to Sir Amik again, then find Sir Tiffy Cashien on his bench at the entrance to Falador Park and "},{"t":"Start Heroes' Quest and Wanted!","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Rolad and Falador: Recruitment Drive and Wanted!","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t27-h","x":"Walk to Burthorpe and start Heroes' Quest with Achietties, who waits outside the Heroes' Guild between Taverley and Burthorpe (55 quest points). She asks for three things, all handed over together: a fire feather from the Entrana firebird, a cooked lava eel and a Master Thieves' armband. The feather is too hot to pick up without ice gloves, which is why the Ice Queen is left for later and the feather waits for the ice gloves block. The lava eel is what the oily fishing rod in the next block is for. Back in Falador, start Wanted! with Sir Tiffy. The celestial ring waits for the ice gloves block: Dusuri sells it in the Mining Guild, which needs 60 Mining, and you are only about 43 here. Sir Ti"},{"t":"Shilo Village, the Shilo gems and the first leg of One Small Favour","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b7-h","x":"This block takes you from Karamja back to Draynor and Lumbridge in one sweep. It finishes Shilo Village, mines every gem the next part of the chapter needs, carries One Small Favour as far as Seth Groats and finishes Death to the Dorgeshuun. You can't get the Heroes' Quest fire feather from Entrana here, because the feather has to be picked up wearing ice gloves and the Ice Queen needs 50 Mining. Entrana moves to the block after the sandstone mining. Gate in Jungle Potion, 20 Crafting and 32 Agility for Shilo Village; 36 Agility, 25 Crafting, 18 Herblore and 30 Smithing for One Small Favour; The Lost Tribe, 23 Agility and 23 Thieving for Death to the Dorgeshuun. Carry in slots rather than it"},{"t":"Shilo Village with a light inventory","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Shilo Village, the Shilo gems and the first leg of One Small Favour","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t29-h","x":"The wiki lists a spade, a lit candle or torch, a rope, a chisel, bronze wire and three regular bones for Shilo Village, plus a tinderbox to relight the candle. Everything except the bones and the wire is sold at Jiminua's Jungle Store, north of Tai Bwo Wannai, for under 100 coins, so arrive with the slots, not the items. Smelt one bronze bar from a copper and a tin ore (the Rimmington mine on the way to Port Sarim has both; Chapter 1 carries no bars) and smith it into bronze wire (4 Smithing) before you leave the mainland. If you reach Shilo without the wire, Jiminua also sells a bronze bar and a hammer for 13 coins together, and the wiki says there is an anvil nearby, so a forgotten wire co"},{"t":"Mine and cut the gems you need","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Shilo Village, the Shilo gems and the first leg of One Small Favour","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t30-h","x":"Mine the gem rocks in Shilo Village until you have what the next blocks use, cutting as you go and dropping or selling whatever you don't need: one cut jade, for the necklace of passage you make at the Al Kharid furnace two blocks later; three cut red topaz: two become Efaritay's aid rings at the Al Kharid furnace, and the third is a spare, so keep it and sell it if nothing has used it by Sins of the Father; one cut sapphire, for the sapphire lantern in Tears of Guthix (next block); not the machete's gems: the opal machete is bought in 2.2's Tai Bwo Wannai block, a cart ride from these rocks, so you mine its three opals and trade gems then instead of carrying them for most of 2.1. The gem ro"},{"t":"One Small Favour from Shilo to Port Sarim","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Shilo Village, the Shilo gems and the first leg of One Small Favour","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t31-h","x":"Talk to Yanni Salika in the antiques shop north of the river to start One Small Favour. He wants red mahogany logs, so go through the village's south-eastern gate, climbing over the broken cart, and find the Jungle Forester just south-west of the gate, who gives you a blunt axe to have sharpened. Get to Cairn Isle on the south-west coast of Karamja, where Captain Shanks's Lady of the Waves docks south of the island (the wiki lists no Shilo departure); buy a ship ticket from him on the spot (the price is randomised between 20 and 50 gp each time you ask) and sail to Port Khazard, which is a medium Karamja diary task (the boat is one-way), then charter from Port Khazard to Port Sarim. In Port "},{"t":"Draynor, Lumbridge and the H.A.M. hideout","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Shilo Village, the Shilo gems and the first leg of One Small Favour","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t32-h","x":"In Draynor, buy the Chronicle back from Diango in the market for 300 gp: the Recruitment Drive death destroyed it, and its 100 charges come back with it. Talk to Aggie for One Small Favour: she will witness for Brian's friend only if you look into the H.A.M. hideout for her missing apprentice, Jimmy the Chisel, which is the trip you make next. Make a harralander potion (unf), add the blamish snail slime to make blamish oil (25 Herblore) and use the oil on the fishing rod to get the oily fishing rod. You need four harralanders over the chapter: this one, one for the combat potion in Nardah, one for the Guthix rest in One Small Favour and one for the Guthix balance in In Aid of the Myreque. Ta"},{"t":"Dorgesh-Kaan, Another Slice of H.A.M. and Tears of Guthix","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b8-h","x":"This block stays underground under Lumbridge and finishes three quests in the Lumbridge Swamp Caves and Dorgesh-Kaan. It ends with the train to Keldagrim and Dondakan. Gate in Death to the Dorgeshuun, The Giant Dwarf and The Dig Site; 15 Attack and 25 Prayer (not boostable); 43 quest points, 49 Firemaking, 20 Crafting and 20 Mining for Tears of Guthix; a lockpick (bought at the start of this block); the cut sapphire. Carry in Ranged or Magic for the two H.A.M. fighters, eight free slots, a pickaxe, a chisel and a tinderbox: about 16/28. Exit Another Slice of H.A.M. and Tears of Guthix done (minigame not played yet); the lit sapphire lantern; Between a Rock... advanced at Dondakan; about 320,"},{"t":"Prepare the sapphire lantern in Dorgesh-Kaan","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Dorgesh-Kaan, Another Slice of H.A.M. and Tears of Guthix","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t34-h","x":"Tears of Guthix needs a lit sapphire lantern, which is made from a bullseye lantern. Miltog in the Dorgesh-Kaan marketplace sells empty bullseye lanterns, one in stock at a time, and his shop has a lamp oil still. Buy one, fill it with lamp oil at the still (it distils swamp tar: Chapter 1 carried none, so pick one from the spawns in the Lumbridge Swamp on your way to the cave entrance) and use your cut sapphire on it. If the lantern has a lens, using the sapphire on it gives you that lens back: keep the lantern lens, because it is what swaps the sapphire back out of the lantern if a later step wants a plain bullseye lantern. If you don't get one, blow a lantern lens from a molten glass (49 "},{"t":"Another Slice of H.A.M.","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Dorgesh-Kaan, Another Slice of H.A.M. and Tears of Guthix","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t35-h","x":"Requirements Another Slice of H.A.M: 15 Attack and 25 Prayer, neither boostable, and Ranged or Magic against the two level 30 fighters, which melee can't hurt (Sigmund can be fought in any style). Another Slice of H.A.M. starts with Ur-tag in Dorgesh-Kaan. If you have no ranged weapon for the tower, a bronze crossbow and 50 bronze bolts spawn upstairs in it; leaving and re-entering the instance respawns the bolts, but it also resets the enemies. The H.A.M. mage and archer (level 30) in the goblin village tower hit at the same time and never miss. Hiding behind the crates stops their damage, and you can attack one and step back behind the crates straight away. Dismiss any follower before you "},{"t":"Tears of Guthix in the same caves","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Dorgesh-Kaan, Another Slice of H.A.M. and Tears of Guthix","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t36-h","x":"Do Tears of Guthix while you are in the Lumbridge Swamp Caves. Talk to Juna, deep in the Chasm of Tears, then use the lit sapphire lantern on a light creature to cross the chasm. The wiki calls the route from the Lumbridge Castle cellar the faster and safer one, with no wall beasts, cave crawlers or swamp gas, and it goes south over a stepping stone to the chasm. Tell Juna a story before you try for the bowl, then mine a magic stone and chisel it into a stone bowl (20 Crafting), cross back and give the bowl to Juna. One bowl is enough. You need a pickaxe and a chisel; a rope is needed only if you have never been into the caves. Don't play the minigame yet: the next block's first visit is the"},{"t":"Keldagrim and Dondakan","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Dorgesh-Kaan, Another Slice of H.A.M. and Tears of Guthix","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t37-h","x":"Take the train from Dorgesh-Kaan to Keldagrim for the diary; the wiki lists the ride as a hard Lumbridge & Draynor task, and it is free once Another Slice of H.A.M. is done. Walk to Dondakan at Dondakan's Rock and use a gold bar (or gold ore) on him to progress Between a Rock.... Leave Keldagrim with the ferry or a house tablet. Done when Dondakan has the gold bar. Coins: about 320,000 gp · Slots: about 16/28 · Requirements: Death to the Dorgeshuun, The Giant Dwarf, The Dig Site, 15 Attack and 25 Prayer for Another Slice of H.A.M.; 43 quest points, 49 Firemaking, 20 Crafting and 20 Mining for Tears of Guthix Wiki references Bullseye lantern (empty) Sapphire lantern Chest (Dorgesh-Kaan Averag"},{"t":"Varrock, Temple of the Eye, the first Tears of Guthix and the Al Kharid furnace","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b9-h","x":"A short loop between Al Kharid, Varrock, the Abyss and the Wizards' Tower. You do Temple of the Eye from its start, play the first Tears of Guthix and make the furnace items the rest of 2.1 needs, so that the desert block starts with nothing left to make. Gate in Enter the Abyss, Rune Mysteries and 10 Runecraft for Temple of the Eye; 16 Crafting and 49 Magic for the topaz rings; 18 Crafting for the silver sickle; the jade, red topaz, silver and gold bars and the ammo mould. Carry in the Barcrawl card, a bucket, runes for Lvl-2 and Lvl-3 Enchant and a pickaxe for the silver: about 19/28. Exit Temple of the Eye and The Birds and the Wasps done; the first Tears of Guthix played; the golden cann"},{"t":"Varrock diary steps and Temple of the Eye","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Varrock, Temple of the Eye, the first Tears of Guthix and the Al Kharid furnace","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t39-h","x":"Start in Al Kharid: take a ring of dueling to Emir's Arena, walk into town and talk to Wizard Persten, west of the Emir's Arena, to start Temple of the Eye. She gives you the eye amulet; Chapter 1 no longer starts the quest, so the amulet never rode in your bag. Teleport to Varrock. Ask the Apothecary to make you a strength potion for the Varrock diary (a limpwurt root, red spiders' eggs and 5 gp), then collect the Varrock easy and medium rewards and put both lamps on Herblore. Keep Varrock armour 2 in a slot: you wear it instead of the initiate hauberk while mining sandstone in the next block. Before the temple, walk north-east out of Varrock to the Jolly Boar Inn. Buy its drink for Alfred "},{"t":"The Birds and the Wasps","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Varrock, Temple of the Eye, the first Tears of Guthix and the Al Kharid furnace","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t40-h","x":"From Varrock, walk to Farmer Bea on the ridge just east of the south-east Varrock mine, inside the Digsite, and do The Birds and the Wasps, a Quest Month quest with no skill or quest requirements. Every item it uses (insect repellent, a beekeeper's or bee hunter's hat, an insect net and bird snares) comes during the quest, and one leg sends you to the Bee dealer just inside the eastern entrance of the Grand Exchange. Nothing has to be killed, but carrying the box of bees back to Bea you must shake it at the right moments: a wrong or missed shake damages you, and that damage can kill you, so keep your Hitpoints high and food in the inventory for that walk, because a death here leaves a deathp"},{"t":"The first Tears of Guthix","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Varrock, Temple of the Eye, the first Tears of Guthix and the Al Kharid furnace","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t41-h","x":"Teleport with a games necklace to Tears of Guthix and play the minigame for the first time. From now on, visit it once a week whenever you are near Lumbridge. The XP goes to your lowest-XP skill. Check which skill that is before you play: Runecraft would be useful (The Eyes of Glouphrie in Chapter 1 added 6,000 Runecraft XP and Temple of the Eye adds about 9,200 more, so you should be on about 31 already and clear The Slug Menace's 30; What Lies Below needs 35, so check the real level). At some point you need to collect at least 100 tears in one visit for the diary. Done when the first Tears of Guthix game is played."},{"t":"The Al Kharid furnace","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Varrock, Temple of the Eye, the first Tears of Guthix and the Al Kharid furnace","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t42-h","x":"Take a ring of dueling to Emir's Arena, walk into Al Kharid and do everything here in one visit: buy one pair of steel platelegs at Louie's Armoured Legs. In Aid of the Myreque, later in this section, gives a steel med helm, chainbody and platelegs to Ivan Strom. Buy only one pair, because the wiki's item list needs only one; at the furnace, make the golden cannonball for Between a Rock... from a gold bar and the ammo mould from Nulodion; make a jade necklace (a silver bar, the jade and a necklace mould) and enchant it into a necklace of passage with Lvl-2 Enchant (27 Magic, a cosmic rune and 3 air runes), then make two topaz rings (a silver bar, a red topaz and a ring mould each, from the s"},{"t":"Sandstone to the edge of 60 Mining, Enakhra's Lament and the ancient staff","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b10-h","x":"The big Mining block of 2.1. Take Ferryman Sathwood's free ferry from just south of the Al Kharid bank to the Ruins of Unkah (go through the eastern Shantay Pass at the ruins, as the wiki's route to the quarry does, with the Shantay pass you carry), walk north to the Desert Quarry and mine sandstone there until you are about 10,000 XP short of level 60 Mining, where Enakhra's Lament follows if your Crafting is 50. Buy the ancient staff from Eblis on the way out. Getting past 50 Mining here is also what opens the Ice Queen's rock slide, so the ice gloves follow this block. Gate in 35 Mining; a Shantay pass; 50 Crafting for Enakhra's Lament (otherwise it waits for the glassblowing); Desert Tre"},{"t":"Mine and drop sandstone at the Desert Quarry","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sandstone to the edge of 60 Mining, Enakhra's Lament and the ancient staff","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t44-h","x":"Mine sandstone in the quarry south of the Bandit Camp (35 Mining; the wiki notes 3-tick mining, 3t4s, as a faster but intensive option; the wiki lists 36 sandstone rocks there, each worth 30 to 60 XP); the wiki's Ruins of Unkah mine page lists no sandstone. You need to buy no sand for this. For a UIM it is even simpler: drop every sandstone as you go, so the method costs no storage and your inventory size doesn't matter. Wear Varrock armour 2 instead of the initiate hauberk, carry waterskins or wear desert robes against the heat, and keep some wines for the stretch. The heat hurts you while you walk the desert or stay in the quarry unless you carry waterskins or wear heat-proof gear, and fin"},{"t":"Enakhra's Lament","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sandstone to the edge of 60 Mining, Enakhra's Lament and the ancient staff","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t45-h","x":"If you are still below 50 Crafting, skip this quest for now and do it right after the glassblowing at the end of 2.1; you mine the granite then. Otherwise walk to Lazim, north-east of the Desert Quarry, and do Enakhra's Lament. The wiki lists: a chisel, a pickaxe, a tinderbox and a lit candle (not a black candle); one bread, pie, cake, chocolate cake, pizza or topped baked potato (not partial or burnt); normal, oak, willow and maple logs, one each, for the braziers; coal, which you can mine in the quarry at 30 Mining; soft clay, or mine clay in the quarry and wet it with a bucket of water from the Bandit Camp general store to the north; 52 kg of sandstone (32 kg for the base, then 20 kg for "},{"t":"Eblis, jackals and vultures","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sandstone to the edge of 60 Mining, Enakhra's Lament and the ancient staff","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t46-h","x":"Eblis stands south-east of the Bandit Camp. Buy the ancient staff from him: the wiki gives a one-time price of 80,000 coins after Desert Treasure I, and it needs 50 Attack and 50 Magic to wield. Its +50 melee strength makes it a good melee weapon for Slayer later in this section. The wiki advises ironmen not to alch or drop it, because a master clue step uses it and the only other sources are rare boss drops and a very rare mummy drop. Kill jackals and vultures in the desert for Rag and Bone Man II and the desert diary on your way to Nardah. Done when the ancient staff is bought and the desert bones are collected. Coins: about 230,000 gp · Slots: about 22/28 for the quest, 18/28 after · Requ"},{"t":"Nardah: the desert diary tasks and Spirits of the Elid","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b11-h","x":"Nardah is the base for one quest and a cluster of desert diary tasks. Do them in one pass so you only cross the desert once. Gate in 33 Magic, 37 Ranged, 37 Mining and 37 Thieving (boostable) for Spirits of the Elid; the standard spellbook; 40 Defence for rune platelegs; the grimy harralander; 60,800 gp for the platelegs. Carry in the stage items for each part of the quest, the ancient staff and rune sword for the golems, the necklace of passage and enough food not to die: about 22/28. Exit Spirits of the Elid and the Nardah diary tasks done; the combat potion made; the rune platelegs carried; about 165,000 gp. Carries forward the rune platelegs (worn after the Altar of Guthix), the waterski"},{"t":"Nardah on arrival","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Nardah: the desert diary tasks and Spirits of the Elid","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t48-h","x":"On the way in, kill a goat north-west of Nardah for its horn and grind it to goat horn dust. In town: leave the mayor's balcony for later: burning a yew log there is a Desert hard diary task, which Chapter 3 claims; have Zahur clean your grimy harralander for the diary: it costs 200 gp; buy rune platelegs (or a plateskirt) at Seddu's Adventurer's Store for 60,800 coins. They are your legs from the Altar of Guthix onwards, including Dagannoth Rex later in 2.1. Carry them until the initiate armour has done its job at the altar, then wear them. Done when the goat horn is ground, the harralander is cleaned and the rune platelegs are bought."},{"t":"Spirits of the Elid","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Nardah: the desert diary tasks and Spirits of the Elid","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t49-h","x":"Talk to Awusah the Mayor to start Spirits of the Elid. You must be on the standard spellbook. The wiki splits the items by stage: start: Telekinetic Grab runes for the ancestral key, a needle and one or two thread to repair the robes of Elidinis. The costume needle does not work for this quest. The robes are the two torn pieces in the cupboards of the building with Shiratti the Custodian, and the ancestral key comes from casting Telekinetic Grab at the enclosed area. Ghaslor the Elder, in the house just north of the mayor's, gives you a ballad; the wiki says not to drop it, because you need it at the golem door and to finish; golems: the ancestral key, the ballad, the robes of Elidinis (worn"},{"t":"A money check before Sophanem","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Nardah: the desert diary tasks and Spirits of the Elid","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t50-h","x":"After the ancient staff and the platelegs your stack is about 165,000 gp, because Chapter 1 ended about 150,000 gp above the 1.27 million this chapter was first planned on. That covers the roughly 50,000 gp of small purchases up to the Yanille stop (Olaf's Quest pays 20,000 gp back), so this block no longer needs the hour of blackjacking it used to (a quarter hour of it now sits in the Yanille top-up): only if your stack is below about 100,000 gp here, take the carpet to Pollnivneach and blackjack Menaphite thugs, as in Chapter 1, at roughly 200,000 gp an hour. The big top-up waits until the Yanille block, which spends about 835,000 gp. Done when you hold about 165,000 gp. Coins: about 165,0"},{"t":"Sophanem: Icthlarin's Little Helper, Pyramid Plunder and the start of Contact!","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b12-h","x":"This block needs your cat, so it starts with a trip home. Gate in Gertrude's Cat and the cat; Prince Ali Rescue for Contact!; 31 Prayer and the fully stamped Barcrawl card for Scorpion Catcher (the wiki marks a completed Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl as required to start, and you hand the card in during this block); a full waterskin. Carry in the cat and the quest's item list, a light source, antipoisons and food for a level 91 fight: about 21/28. Treat it as a no-death block. Exit Icthlarin's Little Helper and the Pyramid Plunder diary tasks done; Contact! stopped at Osman; Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl complete and Scorpion Catcher started; the cat back in the menagerie; about 165,000 gp. Carrie"},{"t":"Fetch the cat","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sophanem: Icthlarin's Little Helper, Pyramid Plunder and the start of Contact!","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t52-h","x":"Break a house tablet, pick up your cat from the pet house in the menagerie and come back to the desert. Any of the regular cat, overgrown cat, hellcat or kitten works, and it needs no food. Use a Nardah teleport scroll, fairy ring DLQ or the Pollnivneach carpet (then walk south to Nardah), whichever is closer to where you left off, and find the Wanderer in the camp west of the Agility Pyramid, where Icthlarin's Little Helper starts. The cat matters here: the wiki says you lose it if you die during a flashback or to the guardian, or if you answer the Sphinx's riddle wrongly, and you then need a new one from Gertrude. Treat this as a no-death block. A death in the pyramid leaves your pile wher"},{"t":"Icthlarin's Little Helper","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sophanem: Icthlarin's Little Helper, Pyramid Plunder and the start of Contact!","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t53-h","x":"Icthlarin's Little Helper needs Gertrude's Cat and the ability to beat a level 91 enemy. The wiki lists: the cat; a tinderbox and a willow log (cut one from a willow tree at 30 Woodcutting); a bag of salt, or an empty bucket to make a pile of salt in Sophanem (the wiki also lets you collect a bucket of salt water at the pond west of the Wanderer); a bucket of sap (use a knife on an evergreen or pointy common tree, such as the one outside Lumbridge Castle, with an empty bucket in your inventory); a full waterskin to give away (cut a cactus to fill it, as in the diary task); one linen, which Raetul in Sophanem sells for 30 coins, but only once you have spoken to the Embalmer. Hand the Embalmer"},{"t":"Pyramid Plunder for the diary","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sophanem: Icthlarin's Little Helper, Pyramid Plunder and the start of Contact!","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t54-h","x":"Right after the quest, enter Pyramid Plunder for the desert diary. The pyramid is in Sophanem, behind one of four anonymous doors; only one door is correct, it changes every 25 minutes, and a failed attempt stuns you and deals 1 to 4 damage. Both easy tasks need Icthlarin's Little Helper started, and the sarcophagus task needs 21 Thieving. Open the sarcophagus in the first room (it uses Strength, not Thieving) for the first easy task, and keep one artefact from the pyramid to sell to Simon Templeton, at the Agility Pyramid just north-east of Sophanem, for the other. You don't need to stay longer than that. Done when both Pyramid Plunder easy tasks are done."},{"t":"Start Contact! and Scorpion Catcher","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sophanem: Icthlarin's Little Helper, Pyramid Plunder and the start of Contact!","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t55-h","x":"Start Contact! with the High Priest in the Great Temple in the south-west of Sophanem and continue until it sends you to Osman in Al Kharid, outside the palace; stop there. The route goes through Jex, in the temple at the north-eastern corner of the city, then down the trapdoor into the Sophanem Dungeon, to Kaleef's corpse and to Maisa across a chasm. Turn auto-retaliate off in there, because retaliating at the wrong moment can set off a trap, and use Evade on floor traps and Disable on wall traps. A scarab trap puts your light out and drops you to the bottom level, and the wrong ladder leads to a much more dangerous multicombat level. Carry teleport jewellery for the way out. Then leave the"},{"t":"The ice gloves and the Entrana fire feather","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b13-h","x":"These are two Heroes' Quest steps that wait until here. With more than 50 Mining they fit here, between Seers' Village and Taverley. The order is fixed by the feather: it is too hot to pick up without ice gloves, so the Ice Queen comes before Entrana, and the celestial ring comes last because the Entrana loop ends in Falador, where the Mining Guild is. You don't hand the feather in yet: Achietties wants it together with the cooked lava eel and the armband, so it stays in your inventory until the Heroes' Quest block that ends in Burthorpe. Gate in 50 Mining (boostable) and a pickaxe; Heroes' Quest started; respawn in Falador; 59 Mining or more and 2,000 stardust for the celestial ring. Carry "},{"t":"The Ice Queen","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › The ice gloves and the Entrana fire feather","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t57-h","x":"Requirements a pickaxe and 50 Mining, boostable, and that no one else can mine it for you. Walk from Catherby to the north side of White Wolf Mountain (or take the gnome glider to Sindarpos) and mine the rock slide north-west of the glider. At 59 Mining or more you need no boost for the slide. Past it, the lair holds level 53 ice giants, level 57 ice warriors and level 61 ice spiders, which is why the wiki's route below is worth following exactly. The wiki's route: Past the rock slide, go down the southernmost ladder. Take the south-west tunnel and climb the ladder at the end, killing ice giants for Rag and Bone Man II on that floor. The bone is called ice giant ribs, and each kill has a one"},{"t":"Entrana with a Falador deathpile","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › The ice gloves and the Entrana fire feather","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t58-h","x":"Entrana bans weapons and armour, and the wiki's allowed list includes ice gloves, so keep only the gloves. The monks on the Port Sarim dock search you before the boat sails: the wiki says most equippable weapons and most armour with attack or defence bonuses are banned, while runes, ammunition other than darts and plain clothing are fine. A UIM can't bank the rest, so use the Falador respawn you set during Recruitment Drive: Teleport to Falador. In the Falador Castle courtyard, take off everything and die to a White Knight, as in Recruitment Drive. You respawn in Falador with nothing, and your hour of logged-in time starts the moment you die. Walk back to the pile and pick up only the ice gl"},{"t":"Taverley: the Altar of Guthix and the Taverley Dungeon multiquest","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b14-h","x":"You come back from Entrana into Falador still in full initiate, which is exactly what the first stop needs. Then one trip through Taverley Dungeon advances four quests: Wanted!, Heroes' Quest, Scorpion Catcher and Bear Your Soul. They follow the dungeon's layout: the Black Knights' base is in the first half, before the dusty key's gate, and the lava eel, the scorpion and Cerberus' Lair are past it, so you walk in once and out once. Many monsters down there are poisonous, so don't let your Hitpoints run low waiting for a poison to wear off. A Tail of Two Cats starts after Olaf's Quest, because the cat lives in your Rellekka menagerie, next to Olaf, and a death in Taverley Dungeon is safer wit"},{"t":"The Altar of Guthix in full initiate","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Taverley: the Altar of Guthix and the Taverley Dungeon multiquest","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t60-h","x":"Walk to the stone circle in Taverley and pray at the Altar of Guthix while wearing full initiate, for the medium Falador diary. The task says full Initiate armour, so check that every piece is on before you click. That was the set's last job: put on the rune platelegs and drop the initiate pieces, which frees the slots before the dungeon. Carry into the dungeon: the oily fishing rod and the fishing bait, the scorpion cage, the commorb, the damaged soul bearer from Chapter 1, an anti-dragon shield, the rune sword, food and prayer potions, and your usual teleports. The commorb is for Wanted!; the wiki says Sir Tiffy lends you his if you lose it. Done when the altar task is done, the rune plate"},{"t":"The Black Knights' base: Wanted! and the dusty key","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Taverley: the Altar of Guthix and the Taverley Dungeon multiquest","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t61-h","x":"The wiki's route to the Black Knights goes north, then east, then south past the magic axes, poison scorpions and chaos dwarves (don't cross the bridge), then past the hill giants into the Black Knights' rooms. Black Knights are aggressive below 67 combat. The base is in the first half of the dungeon, so it needs no dusty key. If a crowd gathers, the wiki says you can hop worlds from the north-western corner of their room. For Wanted!, talk to Lord Daquarius in the south-west room first. Then kill a level 33 Black Knight in that room without leaving or being interrupted, so let his dialogue run to the end first; a kill made before talking to him, or after leaving the room, doesn't count. Daq"},{"t":"Past the dusty key gate","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Taverley: the Altar of Guthix and the Taverley Dungeon multiquest","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t62-h","x":"Use the dusty key on the gate between the lesser demons and the blue dragons. Left-click the gate with the key in your pack. Beyond it the dungeon gets harder, with Cerberus (level 318) deep in the second half. On the far side: fish a lava eel with the oily fishing rod and bait for Heroes' Quest (53 Fishing). Don't cook it yet; you cook it in Edgeville later in 2.1, and until then keep it on you rather than in a deathpile: the wiki doesn't say whether raw fish survives one, so this guide never relies on it. Guard the rod as well: the wiki warns that a death while holding it will probably cost you the rod, and as Gerrant may not give more blamish snail slime, the fallback is a Myre blamish sn"},{"t":"Cerberus' Lair: Bear Your Soul","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Taverley: the Altar of Guthix and the Taverley Dungeon multiquest","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t63-h","x":"Carry on to Cerberus' Lair. The Key Master is inside the lair, whose entrance is a cave in the east wall of the hellhound area. The wiki says entering the lair no longer needs a hellhound Slayer task, so you can talk to him without one. Give him the damaged soul bearer and he repairs it into a soul bearer, which completes Bear Your Soul. If you lose the damaged soul bearer, the wiki says you can dig up another in the crypt of the Arceuus church, east of the library, with a spade. Keep Protect from Melee up near the hellhounds. If you die here you respawn in Falador, and the pile is past the gate; get a second dusty key from Velrak on the way back. Done when Bear Your Soul is complete. Coins:"},{"t":"Kourend, the hourlies and Olaf's Quest","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b15-h","x":"A short block that ends at your house, ready for the cat quests. It comes first because Olaf's Quest finishes in Rellekka, where your house and the cat's menagerie are. Gate in The Fremennik Trials, 40 Firemaking and 50 Woodcutting for Olaf's Quest; 22 Agility and 20 Thieving for The Writing's on the Wall; the dramen staff for fairy rings AJR and DJR; a limpwurt root and a tarromin potion (unf) if the Kourend easy diary is still open. Carry in an axe, a tinderbox, a spade and ropes, with four free slots: about 20/28. Exit The Writing's on the Wall and Olaf's Quest done; hourlies run; the Kourend easy lamp used if it was open; about 185,000 gp; the cat collected for the next block. Carries fo"},{"t":"Lovakengj and the Kourend easy diary","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Kourend, the hourlies and Olaf's Quest","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t65-h","x":"Chapter 1 dropped Kharedst's memoirs, so use the fairy rings: break a house tablet to Rellekka, walk to fairy ring AJR at the Fremennik Slayer Cave south-east of the town, take it to DJR at the Chasm of Fire, and walk to Lovakengj. If you didn't finish the Kourend & Kebos easy diary in Chapter 1, make the strength potion in the Lovakengj pub now, from a tarromin potion (unf) and a limpwurt root. Then walk to the castle, collect the reward and put the lamp on Herblore. Elise gives it, in the castle courtyard south-east of the statue of King Rada I, and the strength potion task needs 12 Herblore. Stay on the standard spellbook and do your hourlies (farming contracts and bird houses) if you hav"},{"t":"The Writing's on the Wall","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Kourend, the hourlies and Olaf's Quest","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t66-h","x":"Requirements The Writing's on the Wall: 22 Agility and 20 Thieving, neither boostable, and no items; the wiki recommends a few free slots and stamina or energy potions. While you are in Kourend, do The Writing's on the Wall, one of the Quest Month quests (November 2026). It starts with Betty outside the north-easternmost house in Land's End and moves through Hosidius, Port Piscarilius, the Shayzien Encampment and an island in the River Hos. There is nothing to kill, but at Port Piscarilius Sergeant Hudson arrests you and Betty, a guard who catches you sends you back to the cell, you can't teleport out of the cell, and near the end a hooded killer knocks you out: none of it is a death. Reward"},{"t":"Olaf's Quest","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Kourend, the hourlies and Olaf's Quest","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t67-h","x":"Requirements Olaf's Quest: The Fremennik Trials, 40 Firemaking and 50 Woodcutting. Break a house tablet (the house is in Rellekka since the Underground Pass block) and do Olaf's Quest. The wiki lists an axe, a tinderbox, a spade and six ropes, which you can get during the quest. Olaf stands north-east of Rellekka, near the entrance to the snow hunting area. After the carvings he has you light damp planks on embers and gives you Sven's last map: read it, and dig beside the windswept tree to fall into the Brine Rat Cavern; it asks for four free slots if you bring your ropes and ten if you don't. Cut windswept logs from the windswept tree on the hill east of Rellekka and give them to Olaf. He m"},{"t":"Burthorpe and Varrock: the cat quests, Wanted!'s essence and Horvik's steel bars","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b16-h","x":"The first half of this block uses the cat; the second half is a planned death. Wanted! needs 20 unnoted essence in your inventory at once, and One Small Favour needs three steel bars for Horvik, which a UIM has to mine and smelt. Neither fits in a full inventory, so you do both from an empty one while your gear waits in a Falador deathpile. Gate in Gertrude's Cat and Icthlarin's Little Helper; the catspeak amulet and five death runes; Keldagrim access and The Giant Dwarf started for Ratcatchers; 30 Mining and 30 Smithing; respawn in Falador. Carry in the cat for the first half; for the planned death, only a pickaxe and a few thousand coins (25/28 at most). Exit A Tail of Two Cats and Ratcatc"},{"t":"A Tail of Two Cats and the start of Ratcatchers","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Burthorpe and Varrock: the cat quests, Wanted!'s essence and Horvik's steel bars","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t69-h","x":"From your house in Rellekka, with the cat following, take a games necklace to Burthorpe. Wear the catspeak amulet and talk to Unferth to start A Tail of Two Cats, then pay Hild five death runes to enchant the amulet into a catspeak amulet (e), which finds Bob. You must have a cat or kitten with you throughout the quest (it can stay in your inventory). Hild lives in the house north-east of Unferth's, and the five death runes are the whole fee. The amulet shows where Bob is, but he roams Misthalin, Asgarnia and the northern Kharidian Desert and can't enter the Wilderness or pass the Shantay Pass. Use the chronicle to the Champions' Guild and run to Varrock. Bob often hides in the anvil buildin"},{"t":"The planned death: essence for Wanted! and steel bars for Horvik","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Burthorpe and Varrock: the cat quests, Wanted!'s essence and Horvik's steel bars","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t70-h","x":"Teleport to Falador. In the Falador Castle courtyard, take off everything and die to a White Knight, as before. You respawn in Falador with nothing, and the pile's hour of logged-in time starts at that moment. From the pile, take only: your pickaxe (wield it); a few thousand coins. The death destroys the Chronicle, as every death does; you buy it back in Draynor on the way to Ernest the Chicken. You carry no nature runes, so don't plan on Superheat. Smelting at a furnace works: steel bars don't fail, unlike iron bars. In the Dwarven Mine under Falador, mine five iron ore and eleven coal, then smelt five steel bars at the Falador furnace (30 Smithing, boostable). A steel bar takes one iron or"},{"t":"Wanted!'s chase, Canifis and Ernest the Chicken","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b17-h","x":"Wanted! finishes with a chase that sends you around the map, and a UIM can't stop at a bank between legs. Carry your full set of teleports for the whole chase, and the Dorgesh-Kaan sphere from the Lumbridge block. Falador Teleport (or a tablet) brings you back to Falador between legs, and the Morytania blocks after it travel by Varrock Teleport and the fairy rings, not by the Arceuus teleports, which need soul runes you cannot buy yet. The chase moves you around by force: leg two throws you to Camelot and leg four sends you to Falador. Gate in the commorb and the Dorgesh-Kaan sphere; 40 Agility for the rooftops; earmuffs and 15 Slayer for banshees; the wolfbane dagger from Drezel; a cowhide;"},{"t":"Canifis and the chase","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Wanted!'s chase, Canifis and Ernest the Chicken","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t72-h","x":"Go to Canifis, where the Mage of Zamorak's tip pointed, on foot through the Paterdomus temple east of Varrock: Drezel, in the dungeon below it, gives you a new wolfbane dagger for the werewolf task below (the wiki says he replaces a lost one), since Chapter 1 didn't carry it. Use the commorb's scan option around the town until Solus appears, speaks briefly and vanishes. Savant explains the scan; if you skip his conversation, step out of town to the fairy ring to trigger it again. The wiki gives seven chase locations: the third is the Champions' Guild, the fifth is the Dorgesh-Kaan mine (use the sphere; the wiki lists a light source for this leg, and the lit sapphire lantern you carry from Do"},{"t":"Ernest the Chicken and the start of Animal Magnetism","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Wanted!'s chase, Canifis and Ernest the Chicken","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t73-h","x":"Teleport to Falador and put on your ring of charos (a): Ghosts Ahoy, the Ratcatchers snake charmer and several charters are cheaper with it. If you have lost it, pickpocket Dr Fenkenstrain at Fenkenstrain's Castle (25 Thieving) for another. Then teleport to Lumbridge, run west to Draynor, buy the Chronicle back from Diango in the market, and run north to Draynor Manor and do Ernest the Chicken, which Veronica starts at the gate south of the manor. Everything it needs is inside the manor, including the spade. The fish food, poison and key come from inside, and the oil can sits behind the basement lever puzzle; Telekinetic Grab can't take it. The fish food is in a blue box on the first floor, "},{"t":"Morytania: ecto-tokens, Ghosts Ahoy, desert lizards and the Myreque steel kit","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b18-h","x":"The ecto-tokens are the slot-heavy part of this block, so the Myreque steel kit waits until the tokens are made. Gate in Priest in Peril and The Restless Ghost; 22 Slayer and ice coolers; The Fremennik Trials for Skulgrimen's shop; the ghostspeak amulet; a silver bar for the dust. Carry in four bones, four pots and four buckets per Ectofuntus batch (about 26/28), then the steel kit (about 26/28). Exit about 40 ecto-tokens; Ghosts Ahoy started; the desert lizard tasks and A Shell of a Friend done; the six steel weapons and the med helm bought; about 170,000 gp. Carries forward the ecto-tokens, the silver dust (Guthix balance), the steel kit (both Myreque quests)."},{"t":"Bones and the Ectofuntus in two batches","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Morytania: ecto-tokens, Ghosts Ahoy, desert lizards and the Myreque steel kit","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t75-h","x":"Teleport to Varrock and take fairy ring DKR, by the Grand Exchange, to ALQ, in the Haunted Woods, from where Alice's farm is a short run north. For Animal Magnetism, talk to Alice and her husband Malcolm at their farm with the ghostspeak amulet itself on (the wiki says Morytania legs don't count for the quest's ghostspeak amulet). Go back and forth between the two until Alice mentions the witch who changes ghostspeak amulets, who is the Old Crone; stop there, because you visit her for both quests in the next block. You need about 40 ecto-tokens with the ring of charos (a) worn: Animal Magnetism takes 20 for two undead chickens, and the wiki lists 31 tokens for Ghosts Ahoy, 16 with the ring. "},{"t":"Start Ghosts Ahoy","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Morytania: ecto-tokens, Ghosts Ahoy, desert lizards and the Myreque steel kit","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t76-h","x":"In Port Phasmatys, start Ghosts Ahoy with Velorina and continue until it sends you to the Old Crone. Stop there for now. You pay 2 tokens at the energy barrier to get into town, and the wiki says to keep enough tokens to travel in and out. The nearest bank outside is in Canifis, no use to a UIM, so leave the 20 for the chickens alone. If you took Chapter 1's Isle of Souls option and finished Ghosts Ahoy there, skip its steps here and in the Ectophial block; Animal Magnetism still needs its 20 ecto-tokens. Done when Velorina has sent you to the Old Crone."},{"t":"Desert lizards","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Morytania: ecto-tokens, Ghosts Ahoy, desert lizards and the Myreque steel kit","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t77-h","x":"Take fairy ring ALQ, in the Haunted Woods west of Port Phasmatys, to DLQ, which the wiki lists as the quick way in; it lands north of Nardah, so you still walk to the lizards. The wiki puts them south-east of the Shantay Pass across the River Elid and west of the Ruins of Ullek, so you walk the rest. Desert heat applies there; the spot without it is the edge of Uzer Oasis, south-west of the tea shop. Kill a level 24 desert lizard for the desert diary and a level 42 one for Rag and Bone Man II, finishing each with an ice cooler (22 Slayer). The cooler only works on a lizard below 5 Hitpoints; used earlier it is consumed and does nothing, so wait until the lizard is nearly dead and bring spare"},{"t":"A Shell of a Friend","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Morytania: ecto-tokens, Ghosts Ahoy, desert lizards and the Myreque steel kit","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t78-h","x":"Requirements A Shell of a Friend: Priest in Peril, 16 Herblore and 15 Construction, and an axe: a bronze axe spawns near the fairy ring, so you don't need to carry one. Take fairy ring ALQ, east of Canifis, and cross the stepping stone south-east of the small island just west of it to start A Shell of a Friend with the Juvenile Snail, a short Quest Month quest. The Haunted Woods have aggressive feral vampyres, you kill a leech (level 39), and the last fight is against SnelmLover500 (level 50); the snail can't die. Your current combat gear and a little food are enough. Rewards 2 quest points, 2,500 Herblore XP, 2,500 Construction XP and a pink snelm; drop the snelm and the axe. Done when A Sh"},{"t":"The Myreque steel kit","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Morytania: ecto-tokens, Ghosts Ahoy, desert lizards and the Myreque steel kit","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t79-h","x":"In Search of the Myreque needs a steel longsword, two steel shortswords, a steel mace, a steel warhammer and a steel dagger in your inventory at the same time: Cyreg Paddlehorn in Mort'ton won't continue the dialogue unless all six are there. Buy them from shops rather than smithing them, and only now, after the ecto-token batches: break a house tablet: your house is in Rellekka, and Skulgrimen's Battle Gear there sells steel warhammers; from Rellekka, walk to fairy ring AJR at the Fremennik Slayer Cave and take it to DJR at the Chasm of Fire, then walk to Shayzien. Briget's sells everything except the warhammer, which is why you collect it in Rellekka first. Briget's Weapons sells steel swo"},{"t":"In Search of the Myreque","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b19-h","x":"You arrive in Canifis with the steel kit. The cat is already in your menagerie, which matters for the next block: the wiki says pets aren't allowed in the Ivan Strom escort instance. Gate in Nature Spirit, Priest in Peril and The Restless Ghost; 25 Agility (boostable); the six steel weapons; the silver sickle from the Al Kharid furnace; 50 Agility for fairy ring BIP; the cat left at home. Carry in the weapons, the silver sickle, 17 planks in the plank sack and the nail stack, with the druid pouch and its fungus collected at the grotto: about 25/28. Exit In Search of the Myreque done; the DLS fairy ring open; Ghouls and bats for Rag and Bone Man II; about 165,000 gp; about 18/28. Carries forw"},{"t":"The Nature Grotto: the druid pouch and the blessed sickle","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › In Search of the Myreque","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t81-h","x":"Chapter 1 left the druid pouch and its silver sickle behind after Nature Spirit, and this quest's ghasts drain the pouch on the walk to the Myreque. Take fairy ring BIP, which the wiki says needs 50 Agility and lands you on the small island west of the grotto, and jump the broken bridge to the cave. Pick up a druid pouch: the wiki says a lost one can be reclaimed in the grotto, where one respawns near the pool. Bless the silver sickle you cast in Al Kharid; the wiki's silver sickle (b) page says you use it on the altar of nature in the grotto. Outside, cast Bloom with the blessed sickle next to rotting logs, pick the Mort myre fungi and fill the pouch. Each fill takes three blossomed items a"},{"t":"Ghouls, bats and Mort'ton shopping","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › In Search of the Myreque","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t82-h","x":"Kill ghouls west of Canifis, by the gravestones near fairy ring CKS, for Rag and Bone Man II and the Morytania diary, and bats just outside the Slayer Tower entrance for Rag and Bone Man II. Then talk to Vanstrom Klause in the north-east corner of the Hair of the Dog in Canifis to start In Search of the Myreque. He sends you to deliver weapons and mentions a boatman in Mort'ton. Each ghoul and bat kill has a one in four chance of dropping its bone (a bat wing, for bats). Shades of Mort'ton, done in Chapter 1, lets you buy planks and a hammer in Mort'ton. The swamp paste for In Aid of the Myreque's bank repair is the one item nothing earlier in the guide supplies, so buy one at the Razmire Bu"},{"t":"The boat, the bridge and the Myreque","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › In Search of the Myreque","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t83-h","x":"Find Cyreg Paddlehorn by his boat at the eastern edge of Mort'ton and persuade him. The wiki gives the replies in order: \"Well, I guess they'll just die without weapons...\", \"Resourceful enough to get their own steel weapons?\", \"If you don't tell me, their deaths are on your head!\" and \"What kind of man are you to say that you don't care?\". Pick them in exactly that order, with the six weapons in your inventory. Show him the druid pouch and hand over the planks he asks for. He refuses to take you himself and rents the boat only if the pouch holds at least 5 charges. He takes 3 planks for his boat, and the other 3 stay in your bag for the Hollows bridge (the wiki's item list for the whole que"},{"t":"In Aid of the Myreque to the rod mould","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b20-h","x":"Burgh de Rott has no working bank until you repair it, and for a UIM the bank itself changes little. What matters is that the general store's stock is 23 items that you don't need to carry all at once. This block goes as far as the rod mould; the Rod of Ivandis waits for 2.2. Gate in In Search of the Myreque; 25 Agility and 7 Magic (boostable); 25 Crafting and 15 Mining (not boostable); two steel bars and one coal; the steel chainbody, platelegs and med helm; one soft clay; 22 Herblore for the Guthix balance. Carry in one food, a hammer, a pickaxe, a spade, one to five buckets, the planks and nails, a tinderbox and five free slots: about 25/28. Exit Burgh de Rott's store, bank and furnace re"},{"t":"Into Burgh de Rott","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › In Aid of the Myreque to the rod mould","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t85-h","x":"Talk to Veliaf in the Myreque Hideout (fairy ring DLS) to start In Aid of the Myreque. For the first entry the wiki lists one food (you use it on the open chest at the gate), a hammer, a pickaxe, a spade, one to five buckets, the planks and the nails, plus six free slots. Florin at the gate refuses you until you use the food on the open chest in front of it; after that the shades stop attacking you. Mine the rubble in the bar cellar, bucket it and empty the buckets on the pile outside the bar. Anything you drop in the cellar vanishes when you leave, and mined rubble comes back if you didn't remove it, so don't leave until it is cleared. Repair the general store's roof and wall with 3 planks "},{"t":"Stocking Aurel's store","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › In Aid of the Myreque to the rod mould","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t86-h","x":"Aurel wants 10 bronze axes, 3 tinderboxes and either 10 mackerel or 10 snail meats, raw or cooked. The items can't be noted and go into a crate that you then return to him. It also says you can reroll the fish type by leaving his dialogue before he hands you the crate. The crate is one slot, so fill it in batches instead of carrying 23 items: Take the crate and check whether he wants mackerel or snails; if it is mackerel, leave his dialogue and ask again until it is snails. Teleport out and buy the bronze axes and four tinderboxes (three for the crate, one kept to light the furnace), putting the axes and three tinderboxes into the crate as you go. Bob's Brilliant Axes in Lumbridge sells bron"},{"t":"The bank, the furnace and the juvinates","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › In Aid of the Myreque to the rod mould","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t87-h","x":"Repair the bank with 5 planks, 20 nails and a swamp paste, then talk to Cornelius. Inspect the bank booth first, repair the wall on the bank's west side and then ask Cornelius what to do next; he agrees to become the banker. The wiki lists the repair items as 5 planks, a hammer, swamp paste and 20 nails, which in a normal game you fetch from your bank and a UIM carries in. Repair the furnace in the south-east of town with the two steel bars, add the coal and light it with a tinderbox. That starts a fight with Gadderanks and two Vampyre Juvinates in the general store. Wear Efaritay's aid: the wiki recommends it or a silver weapon, and says juvinates can be flinched or safespotted. Leaving the"},{"t":"Escort Ivan Strom","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › In Aid of the Myreque to the rod mould","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t88-h","x":"Give Ivan the steel chainbody, platelegs and med helm; you won't get them back. Start the escort from Veliaf at the hideout, with pets left at home. The wiki also suggests a silver sickle for him. He accepts up to 15 stews, salmon, snails or slimy eels. You can bring fewer than 15 salmon on the short route, because if Ivan runs out of food or health he only teleports out and the escort resets. Take the short route (two level 75 juvinates), keep Ivan behind you and keep Efaritay's aid on. After the first vampyre dies, stand behind Ivan, talk to him and step into his square so he moves behind you. If he teleports out, leave south toward Canifis, come back and retry; he keeps his gear but needs"},{"t":"The rod mould and the Guthix balance","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › In Aid of the Myreque to the rod mould","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t89-h","x":"Read The Sleeping Seven in the Paterdomus library, behind the keyhole wall that the key opens (use it on the empty east wall, then search the middle bookcase facing the west wall). Reading it matters: the wiki says nothing happens at the coffin if you skipped that step. Then hammer the boards near the hideout to open the cave, and use a soft clay on the coffin (keep one from the house-tablet run) to get the rod mould. Stop there. The silvthrill rod is made in 2.2 at the Neitiznot furnace, and the quest ends much later in 2.2. Make a Guthix balance in Morytania for the diary: a harralander potion (unf), red spiders' eggs, garlic and the silver dust from the Ectofuntus. That uses one of your t"},{"t":"Ghosts Ahoy to the Ectophial, and Animal Magnetism to the magnet","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b21-h","x":"The Old Crone, east of the Slayer Tower, is the next stop for both quests, so go there once. Her house sits between the Slayer Tower and the Mausoleum. Fairy ring CKS is the closest. Gate in 25 Agility and 20 Cooking (boostable) for Ghosts Ahoy; about 40 ecto-tokens; the ghostspeak amulet; 30 Mining; an oak longbow (25 Fletching). Carry in the nettle tea items, the model ship materials, a spade and the ring of charos (a): about 24/28. Exit Ghosts Ahoy done with the Ectophial; Animal Magnetism at the bar magnet; the mithril axe and three balls of wool ready; Troll Romance's iron bar, rope, swamp tar, cake tin and bucket collected; about 155,000 gp. Carries forward the Ectophial (Morytania tel"},{"t":"The Old Crone and the model ship","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Ghosts Ahoy to the Ectophial, and Animal Magnetism to the magnet","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t91-h","x":"Wear the ghostspeak amulet and keep it on, since without it ghosts speak only in ghost language. For Animal Magnetism, the Old Crone gives you a crone-made amulet; take it to Malcolm and buy the two undead chickens for 10 ecto-tokens each. For Ghosts Ahoy, make nettle tea (nettles picked with gloves, a bowl of water, logs and a tinderbox, 20 Cooking), add a bucket of milk and give it to her for the model ship. The gloves must be closed-fingered (the wiki says Slayer, ranger, Infinity, Moonclan and Lunar gloves fail); pick the nettles near Mazchna, heat the bowl over a fire without drinking it, pour the tea into the porcelain cup she gives you and then add the milk. Repair the model ship with"},{"t":"The map, Dragontooth Island and the robes","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Ghosts Ahoy to the Ectophial, and Animal Magnetism to the magnet","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t92-h","x":"Open the chest with the key for the first map scrap, cross the rocks (25 Agility) for the second and kill the level 32 giant lobster for the third, then combine them. The lobster can be safespotted, but if it isn't dead within two minutes it disappears and you fight it again at full health. Take the ghost captain's boat to Dragontooth Island and dig at the marked spot with a spade for the Book of Haricanto; the ring of charos (a) cuts the token cost of the trips from 25 to 10. Win Robin's signature at Rune-Draw (100 coins) and trade it to Ak-Haranu for the translation manual. Bring an oak longbow for Robin to sign: fletch one from an oak log and a bowstring (25 Fletching) before you start. G"},{"t":"Animal Magnetism to the magnet","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Ghosts Ahoy to the Ectophial, and Animal Magnetism to the magnet","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t93-h","x":"Teleport to Lumbridge and pick up three of Troll Romance's sled materials while you are here: a cake tin and a bucket from the general store north of the castle (13 and 2 gp) and a swamp tar from the spawns in the Lumbridge Swamp. Then run north-west to Draynor Manor and give Ava the two undead chickens, and buy a rope from Ned in Draynor (18 gp) for the sled. The witch near Ava swaps five unnoted iron bars for a selected iron. A UIM makes the bars on the spot: take the Pest Control minigame teleport and its boat to Port Sarim, walk to Rimmington mine, mine iron and smelt it at the Falador furnace. Iron bars fail about half the time at a furnace, so mine about twelve ore for six bars: five f"},{"t":"Catherby and Trollheim: Caleb and Troll Romance","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b22-h","x":"Chapter 1 moved both of these here. Two Catherby stops open the block: Caleb, the first Family Crest brother, and the wax for Troll Romance's sled. The rest of Troll Romance is Trollheim and Burthorpe, and the sled's iron bar, rope, swamp tar, cake tin and bucket came with you from the Animal Magnetism block. Caleb goes first because the whole Family Crest chain hangs on one question to him (below), and the wax stop sits in the same town because the insect repellent spawns in a Catherby house. Gate in Family Crest started with Dimintheis in Chapter 1; Troll Stronghold, Death Plateau and 28 Agility (boostable) for Troll Romance; 61 Magic for Trollheim Teleport (or climbing boots); 46 Fishing "},{"t":"Caleb's fish","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Catherby and Trollheim: Caleb and Troll Romance","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t95-h","x":"Teleport to Ardougne and walk into West Ardougne. Buy one cooked salmon at the West Ardougne General Store, which the wiki's Family Crest guide gives as the ironman source; Catherby has no salmon. The cooked salmon is the only fish you buy ready-made, so it needs no range. Teleport to Camelot and walk east to Catherby. Unnote the raw swordfish from your stack at the bank booth (you get one per free slot), keep one and drop the rest. At Harry's Fishing Shop buy a small fishing net (5 gp), a harpoon (5 gp) and a big fishing net (20 gp), and catch one shrimp, one tuna (35 Fishing) and one bass (46 Fishing) on the Catherby shore. Cook the four on a range (43 Cooking for the bass, 45 for the swor"},{"t":"The wax and the maple log","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Catherby and Trollheim: Caleb and Troll Romance","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t96-h","x":"Pick up the insect repellent that spawns in the house north of the Catherby bank. Use it on a beehive in the apiary west of Catherby, then use the bucket on the hive for a bucket of wax. Use the swamp tar on the bucket of wax: the wiki's sled page says that makes the wax, held in the cake tin. Drop the repellent. The hives lie south of Camelot, and an empty bucket spawns near them if you need a spare. The order matters: use the tar on the bucket of wax, not the wax on the tar. Walk west to Seers' Village and chop one maple log (45 Woodcutting). Dunstan accepts maple or yew logs, so the maple is the one you can cut at this level. Done when you hold the wax, the maple log, the iron bar and the"},{"t":"Troll Romance","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Catherby and Trollheim: Caleb and Troll Romance","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t97-h","x":"Cast Trollheim Teleport (61 Magic, 2 law and 2 fire runes, open since Eadgar's Ruse); the wiki says it saves the climbing boots. In the Troll Stronghold, talk to Ug in the south-west corner of the middle level to start Troll Romance, then to Aga in the room to the north, then to Ug again. Take the wiki's dialogue options. With Ug, choose 'Aww, you poor troll. What seems to be the problem?' and then 'Don't worry now, I'll see what I can do.' With Aga, ask 'So... how's your... um... love life?' and finish with 'Errr... I've got to go.' Go down to Burthorpe. Talk to Tenzing in his hut west of the Warriors' Guild: choose 'Do you know where I can find Trollweiss?' and then 'What would I need to m"},{"t":"Family Crest: Avan, Boot, the perfect gold and Johnathon","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b23-h","x":"The rest of Family Crest is a loop from Al Kharid to the Dwarven Mine, Witchaven and back, ending with Johnathon in Varrock just before the Edgeville block's Chronozon fight. The Al Kharid furnace visit also casts the holy symbol that Animal Magnetism's blessed axe needs. The order is fixed by the quest: Avan won't take his jewellery until Boot has spoken to you, and Johnathon's cure is what makes him say that Chronozon holds the last piece. Gate in Caleb's crest piece and the two cut rubies; 40 Mining, 40 Smithing, 40 Crafting and 59 Magic for Fire Blast (all boostable); 16 Crafting for the holy symbol. Carry in the core kit, a pickaxe, the crest piece, the rubies, an antipoison for Johnath"},{"t":"Avan and Boot","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Family Crest: Avan, Boot, the perfect gold and Johnathon","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t99-h","x":"Take a ring of dueling to Emir's Arena and walk to Al Kharid. Ask the gem trader 'I'm in search of a man named Avan Fitzharmon', then talk to Avan, a man in a yellow cape at the entrance to the northern Al Kharid mine pit. He wants a ring and a necklace of perfect gold, and you need your pickaxe and the two cut rubies for the steps that follow. At Dommik's Crafting Store buy a ring mould, a necklace mould and a holy mould (5 gp each). Teleport to Falador and go into the Dwarven Mine underneath Ice Mountain and run to its far western end, where Boot stands by two rock columns; the wiki says Avan won't take the jewellery until you have spoken to Boot. He tells you where the perfect gold is; op"},{"t":"The perfect gold in the Witchaven Dungeon","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Family Crest: Avan, Boot, the perfect gold and Johnathon","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t100-h","x":"Teleport to Ardougne, walk east to the old ruin entrance and climb down into the Witchaven Dungeon. Follow the wiki's five-step lever sequence between the north and south rooms; it opens the locked east room without your going through its wall. The order is: outer lever in the north room up; lever in the south room up (go in by the east door, leave by the west); back in the north room pull the outer lever down, go in and lift the inner lever up; leave and lift the outer lever up again; last, the south room's lever down (enter by the west door, leave by the east). Out of order is the usual way to stall here, and once the east room opens it stays open. Level 28 hobgoblins attack you on the way"},{"t":"The Al Kharid furnace and Avan","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Family Crest: Avan, Boot, the perfect gold and Johnathon","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t101-h","x":"Take the ring of dueling to Emir's Arena and walk to the Al Kharid furnace. Smelt the two ores into perfect gold bars (40 Smithing), then make one perfect ruby ring and one perfect ruby necklace with the moulds and the cut rubies (40 Crafting each). Choose each item once: the wiki warns that make-all makes two of each, and avoid the plain gold ring and necklace in the menu. Mine one silver ore in the Al Kharid mine, smelt it, cast an unstrung holy symbol with the holy mould (16 Crafting) and string it with a ball of wool. Sell the three moulds back to Dommik. Give Avan the ring and the necklace for his crest piece. He then tells you where Johnathon is. Done when you hold Caleb's and Avan's c"},{"t":"Johnathon","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Family Crest: Avan, Boot, the perfect gold and Johnathon","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t102-h","x":"Teleport to Varrock and walk to the Jolly Boar Inn north-east of the city. Upstairs, in the north-western room, Johnathon is poisoned. Use the antipoison on him, and since he takes the whole dose whatever its strength a one-dose potion is enough; it is used up. He tells you where his piece is: Chronozon has it, by the Earth Obelisk in the Wilderness part of the Edgeville Dungeon, which is the next block's first fight. Done when Johnathon is cured. Coins: about 155,000 gp · Slots: about 20/28 · Requirements: 40 Mining for the perfect gold, 40 Smithing for the bars and 40 Crafting for the ruby jewellery and 59 Magic for Chronozon's Fire Blast (all boostable); 16 Crafting for the holy symbol Wi"},{"t":"Edgeville and the Gnome Stronghold: Scorpion Catcher, Family Crest and Monkey Madness I","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b24-h","x":"Gate in 31 Prayer; 59 Magic (boostable) for Fire Blast; the raw lava eel, the scorpion cage and the strung holy symbol; Caleb's and Avan's crest pieces; Blast spell runes and an air staff; The Grand Tree and Tree Gnome Village for Monkey Madness I. Carry in the Monkey Madness I item list and three free slots for the diamonds: about 26/28. Exit the lava eel cooked; the holy symbol blessed; the monastery scorpion caught; Family Crest and Monkey Madness I done; the goldsmith gauntlets collected; Gnome Stronghold diary tasks done; about 140,000 gp. Carries forward the cooked lava eel (Heroes' Quest), the goldsmith gauntlets (Blast Furnace), premade chocolate bombs, three diamonds."},{"t":"Edgeville and the monastery","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Edgeville and the Gnome Stronghold: Scorpion Catcher, Family Crest and Monkey Madness I","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t104-h","x":"Take fairy ring DKR to Edgeville. Cook the lava eel on a range or fire there. Have Brother Jered, in the Edgeville Monastery, bless the holy symbol you strung in Al Kharid; he is on the upper floor, so the 31 Prayer (not boostable) needed for the stairs applies to him as well. The monastery scorpion is on the same floor, either at the top of the south-east ladder or in the bedroom directly north of it. Catch it with the cage for Scorpion Catcher. Use the cage on it. The wiki only warns of a 3 Hitpoint sting for the Taverley scorpion, so keep a few Hitpoints spare in case this one does the same. Done when the lava eel is cooked, the holy symbol is blessed and the scorpion is caught."},{"t":"Chronozon and Family Crest","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Edgeville and the Gnome Stronghold: Scorpion Catcher, Family Crest and Monkey Madness I","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t105-h","x":"In the Edgeville Dungeon, defeat Chronozon for Family Crest. He has to be hit with Wind, Water, Earth and Fire Blast, so bring an air staff and the runes for all four. He is level 170. A spell that splashes doesn't count and the chat message \"Chronozon weakens\" confirms each one, so bring runes for several casts of each. Poison spiders can attack on the way to him, so carry a poison cure for yourself too. The wiki's route is the trapdoor in the south-east corner of the building south of the Edgeville bank, then north and east through the skeleton gate, north through the thug gate past the thugs, west past the red spiders and black demons and south to the Earth Obelisk. The four spells can la"},{"t":"Monkey Madness I","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Edgeville and the Gnome Stronghold: Scorpion Catcher, Family Crest and Monkey Madness I","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t106-h","x":"Start Monkey Madness I with King Narnode Shareen in the Grand Tree (Chapter 1 no longer starts it) and complete it. The item list for it is food and prayer potions, four or more energy potions, antipoison, a gold bar and a ball of wool for the monkey amulet, a lockpick, a wind staff with chaos, law and water runes, an axe, a tinderbox, a knife, an oak log, a big fishing net and a bow string. Along the way, for the Karamja diary, catch a bass and chop and burn teak and mahogany logs on Ape Atoll. Follow the wiki's steps to set aside greegree materials for Recipe for Disaster and Monkey Madness II if you have room, because Ape Atoll is a long trip. On Crash Island, Lumdo refuses at first: talk"},{"t":"The Gnome Stronghold diary tasks","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Edgeville and the Gnome Stronghold: Scorpion Catcher, Family Crest and Monkey Madness I","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t107-h","x":"In the Gnome Stronghold: buy a stack of premade chocolate bombs from Gianne as food for the next fights, and one premade toad crunchies; make a chocolate bomb for the diary; fletch an oak shortbow for the diary. Keep it only if you want to woo the princess in Throne of Miscellania later; score a goal in Gnome Ball, and do a lap of the Gnome Agility Course; take a delivery order for the gnome restaurant, take the agility shortcut to Otto's Grotto for the diary, and complete the delivery for the diary; kill terrorbirds for Rag and Bone Man II. Don't buy 20 potatoes, 10 cabbages and 10 onions in sacks at Grand Tree Groceries for Dream Mentor and Mourning's End Part II, and don't collect 50 or m"},{"t":"Haunted Mine, Heroes' Quest and the end of Animal Magnetism","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b25-h","x":"Gate in Priest in Peril, 15 Agility and 35 Crafting for Haunted Mine; for Heroes' Quest, a partner from the other gang, the fire feather and the cooked lava eel; the mithril axe and blessed holy symbol; the hard leather and the polished button. Carry in the Iban's staff with death and fire runes, food and potions, and two free slots inside the mine: about 22/28. Exit Haunted Mine, Heroes' Quest and Animal Magnetism done; the salve amulet and Ava's device; about 135,000 gp. Carries forward the crystal-mine key (the Lair of Tarn), the salve amulet."},{"t":"Haunted Mine","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Haunted Mine, Heroes' Quest and the end of Animal Magnetism","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t109-h","x":"Requirements Cutting the salve shard needs 35 Crafting (boostable): use your chisel on a crystal outcrop in the south-east corner of the crystal room, then use the ball of wool on the shard. Take the Shades of Mort'ton minigame teleport and do Haunted Mine, which lies in the south-west corner of Morytania with the Zealot who starts it standing outside. The 15 Agility lets you climb the cart that blocks the front entrance (the southern entrance works without it), and feral vampyres roam near the cart track outside. The items are the Iban's staff with death and fire runes, a ball of wool, a chisel, energy and prayer potions, food and the premade chocolate bombs. Keep two slots free inside, one"},{"t":"Heroes' Quest","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Haunted Mine, Heroes' Quest and the end of Animal Magnetism","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t110-h","x":"Go to Brimhaven for the gang mansion. Heroes' Quest needs a partner from the other gang; use the \"osrs soa\" clan chat or the Join button on the Grouping interface's Shield of Arrav category to find one. The wiki says the armband steps need none of the quest's skill requirements, and that someone who has finished the quest can go back and help. Follow your gang's steps from the wiki: the Black Arm Gang needs full black armour (helm, platebody, platelegs) to enter as Hartigen, and the Phoenix Gang needs a ranged or magic setup to shoot Grip. The Black Arm side is given the key by Grip and trades it to the Phoenix partner, who must land the killing blow: Black Arm members can never kill Grip, a"},{"t":"Finish Animal Magnetism","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Haunted Mine, Heroes' Quest and the end of Animal Magnetism","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t111-h","x":"You're in Burthorpe, so give Turael the mithril axe and the holy symbol for the blessed axe. He takes only a mithril axe, and take care in his dialogue not to accept a Slayer task you don't want. If you lose the blessed axe, Turael makes another from a new mithril axe and holy symbol. Return to Draynor Manor, chop the undead trees around the manor with the blessed axe, which is the only axe that cuts them, for undead twigs, and give them to Ava. The wiki doesn't say how many twigs she wants, so keep chopping until she is satisfied. Translate her research notes, then combine the hard leather, the polished button and the pattern into a container and give it to her. Rewards 1,000 Crafting, 1,00"},{"t":"Money, Yanille runes, Big Chompy, Zogre Flesh Eaters and the Blast Furnace to 50 Smithing","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b26-h","x":"This is the most expensive block of 2.1. This block budgets about 835,000 gp, mostly runes and 1,100 gold ore, and you arrive with about 135,000. Gate in about 1,000,000 gp after blackjacking; 30 Ranged (not boostable) for both ogre quests; 49 Crafting for The Hand in the Sand; 66 Magic for the Magic Guild (63 plus a wizard's mind bomb); 40 Smithing for gold; the goldsmith gauntlets and ice gloves; 42 Crafting for fishbowls. Carry in the quest items for each part; for the Blast Furnace, the gauntlets, ice gloves, nature runes and an inventory of ore cycling: about 22/28. Exit Big Chompy, Zogre Flesh Eaters, The Hand in the Sand and Freeing Pirate Pete done; 61 Crafting; 50 Smithing; Magic cl"},{"t":"Top up the stack first","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Money, Yanille runes, Big Chompy, Zogre Flesh Eaters and the Blast Furnace to 50 Smithing","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t113-h","x":"Blackjack Menaphite thugs in Pollnivneach before you start, as in Chapter 1, until you have about 1,000,000 gp. You arrive with about 135,000, so that is about 865,000 gp to earn: at the rate above, roughly 200,000 gp an hour, about four and a quarter hours, and it also pushes Thieving toward the next level. If you'd rather blackjack less, cut the law and death runes below, not the gold ore or the natures: those two are what get you to 50 Smithing and 65 Magic. Done when you hold about 1,000,000 gp."},{"t":"Big Chompy Bird Hunting and Zogre Flesh Eaters","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Money, Yanille runes, Big Chompy, Zogre Flesh Eaters and the Blast Furnace to 50 Smithing","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t114-h","x":"Requirements Big Chompy Bird Hunting: 30 Ranged (not boostable), 5 Fletching and 30 Cooking (both boostable). Do Big Chompy Bird Hunting, killing the nearby wolves for Rag and Bone Man II. Bring an axe you can use (the wiki says the blessed axe doesn't work), 100 feathers to be safe (or 50 coins for 25 from Fycie), and a knife and chisel, or 10 coins to buy both from Bugs. The cabbage, tomato, onion, potato and leaves are found during the quest, and a Draynor cabbage doesn't work. Save one raw chompy for later and keep it on you: nothing confirms that raw meat survives a deathpile. Rewards 2 quest points, 262 Fletching, 1,470 Cooking and 735 Ranged XP, an ogre bow and the ability to make ogr"},{"t":"Zogre Flesh Eaters","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Money, Yanille runes, Big Chompy, Zogre Flesh Eaters and the Blast Furnace to 50 Smithing","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t115-h","x":"Requirements Zogre Flesh Eaters: 30 Ranged (not boostable) and 4 Smithing and 8 Herblore (boostable), and 5 free slots near the start, where the wiki recommends 5 to 10. Then do Zogre Flesh Eaters, using rings of dueling to speed up the travel, and kill zogres for Rag and Bone Man II along the way. Below 89 Combat, level 44 zogres and skogres may attack, and their disease lowers a random stat by up to 10 every 18 seconds. Slash Bash is level 111 and takes only 25% damage from most attacks: Crumble Undead does 50%, and he is fully vulnerable to brutal arrows. He can be safespotted, but his ranged attack still reaches you, so use Protect from Missiles (40 Prayer); his attacks drain Prayer whil"},{"t":"Glassblowing to 61, The Hand in the Sand and the Yanille runes","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Money, Yanille runes, Big Chompy, Zogre Flesh Eaters and the Blast Furnace to 50 Smithing","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t116-h","x":"Crafting to 61 before 2.2: glassblowing at Port Phasmatys. Nothing earlier in 2.1 trains Crafting, and 2.2 needs it: The Fremennik Isles needs 46 Crafting and Lunar Diplomacy 61. From about 46, where Chapter 1 leaves you, that is roughly 235,000 XP: about six hours at the wiki's rate, and more without a bank. Do it before the Blast Furnace below: the Yanille rune store (law, death, nature and soul runes) needs The Hand in the Sand, which needs 49 Crafting, and the gold-bar alching at the Blast Furnace needs those nature runes. The wiki's UIM Crafting guide recommends glassblowing at Port Phasmatys for this range. Ectophial there (it lands you at the Ectofuntus outside the town), buy buckets "},{"t":"The Hand in the Sand and the Yanille runes","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Money, Yanille runes, Big Chompy, Zogre Flesh Eaters and the Blast Furnace to 50 Smithing","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t117-h","x":"The Hand in the Sand, the Magic Guild store and the Yanille runes. Crafting passes 49 during the glassblowing, which is what The Hand in the Sand needs (49 Crafting, not boostable; talk to Bert near the sand pit in Yanille; it gives 9,000 Crafting XP and access to the Wizards' Guild rune store). This stop comes after the first stretch of glassblowing and before the Blast Furnace for that reason: stop blowing glass as soon as you reach 49, take the Watchtower Teleport to Yanille and finish the quest. Bert lives in the house next to the house portal by the sand pit, and the Guard Captain he sends you to is in the Ye Olde Dragon Inn, where a beer is the price. Ring the bell on the eastern side "},{"t":"Gold at the Blast Furnace","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Money, Yanille runes, Big Chompy, Zogre Flesh Eaters and the Blast Furnace to 50 Smithing","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t118-h","x":"Go to the Blast Furnace with the goldsmith gauntlets and the ice gloves, on a themed world where the dwarves run the furnace and the fee is paid into a coffer (about 72,000 gp an hour). You pay it into the coffer by the bank chest, it drains only while you stand in the basement (also while the chest window is open), unspent coins can be taken out at any time, and walking up the stairs stops it. On other worlds the foreman asks 2,500 gp per 10 minutes instead, doesn't carry the payment across a world hop, and the ring halves it only if you finish his dialogue. You already have Keldagrim access from The Giant Dwarf, and fairy ring DKS leaves you a short walk from the entrance. The ring of char"},{"t":"Freeing Pirate Pete","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Money, Yanille runes, Big Chompy, Zogre Flesh Eaters and the Blast Furnace to 50 Smithing","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t119-h","x":"The wiki's requirements for Freeing Pirate Pete are 31 Cooking (boostable), Another Cook's Quest and the ability to beat five level 30 monsters. Bring at least three raw cod (catch them with a big fishing net at the Catherby shore, where the next errand is anyway; keep one seaweed from the same net for Harry's fish), a pestle and mortar, at least three bread (steal them from the baker's stall in the East Ardougne market, 5 Thieving), a knife, an empty fishbowl, a regular needle (the costume needle doesn't work) and three bronze wire (4 Smithing; smelt three bronze bars from copper and tin ore first, since each bar makes one wire). While diving you must weigh under 27 kg (the quick guide's fi"},{"t":"Sailing: Pandemonium, Prying Times, Current Affairs and the skiff to 39","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b27-h","x":"Sailing eases a UIM's storage problem a little. Your ship's cargo hold is storage you can return to, and the wiki's UIM restrictions on it were removed on 18 February 2026, but it only takes Sailing supplies (salvage, cargo crates, charting supplies, repair kits, cannonballs), cider, beer glasses, whirlpool surprises and fish with their tools and bait. It doesn't take gear, potions, bars, quest items or noted items. From this block on, keep repair kits, cannonballs and fish in it; everything else stays on you, in the costume room or in a deathpile. Gate in Prying Times: 30 Smithing and 12 Sailing (not boostable), a steel bar and a redberry pie; Current Affairs: 22 Sailing (not boostable), 10"},{"t":"Pandemonium and the first 14 levels","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sailing: Pandemonium, Prying Times, Current Affairs and the skiff to 39","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t121-h","x":"Keep the ring of charos (a) on. Take the Pest Control minigame teleport and the boat to Port Sarim, then start and complete Pandemonium. It has no requirements. Talk to Will or Anne on the south docks of Port Sarim and take the salvage job, sail south through the Bay of Sarim to the east side of the Karamja Shipyard, trim the sails when a gust arises, un-set them when Will says you have arrived and deploy the salvaging hook, which drops you in the water. Junior Jim then gives you the raft for the old cup, and a hammer and a saw lie in the crates just south of him. The cargo courier part needs free hands, so unequip your weapon. Trim the sails whenever a burst of wind comes: it gives XP and s"},{"t":"Prying Times","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sailing: Pandemonium, Prying Times, Current Affairs and the skiff to 39","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t122-h","x":"Requirements Prying Times needs 30 Smithing and 12 Sailing (neither boostable) and the Captain's log, and Thurgo uses up a steel bar and a redberry pie, so have both on you before you start. The wiki also lists The Knight's Sword as a requirement and an open port task slot, because Steve Beanie adds the task to your Captain's log; with no free slot he can't give it. A hammer is in the crate by Junior Jim if you have none. Make the bar at the Blast Furnace in the block before this (one iron ore and one coal there). Buy the pie at the Pie Shop in the Cooks' Guild (32 Cooking and a chef's hat to enter), or bake one from a pie shell and a redberry (10 Cooking). Rewards 1 quest point, 1,000 Smith"},{"t":"Charting to 22 and Current Affairs","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sailing: Pandemonium, Prying Times, Current Affairs and the skiff to 39","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t123-h","x":"Chart around the area along the 14–22 charting route, finishing at Catherby at 22 Sailing; it starts deep in the Lumbridge Basin, and don't forget the spyglass for Keep le Faye just north of it. Whenever you chart, collect the drinks and only drink them after docking. The wiki's sealed crate page says which drinks have negative effects. Requirements Current Affairs: 22 Sailing (not boostable), 10 Fishing and Pandemonium, and the wiki's item list is 50 coins (Harry in the easternmost building of Catherby sells the mayoral fishbowl and tiny net for that) plus charcoal, which the cabinet in the council office gives you if you didn't bring any. Then start and complete Current Affairs. On the for"},{"t":"The skiff and the Ardent Ocean","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sailing: Pandemonium, Prying Times, Current Affairs and the skiff to 39","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t124-h","x":"Buy a skiff from a shipwright (15 Sailing, 15,000 coins) and build an iron helm (3 oak planks and 6 iron bars; 17 Sailing and 14 Construction) and an oak mast and linen sails (10 oak logs, 40 iron nails and 5 bolts of linen; 24 Sailing and 11 Construction) on it; all four levels are boostable. The iron bars come from your last Blast Furnace load; buy the 40 iron nails from any sawmill's construction supplies shop (5 gp each) rather than smithing them; spin 10 flax into linen yarn at a spinning wheel and weave the yarn into the 5 bolts of linen at a loom (12 Crafting; the Falador farm has one); and chop the oak logs into your log basket. If you aren't 24 Sailing yet, chart nearby until you ar"},{"t":"Tempor Tantrum and the Unquiet Ocean","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sailing: Pandemonium, Prying Times, Current Affairs and the skiff to 39","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t125-h","x":"At 31 Sailing, upgrade the skiff with a teak hull at the boat schematics: 10 teak hull parts, 300 steel nails, 20 swamp tar and the 5 lead bars, with 31 Sailing and 23 Construction (both boostable), for 345 Construction XP. Each hull part is 5 teak planks made at a shipwrights' workbench with a saw and a hammer (23 Construction, 225 XP), so that is 50 teak planks. The parts don't stack, so the final load is about 17 slots: ten parts, the nails, the tar and five bars. If you aren't 31 yet, sail south and complete the swordfish rank of the Tempor Tantrum for it, then upgrade. Done when the skiff has its teak hull."},{"t":"The Tempor Tantrum trial","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sailing: Pandemonium, Prying Times, Current Affairs and the skiff to 39","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t126-h","x":"Requirements 30 Sailing (not boostable), a skiff with at least an iron helm and an oak mast, and no crew aboard (Rum-dashed Ralph can dismiss them). Keep doing laps of the Tempor Tantrum (unlock every difficulty, then the marlin rank for XP) until at least 35,000 Sailing XP (level 39). Each rank must be earned before the next. Laps are worth 595, 1,025 and 1,790 XP at swordfish, shark and marlin, and beating the target times of 1:48, 2:51 and 4:30 gives a one-time 1,000, 2,000 and 3,000 XP. Collect the stormy key (swordfish), the barrel stand and a whirlpool surprise (shark) and Ralph's fabric roll (marlin). The stormy key opens the chest in Pandemonium Cave, next to the mining area: the fir"},{"t":"Crab Quest and the Unquiet Ocean","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Sailing: Pandemonium, Prying Times, Current Affairs and the skiff to 39","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t127-h","x":"Requirements Crab Quest needs 40 Sailing and 30 Fishing, has no enemies and recommends 9 empty slots, so arrive with them free; the big fishing net is given during it. At Dognose Island, dock, start and complete Crab Quest, and open the rusty chest for a medallion fragment. This also unlocks coral farming. Rewards 1 quest point, 10,000 Sailing XP, 3,000 Fishing XP and the shell collection. Teleport home and charter to the Pandemonium. Collect the Ardent Ocean XP reward from Chartin' Charles McAtless and buy 48 whirlpool surprises in the Pandemonium pub. Build a keg on the skiff and fill it with whirlpool surprise; spares can go in the cargo hold, which takes them. Don't buy the 25 kraken ink"},{"t":"Rellekka, Slayer to 50 Defence and Barbarian Assault","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b28-h","x":"Gate in The Fremennik Trials; about 200,000 gp from an hour of blackjacking; 45 Defence for the berserker helm; 50 Attack for the ancient staff; a Barbarian Assault team; 50 Defence and 50 Strength to wear the granite body. Carry in melee gear and Slayer kit: about 18/28. Exit Fremennik easy diary claimed; 50 Defence; a Penance Queen kill; the berserker helm and granite body, worn (and the fighter torso if you stayed); about 145,000 gp. Carries forward one pet rock (the Waterbirth doors)."},{"t":"The Fremennik easy diary and pet rocks","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Rellekka, Slayer to 50 Defence and Barbarian Assault","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t129-h","x":"Break a house tablet to Rellekka and collect the Fremennik easy diary reward (lamp on Herblore; the wiki makes it 2,500 XP in a skill you have at level 30 or above) from Thorodin, who stands just south of Rellekka. Get a few pet rocks from Askeladden in Rellekka: he gives you one after The Fremennik Trials and another whenever you talk to him again, so a lost rock costs you a walk, not a quest. Put one in your menagerie and collect it again for the diary. The wiki lists that pet rock task under the medium Fremennik diary, so it is banked now and pays out when you claim the medium diary later in this chapter. Keep one pet rock with you: it is your partner for the Waterbirth Island doors in th"},{"t":"Slayer to 50 Defence","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Rellekka, Slayer to 50 Defence and Barbarian Assault","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t130-h","x":"Your Attack should be at least 50 by now. Train Slayer, using the ancient staff as a melee weapon, until 50 Defence. If you want the fighter torso for this training, do Barbarian Assault first; the torso needs only 40 Defence to wear, so it works for you well before 50. Slayer suits a UIM: your gear is already on you, and the task drops you don't keep can stay on the floor. The 50 Defence is also the Defence half of what the granite body asks for just below, and the Helm of Neitiznot in 2.2 wants 55. Done when you are 50 Defence."},{"t":"Barbarian Assault","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Rellekka, Slayer to 50 Defence and Barbarian Assault","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t131-h","x":"Take the Barbarian Assault minigame teleport and do at least one full queen run in any role, then buy a granite body from Commander Connad for 95,000 gp (it needs 50 Defence and 50 Strength, and you must have killed the Penance Queen once). Equip it straight away: the Kandarin hard diary task is to purchase and equip a granite body, the wiki counts the buying and the equipping as two steps, and completing or updating any other diary task in between resets the task's progress. Done like this, the task is ticked now and the body can be alched later without a second purchase. The minigame is at the Barbarian Outpost, just north of Baxtorian Falls, and Connad sells from the Outpost's ground floo"},{"t":"The Barbarian Outpost, Horror from the Deep and Dagannoth Rex","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b29-h","x":"Gate in Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl; 35 Agility (boostable) for the pipe; the scorpion cage; the Horror from the Deep item list; a pet rock and a rune thrownaxe; Iban's staff (u) with charges. Carry in the Rex setup in the fourth step, plus a second pet rock and a spare thrownaxe. Plan it as a no-death trip. Exit Scorpion Catcher and Horror from the Deep done; the berserker ring; about 145,000 gp plus drop alchs. Carries forward the berserker ring (imbue next block)."},{"t":"Scorpion Catcher and Horror from the Deep","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › The Barbarian Outpost, Horror from the Deep and Dagannoth Rex","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t133-h","x":"Catch the last scorpion inside the Barbarian Outpost agility course for Scorpion Catcher. The wiki puts it in the north-eastern gated building of the course, wandering just inside the entrance, and the Barcrawl is what lets you in. Do a lap of the course for the diary; return the cage to Thormac to complete the quest when you next pass the Sorcerer's Tower. That is in 2.2, in the What Lies Below block, so there is no detour now: Thormac is on the tower's top floor, south-east of the Ranging Guild. Rewards 1 quest point and 6,625 Strength XP, and from then on Thormac turns a battlestaff into a mystic staff for 40,000 coins. Done when the last scorpion is caught."},{"t":"Horror from the Deep","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › The Barbarian Outpost, Horror from the Deep and Dagannoth Rex","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t134-h","x":"Then do Horror from the Deep, which Larrissa starts outside the Lighthouse, north of the Barbarian Outpost. You cross to the Lighthouse over basalt platforms that fail often and can hurt for up to 10 damage each time, so bring food, or take fairy ring ALP to the island. The items are a bronze sword and an arrow (one of the iron arrows from Underground Pass), an air staff with earth, water, fire and chaos runes, a molten glass, a tinderbox, a hammer, 60 steel nails and a swamp tar, plus two planks from the plank sack for the bridge. Use a plank on the near side of the broken bridge east of Larrissa, jump across and use the second on the far side; the bridge looks unchanged afterwards, so chec"},{"t":"Dagannoth Rex for the berserker ring","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › The Barbarian Outpost, Horror from the Deep and Dagannoth Rex","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t135-h","x":"Get the berserker ring from Dagannoth Rex. Bring the pet rock for the dungeon doors (the wiki says it stands in for a second player on the button) and a rune thrownaxe for the doors that block the ladder (Authentic Throwing Weapons in the Ranging Guild sells them for 572 gp; buy two, so the spare below is covered): its special attack bounces between the three doors and breaks them all. The wiki describes three paths east from the entrance cavern, each ending at a door with two buttons that need two players: giant rock crabs (level 137, melee) hold the north path, Wallasalkis (level 98, magic) the middle and ranged dagannoth (level 88) the south. Drop the pet rock in place of the second playe"},{"t":"The imbue, Slayer to 40, and the starts of The Slug Menace, Eagles' Peak and Making History","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b30-h","x":"Gate in the berserker ring; 60 Attack, Monkey Madness I, a greegree and a diamond for the dragon weapons; about 250,000 gp after half an hour of blackjacking; 30 Crafting, Runecraft, Slayer and Thieving (none boostable) for The Slug Menace; 27 Hunter for Eagles' Peak; the commorb. Carry in Slayer gear; for the runes leg, a chisel, the essence pouches, about six loose essence and five free slots (about 17/28). Exit the berserker ring (i); 40 Slayer; the dragon scimitar and dragon dagger; the house in Kourend; The Slug Menace, Eagles' Peak and Making History started; the five blank runes chiselled. Carries forward the five blank runes (empowered in 2.2), the Eagles' Peak feathers."},{"t":"Imbue the berserker ring and train Slayer","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › The imbue, Slayer to 40, and the starts of The Slug Menace, Eagles' Peak and Making History","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t137-h","x":"Imbue the berserker ring at the PvP Arena, either with a friend on another account (go at off-peak hours, hope to be matched, and trade quick deaths for points) or by losing quickly to random players for points. PvP Arena deaths don't cost items, so this is safe for a UIM: you can't take items in or out, and a death costs nothing, even from a deathbank. The arena is Emir's Arena in Al Kharid (a ring of dueling lands you at its gate), and Mubariz's shop in the welcome centre sells the scroll of imbuing for 200 reward points, on an ordinary world only. A ranked loss pays 12 points and a win 16, with streaks adding up to 10 more. Only fights the game sets up pay anything, so unranked duels and "},{"t":"The Slug Menace, Eagles' Peak and Making History","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › The imbue, Slayer to 40, and the starts of The Slug Menace, Eagles' Peak and Making History","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t138-h","x":"Before the chiselling leg, get back the small pouch that Chapter 1 dropped. The wiki says the Mage of Zamorak will not replace a lost small pouch, but the Dark mage in the Abyss will, free of charge (Astral Contact reaches him too, but you have no Lunar spells yet). Enter the Abyss from the Mage of Zamorak north of Edgeville with everything this trip doesn't need left in the Edgeville Monastery deathpile, as in Chapter 1 and in the altars block of 2.2, go through to the centre of the Abyss, talk to the Dark mage and ask for a new small pouch, then teleport out. Buy the Chronicle back afterwards if the planned death destroyed it. Then check Runecraft: The Slug Menace needs 30, and What Lies B"},{"t":"Miscellania, Royal Trouble and the Lair of Tarn","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b31-h","x":"Gate in The Fremennik Trials and Heroes' Quest; an iron bar, a non-silver ring, a favour source and a cake or bow; 9 free slots and 5 coal for the lift; Haunted Mine, the crystal-mine key and 40 Slayer (not boostable) for the Lair of Tarn. Carry in melee gear, food, energy and prayer potions and an antipoison: about 20/28. Exit Throne of Miscellania, Royal Trouble and the Lair of Tarn done; the salve amulet (e); about 500,000 gp after blackjacking; the checkpoint below met. Carries forward the salve amulet (e)."},{"t":"Throne of Miscellania and Royal Trouble","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Miscellania, Royal Trouble and the Lair of Tarn","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t140-h","x":"Take fairy ring CIP and do Throne of Miscellania and Royal Trouble, killing rabbits for Rag and Bone Man II. The ring drops you on Miscellania, and you start by speaking to King Vargas upstairs in the castle, who asks which child you want to pursue; you can switch later by talking to him again. The items are an iron bar, any common non-silver ring such as a gold ring, a favour source (an axe and 45 Woodcutting for maples, or a pickaxe and 35 Mining for coal), a cake or a shortbow or longbow (cake to befriend, bow to woo the princess; your choice), energy and prayer potions, melee gear and food. Astrid wants you to agree with her until she runs out of questions, then the Blow Kiss emote once "},{"t":"Royal Trouble","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Miscellania, Royal Trouble and the Lair of Tarn","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t141-h","x":"Advisor Ghrim in Miscellania Castle starts Royal Trouble, and the quest runs through the Miscellania dungeon. Repairing the lift needs 9 free slots and 5 coal: use the mining prop on the crevice, take the engine, beams, pulley beams and rope from the crates, put the coal in the engine and then build the scaffold, pulleys and platform. Past the lift you collect five burnt diary pages, use a plank on the slippery rocks, avoid the steam vents and falling rocks, and read the finished diary before the last crevice. The Giant Sea Snake is level 149 with 100 Hitpoints and its poison hits 9, so bring an antipoison; 40 Agility and 40 Slayer are boostable and not needed to start. Use Protect from Mele"},{"t":"The Haunted Mine and the Lair of Tarn","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.1: Quests and combat › Miscellania, Royal Trouble and the Lair of Tarn","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t142-h","x":"Take the Shades of Mort'ton minigame teleport to the Haunted Mine and use the crystal-mine key for the quick way in. The crystal mine key is the innocent-looking key from the Haunted Mine quest, and it opens the locked room on Level 2 of the Abandoned Mine, which has its own entrance on the surface. Mine a mithril ore in the Abandoned Mine for the Morytania hard diary (55 Mining): the wiki recommends the key because it gives you the Level 2 veins right by that entrance. Then visit the Lair of Tarn Razorlor and complete the miniquest, killing a terror dog on the way for the Morytania medium diary (terror dogs aren't on the Rag and Bone Man II list). Turn Auto Retaliate off in the lair, and wa"},{"t":"2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","p":"Chapter 2","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-s5-h","x":"You start 2.2 with about 500,000 after the blackjacking at the end of 2.1. This section is long and quest-dense: The Fremennik Isles, Lunar Diplomacy, the long middle of One Small Favour, Tai Bwo Wannai Trio, Contact!, most of Recipe for Disaster, Cold War, Legends' Quest, Between a Rock..., Swan Song, then green dragons, Varlamore, Sailing to 50 and the Hallowed Sepulchre. Three things make it easier for a UIM than 2.1: Storage. The skiff's cargo hold carries repair kits, cannonballs, spare whirlpool surprises and fish, nothing else. Long-term gear lives in the costume room, and the rest is carried or left in a deathpile. Hespori, at 65 Farming, adds the item retrieval service Chapter 1 poi"},{"t":"Tithe Farm to 85 Farming and the herb runs","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b32-h","x":"Chapter 1 stopped the Tithe Farm at 62 Farming, because that was all the Hespori and the contracts needed. The rest of the guide needs far more: Song of the Elves wants 70 and it cannot be boosted, the spirit tree in 2.3 wants 83 (boostable), the hard farming contracts start at 85, and a UIM cannot buy tree seeds, so tree runs and contracts alone would leave you around 83 to 84 by the end of the chapter (an estimate from the wiki's seed-pack odds, not a timed figure). The Tithe Farm is the only reliable Farming XP, so go back to it once, now, and let the daily runs carry the rest. Gate in 62 Farming and the Tithe Farm kit from Chapter 1 (34 Farming to start, 54 for bologano seeds, 74 for log"},{"t":"The Tithe Farm from 62 to 85","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Tithe Farm to 85 Farming and the herb runs","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t145-h","x":"Use bologano seeds from 54 and logavano from 74: a full sack of 100 is worth about 22,540 XP on bologano and about 37,030 on logavano, bonus included. At about 22 minutes a sack (19 on the wiki's best layout; time your own first sack and rescale) that is about 34 hours for the whole 62 to 85, about 21 hours of it to reach 80, and about 6.5 hours to reach the 70 that Song of the Elves needs. Do the first 6 or 7 hours before anything else in 2.2, and split the rest into sessions of a few hours: nothing here has a deadline, and a contract or bird house can wait the hour or two a session lasts. Done when you are 85 Farming."},{"t":"A New Leaf","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Tithe Farm to 85 Farming and the herb runs","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t146-h","x":"Requirements A New Leaf: Priest in Peril, 45 Farming, 35 Cooking, 32 Herblore and at least one completed Farming Guild contract, all of which you have. You are in Hosidius, so do A New Leaf, a Quest Month quest. Start it by picking and eating a communication cabbage in the cabbage field east of the Hosidius farm patch; Dishop Dennis is at the farm east of the Farming Guild. The quest gives you its cabbages (not Draynor Manor ones), compost (supercompost and ultracompost don't work for its potion), seeds and four bowls; bring a vial of water, a spade, a seed dibber and a rake. It travels to Falador, Hosidius, the Gnome Stronghold, Port Phasmatys and Al Kharid, so the Ectophial and a ring of d"},{"t":"The daily runs","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Tithe Farm to 85 Farming and the herb runs","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t147-h","x":"From 85 on, do these every day you play: the tree, fruit tree and hardwood runs, one hard contract from Jane, and the bird houses. Every seed a contract pack or a seed nest gives is worth planting: yew, magic, palm, papaya, dragonfruit, mahogany and teak are grown in a plant pot into a sapling first (a UIM has no shop sapling; check in game how you get the soil for the pot), and the spirit seed is for the spirit tree in 2.3. Pay the gardeners in coins (about 1,400 gp for a tree run, 2,000 for a fruit tree run), or with your own produce once you have it; allow about 3,000 gp a day, roughly 400,000 gp over the chapter, which is felt in the early blocks of 2.2 because they start near 500,000 gp"},{"t":"Herb runs that feed Herblore","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Tithe Farm to 85 Farming and the herb runs","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t148-h","x":"Requirements Song of the Elves needs 70 Herblore, which cannot be boosted, and the lamps and quests in this chapter bring you to only about 64 (an estimate from the lamp values; check yours; A Shell of a Friend and A New Leaf add 4,500 of it). About 311,000 XP has to come from potions, about 2,500 potions, so about 2,500 herbs (a few hundred more if you mix in cheaper herbs), and seeds are the limit, not secondaries. From the first herb run of 2.2, plant a seed only when it makes something worth drinking: irit for super attack (45 Herblore, 100 XP, an eye of newt at 3 gp from Jatix in Taverley, who stocks them in bulk); kwuarm for super strength (55, 125 XP, a limpwurt root); cadantine for s"},{"t":"Barbarian Fishing to about 88 Fishing","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b33-h","x":"Do Barbarian Fishing at the Mount Quidamortem spot by the Chambers of Xeric until about 88 Fishing; Agility, which Chapter 1's Canifis laps left near 62, ends up near 69. Reach the spot with the Arceuus Library Teleport (the spell, not Kharedst's memoirs; swap to the Arceuus spellbook first by talking to Tyss at the Dark Altar north of Arceuus, now that you hold soul runes) into the minecart, which is faster than the memoirs to Lovakengj. The barbarian rod is the one under Otto Godblessed's bed in his grotto above Baxtorian Falls. The wiki puts AFK Barbarian Fishing at about 23,000 Fishing XP an hour at 48 Fishing and about 57,000 an hour at 99, so the early levels are the slow ones. Feather"},{"t":"The Fremennik Isles, the silvthrill rod, and Lunar Diplomacy to the altars","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b34-h","x":"Gate in The Fremennik Trials; 20 Construction (boostable), 30 and 46 Crafting, 56 Woodcutting for The Fremennik Isles; the rod mould, a silver bar, a mithril bar and a cut sapphire; 60 Mining (not boostable), 61 Crafting, 65 Magic, 40 Defence, 49 Firemaking, 55 Woodcutting and 5 Herblore for Lunar Diplomacy; 30 Runecraft and the five blank runes. Carry in the Fremennik Isles list, then the Lunar Diplomacy list with the talismans and tiara: about 25/28 at the Fire altar. Exit The Fremennik Isles done with the Helm of Neitiznot (worn from 55 Defence); the silvthrill rod enchanted; the lunar staff made and the five Slug Menace runes empowered; lava runes made; about 430,000 gp. Carries forward "},{"t":"The Fremennik Isles","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Fremennik Isles, the silvthrill rod, and Lunar Diplomacy to the altars","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t151-h","x":"Requirements The helm needs 55 Defence to wear and you are about 51 or 52 here, so keep the berserker helm on until the Warriors' Guild and green dragon blocks take you to 55, then sell it back to Skulgrimen. Use your Fremennik boots to get to Rellekka and do The Fremennik Isles, making a Neitiznot shield along the way for the diary. It starts with Mord Gunnars at the northernmost dock in Rellekka, who takes you to Jatizso and King Gjuki Sorvott IV. Put the XP on Attack, or Defence if you're already 60 Attack. The items are the Fremennik boots, a bronze nail, 6 mithril ore, 9 ropes, a knife, a rune axe, a hammer, a needle with 2 thread, melee gear, food and prayer potions. From the wiki: the"},{"t":"The silvthrill rod","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Fremennik Isles, the silvthrill rod, and Lunar Diplomacy to the altars","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t152-h","x":"At the Neitiznot furnace, make the silvthrill rod from a silver bar, a mithril bar and a cut sapphire with the rod mould from In Aid of the Myreque, then swap to the standard spellbook and enchant it with Lvl-1 Enchant (a cosmic rune and a water rune). The wiki asks for 25 Crafting (boostable) to make the rod and 7 Magic for the enchant, and the enchant has to be cast, so don't count on a tablet. Smelt the mithril bar at your last Blast Furnace visit or here from mithril ore and coal. The silver bar is the fifth one from Al Kharid, kept for this; the cut sapphire is one of the ten uncut sapphires from the Tempor Tantrum chest, unnoted at a bank booth and cut. The rod waits in your inventory "},{"t":"Lunar Diplomacy and the five altars","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Fremennik Isles, the silvthrill rod, and Lunar Diplomacy to the altars","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t153-h","x":"Requirements Lunar Diplomacy needs 60 Mining to start, and it can't be boosted. The sandstone stop left you about 10,000 XP short, Enakhra's Lament took 7,000 of that and the ores of 2.1 a little more, so you arrive up to about 3,000 XP short (about 10,000 if you deferred Enakhra's Lament). Mine coal in the Rellekka mine, 50 XP a rock (about 60 for 3,000 XP), dropping it as you go, until you are 60 first. Then start Lunar Diplomacy and continue until you have to use your dramen staff on the elemental altars to make a lunar staff. While on the Lady Zay, collect at least 45 swamp tar. The items for this part are a tinderbox, a bullseye lantern (use the lantern lens on your sapphire lantern to "},{"t":"The Slug Menace, proselyte armour and the rest of Lunar Diplomacy","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b35-h","x":"Gate in 41 Hunter for graahk; the empowered runes; the Lunar Diplomacy list, with the seal of passage worn. Carry in Lunar Diplomacy's long item list: about 26/28 for the finish. Exit The Slug Menace and Lunar Diplomacy done; the proselyte set bought; three graahk furs; the Lunar spellbook open; about 390,000 gp. Carries forward three graahk furs (the medium fur pouch), the proselyte set, the seal of passage. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect them before you start: an unsafe death here deletes them."},{"t":"Graahk furs for the fur pouch","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Slug Menace, proselyte armour and the rest of Lunar Diplomacy","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t155-h","x":"Take fairy ring CKR, which lands south of Tai Bwo Wannai Village, and catch horned graahk (41 Hunter, with a teasing stick or hunter's spear, a knife and logs for the trap) until you have three graahk furs; they become the medium fur pouch later. Tatty graahk fur is a different item and the pouch recipe lists graahk fur, so keep catching until you have three intact ones. Done when you hold three intact graahk furs."},{"t":"Finish The Slug Menace","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Slug Menace, proselyte armour and the rest of Lunar Diplomacy","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t156-h","x":"Teleport to Ardougne (fairy ring BLR), continue The Slug Menace and kill the Slug Prince (level 62, melee only; its attacks drain Prayer by the damage dealt, so bring prayer potions). Savant teleports you to Falador to complete the quest. Rewards 3,500 Crafting, Runecraft and Thieving XP and promotion to Proselyte: buy the full proselyte set from Sir Tiffy in Falador Park (wearing it needs 30 Defence and 20 Prayer, and a UIM can't take single pieces out of the armour case until the whole set is stored, so keep the set together), which the wiki prices at 25,000 coins as a pack against 30,000 separately. Done when The Slug Menace is complete and the proselyte set is bought."},{"t":"The chainbody and the bowl of hot water","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Slug Menace, proselyte armour and the rest of Lunar Diplomacy","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t157-h","x":"Buy an adamant chainbody at the chainmail shop and heat a bowl of water on the range on the east side of Falador. Done when you hold the adamant chainbody and the bowl of hot water."},{"t":"Complete Lunar Diplomacy","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Slug Menace, proselyte armour and the rest of Lunar Diplomacy","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t158-h","x":"Teleport to Rellekka with the Fremennik boots (or fairy ring AJR) and complete Lunar Diplomacy. The items are long: law, air, earth and water runes, the dramen staff, a teasing stick, a knife, logs or an axe, the seal of passage, coins, the bowl of water, a pickaxe, a hammer, a needle with 2 thread, 4 suqah hides, a tinderbox, a spade, potions and food, cosmic and astral runes, a staff of air, a chisel and the abyssal book. For the Dream World, enter through the brazier in the long western building with all nine lunar items and the lunar staff equipped, and use the soaked kindling on the lit brazier; progress is saved if you log out, but you need more kindling to return. If the fight with Me"},{"t":"What Lies Below, One Small Favour's middle chain and the end of Scorpion Catcher","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b36-h","x":"Gate in Rune Mysteries and 35 Runecraft (not boostable) for What Lies Below; the last carried harralander for the Guthix rest; a bronze, an iron and a steel bar's ores for the weathervane; the scorpion cage with three scorpions. Carry in the One Small Favour chain items: about 24/28. Exit What Lies Below started (outlaws done); One Small Favour at Petra; Scorpion Catcher complete; five pigeon cages. Carries forward the pigeon cages (Eagles' Peak), the folder (Rat Burgiss)."},{"t":"Start What Lies Below","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › What Lies Below, One Small Favour's middle chain and the end of Scorpion Catcher","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t160-h","x":"Use the chronicle, run east and start What Lies Below: Rat Burgiss stands at the crossroads south of Varrock, wants Rune Mysteries and 35 Runecraft, and hands you an empty folder for five stolen papers. Use the chronicle again, run north-west and kill five outlaws for it, then run to Barbarian Village. They are level 32, and the wiki places them between Edgeville and the Grand Exchange; each drops a paper, and you use the papers on the folder. Done when the five outlaws are dead."},{"t":"One Small Favour as far as Petra","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › What Lies Below, One Small Favour's middle chain and the end of Scorpion Catcher","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t161-h","x":"Requirements The Guthix rest needs 18 Herblore. Continue One Small Favour from Barbarian Village: grab a cooked meat from the longhall, deal with Hammerspike in the westernmost cave of the Dwarven Mine, past the anvils (the wiki suggests asking \"Have you always been a gangster?\"; his gang of three, in their mid to high 40s, attacks when you talk to him again, so bring a weapon and armour), then Sanfew on the upper floor of the central house in Taverley, Captain Bleemadge on White Wolf Mountain (he takes the Guthix rest; a level 73 Big Wolf spawns nearby, so keep him between you and it, and use \"Talk-to\" if you haven't finished The Grand Tree), Arhein in the general store south of Catherby's "},{"t":"Finish Scorpion Catcher","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › What Lies Below, One Small Favour's middle chain and the end of Scorpion Catcher","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t162-h","x":"Visit Thormac in the Sorcerer's Tower to complete Scorpion Catcher, then go to Wizard Cromperty in the north-east Ardougne marketplace house with the blue checkerboard floor for One Small Favour. Pick up five pigeon cages along the east wall outside the house south of East Ardougne's northern bank. Done when Scorpion Catcher is complete and you hold five pigeon cages. Coins: about 385,000 gp · Slots: about 24/28 for One Small Favour's chain · Requirements: Rune Mysteries and 35 Runecraft (not boostable) for What Lies Below; One Small Favour's quests and skills as before; the cage with all three scorpions for Scorpion Catcher Wiki references What Lies Below One Small Favour Scorpion Catcher"},{"t":"Ardougne: the emerald lantern, Jimmy Dazzler and the start of Cold War","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b37-h","x":"Gate in the emerald lantern and the lantern lens; 49 Firemaking; the cat; Ratcatchers' first segment done; 10 Hunter, 15 Thieving, 30 Agility, 30 Crafting and 34 Construction for Cold War. Carry in the cat, 10 oak planks in the sack, steel nails, a hammer, a spade, the dramen staff and a butterfly net and jar. Exit the Falador medium lantern task done; Jimmy Dazzler's segment finished; Cold War at the penguin suit; the cat back home; about 385,000 gp. Carries forward the bullseye lantern and both lenses."},{"t":"The emerald lens and Jimmy Dazzler","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Ardougne: the emerald lantern, Jimmy Dazzler and the start of Cold War","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t164-h","x":"Have Barnaby take you to Rimmington. Lunar Diplomacy left you with an emerald lantern. Use your lantern lens on it to take the emerald lens back out (the chemist doesn't supply a lens), then light the bullseye lantern in the chemist's house for the Falador medium diary (49 Firemaking), and return to Ardougne. Fetch the cat from your house first if it isn't with you: Ratcatchers continues with Jimmy Dazzler in the house west of the Flying Horse Inn. Jimmy's directions teleport you to the mansion gardens once read, so you need your cat (an overgrown cat won't do) and a free slot. The guards catch you if they see you, whichever way they face, but they ignore the cat; there are three checkpoints"},{"t":"Start Cold War","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Ardougne: the emerald lantern, Jimmy Dazzler and the start of Cold War","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t165-h","x":"Start Cold War with Larry at the south entrance of the Ardougne Zoo and continue until you have to make the penguin suit. The items include 10 oak planks and 10 steel nails (your plank sack takes the planks), a hammer, a spade, the dramen staff, and a butterfly net and jar for catching a snowy knight for the diary on the way. Any follower stops Larry's teleport, so if he won't take you, put the cat away first. Put the cat back in the menagerie afterwards; the next block is in the Brimhaven Dungeon. Done when Cold War waits at the penguin suit and the cat is home. Coins: about 385,000 gp · Slots: about 24/28 for One Small Favour's chain · Requirements: Rune Mysteries and 35 Runecraft (not boo"},{"t":"Tai Bwo Wannai Trio and the Brimhaven Dungeon","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b38-h","x":"Gate in Jungle Potion and Druidic Ritual, 30 Cooking (not boostable), 15 Agility and 5 Fishing for Tai Bwo Wannai Trio; an iron or better spear and a 4-dose agility potion; a pickaxe for the Shilo Village gem rocks (the machete's gems); 47 Farming for the watermelon. Carry in Earth Blast runes, an axe, a small fishing net, coins, the anti-dragon shield, the Trio items and food: about 25/28 in the dungeon. Exit Tai Bwo Wannai Trio done; the opal machete bought; the scarecrow placed in Morytania and the Morytania easy diary ready; about 370,000 gp. Carries forward the 2-dose agility potion (Making Friends with My Arm), the karambwan-poisoned spear."},{"t":"Rat Burgiss and the Karamja kit","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Tai Bwo Wannai Trio and the Brimhaven Dungeon","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t167-h","x":"Return the folder to Rat Burgiss for What Lies Below, then teleport to Varrock and continue it until you have to use the wand on the Chaos altar. Rat sends you to Surok Magis in the Varrock Palace library for a wand and Sin'keth's diary; the altar absorbs 15 chaos runes into the wand, and the wiki lists a route through the Tunnel of Chaos (42 Mining and a bronze pickaxe from Anna Jones) that avoids the Wilderness. For Karamja, carry Earth Blast runes, an axe, a small fishing net (Harry's in Catherby sells one for 5 gp), coins, the anti-dragon shield, the Tai Bwo Wannai Trio items and food, and have Barnaby take you to Brimhaven. Keep the 2-dose agility potion for Making Friends with My Arm l"},{"t":"Tai Bwo Wannai Trio and the Brimhaven Dungeon","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Tai Bwo Wannai Trio and the Brimhaven Dungeon","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t168-h","x":"Catch the raw karambwanji on site rather than carrying them in: the wiki's quick guide puts the karambwanji spots north of fairy ring CKR, south of Tai Bwo Wannai, and Lubufu alone wants 20. They stack, so fish a few dozen into one slot with the small net. If you didn't make one earlier, buy a karamjan rum and a banana, slice the banana with a knife and add it to the rum before you leave the island, or the rum breaks; a whole banana makes a useless item. Talk to Lubufu to continue Tai Bwo Wannai Trio. A drop trick gets you two karambwan vessels: bait one with karambwanji and give it to Tiadeche for a raw karambwan, and keep the spare for Tinsay. Kill snakes for Rag and Bone Man II and go int"},{"t":"Finish Tai Bwo Wannai Trio","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Tai Bwo Wannai Trio and the Brimhaven Dungeon","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t169-h","x":"Requirements Cairn Isle needs 15 Agility for the rock slide, and Tinsay is across the bridge beyond it. Then complete Tai Bwo Wannai Trio. Kill jogres for the diary and Rag and Bone Man II, catch a karambwan, explore Cairn Isle and trap a horned graahk on the way. Poison the spear with karambwan paste before you give it to Tamayu, and don't hand it over unpoisoned. Claim the rewards from all three brothers in their houses along the southern fence. Done when Tai Bwo Wannai Trio is complete and all three rewards are claimed."},{"t":"The machete and the gout tuber trade","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Tai Bwo Wannai Trio and the Brimhaven Dungeon","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t170-h","x":"Afterwards, buy an opal machete (or better) from Safta Doc for the diary. The trading sticks come from Gabooty in exchange for semi-precious gems: he pays 60 for a cut opal, 90 for a cut jade and 120 for a cut red topaz, and a fifth of that for uncut ones. Safta Doc wants 300 sticks, three opals and a gout tuber for the opal machete, and the wiki lists a tuber at Gabooty for 240 sticks if you didn't keep one from Tai Bwo Wannai Cleanup, so plan on 540 sticks. A UIM can't note gems, so mine them now: take the cart from Brimhaven to Shilo Village (the ride is itself a medium Karamja diary task) and mine the gem rocks, which need 40 Mining and give one random gem each (a red topaz from them is "},{"t":"The scarecrow","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Tai Bwo Wannai Trio and the Brimhaven Dungeon","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t171-h","x":"Make a scarecrow for the Morytania easy and Falador medium diaries (it needs 23 Farming to make, and a poisoned spear won't do): use an empty sack on a hay bale for a hay sack, add a bronze spear, then a watermelon (an ironman needs 47 Farming to grow one, which Chapter 1 gives you, so plant one in an allotment on a farm run). Place the scarecrow in the Falador farm flower patch, take it back with a spade and place it in the Morytania flower patch by Canifis; the herb patches don't count. With the scarecrow in the Morytania patch you have finished every Morytania easy task; collect the reward when convenient and put the lamp on Herblore. Done when the scarecrow stands in the Morytania flower"},{"t":"Contact!, A Tail of Two Cats' chores and the Feldip Hills","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b39-h","x":"Gate in Prince Ali Rescue and Icthlarin's Little Helper; Fire Blast runes; the camulet; 30 Agility for the Agility Pyramid; 31 Hunter for spined larupia; the cat; 40 and 50 Cooking for the chocolate cake. Carry in a light source traps can't put out, Fire Blast runes and food; then the chore items with the cat: about 26/28. Exit Contact! done (Keris locust kill for the desert hard diary); Bob's chores done; the landing strip repaired; four larupia furs and the small fur pouch; about 360,000 gp. Carries forward the Contact! lamp (Attack or Defence), the fur pouches. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect "},{"t":"Making History, Contact! and the Sphinx","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Contact!, A Tail of Two Cats' chores and the Feldip Hills","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t173-h","x":"Take the minigame teleport to Port Khazard and continue One Small Favour with Tindel Marchant. Teleport to the Ardougne market and talk to Erin the silver merchant for Making History; he keeps the north-west stall of the central market and won't talk to you if you have recently stolen from his stall, so don't thieve from it on this visit. Carry Fire Blast runes for the fight in Contact!, because fire spells do extra damage to the Giant Scarab, as the next step explains. Requirements The climb needs 30 Agility, though the first set of rock-climbing obstacles that leads to Simon needs none. Take a ring of dueling to Emir's Arena, walk into Al Kharid and talk to Osman, who stands outside the pa"},{"t":"The Giant Scarab","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Contact!, A Tail of Two Cats' chores and the Feldip Hills","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t174-h","x":"Requirements The task also needs 50 Attack and a light source. Enter Sophanem and finish Contact!. The dungeon is entered by a ladder inside the temple and then a trapdoor, and the maze beyond is a multicombat area, so don't stop to fight anything in it. The dungeon needs a light source; the wiki strongly recommends one traps can't put out (Kandarin headgear, an abyssal lantern or a bruma torch), and a Sophanem guard sells a torch and tinderbox otherwise. Floor and wall traps in the maze take 10% of your current Hitpoints plus 10, and a scarab trap puts out an ordinary light and drops you to the bottom level, where level 98 and 106 locust riders and many scarab mages wait in a multicombat ar"},{"t":"The Feldip Hills","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Contact!, A Tail of Two Cats' chores and the Feldip Hills","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t175-h","x":"Ring of dueling to Castle Wars and continue One Small Favour until the gnome glider landing strip is repaired. Cut the gems from the landing lights; the eight lights take opal, jade, red topaz and sapphire. If you crush one, Gnormadium sells up to 2 spare gems of each type for 500 coins each, but only while the crushed gem is in your inventory, so keep the crushed pieces and buy only after a crush (at most 4,000 gp for all eight spares). The wiki mentions a drop trick to keep the cost down, which you can use here. Catch spined larupia in the Feldip Hunter area until you have four larupia furs (intact ones, for the same reason as the graahk), which is also a diary task, and kill wolves for Ra"},{"t":"Varrock and Keldagrim: Hooknosed Jack, the penguin suit and Between a Rock...'s schematics","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b40-h","x":"Gate in the Rantz step of One Small Favour done; The Giant Dwarf started; 34 Construction for the workbench; the golden cannonball and the dwarven lore book; the cat. Carry in the Ratcatchers list (cheese, poison, milk, marrentill, unicorn horn dust, fish) and the catspeak amulet, worn, then the penguin suit materials: about 25/28. Exit Hooknosed Jack's segment and Smokin' Joe done; the penguin suit made; three of the four schematics; about 355,000 gp. Carries forward the penguin suit (Cold War), the schematics (Between a Rock...)."},{"t":"Burthorpe and Varrock with the cat","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Varrock and Keldagrim: Hooknosed Jack, the penguin suit and Between a Rock...'s schematics","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t177-h","x":"After the Rantz step of One Small Favour, teleport to Burthorpe and progress A Tail of Two Cats (the potatoes should be grown): with the garden chore counted, Unferth insists on seeing a doctor, and that sends you to the Apothecary in Varrock. Then use the chronicle to the Champions' Guild and run to Varrock with the cat. Done when you are in Varrock with the cat."},{"t":"Ratcatchers: Hooknosed Jack and the King rat","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Varrock and Keldagrim: Hooknosed Jack, the penguin suit and Between a Rock...'s schematics","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t178-h","x":"For Ratcatchers at Hooknosed Jack's warehouse in south-eastern Varrock, south of the pub, bring a cat with decent combat stats, since the King rat fight is the cat's. The wiki lists four cheese, rat poison (a vial, red spiders' eggs and a cleaned kwuarm, or have Jack make it), a bucket of milk, a cleaned marrentill and unicorn horn dust, plus fish to heal your cat. Buy the cheese and milk at the Culinaromancer's Chest before you come. Poison the four cheese and place them on the four rat holes (climb the ladder inside the warehouse to reach them), return to Jack, and make the cat antipoison at the Apothecary in west Varrock (marrentill, unicorn horn dust and milk). The Apothecary also gives "},{"t":"The penguin suit and Smokin' Joe","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Varrock and Keldagrim: Hooknosed Jack, the penguin suit and Between a Rock...'s schematics","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t179-h","x":"Make the penguin suit for Cold War after upgrading your workbench, using a steel bar for the clockwork (smelt it at the Blast Furnace, which is next). The suit is made at a clockmaker's bench (crafting table 3): the steel bar becomes a clockwork mechanism, then a toy, then the suit, and Crafting can be boosted for it. The items are two molten glass, a plank, silk and the steel bar. Take the Blast Furnace minigame teleport to Keldagrim. Do the Smokin' Joe part of Ratcatchers (pot of weeds, tinderbox, cat, catspeak amulet): light the pot and smoke the rat hole east of Joe, then use the smouldering pot on the hole again so your cat ambushes the rats. The amulet is only required while Dragon Sla"},{"t":"Legends' Quest, One Small Favour to Horvik, What Lies Below and the end of A Tail of Two Cats","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b41-h","x":"Gate in 107 quest points and Legends' Quest's quests; two gold bars; a pickaxe to wield for Slagilith; the Stronghold of Security's floors; the cat; 15 chaos runes and the wand; ten eagle feathers, a swamp tar, a yellow dye and 50 coins for Asyff. Carry in the Cold War and One Small Favour items listed in the steps: about 25/28. Exit Legends' Quest started; Petra freed; What Lies Below and A Tail of Two Cats done; the skull sceptre imbued; the eagle disguises made; about 345,000 gp. Carries forward the Dagon'hai history book (Historian Minas), the eagle disguises (Eagles' Peak), the beacon ring. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval se"},{"t":"Start Legends' Quest","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Legends' Quest, One Small Favour to Horvik, What Lies Below and the end of A Tail of Two Cats","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t181-h","x":"Teleport to Burthorpe to progress A Tail of Two Cats (this is Unferth's cure: wear the doctor's hat with white robes (the desert shirt and robe the guide has you carry), take off your weapon and shield, and give him the vial of water as a miracle cure; princess robes and graceful outfit pieces do not work in place of the robes), then take the minigame teleport to Port Khazard and continue One Small Favour. Take fairy ring BLR to the Legends' Guild, talk to the Legends' Guards at the gate (they let you in only if you meet the requirements) and start Legends' Quest with Sir Radimus Erkle, and take five papyrus from the table in the guild during its start, and bring two gold bars for the gold b"},{"t":"One Small Favour: Slagilith and Petra","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Legends' Quest, One Small Favour to Horvik, What Lies Below and the end of A Tail of Two Cats","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t182-h","x":"The One Small Favour steps here run through Tindel in Port Khazard, whose iron oxide Wizard Cromperty in Ardougne turns into the animate rock scroll. Tindel only parts with the oxide once he has his mattress stuffed with chompy bird feathers, which is why Rantz's work in the Feldip Hills came first. In the Goblin Cave near the Fishing Guild, follow the eastern wall to Petra's sculpture and read the scroll in front of it to summon Slagilith (level 92); if the game says there are enemies around when you read it, kill the nearby bats first. Wield your pickaxe: without a pickaxe equipped your damage is reduced by 67%, while with one combat spells do full damage, and if you melee with it, set it "},{"t":"One Small Favour and Cold War, continued","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Legends' Quest, One Small Favour to Horvik, What Lies Below and the end of A Tail of Two Cats","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t183-h","x":"Continue One Small Favour, then Cold War until just after the raw cod and ring of charos (a) step, so that the intelligence is next. Larry only teleports you to the iceberg when no follower is with you, so leave the cat out of it. The raw cod or the ring decides how the penguins talk: with the ring the penguin gives you the secret phrase outright, and without it the penguin asks for a raw cod in exchange. The mission report and Crazy penguin outcome depends on whether Between a Rock... or Enlightened Journey is finished, permanently; you reach it with neither done. The items include the doctor's hat, a desert shirt and robe, a vial of water, law runes, a water staff, melee gear with your pic"},{"t":"One Small Favour from Seers' Village to Horvik","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Legends' Quest, One Small Favour to Horvik, What Lies Below and the end of A Tail of Two Cats","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t184-h","x":"Continue One Small Favour all the way from Seers' Village to Horvik in Varrock: under White Wolf Mountain, in the White Wolf Tunnel, talk to Khorvak for the fourth schematic of Between a Rock...; he asks for a dwarven stout, but you can refuse and still get the schematic; in Barbarian Village, make a second pot lid for Swan Song: Tassie Slipcast teaches the craft, so use soft clay on the potter's wheel and fire the result in the pottery oven (25 Crafting); in the Stronghold of Security, collect the skull sceptre, imbue it with fancy or fighting boots, and spend one charge teleporting for the diary. Its four pieces drop at roughly 3% each from the monsters of the four floors (minotaurs, flesh"},{"t":"Asyff's eagle disguises","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Legends' Quest, One Small Favour to Horvik, What Lies Below and the end of A Tail of Two Cats","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t185-h","x":"Reclaim the herbal tincture from the Apothecary instead of carrying it, and bring two soft clay, five pigeon cages and a dwarven stout from a table. Then go to the south-east corner of Varrock and ask Asyff in the Fancy Dress Shop about bird costumes: for the 10 eagle feathers, a swamp tar, a yellow dye and 50 coins he makes two eagle disguises for Eagles' Peak, each an eagle cape and a fake beak. You wear the whole disguise to walk past the guard eagle in the Eagles' Peak dungeon, which otherwise hits you for small damage. The wiki's UIM note for this quest is to take off your headgear and cape and have 6 free slots besides. Have the shop make the spottier cape too if your Hunter allows: tw"},{"t":"Finish A Tail of Two Cats","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Legends' Quest, One Small Favour to Horvik, What Lies Below and the end of A Tail of Two Cats","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t186-h","x":"Hop worlds at the anvils south of Varrock West bank until you find Bob (the cat must still be with you; the wiki lists the Varrock anvil building by the Smithing tutor as one of the three places where Bob tends to get stuck) and, for 2 quest points, a doctor's or nurse hat, a mouse toy and two 2,500 XP lamps for skills at 30 or more, complete A Tail of Two Cats (lamp on Slayer). Done when A Tail of Two Cats is complete. Coins: about 345,000 gp · Slots: about 25/28 · Requirements: Legends' Quest's quests and 107 quest points to start, and 50 Agility, Crafting, Smithing, Strength, Thieving and Woodcutting, 56 Magic, 52 Mining, 45 Herblore and 42 Prayer (all boostable) to finish; the Stronghold"},{"t":"Recipe for Disaster in Misthalin, Cold War, Making History and the end of One Small Favour","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b42-h","x":"Gate in the hellcat path through Evil Dave; the Lumbridge Guide items; a purple dye; the Cold War list. Carry in the long list for the three quest finishes: about 27/28, so the cat stays at home. Exit One Small Favour, Cold War and Making History done; Evil Dave freed; Awowogei, Sir Amik, the Lumbridge Guide and Skrach started; black gloves bought; about 340,000 gp. Carries forward the hellcat, the One Small Favour lamps (Slayer)."},{"t":"Lumbridge: Cold War and Evil Dave","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Recipe for Disaster in Misthalin, Cold War, Making History and the end of One Small Favour","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t188-h","x":"Get to Lumbridge and continue Cold War. Start and complete Recipe for Disaster's Evil Dave subquest: inspect Evil Dave in the dining room, then take fairy ring DKR to his house in Edgeville, the one west of the bank where his mother Doris lives, with the cat and feed him spicy stew, making more at the Edgeville range if the spice combination needs them (the cat becomes a hellcat; it is the one item here you can't replace cheaply, so keep it out of fights). Evil Dave sits in the basement below a trapdoor, surrounded by hellrats that stole the spices, and your cat catches them: each catch gives one of four spice colours, and seven catches turn the cat into a hellcat. The stew needs all four sp"},{"t":"One Small Favour in Misthalin","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Recipe for Disaster in Misthalin, Cold War, Making History and the end of One Small Favour","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t189-h","x":"Continue One Small Favour's Misthalin steps. In Draynor, talk to the Wise Old Man, in the large house across from the bank, for Sir Amik Varze and ask him about the Evil Chicken. Do this before Swan Song: once that quest is started, its dialogue stops you asking him about the Evil Chicken until you have finished its Repairing the Colony section. Then go to the Wizards' Tower and talk to Wizard Traiborn for the Lumbridge Guide (his quiz enchants the milk, egg and pot of flour; bring those and a cake tin from the Culinaromancer's Chest). In Port Sarim, kill seagulls for Rag and Bone Man II, then talk to The Face, who stands next to the fishing shop, and Felkrash for Ratcatchers until you need "},{"t":"Complete One Small Favour","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Recipe for Disaster in Misthalin, Cold War, Making History and the end of One Small Favour","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t190-h","x":"Complete One Small Favour: charter to Brimhaven, take the cart to Shilo Village, then leave the city; lamps on Slayer. The quest does not count as complete until you have used both reward lamps (10,000 XP each, for skills at level 30 or higher), and if you drop one first, Yanni gives it back. The other rewards are 2 quest points, a steel key ring, the Guthix rest tea, pot lid crafting and the gnome glider route to the Feldip Hills. Done when One Small Favour is complete."},{"t":"Complete Cold War and Making History","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Recipe for Disaster in Misthalin, Cold War, Making History and the end of One Small Favour","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t191-h","x":"Complete Cold War and Making History, which teleports you around a bit. For Making History, Erin lends you an enchanted key that changes temperature as you walk: in the Castle Wars area, cross both northern bridges and stand about four steps north of the east end of the second bridge, and when the key starts steaming, dig up the chest with your spade and open it with the key for the journal. The wiki's Ironman note is that making your own unstrung sapphire amulet takes 24 Crafting, and a wrong answer in Dron's quiz in Rellekka ends the conversation, so start it again if that happens. If you don't have a spare purple dye, get one in Ardougne for Making History. For Cold War, the wiki's notes:"},{"t":"The desert easy diary, Ratcatchers' end and Between a Rock... in the Wilderness","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b43-h","x":"Gate in Kalphite Hive access by fairy ring; the hellcat; the ring of charos (a); for Between a Rock..., 30 Defence, 40 Mining and 50 Smithing, a pickaxe and no gold in your pack; 7,500 coins and three gold bars for the Wilderness helmet. Carry in for the Wilderness, only 7,500 coins, three gold bars, a slash weapon, a hammer, a pickaxe, melee gear, prayer potions and food; everything else in a deathpile outside. Exit the desert easy diary claimed; Ratcatchers and Between a Rock... done; the Wilderness gold helmet smithed; about 340,000 gp; the quest's rune pickaxe replaces your adamant one. Carries forward the gold helmet (quest reward). Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is"},{"t":"The desert easy diary","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The desert easy diary, Ratcatchers' end and Between a Rock... in the Wilderness","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t193-h","x":"Take fairy ring BIQ, go into the Kalphite Hive and collect five potato cacti for the diary (the wiki's tip is to drop and pick up a single cactus five times), then return to the Shantay Pass and collect the desert easy diary from Jarr (lamp on Slayer). Entering the hive is itself an easy task, and the wiki lists a rope for it. Claim the easy tier now: each tier has to be finished before you can claim the next one's rewards, and the Eagles' Peak block claims the medium. Done when the desert easy diary is claimed."},{"t":"Ratcatchers: the snake charmer and Port Sarim","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The desert easy diary, Ratcatchers' end and Between a Rock... in the Wilderness","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t194-h","x":"Fetch the cat and continue Ratcatchers with the snake charmer in Pollnivneach (Ali, who goes by Badir since The Feud, south of the bar). Talk to The Face first, or the charmer won't discuss the alternative; then use a coin on his money pot, and he gives you a music scroll and snake charm for 100 coins, or 50 with the ring of charos (a), which also skips the walking-away step. On any herb run that passes Port Sarim, stand on the docks (not beside the hole), compose the scroll's tune on the snake charm and play it, then finish Ratcatchers there by talking to Felkrash in the Port Sarim Rat Pits, and enter the rat pits for the diary. You can't play the tune without the scroll. Your cat is a hell"},{"t":"Complete Between a Rock...","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The desert easy diary, Ratcatchers' end and Between a Rock... in the Wilderness","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t195-h","x":"Then complete Between a Rock..., which finishes with the fight in Dondakan's rock in the Arzinian Mine. The fight is timed: you have about 8 minutes to mine and kill the avatar, and its form depends on your highest combat stat, so choose your gear and protection prayer to match. Mine 15 pieces of gold there (the wiki's minimum is 6), as the wiki highly recommends: it lowers the Arzinian Being from level 125 to 75. Use Prayer and bring food; if you are close to dying, removing the gold helmet teleports you out next to Dondakan. Keep a slot free before the last hit, because with a full inventory the reward helmet drops on the ground. UIM risk The wiki warns that any gold ore or bars in your in"},{"t":"The gold helmet in the Wilderness","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The desert easy diary, Ratcatchers' end and Between a Rock... in the Wilderness","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t196-h","x":"Smithing a gold helmet in the Wilderness Resource Area counts for the Wilderness medium diary and needs only partial progress in the quest, but you can't have another gold helmet in your inventory or bank when you smith it: the wiki says it must be dropped first. The helmet you smith here is the one you wear into Dondakan's rock, so smith it first; the quest's reward helmet comes only after the fight. The entry fee is 7,500 coins (6,000 after the medium diary, 3,750 after the hard). Take only 7,500 coins into the Wilderness, three gold bars (smelted beforehand from Rimmington gold ore), a slash weapon, a hammer and a pickaxe (an adamant one is preferable to a rune one, and the diary accepts "},{"t":"Motherlode Mine, the coal bag and gem bag, and Volcanic Mine","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b44-h","x":"Gate in 30 Mining (57 for the upper level); 50 Mining and Bone Voyage (for Fossil Island) for Volcanic Mine; a team for Volcanic Mine; no celestial ring worn at MLM. Carry in a pickaxe and the hourly kit: about 6/28. Exit the coal bag and gem bag; the prospector hat (and outfit if you want it); 72 Mining by Making Friends with My Arm; the Falador easy diary and the hard step done; about 340,000 gp. Carries forward the coal bag and gem bag (core kit), the prospector helmet (the Falador hard diary)."},{"t":"Motherlode Mine","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Motherlode Mine, the coal bag and gem bag, and Volcanic Mine","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t198-h","x":"Mine in the Motherlode Mine for the coal bag and gem bag, repairing the strut along the way for the diary. The north entrance, outside the Mining Guild's underground entrance, has no Mining requirement. The strut task is an easy Falador task and needs a hammer (the crates in the mine hold one) and any pickaxe: a broken strut stops pay-dirt reaching the sack, a repair serves everyone on that world, and it gives Smithing XP. Pay-dirt in the tray stays there if you log out or hop, and rockfalls that block passages deal 1 to 4 damage and clear with your pickaxe. Don't wear the celestial ring here: it is bugged and reduces the nuggets you get. For a UIM the two bags matter more than for an Ironma"},{"t":"Volcanic Mine","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Motherlode Mine, the coal bag and gem bag, and Volcanic Mine","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t199-h","x":"Then do a low-level group Volcanic Mine for the prospector hat, and optionally the rest of the outfit (each entry costs 30 numulite, mined on Fossil Island, or 3,000 numulite once for permanent access); a Discord can help you find teams. The mine is in the north-east of the Fossil Island volcano. The helmet costs 26,000 points in Petrified Pete's Ore Shop (the jacket 39,000, the legs 34,000 and the boots 21,000). The mine kills: keep the gas chamber pressure around 40 to 60% or the mine becomes unstable, don't stand on hardened lava, which melts after 90 seconds, and leave with about 40 seconds left on the 10-minute timer, because the volcano erupts at the end and kills anyone still inside. "},{"t":"Enlightened Journey: the first trip to Entrana","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b45-h","x":"Chapter 1 moved this quest here because its first Entrana trip needs 25 unnoted items at once, and Entrana bans weapons and armour. The monks search you before you sail, and if you log in on Entrana carrying prohibited equipment a monk knocks you unconscious and you wake in Port Sarim. With Falador as your respawn that is another courtyard deathpile, as in 2.1's Entrana block, and the shopping is done before the death so that the hour is spent on the island. The second trip, for the balloon itself, opens the Recipe for Disaster block, by which time Auguste's willow has grown. Gate in 20 quest points; 20 Firemaking, 30 Farming and 36 Crafting (all boostable); respawn in Falador; Prince Ali Re"},{"t":"The shopping","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Enlightened Journey: the first trip to Entrana","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t201-h","x":"Take a ring of dueling to Emir's Arena and walk to Al Kharid. Buy three papyrus at Ali's Discount Wares (10 gp each) and ten silk from the silk trader north of the palace (2 to 3 gp each). Opening Ali's basic stock with coins and a free slot can make him force-sell you a cheap item; drop it. Walk through the toll gate to Lumbridge. Buy shears at the general store (1 gp), shear a sheep at Fred the Farmer's, spin the wool at the castle spinning wheel, pick two onions in the field by Fred's farmhouse and drop the shears. Walk on to Port Sarim and buy three redberries at Wydin's Food Store, which stocks one at a time and restocks every minute. Walk back to Aggie in Draynor for a red dye (three r"},{"t":"Entrana with a Falador deathpile","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Enlightened Journey: the first trip to Entrana","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t202-h","x":"Teleport to Falador, take off everything in the castle courtyard and die to a White Knight. Pick up only the 16 quest items and about 400 coins: the death destroys the Chronicle again, and Diango sells it back for 300 gp. At Sarah's Farming shop on the farm south of Falador, buy nine empty sacks (1 gp each). Walk to Port Sarim and take the monks' boat to Entrana. Talk to Auguste, north of the Herblore shop, three times and agree to help (if you rely on boosts for the requirements, apply all of them before you talk to him). Use a papyrus on the ball of wool, steal a candle from the church and use it on the balloon structure, and talk to him again. Don't light the origami balloon during his te"},{"t":"Swan Song, Eagles' Peak, Making Friends with My Arm and the Weiss salts","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b46-h","x":"Gate in 100 quest points, 66 Magic, 62 Cooking, 62 Fishing, 45 Smithing, 42 Firemaking and 40 Crafting for Swan Song; 66 Firemaking (not boostable), 72 Mining, 68 Agility (both boostable) and 35 Construction for Making Friends with My Arm; 29 Farming, at least 60% Tai Bwo Wannai favour, eight buckets of supercompost (seven, plus one spare) and three of ugthanki dung for My Arm's Big Adventure; the eagle disguises; 27 Hunter (boostable) for Eagles' Peak; a rope; 35 Agility and 45 Strength for the eyries. Carry in 10 mist, 10 lava and 5 blood runes, 5 iron bars, logs, a hammer, a tinderbox and the airtight pot: about 24/28 for Swan Song. Exit Eagles' Peak, Swan Song, My Arm's Big Adventure and"},{"t":"Start Swan Song and finish Eagles' Peak","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Swan Song, Eagles' Peak, Making Friends with My Arm and the Weiss salts","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t204-h","x":"Take fairy ring AKQ to the Piscatoris Fishing Colony and start Swan Song with Herman Caranos, then continue Eagles' Peak at the Ardougne Zoo until you only need to report back to Charlie. Charlie stands just south of the scorpion cage. For Eagles' Peak, the eagle door needs three feathers: bronze (lift the net trap by taking the feather, then operate all four winches), silver (inspect the empty pedestal, which needs 27 Hunter, and follow the rocks to a level 13 kebbit) and gold (the lever and bird-feeder puzzle with six odd bird seeds, which has a reset lever outside the chamber if you get stuck). Then Nickolaus teaches you ferret catching outside the dungeon: don't trigger the box-trap retr"},{"t":"Eagles' Peak and the eagle rides","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Swan Song, Eagles' Peak, Making Friends with My Arm and the Weiss salts","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t205-h","x":"Report to Charlie to complete Eagles' Peak (2 quest points, 2,500 Hunter XP, a box trap, the use of box traps and the eagle transport system), then take fairy ring AKQ to Eagles' Peak (the necklace of passage only reaches the desert eyrie near Uzer) and take several eagle rides back and forth (bring a rope), finishing in the desert, for the Fremennik, Desert and Western Provinces medium diaries. Each diary task is arriving at that eyrie from another one. The wiki's requirements: the polar eyrie by Rellekka needs 35 Agility to climb; the desert eyrie at Uzer needs 45 Strength (boostable) to push the boulder; and the jungle eyrie in the Feldip Hills needs its young vine grown with a teasing st"},{"t":"Complete Swan Song","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Swan Song, Eagles' Peak, Making Friends with My Arm and the Weiss salts","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t206-h","x":"Requirements Swan Song needs 100 quest points, and its boss is the level 170 Sea Troll Queen. Take fairy ring AKQ to the Piscatoris hunter area. Run to Piscatoris and complete Swan Song, bringing 10 mist, 10 lava and 5 blood runes (the mist and lava runes come from the Air and Fire altars in 2.2; the wiki's Ironman note adds that combination runes can be bought from the Rewards Guardian in the Mage Training Arena), 5 iron bars, logs, a hammer, a tinderbox and the airtight pot. The repairs can be done in any order: for Arnold Lydspor, catch and cook five fresh monkfish (catch extras, because some burn, and three trolls of levels 65, 87 and 101 attack while you fish and must be killed); for Fr"},{"t":"My Arm's Big Adventure","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Swan Song, Eagles' Peak, Making Friends with My Arm and the Weiss salts","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t207-h","x":"Chapter 1 moved this quest here, because it needs seven unnoted buckets of supercompost carried to the Troll Stronghold on top of a kit. The wiki's requirements are Eadgar's Ruse, Druidic Ritual, Troll Stronghold, Death Plateau, The Feud and Jungle Potion (all done in Chapter 1), 29 Farming, 10 Woodcutting and at least 60% Tai Bwo Wannai favour, which the quest takes from your total; Chapter 1 left you on 100%, and the Karamja medium task for it is already done. Prepare two things first: Supercompost. Fill a compost bin with 15 compostable items and, once it has rotted, add a compost potion for supercompost, as in Chapter 1's Hosidius bin. The bin gives 15 buckets and the tool leprechaun sto"},{"t":"Making Friends with My Arm","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Swan Song, Eagles' Peak, Making Friends with My Arm and the Weiss salts","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t208-h","x":"Requirements Making Friends with My Arm: 66 Firemaking, which can't be boosted; Chapter 1 leaves you on 85 or more. The cave exit needs 72 Mining. Then start and complete Making Friends with My Arm, starting with Burntmeat in the Troll Stronghold kitchen. Wolfbone blocks the start without the Firemaking, and Larry's boat is reached by fairy ring DKS and a run west. Bring a saw, a bolt of cloth, five mahogany planks from the plank sack, cadava berries and Trollheim teleports (or climbing boots), and an agility potion to boost if you need it. A karambwan-poisoned rune spear from Tai Bwo Wannai Trio works; the wiki recommends Ranged with Protect from Missiles against Mother, so bring a ranged s"},{"t":"The Weiss salts","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Swan Song, Eagles' Peak, Making Friends with My Arm and the Weiss salts","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t209-h","x":"Requirements The Fire of Nourishment needs 35 Construction and 66 Firemaking. In Weiss, mine Te, Efh and Urt salts and basalt, which needs Making Friends with My Arm done and 72 Mining; a rock gives 2 to 4 salts at 72 to 80 Mining and 3 to 5 at 81 to 89, so expect many rocks. The minimum is two Eternal Braziers, the Fire of Nourishment (for the Weiss herb patch) and 100 each of stony and icy basalt teleports: 750 Te, 900 Efh, 950 Urt and 200 basalt. Make the teleports inside the mine, so the basalt never needs carrying out. Also mine for the Fire of Eternal Light, the Fire of Dehumidification and the Fire of Unseasonal Warmth: 1,200 Te, 1,350 Efh, 1,400 Urt and 200 basalt in total. Salts and"},{"t":"Barbarian Fishing to 99","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b47-h","x":"Gate in 72 Mining; the Barbarian Fishing spot; a knife and a teak log. Carry in the barbarian rod, feathers and 2-dose potions: about 8/28. Exit 99 Fishing; 70 Cooking for Awowogei; the super defence potion for the Fremennik hard diary. Carries forward nothing new; keep the hourlies going."},{"t":"Fish to 99","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Barbarian Fishing to 99","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t211-h","x":"Back to the Mount Quidamortem spot, this time to 99 Fishing (the heavy rod needs 48 Fishing, 15 Agility and 15 Strength, and every catch also gives Strength, Agility and Cooking XP, which is how this method feeds the 68 Agility and 70 Cooking you need), with Barblore as much as possible and cut-eating the fish for Cooking (you still need 70 for Awowogei). Notes: If you aren't aiming to max, you can skip this and train Agility to 72 manually at the Hallowed Sepulchre instead. At 66 Herblore, make a super defence potion in the Fremennik Province for the Fremennik hard diary (the wiki says it has to be done in or near Rellekka, with a cadantine potion (unf) and white berries). Keep up the hourl"},{"t":"Recipe for Disaster to the barrows gloves","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b48-h","x":"Gate in 175 quest points and every Recipe for Disaster subquest; 70 Cooking; 48 Agility; Legends' Quest's skills; the ice gloves; Auguste's willow grown, Lost City and 36 Woodcutting for this block's Entrana trip (Enlightened Journey's balloon and the dramen branch). Carry in the jungle and subquest items (about 26/28 in the jungle), then the Culinaromancer kit. Exit Enlightened Journey, Legends' Quest and Recipe for Disaster done; barrows gloves bought; the Karamja easy and medium diaries claimed; about 200,000 gp. Carries forward the barrows gloves. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect them before y"},{"t":"Entrana again: the balloon and the dramen branch","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Recipe for Disaster to the barrows gloves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t213-h","x":"Auguste's willow has had far more than its four hours by now. Cut its twelve branches with secateurs from the tool leprechaun: the wiki says you take six at a time and wait half an hour for the other six, so cut six, do a herb run and come back. Axes can't be taken to Entrana, so the logs are chopped beforehand. Chop ten normal logs and keep the tinderbox. Then use the Falador courtyard deathpile again: die to a White Knight and pick up only the branches, the logs, the tinderbox, 300 coins and the runes for one Falador Teleport (3 air, 1 water and 1 law; runes are allowed on Entrana). Take the monks' boat from Port Sarim. Talk to the cave monk and go down into the Entrana Dungeon, kill zombi"},{"t":"The remaining subquests","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Recipe for Disaster to the barrows gloves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t214-h","x":"Swap to the standard spellbook and finish Recipe for Disaster in this order: Ring of dueling to Emir's Arena, walk to Al Kharid and take the gnome glider to the Feldip Hills. Talk to Rantz for Skrach until he asks to meet you in Karamja. Ardougne teleport, the boat to Brimhaven and the cart to Shilo Village. Resume Legends' Quest up to its final step, when you have the totem pole. The wiki's warnings for the jungle: jungle wolves are aggressive, tormented warriors and oomlie birds only attack if provoked, so don't use the bullroarer near them, and a rune axe or better is needed on the yommi tree, with 45 Herblore for the seeds and 50 Woodcutting for the totem. Death wings in the Viyeldi cave"},{"t":"The Culinaromancer fight","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Recipe for Disaster to the barrows gloves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t215-h","x":"Go into the Culinaromancer fight with your ice gloves (without them you cannot wield a weapon against Flambeed), restore potions for Karamel's stat drain, water, air, earth and fire runes for the Gelatinnoth Mother, and plenty of food. Prayer does not work in the dimension, and white portals in it lead back to Lumbridge. The bosses come in this order: Agrith-Na-Na (level 146), Flambeed (149), Karamel (136), Dessourt (121) and the Gelatinnoth Mother (130), then the Culinaromancer himself (75). Karamel's drain can stop you casting your highest spell, so keep a lower one ready, and the Mother's hits can reach 40 combined, which is dangerous at low Hitpoints. The bosses come one after another, b"},{"t":"Sir Amik Varze's brulee","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Recipe for Disaster to the barrows gloves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t216-h","x":"Sir Amik Varze's brulee. The wiki's item list for this subquest is a bucket of milk, a pot of cream, a pot of cornflour (grind your sweetcorn at a windmill into a pot if you haven't yet), the vanilla pod from step 2, cinnamon, a dramen or lunar staff for the fairy rings, an anti-dragon shield and a raw chicken (the plain one, not the green Morytania kind). Combine the food in this order: the bucket of milk on the pot of cream, the cornflour, the vanilla pod, the Evil Chicken's egg and the cinnamon, and a game message says the brulee just needs flambeing. If the Wise Old Man doesn't offer the Evil Chicken question, you skipped the cook or Swan Song isn't past Repairing the Colony. Buy the mil"},{"t":"Check before the final fight","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Recipe for Disaster to the barrows gloves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t217-h","x":"Before the final fight, check that every subquest is done: Another Cook's Quest, Freeing the Mountain Dwarf, Freeing the Goblin Generals (it needs Goblin Diplomacy), Freeing Pirate Pete, the Lumbridge Guide, Evil Dave, Skrach, Sir Amik Varze and Awowogei. Chapter 1 completed the Mountain Dwarf and Goblin Generals subquests. Free the council members from the Culinaromancer's spell and the cutscene triggers, after which he retreats through a portal into the dimension, and you need to be able to beat every enemy without Prayer. Done when Recipe for Disaster is complete and the barrows gloves are bought. Coins: about 200,000 gp after the barrows gloves · Slots: about 26/28 in the jungle · Requir"},{"t":"The Warriors' Guild, the dragon defender and Nightmare Zone","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b49-h","x":"Gate in 130 combined Attack and Strength; a full black armour set (about 7,700 gp); 60 Defence to wield the dragon defender (it has no Attack requirement). Carry in the black set, food bought per trip and a defence potion: about 20/28. Exit the dragon defender; 60 Attack and as much Defence as the grind gave; berserker ring and salve amulet imbued if not already; 200,000 extra NMZ points spent on redirection scrolls; about 190,000 gp. Carries forward the black armour set (King's Ransom), the redirection scrolls. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect them before you start: an unsafe death here deletes t"},{"t":"Get into the Warriors' Guild","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Warriors' Guild, the dragon defender and Nightmare Zone","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t219-h","x":"If you can't enter the Warriors' Guild yet (130 combined Attack and Strength), train them on Slayer tasks until you can; aim for 60 Attack and 70 Strength. The guild is in the west of Burthorpe, behind the statues of Ghommal and Sloane, and the guard at the door checks your levels. The check uses your real levels, so a potion or other boost won't get you in early, and 60 and 70 add up to exactly 130 with nothing to spare. Done when your Attack and Strength total 130."},{"t":"Tokens and defenders","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Warriors' Guild, the dragon defender and Nightmare Zone","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t220-h","x":"Kill cyclopes in the guild for the dragon defender. Learn three places first: the animation room is on the ground floor beside the entrance hall, the cyclops room is on the top floor (the second floor), and the basement is down a ladder just west of the guild's back door. The cyclops room needs 100 warrior guild tokens in your inventory to enter, spends 10 on entry and takes 10 more every minute, and tokens come only from the animation room: put a full set of black armour (helm, platebody and platelegs) on a magical animator and kill the animated armour for 20 tokens. You must fight it in melee, it ignores poison and venom, and it despawns after five minutes, so stay on it. If it despawns or"},{"t":"Food for the grind","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Warriors' Guild, the dragon defender and Nightmare Zone","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t221-h","x":"Food: cheese potatoes (or 15-healing premade gnome food) in bulk are too much for a UIM to hold, so buy potatoes with cheese per trip at the guild's food shop (9 gp each, they heal 16, and it stocks ten at a time). Lidio runs it on the ground floor, and its stock refills every minute, so if ten isn't enough for a trip you can wait a minute and buy again. Buy a defence potion. Done when you have a defence potion and know the food routine."},{"t":"Nightmare Zone and the imbues","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Warriors' Guild, the dragon defender and Nightmare Zone","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t222-h","x":"If you haven't imbued the berserker ring and the salve amulet, do it now at the PvP Arena or Nightmare Zone. Both are safe for a UIM. The PvP Arena is Emir's Arena, where a scroll of imbuing costs 200 arena reward points and turns the berserker ring into the imbued version. At Nightmare Zone the ring costs 650,000 points and the salve amulet 800,000, and each is halved once the Hard Combat Achievements reward is unlocked, so those points come on top of the 200,000 extra ones below. Nightmare Zone is north-west of Yanille bank: you talk to Dominic Onion, pay the dream fee from his coffer, drink the dream potion on the plinth and accept. There are four NMZ approaches: AFK easy rumble (long AFK"},{"t":"Kourend: A Kingdom Divided, the Shayzien outfit and the Barrows run","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b50-h","x":"Gate in 53 Hunter for the chinchompa task (or boost); 20 Defence for Shayzien armour; A Kingdom Divided's quests with 54 Agility, 52 Thieving, 52 Woodcutting, 50 Herblore, 42 Mining, 38 Crafting and 35 Magic (none boostable); Priest in Peril. Carry in melee gear, cheese potatoes, potions and the quest items; a full Barrows inventory: about 25/28. Exit the Kourend & Kebos medium diary; the tier 5 Shayzien set; A Kingdom Divided done; His Faithful Servants done; about 180,000 gp. Carries forward the Shayzien set, the crypt map. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect them before you start: an unsafe death "},{"t":"The herb sack","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Kourend: A Kingdom Divided, the Shayzien outfit and the Barrows run","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t224-h","x":"Your house in Hosidius is next to the Tithe Farm, so buy the herb sack here as soon as you are 58 Herblore, which can't be boosted (lamps have gone on Herblore since 2.1): talk to Farmer Gricoller and spend the 250 points Chapter 1 kept in reserve. If you aren't 58 yet (the lamps alone leave you near 57 until Varlamore), use the leprechaun's noted herbs and buy it the first time you pass at 58. The sack holds only grimy, unnoted herbs of the normal kinds (30 of each), so from then on put your farm-run herbs straight into it. Cleaned herbs, noted herbs and coral can't go in, so it saves you slots only for the grimy ones. Optional later: a pristine spider silk (Sarachnis, 1/50) upgrades it to "},{"t":"The Kourend & Kebos medium diary","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Kourend: A Kingdom Divided, the Shayzien outfit and the Barrows run","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t225-h","x":"In Kourend, tackle organised crime for intelligence along the way and hand it in to Captain Ginea for the diary. Speak to Captain Ginea first: she tells you about a gang meeting, and intelligence drops from the gangsters (about one in five) and always from the gang boss, so kill the boss as well as the gangsters, with combat gear on. Catch a chinchompa in the Kourend Woodland for the diary; it needs 53 Hunter, Eagles' Peak and a box trap, so boost with a hunter potion or trapper's tipple if you are close, and otherwise leave the diary until the blue crabs have trained Hunter. Done when the organised crime and chinchompa tasks are done or set aside."},{"t":"The Shayzien combat ring","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Kourend: A Kingdom Divided, the Shayzien outfit and the Barrows run","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t226-h","x":"Collect the tier 5 Shayzien outfit from the combat ring (20 Defence). The ring is in the Shayzien Encampment, and you start each duel by talking to the soldier of the tier you want. If you lose a piece before the next tier's set is complete, you have to beat the previous tier again, so wear each finished set while you earn the next. Pieces in your house still count towards a set, but don't put loose pieces in the armour case yet: the wiki says a UIM can't take individual pieces back out until the full set is stored. The soldiers are level 39, 48, 58, 70 and 99, and the last hits up to 10 against 5 for the first. Collect the Kourend & Kebos medium diary from Elise, southeast of the King Rada "},{"t":"A Kingdom Divided","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Kourend: A Kingdom Divided, the Shayzien outfit and the Barrows run","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t227-h","x":"Do A Kingdom Divided on the standard spellbook, using melee for the fights; lamps on Slayer. Don't grab a skull near the Shayzien graveyard dungeon entrance or buy redberries at Kenelme's Wares in Piscarilius: the wiki's item list for the quest names neither, so skip both unless a later step asks for them. The items are melee gear, cheese potatoes, stat-boosting and prayer potions, a 3-dose defence potion, volcanic sulphur, a molten glass, a dark essence block, an axe and Fire Bolt runes. Start by talking to Martin Holt at the entrance to Kourend Castle in Kingstown. Most ways of getting stuck are small. In the Rose cutscene, clicking outside the chat box ends it and sends you back to the sh"},{"t":"The Barrows run","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Kourend: A Kingdom Divided, the Shayzien outfit and the Barrows run","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t228-h","x":"Take the minigame teleport to Mort'ton and do a full Barrows run of all six brothers; the mounds are a short walk east of Mort'ton, and the teleport has a 20-minute cooldown, so plan the way home. The His Faithful Servants miniquest asks for exactly that run (kill all six, then open the chest for the strange icon, with at least six free slots). The icon never drops to the floor, so if your inventory is full at the chest you have to kill all six again. Talk to the Strange Old Man in the Barrows before you go in to start it and again afterwards to finish it; the wiki lists only Priest in Peril as a requirement, and the reward is a dusty lamp (20,000 Prayer XP) and a crypt map. Starting it firs"},{"t":"Green dragons, King's Ransom and the Knight Waves","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b51-h","x":"Gate in Holy Grail, Murder Mystery and One Small Favour; 65 Defence and 45 Magic (not boostable) for King's Ransom; a piece of granite (mined in this block), the black set and a guard disguise; 76 Magic (boost from 73) for Greater thralls. Carry in the green dragon setup in the fourth step and food; for the Wilderness method, nothing else (the rest in a deathpile). Exit King's Ransom and the Knight Waves done; 70 Defence and about 70 Prayer (Piety); 1,300 green dragons; the King Black Dragon Lair task; a Pest Control novice and intermediate game; about 70,000 gp at the low point. Carries forward green dragonhides a trip at a time (the next block), Piety. Deathbank check this block has fights"},{"t":"Green dragons to 65 Defence","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Green dragons, King's Ransom and the Knight Waves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t230-h","x":"Kill green dragons with defensive melee and thralls until 65 Defence, handling the bones in one of the two ways under \"Choose how to handle the bones\" below; read that before your first trip. The Wilderness green dragons are level 79 and aggressive. They hit up to 8 in melee, and without a dragonfire shield or an antifire potion their breath can hit for up to 50, so eat before you drop low. They always drop dragon bones and a green dragonhide. Player killers target green dragon hunters often, which is why the planned death at the Monastery below matters. Done when you are 65 Defence."},{"t":"King's Ransom","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Green dragons, King's Ransom and the Knight Waves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t231-h","x":"Requirements King's Ransom: 65 Defence and 45 Magic, neither boostable. Then do King's Ransom (XP on Herblore). Besides the quests in the Gate in line, the wiki also lists Black Knights' Fortress, Merlin's Crystal, Rune Mysteries, Shilo Village, Jungle Potion and Druidic Ritual, so check your quest log before you carry anything over. Start by talking to Gossip outside Sinclair Mansion, north-west of Camelot Castle. First use the camulet's teleport to Enakhra's temple and mine one piece of granite of any size in the Desert Quarry just south-west of it (45 Mining; without the camulet, take the carpet from the Shantay Pass), then bring it, the black armour set you bought for the Warriors' Guild"},{"t":"The Knight Waves","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Green dragons, King's Ransom and the Knight Waves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t232-h","x":"Afterwards do the Knight Waves Training Grounds. The easiest way through the waves is to fight with food and potions and let the knights kill you when you run low: the minigame is safe, you continue from the knight that killed you, and a UIM keeps everything. The room is at the top of Camelot Castle, up the ladder in the south-western tower, and a squire outside the door explains the rules. Only melee works inside, because Prayer, Ranged and Magic are all disabled, so bring restore potions rather than super restores. There are eight knights, from Sir Bedivere at level 110 to Sir Lancelot at level 127, and the last one hits up to 23. When you die you respawn outside the room with everything y"},{"t":"Green dragons for Prayer","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Green dragons, King's Ransom and the Knight Waves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t233-h","x":"Return to the green dragons and kill 1,300 in total, defensive melee to 70 Defence and accurate after that. The setup is the Helm of Neitiznot, dragon scimitar, the anti-dragon shield (not the dragon defender: without the shield or an antifire potion their breath hits for up to 50; Oziach in Edgeville sells another if you lost yours), amulet of strength, barrows gloves, proselyte top and bottom, berserker ring (i), Ardougne cloak, climbing boots, Rada's blessing 2, and runes and a book for Resurrect Superior thralls (Greater at 76 Magic, boostable from 73 with a wizard's mind bomb). Take a games necklace to the Corporeal Beast, run east to the dragons (1,250 and 1,500 total-level worlds are "},{"t":"Choose how to handle the bones","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Green dragons, King's Ransom and the Knight Waves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t234-h","x":"The UIM difference is the loot, and neither of the usual tools works for you. A UIM's looting bag can't be emptied: what goes in only comes out when you die or destroy the bag in the Wilderness (destroying it anywhere else, the Ferox Enclave included, deletes the contents, as does destroying it within the first two tiles beyond the Wilderness Ditch), so you can't offer bones from it. And a UIM gets no gravestone, so gravestone and suicide methods at the Chaos Altar don't apply. Choose one of these instead. UIM risk If a player kills you the bag is lost to them, and they take everything in it except food and potions. The Wilderness with a deathpile, as in Chapter 1 (faster). Start each sessio"},{"t":"The King Black Dragon Lair and Pest Control","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Green dragons, King's Ransom and the Knight Waves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t235-h","x":"After one inventory, run into the King Black Dragon Lair for the diary and leave by ring of dueling to Ferox. The lair is beneath the Lava Maze, and entering it is an easy Wilderness Diary task with no requirement, so claim that tier from the Lesser Fanatic along with the others. Take the Pest Control minigame teleport (the teleport has a 20-minute cooldown) and do one novice and one intermediate game. The novice boat needs combat level 40 and the intermediate 70. You may also be close to finishing the easy Combat Achievements by now, which gives a 5,000 XP lamp (Herblore, probably). Done when the lair task and two Pest Control games are done. Coins: about 70,000 gp at the low point · Slots:"},{"t":"The fossil cases, and green dragonhide for a UIM","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b52-h","x":"Gate in enough fossils and Curse of the Empty Lord for the cases (otherwise later); 57 to 63 Crafting for the hide items; 45 and 50 Fletching for maple bows. Carry in an inventory of hides, a needle and thread, and the bow kit: about 20/28. Exit the fossil cases if ready; the hides crafted and alched; 60 Fletching on the way; about 270,000 gp after an hour of blackjacking. Carries forward headless arrows."},{"t":"The fossil cases","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The fossil cases, and green dragonhide for a UIM","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t237-h","x":"If you have enough fossils for three display cases and have finished Curse of the Empty Lord, teleport to Varrock, pray at the palace altar with Smite active, build the three fossil display cases and talk to the information clerk (XP), Historian Minas (XP lamp) and Orlando Smith (diary). Historian Minas is on the first floor of the Varrock Museum. Collect the Varrock hard diary if you have its 153 kudos (the Varlamore block lists where the rest come from), lamp on Herblore. The kudos is one task, done by speaking to Orlando Smith. Praying with Smite at the palace altar is another, which this step already has you do, and the spottier cape needs the two dashing kebbit furs from the Eagles' Pea"},{"t":"Green dragonhide for a UIM","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The fossil cases, and green dragonhide for a UIM","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t238-h","x":"The green dragonhides look like the money here, but a UIM can't bank 1,300 of them, so tanning and crafting them all into bodies to alch doesn't work. What you can do: Keep the Crafting. Bring an inventory of hides back every third or fourth dragon trip, tan them at Sbott in Canifis (Ectophial) and make the best item your level allows: vambraces at 57, chaps at 60, the shield at 62 (it also needs a maple shield and 15 steel nails) and bodies at 63. Sbott's shop is on the north side of Canifis, close to the CKS fairy ring, and charges 45 gp per dragonhide, a little over double most tanners, which you pay for the convenience. Every hide gives the same XP. Alch them as you go. If you took the c"},{"t":"Varlamore, the Myreque finish and Sins of the Father","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b53-h","x":"Gate in 51 Slayer; 53 Thieving, a ring of visibility and a ghostspeak amulet for Curse of the Empty Lord; Children of the Sun and Eagles' Peak (done in 2.2) for At First Light; the enchanted silvthrill rod and a rope; Sins of the Father's 62 Woodcutting, 60 Fletching, 56 Crafting, 52 Agility, 50 Attack, 50 Slayer and 49 Magic (none boostable); about 100,000 gp for air runes. Carry in the quest items a part at a time and Efaritay's aid: about 24/28 in Varlamore. Exit At First Light, Perilous Moons, The Heart of Darkness, Shadows of Custodia, In Aid of the Myreque, Darkness of Hallowvale, A Taste of Hope and Sins of the Father done; the mixed hide cape; 58 Slayer; about 250,000 gp. Carries for"},{"t":"Curse of the Empty Lord and the book","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Varlamore, the Myreque finish and Sins of the Father","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t240-h","x":"You should be 51 Slayer or higher. Finish Curse of the Empty Lord if you haven't (it needs 53 Thieving, not boostable, a ring of visibility and a ghostspeak amulet or Morytania legs 2; the lamp comes from Historian Minas afterwards, not from the quest). If you haven't started it, Valdez, the ghost outside Glarial's Tomb near the Fishing Guild, begins it. Take the amulet if you can, because Morytania legs don't work in the first of the quest's three sequences. In Varrock, grab the Dagon'hai history book from the palace library if you don't have it, and pray at the palace altar with Smite active. Varlamore has been open since Children of the Sun in Chapter 1: take fairy ring AJP to Avium Savan"},{"t":"Potions to 60 Herblore","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Varlamore, the Myreque finish and Sins of the Father","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t241-h","x":"Sins of the Father's tome gives 15,000 XP a use in any skill at level 60 or higher, six uses, and this guide puts every use on Herblore (A Taste of Hope's tome is only 2,500 XP, three times, at level 35 or higher, so it never needs the 60). By now the lamps and quests leave you at about 58 Herblore, about 40,000 XP short of 60, so make that much in potions before you finish Sins of the Father: about 400 super attacks or about 320 super strengths from your herb runs, made at Catherby in rounds of 9. If you reach the end of the quest below 60, keep the tome (one slot) and spend it the moment you reach 60, because putting it on another skill would leave about 90,000 XP more to make later. Done "},{"t":"The Rod of Ivandis and the Myreque quests","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Varlamore, the Myreque finish and Sins of the Father","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t242-h","x":"Then take a rope and the enchanted silvthrill rod, take fairy ring CKS and go to Paterdomus. Dip the rod in the well to make the Rod of Ivandis and complete In Aid of the Myreque. The rod has 10 charges and turns to dust when they run out. It is untradeable, the wiki says Veliaf has no replacement if you lose it, and A Taste of Hope needs it later. The rest of In Aid of the Myreque (Veliaf, the Burgh de Rott repairs and Ivan's escort) was done in 2.1, so the well is all that is left. Do Darkness of Hallowvale, A Taste of Hope and Sins of the Father, all lamps on Herblore. Sins of the Father starts with Veliaf outside the church in Slepe. Wear Efaritay's aid for the Vanstrom Klause fight in S"},{"t":"Lamps and loose ends","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Varlamore, the Myreque finish and Sins of the Father","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t243-h","x":"The lamp plan: Slayer until 58 for cave horrors (about 30,000 quest XP is still to come), then Herblore. This also unlocks Yarnio's Baked Goods, a better garden pie shop than Romily Weaklax. You can now finish the Varrock hard diary (information clerk, Historian Minas for the Curse of the Empty Lord lamp, Orlando Smith). It needs 153 kudos. Chapter 1 left you at about 105 (the quiz's 28, the five display finds' 50 and Historian Minas's quests); since then, tell Minas about Making History, A Tail of Two Cats, What Lies Below (with the Dagon'hai history book), In Aid of the Myreque and the Observatory if you haven't yet (5 each) and Curse of the Empty Lord (10), which makes about 140. The rest"},{"t":"Sailing to 50, Troubled Tortugans and blue crabs to 61 Hunter","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b54-h","x":"Gate in 51 Slayer, 48 Construction, 45 Sailing, 45 Hunter, 40 Woodcutting and 34 Crafting for Troubled Tortugans; the fish offcuts; a lockpick for the tarnished chest (Martin Thwait's Lost and Found in the Rogues' Den, 20 gp, if you dropped the Dorgesh-Kaan one); 42 Sailing to dock at Chinchompa Island. Carry in an axe and 4 free slots for the quest; then food, teleports, a lockpick, a pickaxe and the camp key (about 15/28), with fish and cannonballs in the cargo hold. Exit Troubled Tortugans done; 50+ Sailing; Ex-Captain Siad recruited; the salvaging station schematic read; the lead bars made and the hooks and keel built; 61 Hunter; coral farming started; about 220,000 gp. Carries forward t"},{"t":"Jobless Jim","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Sailing to 50, Troubled Tortugans and blue crabs to 61 Hunter","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t245-h","x":"Take the Pest Control minigame teleport and the boat to Port Sarim and recruit Jobless Jim; he can man the ship and trim the sails, for half the trimming XP but easier sailing. He is in the Rusty Anchor Inn and needs 40 Sailing to hire. Done when Jobless Jim is recruited."},{"t":"Troubled Tortugans","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Sailing to 50, Troubled Tortugans and blue crabs to 61 Hunter","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t246-h","x":"Requirements Troubled Tortugans: 51 Slayer, 48 Construction, 45 Sailing, 45 Hunter, 40 Woodcutting and 34 Crafting to start, an axe (a better one than the bronze axe found in the quest, for the 10 logs), a hammer and saw (both obtainable during it) and at least 4 free slots. Charter to the Pandemonium, take your skiff to the start of Troubled Tortugans and complete it. The start is the injured tortugan Floopa on a remote island north-west of the Great Conch. The wiki also asks for the Pandemonium quest. The level 95 gryphon only uses melee: stand next to the wall with Protect from Melee. For the level 235 Shellbane gryphon, keep the tortugan shield equipped the whole fight and use Protect fr"},{"t":"Courier tasks to 50 Sailing","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Sailing to 50, Troubled Tortugans and blue crabs to 61 Hunter","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t247-h","x":"Requirements The Summer Shore needs 45 Sailing and Troubled Tortugans, and Ruins of Unkah tasks join at 48. Do port courier tasks to the Summer Shore until 50 Sailing, finishing the Unquiet Ocean charting on the way (the Sea of Shells after 47). Courier tasks come from notice boards: you collect cargo at the pickup port's ledger table with both hands free, put it in your cargo hold and deposit it at the destination's ledger table. The ocean completion bonus (6,000 XP) can take you to 50; aim for 51–53 to need fewer boosts while salvaging. Drink the bottle that sends you home (to your house, with your ship to Port Sarim) only when convenient; it helps set up a courier task. At the Onyx Crest,"},{"t":"Ex-Captain Siad, Chinchompa Island and Port Roberts","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Sailing to 50, Troubled Tortugans and blue crabs to 61 Hunter","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t248-h","x":"Requirements 54 Thieving, which can be boosted, and a lockpick lifts the success chance at 54 from about 32% to about 42%. At 50, ring of dueling and run south to the desert mining camp, run out and recruit Ex-Captain Siad (don't forget the camp key). He is on the first floor of a building in the camp, and hiring him needs 50 Sailing (boostable) and The Tourist Trap. You can get the key again after the quest if you lost it. Teleport to Port Piscarilius with the book of the dead that A Kingdom Divided gave you (Commander Fullore, on the ground floor of Kourend Castle, replaces a lost one; without it, a house teleport to Hosidius and a walk north), recover the skiff and sail south to Chinchomp"},{"t":"Blue crabs to 61 Hunter","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Sailing to 50, Troubled Tortugans and blue crabs to 61 Hunter","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t249-h","x":"Take the minigame teleport to Pest Control or Port Khazard, charter to the Great Conch and catch blue crabs until 61 Hunter (60 is fine). Blue crabs only need 48 Hunter, so you are well inside the range; each is a trap on the Great Conch and gives 136 Hunter XP. Use the fish offcuts you kept, boosting with trapper's tipple for the first two levels, and grind the crabs into crab paste with a pestle and mortar as you go; the paste is what the super hunter potions use. It's a good chance to fletch or alch. Grow pilar coral too, and from 67 Herblore make super hunter potions and keep boosting for all future Hunter; boosting also unlocks an extra trap. If you didn't keep enough offcuts, buy sardi"},{"t":"Coral farming","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Sailing to 50, Troubled Tortugans and blue crabs to 61 Hunter","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t250-h","x":"Requirements Pillar coral needs 52 Farming. Coral farming starts here, so add coral to your farm runs: charter to the Summer Shore, take the small boat to the north-east side of the island and dive. The fairy ring CJQ on the Great Conch is the other way in, and the nurseries sit off the eastern dock. You can dive only with a diving apparatus and a fishbowl helmet, or with a medallion of the deep. Each nursery takes one frag, no compost, and the coral grows over four 40-minute stages. Harvested coral can't go in the herb sack. On your first visit, search the coral on the west side for a medallion fragment. Paying for protection isn't worth it, though the gardener Chet will protect both nurser"},{"t":"Chinchompas, Ranged to 62 and the large fur pouch","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b55-h","x":"Gate in Eagles' Peak and 53 Hunter (63 for red); Monkey Madness I for the tunnels; 45 and 55 Ranged; 72 Hunter (boostable) for the sunlight antelope; 65 Crafting (boostable) for the large fur pouch. Carry in an axe, a knife-log and the chinchompa stacks: about 18/28. Exit 62 Ranged; the accumulator; the kyatt and antelope furs; the large fur pouch; the mixed hide boots ordered; about 200,000 gp. Carries forward the antelope fur (Pellem's boots)."},{"t":"Chinchompas and Ranged","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Chinchompas, Ranged to 62 and the large fur pouch","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t252-h","x":"Catch about 1,500 grey chinchompas at Soul Wars (take an axe for the nearby teaks in case you ruin your knife-log) and about 1,500 red chinchompas between Kastori and Tal Teklan. Grey chinchompas come from box traps and need 53 Hunter and Eagles' Peak; the catch rate is about 146 in 255 at 53 and climbs with every level, so boosts matter. Chinchompas stack, so they're one slot each for a UIM. Use any boosts you have left for catch rate. Train Ranged in the Monkey Madness I tunnels with short fuse to 62: grey chins from 45 (their wield level), red from 55 to 62. Stay within three squares of what you hit, because short fuse is fully accurate only at that range and drops to 75% at four to six s"},{"t":"Alternatives and Ranged upgrades","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Chinchompas, Ranged to 62 and the large fur pouch","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t253-h","x":"Alternatives: AFK the Ranged at crabs instead (70 at most); or after 50 Ranged do A Night at the Theatre for four Ranged lamps (80,000 XP), probably with someone carrying you. At 50 Ranged, upgrade your Ava's attractor to an accumulator through Ava (the wiki lists 75 steel arrows plus 999 gp for the upgrade) or buy it from Perdu. Ava is in Draynor Manor, and the accumulator needs 50 Ranged, not boostable. It stops working while you wear a metal body. If you lose it, Ava sells a replacement for the same arrows and coins. At 60 Ranged, wear the mixed hide cape and, once you have them, the boots. Optionally do the Fight Caves for a fire cape now, though waiting for Chapter 3 is better. Done whe"},{"t":"The large fur pouch","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Chinchompas, Ranged to 62 and the large fur pouch","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t254-h","x":"When convenient, catch three sabre-toothed kyatts north of fairy ring DKS for their furs and the diary, and one sunlight antelope east of fairy ring AJP for its fur (72 Hunter, boostable), which Pellem needs for the mixed hide boots. Kyatts need 55 Hunter and a pitfall trap: a teasing stick, a knife and logs (not redwood or arctic pine). Tatty fur is the common drop and doesn't count, so you need three regular furs. With the kyatt furs you can upgrade to the large fur pouch (65 Crafting, boostable, with a needle and thread), which holds 28 furs instead of 21. Done when you hold the large fur pouch and the antelope fur. Coins: about 200,000 gp at the end (you arrive with about 220,000 gp and "},{"t":"Smelting, nails and planks for the Sepulchre","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b56-h","x":"Gate in 50 Smithing for mithril bars, 54 for nails; 34 Herblore for agility potions; up to 75,000 gp for oak planks. Carry in ore and the coal bag, then the plank sack and log basket: about 10/28. Exit 975 mithril nails; 28 oak planks in the sack and the means to refill it; 12 four-dose agility potions; about 125,000 gp. Carries forward the nails and planks (the Sepulchre), the agility potions (floor 4 boosts)."},{"t":"Smelting and nails","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Smelting, nails and planks for the Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t256-h","x":"Use the wiki's hybrid ore UIM smelting method here, which suits you as it is. Smelt your mithril ore from the Motherlode Mine, your lead ore and your gold ore. At the Varrock west anvils, make 65 mithril bars into 975 mithril nails (each bar gives 15); nails stack. A UIM can't bank the rest of the mithril bars in case you need more nails later, so smelt those later from ore if the nails run short. Done when you hold 975 mithril nails."},{"t":"Planks for the bridges","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Smelting, nails and planks for the Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t257-h","x":"The Sepulchre bridges use oak planks with mithril nails, and you need 300 oak planks. A bridge takes two planks and five nails and needs 56 Construction. A UIM can't bank them. The plank sack holds 28, which is several sessions of bridges, so refill it between sessions at the Auburnvale sawmill with oak logs from the log basket. Planks you buy at the sawmill go straight into the sack. Sawmill operators don't take noted logs, so there is no noted-plank shortcut. The sawmill fee is 250 gp for each oak plank (wiki Oak plank), so 300 planks cost up to 75,000 gp. Done when the plank sack holds 28 oak planks."},{"t":"Agility potions","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › Smelting, nails and planks for the Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t258-h","x":"Make 16 three-dose agility potions and decant them into 12 four-dose potions, for the floor 4 boosts. The cargo hold doesn't take potions, so carry them; make them just before the Sepulchre if the slots matter, or decant them noted at Bob Barter at the Grand Exchange (one slot a type) and unnote them at a bank booth before you go in. Done when you hold 12 four-dose agility potions. Coins: about 125,000 gp (after up to 75,000 gp of oak planks) · Slots: about 10/28 · Requirements: 50 Smithing for mithril bars, 54 for mithril nails; 34 Herblore for agility potions Wiki references Ultimate Ironman Guide Mithril nails Phials Agility potion"},{"t":"The sloop and salvaging to 55 Sailing","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b57-h","x":"Gate in 200,000 gp for the sloop (blackjack an hour first); the salvaging station schematic read (Troubled Tortugans block); 42 Sailing and 34 Construction for the station; Ex-Captain Siad; 50+ Sailing for salvaging. Carry in four empty beer glasses, high alchemy runes, the log basket and the seed box. Exit the sloop with two kegs, the salvaging station and two mithril hooks; 55 Sailing; hemp and cotton seeds planted; about 125,000 gp plus alchs. Carries forward hemp (bolts of canvas in 2.3), the 25 kraken ink stout in the keg."},{"t":"Buy and fit the sloop","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The sloop and salvaging to 55 Sailing","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t260-h","x":"Requirements The sloop needs 50 Sailing and has five crew slots, so Jim and Siad both fit. The sloop costs 200,000 gp at a shipwright (wiki Sloop) and you hold about 125,000 gp, so blackjack in Pollnivneach for an hour (about 200,000 gp) before you charter. Charter to the Pandemonium and buy the 25 kraken ink stout from Chartin' Charles McAtless, then charter to Port Khazard and buy a sloop. Build two kegs (fill one with whirlpool surprise and one with kraken ink stout), a salvaging station and two mithril salvaging hooks. The station needs the salvaging station schematic, which you read from the Chinchompa Island lockbox in the Troubled Tortugans block. The station itself is 4 teak planks a"},{"t":"Sail to the shipwrecks","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The sloop and salvaging to 55 Sailing","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t261-h","x":"Sail the sloop to the large shipwrecks far south, north of the Isle of Serpents; don't detour for charting with the slow sloop. Large wrecks need 53 Sailing, so at 50 you are boosting. Bring four empty beer glasses, high alchemy runes on the standard spellbook, the log basket and the seed box, and optionally a way to 1.5-tick the salvaging. Done when you are at the shipwrecks with the salvaging kit."},{"t":"Salvage to 55 Sailing","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The sloop and salvaging to 55 Sailing","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t262-h","x":"Salvage to 55 Sailing, boosting where needed (it is worth boosting even at 53) and alching diamond rings, except one, which becomes the ring of life for The Curse of Arrav two blocks on. The goal is hemp and cotton seeds. Plant the hemp as soon as you can, with Attas and ultracompost, for at least 40 hemp in total, about six seeds. Hemp goes in a hops patch at 37 Farming, three seeds to a patch, and takes 80 minutes to grow, so six seeds fill two patches. If you don't get enough, either postpone the ship upgrades until after the albatrosses in Chapter 3 or kill them earlier for the seeds. Done when you are 55 Sailing and the hemp is planted. Coins: about 125,000 gp after the sloop's 200,000 "},{"t":"The Hallowed Sepulchre to 84 Agility","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b58-h","x":"Gate in Sins of the Father (Darkmeyer); 77 Agility for floor 4, boostable from 74; the nails, planks and agility potions; 62 Ranged and a mithril grapple before the floor 3 grapples. Carry in agility potions for the floor 4 boost, the plank sack with oak planks, mithril nails, a saw (the crystal saw works) and a hammer (the hallowed hammer once you buy it), the herb sack, arrow shafts, feathers and arrowheads for headless arrows, and the rune bolts you will alch: about 19/28. Exit 84 Agility and about 2.1 million gp (you start near 125,000 gp); the hallowed hammer and focus. Carries forward headless arrows (one stack), hallowed marks. Do, in this order: Take the runs from Darkmeyer (Sins of "},{"t":"Blast mining, UIM gold to 74 Smithing, grapples and the medium diaries","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b59-h","x":"This splits into an essential Smithing part and an optional Mining part for later Sepulchre runs. It costs about 2.8 million gp and you arrive with about 2.1 million, so you cannot pay for all of it. Spend down to about 300,000 gp, the required part first, and leave the optional blast mining and adamant nails (dynamite and bars are most of the bill) until after the next Sepulchre block, when the stack has recovered. Do not blackjack for this block. The required part is the one everything else leans on: the mithril grapples open The Curse of Arrav, The Path of Glouphrie and a Falador diary step here, and they are also what the floor 3 pillars of the Sepulchre were waiting for, because a grapp"},{"t":"The Sepulchre to 98 Agility, and teak planks","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b60-h","x":"Gate in 84 Agility; 87 Agility (boostable) for floor 5; 84 Thieving or 92 Agility (boostable) for the grand coffin; a 300,000 gp margin over each teak refill. Carry in as for floor 4, with teak planks and adamant nails in place of oak and mithril. Exit 98 Agility; about 37.3 million gp; about a million headless arrows; the rune stacks from the loot. Carries forward the headless arrows (broad arrows in Chapter 3), the runes, a ring of endurance if it dropped."},{"t":"Floor 5 and the grand coffin","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Sepulchre to 98 Agility, and teak planks","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t266-h","x":"Requirements A bridge needs a saw (the crystal saw works), a hammer, 2 planks, 5 nails and 56 Construction. Optional, and a very long grind; if you aren't aiming to max, reduce or split it, though you will then have fewer prayer potions for later Slayer. From 84 you can boost for floor 5 with agility potions (make them with the rest of your toad's legs as needed) or from 82 with summer pies. Floor 5 always has an enchantment obstacle, a grapple, a bridge and the grand coffin, and every one is worth looting. The timer starts at 2 minutes on floor 1 and gains 2 more for each floor you descend, which leaves about ten minutes on floor 5 if you waste none, and time you save carries over. If it ru"},{"t":"Teak planks without Miscellania","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Sepulchre to 98 Agility, and teak planks","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t267-h","x":"The bridges need about 2,400 teak planks, and Managing Miscellania isn't available to a UIM, so make them yourself: between Sepulchre sessions, chop teak at Avium Savannah with the log basket open, as in the Mahogany Homes block, and turn the logs into planks at the Auburnvale sawmill with the log basket and plank sack (two inventories a trip), refilling the plank sack between sessions as with the oak. Two planks go into each bridge, so 2,400 planks is about 1,200 bridges, with the adamant nails from the previous block as the matching stock. It costs Woodcutting time and the sawmill's 500 gp for every teak plank, about 1.2 million gp for 2,400. Pay that from the Sepulchre loot as you go: ref"},{"t":"Fletching supplies","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Sepulchre to 98 Agility, and teak planks","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t268-h","x":"Buy arrow shafts (or cut maples) and feathers in smaller batches, for a total of one million headless arrows through fletchpalchre. Keep alching rune bolts. Arrows stack, so a million of them cost one slot, and Chapter 3 turns them into broad arrows. Done when headless arrows are fletched as you go."},{"t":"What the grind gives you","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.2: Barbarian Fishing, green dragons and the Hallowed Sepulchre › The Sepulchre to 98 Agility, and teak planks","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t269-h","x":"The average loot and XP for 84–98 is about 38.2 million gp (before fletching, rune and plank costs); 757,000 Thieving, 511,000 Construction, about 600,000 Fletching and 3.2 million Magic XP; and large stacks of cosmic, death, law, blood and soul runes, 1,700 monkfish, prayer potions, sanfew serums, ranarr weeds and seeds, about 107 strange lockpicks and a 98% chance of at least one ring of endurance. For a UIM the stackables are easy to hold, but the potions, monkfish and weeds aren't: drink or use them as they come, or decant them noted at Bob Barter at the Grand Exchange and unnote them at a bank booth when you need them. The cargo hold takes cooked fish such as the monkfish, but not potio"},{"t":"2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves","p":"Chapter 2","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-s6-h","x":"You start 2.3 with the Sepulchre money; with the Sepulchre taken to 98 you start with about 37.3 million gp, and your total depends on how far you took it. Money stops being a UIM constraint here. Storage is still one: the costume room you upgrade first in this section is where a UIM's quest sets, capes and clue items finally live, but it only takes costumes, armour and mage sets, capes, holiday items and clue rewards, so the elf quests' ingredients are carried, not stored."},{"t":"The costume room, the Kandarin hard diary and karambwans","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b61-h","x":"Gate in 87 Magic for Catherby tablets; 70 Fletching and the Kandarin hard diary's list (the granite body task already done in 2.1, 75 Smithing via a dwarven stout); the Construction levels for each piece with tea and a crystal saw (a deathpile death destroys the saw, so ask Brimstail for a new seed first if yours is gone); 83 Farming for the spirit tree; 750,000 gp for the shield right half. Carry in one piece's materials at a time; about one slot for the shield right half afterwards. Exit the costume room upgraded and every set moved into it; the Kandarin hard diary; the shield right half; about 35.05 million gp. Carries forward the shield right half (the Ardougne hard diary in Chapter 3)."},{"t":"Catherby tablets and the Kandarin hard diary","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The costume room, the Kandarin hard diary and karambwans","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t272-h","x":"Requirements The adamant spear also needs Barbarian Smithing and 75 Smithing, so if you are on 74 a dwarven stout gives the missing level; lamp on Slayer until 58, then Herblore. The water orb needs 56 Magic, an unpowered orb, 30 water and 3 cosmic runes, and a dusty key or 70 Agility, while the shadow hound wants 53 Thieving and Desert Treasure I started. When convenient, make Catherby Teleport tablets for your herb runs at the Lunar lectern in the westernmost building on Lunar Isle (87 Magic, on the Lunar spellbook, with 3 law, 10 water and 3 astral runes and a soft clay for each tablet). If you reached 70 Fletching at the Sepulchre (or are close enough to boost), teleport to Seers' Villag"},{"t":"Upgrade the costume room","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The costume room, the Kandarin hard diary and karambwans","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t273-h","x":"Chapter 1 built the costume room, an oak armour case and an oak magic wardrobe, and 2.1 added the oak treasure chest, toy box and cape rack and the teak wardrobe and fancy dress box. Upgrade and add these, boosting where needed (each tier is built from the one before it, so build the teak cape rack and the carved teak wardrobe on the way): a marble lectern (77 Construction; it replaces your mahogany eagle lectern); a spirit tree (75 Construction and 83 Farming, built in a superior garden; the crystal saw doesn't count for it); a teak armour case (64), upgrading the oak one; a mahogany cape rack (72); a mahogany magic wardrobe (78); a teak treasure chest (66); optionally one or two portal roo"},{"t":"Karambwans, if you have a fish barrel","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The costume room, the Kandarin hard diary and karambwans","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t274-h","x":"If you happen to have a fish barrel (nothing earlier in this chapter earns one), you can move the house to Brimhaven (and back afterwards) and buy 2,000 to 10,000 raw karambwans with the barrel method, for food and for 1-tick karambwan Cooking XP. For a UIM, raw karambwans are good food stock, but the wiki doesn't say whether raw fish survives a deathpile, so keep them on you or in the barrel, which keeps its fish when it drops, but you can only carry a barrel and an inventory, so buy them per trip and cook them as you go. Without the barrel, skip this. Done when the karambwans are bought, or skipped without a barrel."},{"t":"The shield right half","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The costume room, the Kandarin hard diary and karambwans","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t275-h","x":"With the Sepulchre money behind you, also buy a shield right half for 750,000 gp from the Legends' Guild Shop of Useful Items (Legends' Quest is done; the Myths' Guild Armoury sells it too, and the wiki lists no other source). It is one slot until Chapter 3, where the Ardougne hard diary smiths it with a shield left half into a dragon square shield (60 Smithing). Done when you hold the shield right half. Coins: about 37.3 million gp on arrival, about 35.05 million gp after the shield right half (750,000 gp) and the costume room (about 1.5 million gp) · Slots: costumes and sets move into the costume room; one slot for the shield right half · Requirements: the Construction levels listed for ea"},{"t":"Mage Arena I and II, and the Wilderness diary tasks","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b62-h","x":"Gate in 60 Magic for Mage Arena I and 75 for Mage Arena II (not boostable); 160,000 gp for two of the god staves (the Chamber guardian gives you the third free); air, fire and blood runes and a slash weapon; 52 Agility, 55 Mining with a pickaxe, and 50 Slayer for the Wilderness tasks. Carry in only the fight's gear; everything else in a deathpile outside the Wilderness. Exit both Mage Arena miniquests done with the god capes; the listed Wilderness tasks done; about 34.89 million gp. Carries forward one god staff only if you plan the Wilderness hard diary. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect them befo"},{"t":"Mage Arena I","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › Mage Arena I and II, and the Wilderness diary tasks","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t277-h","x":"Requirements Mage Arena I needs 60 Magic and Mage Arena II 75 Magic, neither boostable. Do the Mage Arena I miniquest, then Mage Arena II. Kolodion waits in a cave room where other players can't attack you. The wiki gives two ways in: a lever in the Edgeville ruins (or in the small building by the West Ardougne gate) that drops you in the Deserted Keep, from where you run north, cut a web and walk west to the arena's northern entrance, or the broken-down house north-west of the arena, where you cut two webs and pull the lever on the wall. Bring a slash weapon for the webs and the runes for the fight. The arena itself is not safe, so take only what the fight needs. Kolodion has five forms, an"},{"t":"Mage Arena II","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › Mage Arena I and II, and the Wilderness diary tasks","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t278-h","x":"Mage Arena II needs 100 casts each of Saradomin Strike, Claws of Guthix and Flames of Zamorak inside the arena, so you need all three staves (or a staff of the dead, staff of light or staff of balance), air, fire and blood runes and a slash weapon for the webs. Kolodion sends you after three followers, and each can only be hurt by its own god's spell: Porazdir (level 235) by Flames of Zamorak, Justiciar Zachariah (level 348) by Saradomin Strike and Derwen (level 235) by Claws of Guthix. Their spawn points rotate about every 45 minutes of time spent in the Wilderness, and if a spot is taken, hop worlds or wait. Porazdir's energy ball hits through protection prayers, Zachariah's blue wave land"},{"t":"Wilderness diary tasks on the way","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › Mage Arena I and II, and the Wilderness diary tasks","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t279-h","x":"Requirements The muddy chest needs a knife or slash weapon, or 82 Agility via the stepping stones north of the maze, and the bloodveld safespot only works while you wear one Saradomin and one Zamorak item. Along the way or afterwards: mine a mithril ore at the Pirates' Hideout mine (55 Mining and a pickaxe), do a lap of the Wilderness Agility Course (52 Agility), kill chaos dwarves for a muddy key and open the muddy chest in the middle of the Lava Maze, kill an ankou at the Forgotten Cemetery, and kill a bloodveld in the Wilderness God Wars Dungeon (60 Agility or Strength to enter, 50 Slayer and god protection items; the south-west corner is a safespot). Keep one god staff: Chapter 3's Wilde"},{"t":"The General's Shadow, Dream Mentor, chompies and Sailing to 67","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b63-h","x":"Gate in Curse of the Empty Lord, Fight Arena and a started Desert Treasure I; Lunar Diplomacy, Eadgar's Ruse and 85 combat for Dream Mentor; 70 Mining and 66 Herblore for the diary; 30 Ranged and Fletching for ogre bows; the hemp; 55 Sailing (not boostable) for the Jubbly Jive. Carry in the ghostly outfit and 40 coins until The General's Shadow ends; the Dream Mentor food in sacks; one ship build's materials at a time (up to 28/28). Exit Dream Mentor done; the Fremennik hard diary claimed; the Western Provinces easy and medium diaries; the herb sack; the skiff's mahogany mast, canvas sails and mithril helm; wind catchers on both ships; 67 Sailing. Carries forward the ghostly outfit and sever"},{"t":"The General's Shadow and Dream Mentor","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow, Dream Mentor, chompies and Sailing to 67","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t281-h","x":"The General's Shadow needs an outfit you wear to speak to General Khazard and to every scout: a ghostspeak amulet (the Morytania legs don't work for this quest), your ring of visibility and the full ghostly robes from Curse of the Empty Lord. You can't pray in the Bouncer fight at the end, and the Sin Seer wants 40 coins, so carry the outfit and the coins until the quest is done. Teleport to Rellekka and start The General's Shadow with Khazard's ghost, who wanders the woods south-east of Rellekka between the house portal and the swaying tree (he isn't on the minimap and has a wide range, so search the whole path). Teleport to Seers' Village and talk to the Sin Seer (she is upstairs in the ho"},{"t":"Dream Mentor","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow, Dream Mentor, chompies and Sailing to 67","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t282-h","x":"Before Dream Mentor, take the spirit tree to the Grand Tree and buy 7 potatoes, 7 cabbages and 6 onions at Grand Tree Groceries (it stocks ten of each for a few coins): the quest needs 20 pieces of food of three kinds, 6 of one and 7 of each of the others. Sacks of cabbages, potatoes and onions work, so buy them in three sacks (3 slots instead of 20), but take each piece out before you use it, or the sack counts as one. A death also loses the Seal of Passage, and Brundt the Chieftain gives a replacement. You face four bosses in a row without prayers: the Inadequacy (level 343), the Everlasting (223), the Untouchable (274) and the Illusive (108). All four have low Magic defence, so magic is t"},{"t":"The Fremennik hard diary","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow, Dream Mentor, chompies and Sailing to 67","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t283-h","x":"Swap to the Lunar spellbook, teleport to Waterbirth, visit Jatizso and mine five adamantite ores for two diary steps (70 Mining, with The Fremennik Isles started). Back in Rellekka, make a super defence potion (66 Herblore, a cadantine potion (unf) and white berries, which you can grow in a bush patch at 59 Farming). Before you claim the Fremennik hard diary from Thorodin south of Rellekka (lamp on Herblore), make sure its other tasks are done: cast Trollheim Teleport (61 Magic, standard spellbook) and steal from the Keldagrim gem stall (75 Thieving); the kyatt, the Neitiznot shield, the Blast Furnace foreman and the Miscellania support came earlier. Swap to the Arceuus spellbook, teleport t"},{"t":"Chompies","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow, Dream Mentor, chompies and Sailing to 67","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t284-h","x":"Make a composite ogre bow (achey tree logs, wolf bones, a bow string and a knife; 30 Fletching) and 150 mithril brutal arrows, take ogre bellows from the chest in Rantz's cave if you no longer have them, kill 125 chompies (the Western Provinces medium hat; the easy one needs 30), and talk to Rantz for chompy bird hats. Collect the Western Provinces easy and medium diaries when convenient, lamps on Herblore. Besides the tasks you passed on the way, they still need a swamp toad from the pen north-west of the Grand Tree, Brimstail's teleport to the Essence Mine, iron ore at the Piscatoris mine and gold ore under the Grand Tree (40 Mining). If you haven't bought the herb sack yet (the Kourend bl"},{"t":"Sailing to 67","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow, Dream Mentor, chompies and Sailing to 67","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t285-h","x":"Do this in trips: a bolt of canvas is made from 2 hemp yarn at a loom (Auburnvale has one), it can be noted but it doesn't stack, and the ship parts below also need steel and lead bars that take a slot each. Make 20 bolts of canvas from your hemp, keep them noted and unnote only the few you are about to use (a bank booth unnotes as many as fit, so keep only that many slots free, or pay Phials in Rimmington 5 gp a bolt for an exact number). A skiff's mahogany mast and canvas sails (52 Sailing, 45 Construction) take 5 bolts, 40 mithril nails and 10 mahogany logs; the sloop's take 10 bolts, 60 nails and 15 logs. Build the mahogany mast, canvas sails and mithril helm on your skiff, and the inocu"},{"t":"The Jubbly Jive","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow, Dream Mentor, chompies and Sailing to 67","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t286-h","x":"Do the Jubbly Jive barracuda trial (55 Sailing, not boostable) up to shark rank. Gurtob runs it from Backwater. It takes the skiff, which needs at least a mithril helm and an inoculation station (the one you built at Port Khazard), and no crew aboard; Ros can dismiss them. The first clear of each rank unlocks the next. The trial gives 1,700, 3,000 and 6,200 Sailing XP at swordfish, shark and marlin, and beating the time limits of 2:03, 3:00 and 5:21 adds a one-time 5,000, 7,500 and 10,000 XP. Beating the shark time of 3:00 also gives the captured wind mote that the wind catchers below need, so aim for it on that rank. Done when the barracuda trial is done up to shark rank."},{"t":"Wind catchers and Sailing to 67","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow, Dream Mentor, chompies and Sailing to 67","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t287-h","x":"Buy the 20,000 air runes the two wind catchers need now (10,000 each): they stack in one slot, but Aubury's shop holds only 5,000 at 4 gp each, so buy them over several shops or worlds, about 100,000 gp. Build a wind catcher on both ships (53 Sailing, 47 Construction; for each ship 4 teak planks, 16 steel nails, 8 steel bars, 4 lead bars, 10,000 air runes and a captured wind mote), then return to the Jubbly Jive and train to 67 Sailing on marlin rank with the wiki's method (the trial takes skiffs only and its 55 Sailing can't be boosted; clearing the shark rank for the first time unlocks marlin). Return to the Ardent Ocean meteorologists for their charting tasks when convenient. The alternat"},{"t":"The General's Shadow scouts, Fairytale II, Land of the Goblins and Rag and Bone Man II","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b64-h","x":"Gate in 40 Thieving, 49 Farming and 57 Herblore for Fairytale II; 38 Agility, 40 Fishing, 45 Thieving and 48 Herblore (none boostable) for Land of the Goblins; 32 and 40 Slayer, a fishing explosive and a mirror shield for the last bones. Carry in the ghostly outfit and the Land of the Goblins list: about 22/28. Exit The General's Shadow, Fairytale II, Land of the Goblins and Rag and Bone Man II done; about six goblin mail. Carries forward the goblin mail, flippers if they dropped. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect them before you start: an unsafe death here deletes them."},{"t":"The Stronghold and Tai Bwo Wannai scouts","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow scouts, Fairytale II, Land of the Goblins and Rag and Bone Man II","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t289-h","x":"Teleport to Varrock and take the spirit tree to the Grand Tree. Run south and meet the scout outside the gate for The General's Shadow; the Gnomish scout stands at the entrance of the Tree Gnome Stronghold. Get to Brimhaven (use a Brimhaven house tablet; the Ardougne boat works too) and run to the scout just east of Tai Bwo Wannai, south of the teak and mahogany trees (fairy ring CKR also gets you there). Keep the ghostly outfit on for each one. Done when the Falador, Stronghold and Tai Bwo Wannai scouts are met; the desert scout follows Fairytale II (the Falador scout stands between Falador's east wall and the Draynor Manor west fence)."},{"t":"Fairytale II and the desert scout","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow scouts, Fairytale II, Land of the Goblins and Rag and Bone Man II","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t290-h","x":"Take the fairy ring to Zanaris and complete Fairytale II – Cure a Queen (40 Thieving, which can't be boosted, 49 Farming and 57 Herblore; Martin the Master Gardener in Draynor Village starts it if you haven't; XP lamp on Slayer). Talk to Martin again after about five and a half minutes of logged-in time, and don't pickpocket him, which locks you out for ten minutes. In Zanaris, take and study Nuff's certificate and read the Rune Temple sign at the Cosmic Altar ruins; landing among penguins means you lack the certificate. The ring sequence to the Queen's hideout is AIR, DLR, DJQ, AJS, and if the ring's default click is the last destination, right-click it and choose Configure. Pickpocket the "},{"t":"Land of the Goblins and the Bouncer fight","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow scouts, Fairytale II, Land of the Goblins and Rag and Bone Man II","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t291-h","x":"Requirements Land of the Goblins: 38 Agility, 40 Fishing, 45 Thieving and 48 Herblore, none of them boostable. Teleport to Lumbridge, go into the Dorgeshuun mines and speak to Grubfoot to start Land of the Goblins. The wiki also says a UIM must unequip everything for this quest on top of carrying the items, so take the ghostly outfit off until you reach the Bouncer fight. Bring a light source, a toadflax potion (unf), yellow, blue, orange and purple dye (black dye is made from mushrooms during the quest, so carry a vial and a pestle and mortar), a raw slimy eel, a plain fishing rod (the oily one doesn't work) and 5 coins. The six keys for the crypt door vanish once used. Then finish The Gene"},{"t":"Finish Rag and Bone Man II","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The General's Shadow scouts, Fairytale II, Land of the Goblins and Rag and Bone Man II","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t292-h","x":"Finish Rag and Bone Man II with the last kills. Each listed monster has a 1 in 4 chance to drop its bone, so expect a few kills each, and the wiki lets you hand bones in in batches, so you need not hold them all at once: ogres (Feldip Hills, fairy ring AKS), which drop ogre ribs rather than a bone; mogres (fairy ring AIQ, the only spot), with Skippy and the Mogres done in full, 32 Slayer and a fishing explosive (sea mogres don't drop the bone); stay for flippers for seaweed runs; basilisks (fairy ring AJR, the only spot), with 40 Slayer and a mirror shield (20 Defence); their attacks can lower your stats, so a restore potion helps; trolls, if you didn't get one while questing. Then complete "},{"t":"The Wilderness easy and medium diaries, Grim Tales, and the Mos Le'Harmless quests","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b65-h","x":"Gate in the Wilderness easy and medium tasks' levels; Witch's House and Grim Tales' boostable levels; 42 Slayer (not boostable) for Rum Deal; 42 Agility, 45 Crafting, 50 Smithing and 40 Ranged for Cabin Fever; 40 Cooking for Trouble Brewing; 16 Crafting, 30 Construction and 50 Prayer for The Great Brain Robbery; ten furs from Baraek. Carry in only each Wilderness task's kit; 11 free slots for Cabin Fever; an empty inventory for Trouble Brewing (a Falador deathpile); about 26/28 for The Great Brain Robbery. Exit the Wilderness easy and medium, Falador medium and Morytania medium diaries; Grim Tales, Rum Deal, Cabin Fever and The Great Brain Robbery done; a Trouble Brewing game played; about 3"},{"t":"The Wilderness easy and medium diaries","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The Wilderness easy and medium diaries, Grim Tales, and the Mos Le'Harmless quests","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t294-h","x":"Go to the Edgeville Dungeon and into the Wilderness. Collect five red spiders' eggs (you can drop and pick up the same one five times), cross the handrail and kill an earth warrior. The easy tier also wants iron ore mined in the Wilderness (15 Mining) and a team cape equipped there (put it on inside; entering with it on doesn't count), and the medium tier an Earth Orb charged (60 Magic, an unpowered orb, 30 earth runes and 3 cosmic runes). Have the Mage of Zamorak teleport you to the Abyss if you haven't (an easy task; the one-time Abyss teleport during Temple of the Eye doesn't count), and if you have lost the small essence pouch from Enter the Abyss, the Dark Mage there replaces it for fre"},{"t":"Grim Tales","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The Wilderness easy and medium diaries, Grim Tales, and the Mos Le'Harmless quests","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t295-h","x":"Requirements Grim Tales needs Witch's House and 45 Farming, 52 Herblore, 58 Thieving, 59 Agility and 71 Woodcutting, all boostable. Do Grim Tales, using the tool leprechaun to take out your watering can and seed dibber mid-quest. Sylas in Taverley, just south of the house portal, starts it. The items are two vials of water, two tarromins, leather gloves, a rune axe, food, the Iban's staff with death and fire runes, water runes, an air staff, law runes, a ring of dueling and potions. Wear the leather gloves at the electrified gate, which otherwise hits for 17. In the tower the princess blocks the door, so go round the back and climb the crumbling east wall (58 Thieving). Grimgnash takes a fif"},{"t":"Rum Deal","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The Wilderness easy and medium diaries, Grim Tales, and the Mos Le'Harmless quests","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t296-h","x":"Requirements Rum Deal: 42 Slayer (not boostable) to start, plus 42 Crafting, 40 Farming, 47 Prayer and 50 Fishing (boostable). Do Rum Deal (leave with the Ectophial), killing a fever spider for the diary. Pirate Pete on the dock north of Port Phasmatys starts it. If you lose the blindweed, Captain Braindeath hands over what he stored earlier. The pressure lever only works once all five sea creatures are in the barrel. Davey only blesses the wrench if you have at least 47 Prayer points available, and the blessing doesn't drain them. The level 150 evil spirit's attacks are negated by Protect from Melee, or safespot it with Ranged, Magic or a halberd. Fever spiders give disease on hit even thro"},{"t":"Cabin Fever","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The Wilderness easy and medium diaries, Grim Tales, and the Mos Le'Harmless quests","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t297-h","x":"Do Cabin Fever, which needs 11 free slots and 42 Agility, 45 Crafting, 50 Smithing and 40 Ranged (none boostable), and talk to Bill Teach after it for 10,000 gp. Bill is in The Green Ghost inn in Port Phasmatys, and you board the easternmost ship, The Adventurous. The slots are for what you collect aboard, and on arrival at Mos Le'Harmless everything from the ships is taken back except a hammer, tinderbox, rope and swamp paste. On the enemy ship level 57 pirates attack, a missed rope jump empties your run energy, and leaving that ship loses the plunder you carry; only 10 plunder can be stored. Clean and ram the cannon before every load, because skipping a step blows it up for about 6 damage "},{"t":"Trouble Brewing with a planned death","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The Wilderness easy and medium diaries, Grim Tales, and the Mos Le'Harmless quests","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t298-h","x":"Requirements an empty inventory, no follower and an empty head slot, and a UIM can't use the chest by Honest Jimmy, so make it a planned death: take everything off in the Falador Castle courtyard and die to a White Knight, leave everything in the pile and use the Trouble Brewing minigame teleport, which needs 40 Cooking and Cabin Fever (just done) and no coins, so there is no charter fare and no change to drop. Then play one game of Trouble Brewing for the Morytania medium diary (40 Cooking). Be on the standard spellbook for this errand, so that afterwards the free Home Teleport puts you in Lumbridge, a short walk from Falador: you swapped to Lunar for the Waterbirth step, so before the plan"},{"t":"The Great Brain Robbery","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The Wilderness easy and medium diaries, Grim Tales, and the Mos Le'Harmless quests","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t299-h","x":"Do The Great Brain Robbery (lamp on Herblore; 16 Crafting, 30 Construction and 50 Prayer, none boostable, plus Recipe for Disaster's Pirate Pete and Another Cook's Quest): this is where the ten furs from Baraek go (bear or grey wolf fur; furs from Hunter creatures don't work), so buy them in Varrock just before, along with 18 planks. Brother Tranquility in Mos Le'Harmless starts it. Bring a holy symbol (Animal Magnetism used up the one from 2.1's Family Crest block, so cast a new one from a silver bar with a holy mould and string it with a ball of wool), a normal hammer (not the Imcando one), about 100 nails (the quest uses 38, bronze or iron nails can bend, and running out while building th"},{"t":"The elf quests and Song of the Elves","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b66-h","x":"Gate in 70 in Agility, Construction, Farming, Herblore, Hunter, Mining, Smithing and Woodcutting (none boostable); a runite bar; 60 Ranged and 50 Thieving for Mourning's End Part I; Thorgel's 47 items in two trips. Carry in each part's list only, the rest in a Falador deathpile; for Seren, phoenix necklaces, Guthix rests and the fight's setup. Exit Song of the Elves done and Prifddinas open; 68 Crafting or more (Chapter 3 takes it to 70); about 34.80 million gp. Carries forward the death talisman. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect them before you start: an unsafe death here deletes them."},{"t":"Herblore and Farming before the elf quests","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The elf quests and Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t301-h","x":"Check both before you start Regicide. Hover over Herblore in the skills tab: Song of the Elves needs 737,627 XP (70), and nothing boosts it. Your lamps and quests give about 64, so the rest, about 311,000 XP, should already have come from the herb runs. If you are short, count the herbs you hold (the sack, the leprechaun's noted stacks and your inventory) and make them into potions now, best XP first (cadantine, snapdragon, kwuarm, avantoe, irit, ranarr); if that is still not enough, keep harvesting and making potions before you begin Regicide, and do not start Mourning's End Part II below 70. Master Farmers give seeds too, but only about 10,000 XP of potions an hour, so put the effort into "},{"t":"Levels, Crafting and the runite bar","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The elf quests and Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t302-h","x":"Check your levels first: Song of the Elves needs 70 in Agility, Construction, Farming, Herblore, Hunter, Mining, Smithing and Woodcutting, and none of them can be boosted. Crafting is not on that list. Chapter 3 needs 70, and its Glass block takes you from 68 to 70, so you can stop at 68 here. If you'd rather reach 70 now, use Superglass Make, the wiki's UIM Crafting method from 77 Magic (with Lunar Diplomacy done): buy 10 buckets of sand and 10 soda ash from the charter-ship Trader Crewmembers each cycle, cast it and blow the glass straight away, dropping the products. Plain glassblowing at Port Phasmatys, as in 2.1, still works if you'd rather not use runes. Then make sure you have a runit"},{"t":"The elf quest line","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The elf quests and Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t303-h","x":"Then do the whole elf quest line: Regicide, Roving Elves (pick the crystal bow, as the wiki advises, but drop it once the elf line is done: Chapter 3 buys a fresh one from Islwyn when the Western Provinces hard diary needs it, which saves carrying a slot through the rest of the guide), Mourning's End Part I (60 Ranged and 50 Thieving, neither boostable), Mourning's End Part II and Song of the Elves. The line is linear; follow the wiki. Keep the full Mourner outfit from Mourning's End Part I, gas mask included, for Song of the Elves. The wiki's item list for Song of the Elves adds a steel full helm, platebody and platelegs, red and purple dye, silk, the runite bar, 8 limestone bricks, a tinde"},{"t":"Regicide","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The elf quests and Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t304-h","x":"For Regicide the wiki lists 10 Crafting (not boostable) and 56 Agility (boostable, not needed to start), 6 to 9 coal with at least 25 recommended (the wiki suggests noted coal, which a UIM can't have, so carry them in the coal bag), a bow and some arrows, 2 ropes (3 in case you fail) and a strip of cloth made on a loom from 4 balls of wool, not a bolt of cloth. Talk to King Lathas before you enter the Underground Pass, or the dense forest stops you. The level 110 Tyras guard can be safespotted, and he despawns if you are slow, so be ready before you approach. Add coal to the distiller gradually, since clicking quickly overheats it, and take at least three barrels from Iorwerth Camp in case y"},{"t":"Mourning's End Part II and Thorgel's list","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The elf quests and Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t305-h","x":"For Mourning's End Part II a UIM has no stockpile to draw on: Thorgel in the Death Altar trades a death talisman for a list of 47 items, brought over more than one trip. The list is babydragon bones, ball of wool, bronze bar, bronze med helm, bucket of milk, cake tin, cheese, chisel, cooked meat, egg, facemask, fishing rod, flax, gold ring, hammer, iron axe, iron nails, iron pickaxe, jug of wine, kebab, knife, leather boots, leather gloves, lobster pot, lockpick, necklace mould, needle, oak logs, pie dish, plank, pot of flour, potato cactus, 10 potatoes, pure essence, redberries, rope, rotten tomato, shears, skull, spade, swamp paste, thread, tinderbox, unicorn horn dust, vial of water, whit"},{"t":"Carrying the quest items","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The elf quests and Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t306-h","x":"For a UIM this line is a carrying problem, not a storage one, because the costume room can't hold any of it. Take the list a part at a time and keep what you aren't using in a Falador Castle deathpile (cooked food and potions vanish from a pile, so buy those fresh). The pile's 60 minutes only run while you are logged in, so plan each part to fit inside them. UIM risk Hespori's storage (Arno, 25,000 gp) is lost on any unsafe death, and this line has several fights, so don't use it here. Done when everything not in use waits in a Falador deathpile."},{"t":"The Fragment of Seren","p":"Chapter 2 › 2.3: More quests, and one of them is Song of the Elves › The elf quests and Song of the Elves","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-t307-h","x":"For the Fragment of Seren in Song of the Elves: farm belladonna in the Draynor patch for at least 8 nightshades, though the wiki's phoenix method suggests 20 or more (or use explosive liquid from the Digsite); you put a necklace on when she teleports you and eat a nightshade to trigger it before the big hit lands; buy blood and death runes for Ancient Magicks and make 6 to 10 phoenix necklaces (the wiki suggests 15 to 20 for its phoenix method, so make more if you struggle); the rock cake is reported to work in the fight, though the wiki says otherwise, so test it before you rely on it; it is negated when a ranged projectile is incoming, so it can keep your Hitpoints steady but can't trigger"},{"t":"End of Chapter 2","p":"Chapter 2","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-s7-h","x":"You finish Chapter 2 with Song of the Elves done, about 34.8 million gp (34,800,000) if you took the Sepulchre to 98, a costume room holding your costumes and armour and mage sets, and the skiff and sloop as working storage. End-of-chapter stats: Skill Level Notes Attack / Strength / Defence 62 / 77 / 70 Hitpoints / Ranged / Prayer 64 / 62 / 70 Magic 93 Mostly from Sepulchre alchs Runecraft / Construction 40 / 73 Agility 98 84 if you stopped the Sepulchre after floor 4 Herblore / Thieving 70 / 86 Herblore 70 comes mostly from potions made on the herb runs (lamps and quests give about 64); Thieving a few levels higher if you blackjacked more Crafting / Fletching 68 / 69 Chapter 3 needs 70 Cra"},{"t":"Where things live at the end of Chapter 2","p":"Chapter 2 › End of Chapter 2","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b67-h","x":"Storage What it holds Costume room (armour case, cape rack, magic wardrobe, fancy dress box, toy box, treasure chest) Quest armour sets, capes, magic sets, costumes and clue items Skiff and sloop cargo holds Only what they accept: repair kits, cannonballs, charting supplies, cider, beer glasses, whirlpool surprises, fish offcuts, empty fish crates and fishing tools and bait, which stay; salvage, fish, bounty items and courier crates, which the wiki says are lost when the ship is summoned, quick-transported or recovered (no gear, potions, bars, quest items or noted items) Kegs Whirlpool surprise and kraken ink stout Aldarin windmill nest One unnoted tradeable item whose item value and Grand E"},{"t":"Verification list","p":"Chapter 2 › End of Chapter 2","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b68-h","x":"Every claim this chapter once marked as unchecked has now been checked on the wiki (13 November 2026): (checked: Mahogany Homes pays 3 carpenter points a Novice contract and 4 an Adept one, and the plank sack costs 350; the wiki's averages are about 1,894 XP a Novice contract and 3,260 an Adept one, which is why the block now reaches 62 at the sack and keeps the extra contracts only as a fallback); (checked: the celestial ring is Dusuri's, in the Mining Guild, for 2,000 stardust; the guild needs 60 Mining, boostable with the Rising Sun Inn's dwarven stout, which costs 3 gp); (checked: tea in a porcelain cup, from oak shelves 2, gives +2 Construction; the UIM Construction guide names the Aviu"},{"t":"Sources","p":"Chapter 2 › End of Chapter 2","u":"chapter-2.html#ch2-b69-h","x":"Wiki pages used for this chapter's UIM changes include Ultimate Ironman Guide, Mahogany Homes, Recruitment Drive, Ice Queen's Lair, Heroes' Quest, One Small Favour, Death to the Dorgeshuun, Another Slice of H.A.M., Temple of the Eye, Enakhra's Lament/Quick guide, Icthlarin's Little Helper, Wanted!, Dusty key, Bear Your Soul, Olaf's Quest, A Tail of Two Cats, Ratcatchers, In Search of the Myreque, In Aid of the Myreque, Animal Magnetism, Ghosts Ahoy, Ernest the Chicken, The Slug Menace, Waterbirth Island Dungeon, Kebab, Ancient staff, Efaritay's aid, Lockpick, Mithril axe, Holy symbol, Steel warhammer, Blair's Armour, Varrock Swordshop and Horvik's Armour Shop."},{"t":"Where Chapter 2 left you","p":"Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-s1-h","x":"You start with Song of the Elves done and about 34.8 million gp (34,800,000, which already counts the Sepulchre income, about 1.2 million gp of teak plank fees, the shield right half, the costume room, the two bought god staves and the air runes; it could be 1 to 2 million lower if you count the Sepulchre's fletching and rune costs). You didn't pay into Miscellania. Your house is in Hosidius, Kourend, with a costume room (a teak armour case, a mahogany cape rack and magic wardrobe, a teak fancy dress box and treasure chest, an oak toy box), a marble lectern in place of the mahogany eagle one, a spirit tree and a kitchen for tea. You have the skiff and the sloop, Hespori's item retrieval at 6"},{"t":"What changes for a UIM in Chapter 3","p":"Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-s2-h","x":"Deathbanks are for skilling; the costume room is for everything else. The wiki's UIM use of an item retrieval service, most often Hespori's (Arno, 25,000 gp, from 65 Farming), is to store everything while you do something with no risk of death. Anything stored there is lost if you die an unsafe death, and the wiki does not say how a death at Vorkath counts (his own retrieval, Torfinn, 100,000 gp, holds only that death), so treat it as a risk. So collect your deathbank before any Slayer or boss trip, keep long-term items in the costume room, and carry only the trip's kit. Two exceptions: the Corrupted Gauntlet stores everything you carry in an instanced bank and an Ultimate Ironman who dies t"},{"t":"Chapter 3 at a glance","p":"Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-s3-h","x":"Section Goals UIM handling 3.1 Slayer and the red prison Construction to 78 and the house upgrades, Runecraft to 65 and The Final Dawn, black mask, Crafting to 80, Slayer to 100 combat, elite void, the Fremennik Exiles, chinchompas to 92 Ranged, ship upgrades and charting, the Corrupted Gauntlet for the Bow of Faerdhinen and crystal armour Mahogany Homes instead of Miscellania; Guardians of the Rift instead of daeyalt lavas; Hespori retrieval for Slayer; gems kept in the gem bag and cut at Guardians of the Rift; red chinchompas only; Gauntlet loot carried noted 3.2 Quest cape, quality of life Raiments of the Eye, Dragon Slayer II, Monkey Madness II, Desert Treasure II, The Blood Moon Rises a"},{"t":"3.1: Slayer and the red prison","p":"Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-s4-h","x":"Section 3.1 is long and ends with the Corrupted Gauntlet. It is Slayer to 100 combat, Ranged to 92 or 93 with chinchompas, a round of Sailing upgrades, and about 70 hours of the Corrupted Gauntlet. You start with about 34.8 million gp, spend most of it on broad arrowheads, and end 3.1 with only about 389,000 gp in hand, because the Gauntlet loot is alched in 3.2 and two Sailing purchases (the cannonballs and the sloop's planks) move there with it. Most of it suits a UIM well: Slayer drops are mostly stackable or alchable, chinchompas stack, and the Gauntlet costs only the run if you walk in with an empty inventory and nothing worn."},{"t":"House tablets, the Mage Training Arena and Construction to 78","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b1-h","x":"This block builds the stockpiles and the house the rest of Chapter 3 leans on. Tablets and scrolls stack, so 500 house tablets and 258 redirection scrolls cost you two slots; the Construction levels pay for a jewellery box that replaces every games necklace and ring of dueling you would otherwise carry. It comes first because everything after it leans on it: the tablets and the box replace most of the teleport items you would carry on every Slayer task and diary trip, the scrolls speed up the Slayer trips that follow, and the costume room pieces are where each set you finish from here on is stored. Gate in Song of the Elves done; 70 Construction for Expert contracts; 86 Magic for Plank Make;"},{"t":"House tablets","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › House tablets, the Mage Training Arena and Construction to 78","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t6-h","x":"Aim for about 500 house tablets; a gravestone method won't top them up for a UIM, but tablets stack, so the whole stock is one slot. Make them as Chapter 2 did, in loops of about 24: Mine clay. The Prifddinas mine is a good source. Teleport home and wet the clay with buckets of water from your kitchen sink. Make the tablets at the marble lectern: each costs a law, an air and an earth rune and one soft clay. Repeat until you hold about 500. Keep the runes in the rune pouch so the clay gets the slots, and if the runes run low, finish the loop you are in and restock before you mine again, rather than carrying clay you cannot turn into tablets. A bracelet of clay skips the water, and in the Prif"},{"t":"Redirection scrolls at Nightmare Zone","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › House tablets, the Mage Training Arena and Construction to 78","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t7-h","x":"Earn the redirection scrolls at Nightmare Zone, north-west of Yanille bank (fairy ring CIQ, then walk through Yanille). You have far more than the five qualifying quests it needs. Dreams are paid from Dominic Onion's coffer in multiples of 1,000 gp, and a death inside a dream ends it without losing your items or touching a deathbank, so it is a safe AFK activity. The one thing a death does cost you is anything you dropped on the ground during the dream, so never drop an item to make room. Logging out inside a dream ends it, so finish one before you stop playing; to leave early, drink a wake potion on the north or south side of the arena. Put coins in Dominic's coffer and choose Endurance or "},{"t":"Catherby tablets","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › House tablets, the Mage Training Arena and Construction to 78","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t8-h","x":"Make the Catherby tablets for your herb runs at the Lunar lectern in the westernmost building on Lunar Isle, as Chapter 2 did (the Astral Altar on the island switches you to the Lunar spellbook and back): 87 Magic on the Lunar spellbook, and 3 law, 10 water and 3 astral runes and a soft clay for each. Make enough for the herb runs of the whole chapter; they stack in one slot. Done when the Catherby tablets are made. Coins: unchanged · Slots: soft clay and the rune pouch · Requirements: 87 Magic, Lunar spellbook"},{"t":"The Mage Training Arena","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › House tablets, the Mage Training Arena and Construction to 78","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t9-h","x":"Optional, recommended: go back to the Mage Training Arena for the Mage's book and the infinity boots. The boots cost 120 Telekinetic, 120 Alchemist, 1,200 Enchantment and 120 Graveyard pizazz points and need 50 Magic and 25 Defence to wear. The arena is safe, and you can log out inside most of its rooms without losing progress (the Telekinetic Theatre is the exception). It lies north of the Emir's Arena, north-east of Al Kharid, and the minigame teleport works once you have spoken to the Entrance Guardian. You need points in all four rooms before the Rewards Guardian upstairs sells you anything, and each room pays its own currency with its own cap (8,000 Telekinetic, 8,000 Graveyard, 32,000 "},{"t":"Construction to 78 with Mahogany Homes","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › House tablets, the Mage Training Arena and Construction to 78","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t10-h","x":"Managing Miscellania isn't available to a UIM, and the wiki's UIM Construction method at every level is Mahogany Homes, which gives far more XP per plank than building in the house. From 73, take Expert contracts, which need 70 Construction and use mahogany planks. Your first contract has to come from Amy in Falador; after that, Angelo in Hosidius, next to your house, hands them out too. Contracts can be in any of the four towns (Falador, Varrock, East Ardougne, Hosidius) and can't be cancelled, and invisible boosts like the crystal saw don't count toward a contract's level. Amy stands just south of Falador's park, at the minigame icon; Marlo in Varrock and Ellie in East Ardougne work from a"},{"t":"Build the gallery and the costume room upgrades","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › House tablets, the Mage Training Arena and Construction to 78","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t11-h","x":"The levels are the wiki's. The crystal saw (+3) works on furniture but not on rooms (it is also destroyed on death: if a planned death has taken yours, ask Brimstail in the Tree Gnome Stronghold for a new seed and sing it at the bowl in his cave, free, before you build), so the achievement gallery that holds the jewellery box (80 to build) needs a visible boost. A spicy stew with three doses of orange spice is random, from −5 to +5, and the wiki puts an exact +5 at 8.3%, so from 75 the room is a gamble. At 78 it isn't: your kitchen's tea (+2) builds the gallery, and tea plus the saw (+5) builds every piece below, up to the armour case's 82. Drink tea from your kitchen and build the achieveme"},{"t":"Runecraft to 65, The Final Dawn and two hard diaries","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b2-h","x":"Runecraft is the one skill Chapter 2 left low, and this block fixes it the UIM way: Guardians of the Rift supplies its own essence and pays the pouches and pearls this chapter needs. 65 Runecraft then unlocks the last Varlamore quest and two hard diaries. Gate in 27 Runecraft and 56 Agility for Guardians of the Rift; 66 Thieving, 52 Runecraft and 52 Fletching (not boostable) and the four Varlamore quests for The Final Dawn; 70 Crafting for the Lumbridge hard diary; the shield halves, 60 Smithing and 33,750 gp of house moves for the Ardougne hard diary. Carry in a pickaxe at Guardians of the Rift; each quest part's list. Exit 65 Runecraft; The Final Dawn done with the Arkan blade; the Lumbrid"},{"t":"Guardians of the Rift to 65 Runecraft","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Runecraft to 65, The Final Dawn and two hard diaries","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t13-h","x":"Lava runes from daeyalt essence are possible for a UIM now that Noranna can hand the essence over noted (23 September 2026), but each lap still needs binding necklaces, a ring of dueling and earth runes restocked from your inventory, while Guardians of the Rift supplies its own essence. The wiki's UIM method from 10 to 99 is Guardians of the Rift, so train there to 65. It is safe, and it needs only a pickaxe (a chisel too if you craft rift guardians) and 56 Agility, not boostable, for the large guardian remains. It pays twice for this chapter: the abyssal pearls buy the Raiments of the Eye in 3.2, and the Rewards Guardian pays the medium, large and giant pouches as loot for the colossal pouc"},{"t":"The Final Dawn","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Runecraft to 65, The Final Dawn and two hard diaries","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t14-h","x":"The Final Dawn needs 66 Thieving, 52 Runecraft and 52 Fletching, none boostable (check your Thieving and Fletching in the skills tab and train them first if they fall short), plus The Heart of Darkness, Twilight's Promise, Children of the Sun and Perilous Moons. The items are your emissary robes, any bones (not sun-kissed) or meat for the dog in Janus' safe house, and a knife and a beer, which you can get during the quest. The wiki recommends 85 combat with melee and ranged gear. Take each stage's items only for that stage. The wiki's slot counts are tight for a UIM: two free slots for the first temple stage, one bone or meat item for the dog, four free slots for the drinks in Cam Torum and "},{"t":"The Lumbridge hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Runecraft to 65, The Final Dawn and two hard diaries","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t15-h","x":"Requirements Lumbridge hard diary: 70 Crafting and you start this chapter at 68, so leave it until the Glass block below has taken you to 70. Complete the Lumbridge hard diary, lamp on Herblore. The tasks: cast Bones to Peaches in Al Kharid palace (60 Magic; the tablet doesn't count, so use the spell you unlocked in Chapter 1, with 4 earth, 4 water and 2 nature runes and bones); squeeze past the jutting wall to the cosmic altar (46 Agility, Lost City; you also need a way into Zanaris, a Dramen or Lunar staff, or the Abyss); craft 56 cosmic runes at once from essence, without runic extracts (59 Runecraft and 28 pure or daeyalt essence; guardian essence doesn't count, and you reach the altar b"},{"t":"The Ardougne hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Runecraft to 65, The Final Dawn and two hard diaries","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t16-h","x":"Complete the Ardougne hard diary. The tasks: recharge a skills necklace or combat bracelet at the totem in the Legends' Guild (Legends' Quest done; the piece must be less than fully charged, so use a teleport from it first); enter the Magic Guild (66 Magic); steal from a chest in Ardougne Castle (72 Thieving; a lockpick is recommended: Martin Thwait's Lost and Found in the Rogues' Den sells them for 20 gp, and this chapter uses one again for the Port Piscarilius artefacts, the deathwing dungeon, and Secrets of the North, so keep it in your kit (Desert Treasure II's Ghorrock Prison hides its own lockpick, and the wiki recommends one for Vardorvis)); have a zookeeper put you in Ardougne Zoo's "},{"t":"Cave horrors, the Morytania hard diary and Fallen From Grace","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b3-h","x":"Camp cave horrors off-task for a black mask (1/512 per kill). They need 58 Slayer, Cabin Fever for the Mos Le'Harmless Cave, and a light source; the cave horror page says Protect from Melee fully blocks their special, so you can do without a witchwood icon, and the wiki lists safespots near the entrance. The same stretch finishes the Morytania hard diary, which pays the bonecrusher the chinchompa block needs, and Fallen From Grace, which opens Mortimer and the Mad Angel. Gate in 58 Slayer and Cabin Fever for cave horrors; the 30 quests Rag and Bone Man III needs; the Morytania hard diary's list; 62 Sailing, 60 Crafting, 53 Mining and 47 Runecraft for Fallen From Grace; 50,000 gp for a dragon"},{"t":"Set up the cave session","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Cave horrors, the Morytania hard diary and Fallen From Grace","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t18-h","x":"For a UIM, this is the first long PvM session of the chapter, so set it up the UIM way: Collect any deathbank first. Leave everything you don't fight with in the costume room. Take your regular Slayer gear with Protect from Melee (which allows an amulet of strength), thralls, a light source and the herb sack; a proselyte hauberk or fighter torso is fine either way. Go to Mos Le'Harmless and down into the cave; the wiki's recommended spot is by the swamp near the cave entrance. Cave horrors are level 80 and aggressive, with 55 Hitpoints and a magical melee hit of up to 9. Their special always deals 10% of your base Hitpoints and is an area attack, so it can hit anyone standing beside the horr"},{"t":"Camp cave horrors for the black mask","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Cave horrors, the Morytania hard diary and Fallen From Grace","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t19-h","x":"Kill cave horrors until the black mask drops. Alch as you go and keep the drops that stack. The nature runes (3, 4 or 6 at a time) and the coins stack, and every kill leaves a big bone, which does not stack, so pick up only the 13 you need for the next Robin visit and leave the rest rather than filling your inventory. If it doesn't drop at 1 in 512, about one player in ten still has no mask after 1,180 kills. Don't stall there: finish the Morytania hard diary and Fallen From Grace, kill cave horrors again on Slayer tasks later, and leave the Slayer helmet and the Desert hard diary (it needs the helmet) until the mask drops. Then imbue the black mask at Nightmare Zone (1,250,000 reward points"},{"t":"Rag and Bone Man III","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Cave horrors, the Morytania hard diary and Fallen From Grace","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t20-h","x":"The cave horrors are on the wish list of Rag and Bone Man III, a Quest Month quest (November 2026), so start it now. It needs 58 Slayer and 30 quests, all of which this guide has done by now: Rag and Bone Man I and II, Skippy and the Mogres, Creature of Fenkenstrain, Dragon Slayer I, The Great Brain Robbery, Cabin Fever, Pirate's Treasure, Rum Deal, Priest in Peril, Zogre Flesh Eaters, Big Chompy Bird Hunting, Jungle Potion, Druidic Ritual, Recipe for Disaster's Freeing Pirate Pete and Another Cook's Quest, Cook's Assistant, Defender of Varrock, Shield of Arrav, Temple of Ikov, Below Ice Mountain, Family Crest, Garden of Tranquillity, The Restless Ghost, What Lies Below, Rune Mysteries, Rome"},{"t":"The Morytania hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Cave horrors, the Morytania hard diary and Fallen From Grace","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t21-h","x":"Complete the Morytania hard diary, lamp on Herblore. The tasks: enter the Kharyrll portal in your house (Desert Treasure I, 66 Magic, 50 Construction; 200 law and 100 blood runes, and a portal chamber if you don't have one; a portal nexus that already leads there also counts); climb the advanced spike chain in the Slayer Tower without taking damage (71 Agility, boostable; it is on the first floor, beside the infernal mages, and leads up to the second floor near the nechryael; wear the Slayer helmet or a nose peg for the aberrant spectres, which the wiki ties to the ground-floor chain below); harvest watermelons from the Harmony Island allotment (a started Great Brain Robbery, 47 Farming, 3 w"},{"t":"Charge the bonecrusher","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Cave horrors, the Morytania hard diary and Fallen From Grace","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t22-h","x":"The chinchompa block needs at least 24,000 bonecrusher charges, so start now. Visit Robin, in the Green Ghost inn in Port Phasmatys, with 13 bones each time: he gives a pot of bonemeal and a bucket of slime for each bone, which you worship at the Ectofuntus for ecto-tokens that charge the bonecrusher. He takes 13 bones a day after the medium Morytania diary and 26 after the hard one, so two visits a day give 3,250 charges. He doesn't take noted bones or give noted items, so each visit needs 13 bones and 13 more free slots. Pick the bones up on the Slayer task you're on just before you go; any dragons are good for it, and so are the big bones the cave horrors leave. Robin takes bones of any k"},{"t":"Fallen From Grace","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Cave horrors, the Morytania hard diary and Fallen From Grace","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t23-h","x":"Requirements Fallen From Grace needs 62 Sailing, 60 Crafting, 53 Mining and 47 Runecraft (none boostable) and Pandemonium. Buy a dragon mace at the Heroes' Guild (50,000 gp; it needs 60 Attack and Heroes' Quest): the Mad Angel, the quest's boss, is weak to crush. The shop is the Happy Heroes' H'emporium on the Guild's first floor, and it holds one mace and restocks every five minutes, so if someone has just bought it, wait a few minutes or hop worlds. You keep the mace for the Hallowfell session in the Slayer block, which fights the same Mad Angel again. Bring a pickaxe, a chisel, full combat gear, food and a stamina potion; the wiki recommends 75 combat and 43 Prayer. You can't teleport to "},{"t":"Golem Crafting for the jeweller's chisel","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Cave horrors, the Morytania hard diary and Fallen From Grace","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t24-h","x":"Optional, recommended: do Golem Crafting until you get the jeweller's chisel. Get the furs from falconry (dashing or dark kebbits) and carry them in your fur pouch. Golem Crafting is the activity Fallen From Grace unlocks on Wyrmscraig, and it needs 60 Crafting. Each golem takes four sunstones, a chisel and a hammer: mine the sunstone, chisel some into cores, carve the golem on an empty plinth, then power it with a core and a fur. Bring an empty gem bag, because the uncut gems each golem gives go straight into it, and the wiki wants at least 25 free inventory slots. Only certain furs work, and tatty ones don't. An ironman collects every fur personally; the wiki singles out dark kebbit fur be"},{"t":"Glass, Crafting to 80 and the Pharaoh's sceptre","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b4-h","x":"Crafting is the one skill Chapter 3 needs higher than Chapter 2 left it, and the UIM way to train it is to make each cast's glass and use it on the spot. The same block gets the Pharaoh's sceptre, your teleport to the desert and, in 3.2, the occult altar's material. Gate in 77 Magic and Lunar Diplomacy for Superglass Make; about 265,000 gp for sand and soda ash; 21 Thieving and a started Icthlarin's Little Helper for Pyramid Plunder; 75 Crafting (boosted) for the glory. Carry in one cast's sand and seaweed (21 slots) or sand and soda ash (26 slots), then the orbs. Exit 80 Crafting; an amulet of glory; one Pharaoh's sceptre; about 32,305,000 gp. Carries forward the charged glory (gem mining),"},{"t":"Crafting to 70 with Superglass Make","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Glass, Crafting to 80 and the Pharaoh's sceptre","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t26-h","x":"Chapter 2 leaves you at 68 Crafting, about 133,000 XP short of 70: about 2,500 molten glass blown into unpowered orbs at 52.5 XP each. A UIM can't bank the sand or seaweed, so every cast is its own small loop: Buy 13 buckets of sand and 13 soda ash from a Trader Crewmember on any charter ship, as in Chapter 2 (5 gp each), which is the most a soda ash cast fits (26 slots with the rune pouch and pipe beside them), or harvest giant seaweed from your Fossil Island patches and use 18 sand to 3 seaweed (21 slots). Cast Superglass Make: 10 air, 6 fire and 2 astral runes, kept in the rune pouch. Blow the glass into unpowered orbs with your glassblowing pipe and drop them; you make the Gauntlet's orb"},{"t":"Crafting to 80 with arteglass","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Glass, Crafting to 80 and the Pharaoh's sceptre","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t27-h","x":"From 70, add Thieving to the same loop: blow your glass while stealing artefacts in Port Piscarilius. Arteglass also gives Thieving, which 3.2 needs at 91 for the second sceptre. Talk to Captain Khaled in the foodhall on the east side of Port Piscarilius for a house in the south-western residential district (49 Thieving; you need a lockpick or hair clip). Pick the lock on the drawers that hold the artefact: upstairs in most houses, on the ground floor in the northern one. Each pick gives 750 Thieving XP. Walk back past the patrolling guards, using their routes and the guard lures on the east and south-east bridges. Any teleport, a random event or logging out removes the artefact, and a guard"},{"t":"Pyramid Plunder for the sceptre","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Glass, Crafting to 80 and the Pharaoh's sceptre","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t28-h","x":"Do Pyramid Plunder with the sceptre-and-XP method until you have one Pharaoh's sceptre (a second comes in 3.2, ideally at 91 Thieving or later). You need 21 Thieving, which boosts don't count toward, and a started Icthlarin's Little Helper for Sophanem. Get there by the magic carpet from Pollnivneach (200 gp, 100 with Rogue Trader started, free after the hard Desert diary) or, once you have the sceptre, its Jalsavrah teleport. Jalsavrah is the northern pyramid in Sophanem, and the AKP fairy ring that would shorten the trip only opens with the quest in 3.2, so for now it is the carpet. Find the right one of the four doors into the pyramid; it changes every 25 minutes, and a wrong one stuns yo"},{"t":"Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b5-h","x":"This is the long combat stretch of 3.1. Train Slayer until 100 combat and claim five hard diaries as their Slayer levels arrive, so every diary trip rides on a task you were doing anyway. Gate in the black mask and Slayer setup; a divine magic potion for Ice Barrage; 300 Slayer points for Broader Fletching; each diary's levels and quests as listed. Carry in the task's setup and nothing else. Exit 100 combat (about 78 Attack, 85 Strength, 75+ Defence, 72+ Prayer, 78 Hitpoints, 75 Slayer); the Kourend & Kebos, Wilderness, Falador, Desert and Karamja hard diaries; easy and medium Combat Achievements; about 29,105,000 gp. Carries forward a shield left half if it dropped, Broader Fletching, the S"},{"t":"The UIM Slayer routine","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t30-h","x":"Every trip is a trip with what you carry and nothing else: Collect any deathbank before you start. Keep every set you aren't using in the costume room. Carry the task's setup: gear, food, potions, the rune pouch with thrall or barrage runes, the herb sack and the bonecrusher. Alch as you go. Most drops are runes, coins, noted resources and alchables; carry noted stacks to unnote at a bank when you want to process them. A death leaves a deathpile where you fell. It lasts 60 minutes of logged-in time, so go straight back for it before you resupply or start another fight. The targets for 100 combat are 78 Attack, 85 Strength, 75+ Defence and 72+ Prayer, which should give about 78 Hitpoints and "},{"t":"Attack to 72 and Hallowfell","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t31-h","x":"Train Attack first, to 72, on accurate. Then fight the Mad Angel at Ardeaglais on Wyrmscraig with your standard setup and the dragon mace for Hallowfell. The repeatable fight is open because you finished Fallen From Grace in the cave horror block. Ardeaglais is the cathedral on the southern side of Wyrmscraig; a necklace of passage reaches Wyrmscraig, and a slayer ring's Wyrmscraig Cavern teleport leaves you a short walk from the cathedral's basement. Hallowfell drops at 1/127, so plan a long session. If it hasn't dropped after about 290 kills (about nine players in ten have it by then), carry on with the dragon mace and come back later. Protect from Melee cuts her normal hit from 31 to 5, a"},{"t":"Strength, Defence and Arclight","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t32-h","x":"After Hallowfell, train Strength until it is about seven levels ahead of Attack, then alternate. At 75 Attack, make Arclight. You make it by using Darklight on the altar in the centre of the Catacombs of Kourend while you carry three ancient shards; anywhere else the game tells you it needs the catacombs altar. It starts with 1,000 charges and each successful hit spends one (special attacks spend none), and when the charges run out it falls back to behaving like Darklight, so recharge it with more shards instead of remaking it. If you lose Darklight, Sir Prysin sells another for 1,000 gp. The wiki puts a 70% accuracy and damage bonus against demons on it, so keep it for demon tasks. Use accu"},{"t":"Magic and spellbooks","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t33-h","x":"You start at 93 Magic, so a divine magic potion (or another Magic boost) is what lets you cast Ice Barrage (94) through whole barrage tasks. Without one, use Smoke Barrage for ankou and dust devils and Ice Burst for dagannoths. Always cast on defensive. To switch spellbooks, use the Pharaoh's sceptre's Jaldraocht teleport for Ancient Magicks, and Tyss at the Arceuus dark altar (fairy ring CIS) for Arceuus, until the occult altar in 3.2 swaps them at home. The sceptre holds 25 charges now and 50 once the Desert hard diary below is claimed. Done when you barrage on defensive with a Magic boost on every barrage task."},{"t":"Broader Fletching, the Slayer helmet and the Necklace of Fangs","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t34-h","x":"Unlock Broader Fletching for 300 Slayer points from any Slayer master's reward menu; broad arrows need 52 Fletching. Buy it before you spend coins on arrowheads in the next section, because you can't make broad arrows without it. If your Slayer points allow, buy the Slayer helmet unlock (the wiki lists 400 points) and make the helmet from your black mask. The helmet combines a nose peg, a facemask, earmuffs, a spiny helmet, an enchanted gem and the black mask, plus reinforced goggles because you finished A Porcine of Interest in Chapter 1, and an eternal gem can't stand in for the enchanted one, so check you hold every part. Any charges on the mask are lost when it becomes part of the helmet"},{"t":"Any time: a shield left half","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t35-h","x":"Save a shield left half, if one drops, for the Ardougne hard diary's dragon square shield. Done when you hold a shield left half, or the Ardougne hard diary is claimed."},{"t":"62 Slayer: the Kourend & Kebos hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t36-h","x":"Complete the Kourend & Kebos hard diary, lamp on Herblore, when the last of its requirements is met. The tasks: enter the Woodcutting Guild (60 Woodcutting); smelt an adamantite bar in the Forsaken Tower, not with Superheat (70 Smithing, adamantite ore and 6 coal); kill a Lizardman Shaman in the Lizardman Temple, the cave beneath Molch where six shamans stand (use Protect from Missiles; their acid attack hits for 25 to 30 and can poison you, so have antipoison); mine some lovakite (65 Mining); plant logavano seeds at the Tithe Farm (74 Farming, boostable); kill a zombie in the Shayzien Crypts (a light source); teleport to Xeric's Heart with Xeric's talisman (charged with lizardman fangs, one"},{"t":"68 Slayer: the Wilderness hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t37-h","x":"Do it the Chapter 2 way, one boss or task per trip. The wiki warns that every task is in the Wilderness, so expect attacks from player killers: Leave everything you don't need in a deathpile outside the Wilderness, such as the Edgeville Monastery one. Go in with only that trip's kit. Come back inside the hour. A death to a player hands most of what you carry to the killer. The ten tasks: cast a god spell on another player in the Wilderness (Mage Arena I, 60 Magic, a god staff; the spell has to hit, so you need a second player, and the wiki says a cast inside the Mage Arena counts too; each cast takes 1 to 4 air, 1 to 4 fire and 2 blood runes); charge an air orb (66 Magic, an unpowered orb, 3"},{"t":"72 Slayer: the Falador hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t38-h","x":"The eleven tasks: craft 140 mind runes at once from essence, in one craft and without Extracts (56 Runecraft with 28 pure essence, or 42 with three Raiments of the Eye pieces; mind cores don't count, and you need a mind or catalytic talisman or tiara, or the Abyss, to reach the altar); change your family crest to Saradomin with Sir Renitee (70 Prayer, 16 Construction, 5,000 gp; if your crest is already Saradomin, the wiki says the task needs an extra 5,000 gp to cycle to another crest and back); kill the Giant Mole under Falador Park (a spade and a light source); kill a skeletal wyvern in the Asgarnia Ice Dungeon (72 Slayer and protection from its icy breath); do a lap of the Falador rooftop"},{"t":"The Slayer helmet: the Desert hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t39-h","x":"The ten tasks: knock out and pickpocket a Menaphite thug (The Feud, 65 Thieving, any blackjack); mine granite (45 Mining; Cape Conch granite counts too); refill waterskins with Humidify outside a desert settlement (Dream Mentor, 68 Magic, the Lunar spellbook, a waterskin that isn't full, and 1 fire, 3 water and 1 astral rune); kill the Kalphite Queen (below); do a lap of the Pollnivneach rooftop course (70 Agility); kill a dust devil in the desert cave with the Slayer helmet on (a started Desert Treasure I, 65 Slayer, 10 Defence for the helmet; the helmet has to be equipped for the kill, and the wiki adds that ironmen need Cabin Fever done, which Chapter 2 did); switch to Ancient Magicks at "},{"t":"100 combat: the Karamja hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t40-h","x":"The ten tasks: become a Fight Pits champion (you need at least one other player in the pit); kill a Ket-Zek in the Fight Caves; they appear from wave 31, and the caves are a safe minigame (a death leaves you outside with your items); eat an oomlie wrap (cook a raw oomlie in a palm leaf, 50 Cooking); craft nature runes from essence (44 Runecraft, pure essence); cook a karambwan thoroughly (Tai Bwo Wannai Trio, 30 Cooking; bring a few raw karambwans); kill a deathwing in the dungeon under the Kharazi Jungle (part of Legends' Quest, 50 Agility, 50 Thieving, 52 Mining and 50 Strength, all of which can be boosted; an axe, a machete, a pickaxe and a lockpick); use the crossbow shortcut south of th"},{"t":"Combat Achievements","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Slayer to 100 combat, and the diaries on the way","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t41-h","x":"Complete Combat Achievement tasks along the way. If you're missing any at 100 combat, go back for them, stew-boosting Slayer as needed, then claim the easy and medium rewards, lamps on Herblore. Claim the medium tier before Pest Control, because it raises a veteran win from 5 points to 7 in the next section. His Faithful Servants is already done: Chapter 2 finished it on the Kourend Barrows run, and Desert Treasure II's requirements in 3.2 include it. Done when you are 100 combat and the easy and medium Combat Achievements are claimed. Coins: about 29,105,000 gp (you spend about 3.2 million gp on runes, potions and food over this stretch) · Slots: the task's setup, nothing else · Requirement"},{"t":"Broad arrows and void at Pest Control","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b6-h","x":"Spend most of your coins on broad arrowhead packs, keeping 2,500,000 gp in reserve. The crystal bow and halberd later in this section cost 1,650,000 gp, the skiff's camphor planks about 112,000 gp, and the Hespori collections during the Gauntlet about 350,000 gp, so that is what the reserve is for. You should hold about 29.1 million before this stop, so the packs take about 26.6 million. The broad arrows are for the chinchompa block's Ranged and the rest of the chapter; the void is your ranged set until the Bow of Faerdhinen. Gate in Broader Fletching; 100 combat for the veteran boat; the Sepulchre's headless arrows; a 2,500,000 gp reserve. Carry in the fletching stacks. Exit the arrowheads "},{"t":"Buy the broad arrowheads","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Broad arrows and void at Pest Control","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t43-h","x":"Any Slayer master sells broad arrowheads, singly at 55 gp or in packs of 100 for 5,500 gp. Everything here stacks for a UIM: the arrowheads, the shafts, the feathers and the finished broad arrows. Buy packs from a Slayer master and open them. The stock slowly runs down if you open them fast, so hop worlds if it falls to 700 or lower. Stop when only the 2,500,000 gp reserve is left. For the headless arrows, fifteen of which go into each broad arrow action with fifteen arrowheads (150 Fletching XP an action), use the stack you fletched at the Sepulchre in 2.2 (up to a million, one slot). If it runs out, make more: arrow shafts cost 1 gp at Dargaud's Bow and Arrows in the Ranging Guild (stock 1"},{"t":"Pest Control for the ranged void","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Broad arrows and void at Pest Control","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t44-h","x":"Play Pest Control on the veteran lander (100 combat), fletching broad arrows during the games and contributing only as much as you need for the points. Pest Control is safe: you respawn on the lander with your items, and a deathbank isn't touched. Pets aren't allowed on the landers, and alchemy spells and dwarf multicannons can't be used there. Reach the Void Knights' Outpost with the Minigame Teleport (20-minute cooldown) or the squire at the Port Sarim docks, south of the Lady Lumbridge. Board the veteran lander. In each game, protect the Void Knight from the pests of the four portals. You win by destroying all four portals or by surviving 20 minutes. Keep your activity bar above 0%, or th"},{"t":"The Fremennik Exiles, A Night at the Theatre and Monkey Madness II's start","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b7-h","x":"Do The Fremennik Exiles, A Night at the Theatre (lamps on Ranged) and Hopespear's Will, then start Monkey Madness II until you can reach Kruk's Dungeon and its maniacal monkeys. These are linear quests with long item lists; take each part's items only for that part, and collect any deathbank first. Gate in each quest's skills and quests as listed; a Fremennik shield from Bardur; 75 Woodcutting (you arrive with 73: the two levels are in the step below) and 60 Firemaking for the Grand Tree balloon route, which Monkey Madness II needs unlocked before you can start it, four magic logs and a normal log, and a Falador Castle deathpile for the Entrana trips; 50 Prayer for Hopespear's Will. Carry in"},{"t":"The Fremennik Exiles","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › The Fremennik Exiles, A Night at the Theatre and Monkey Madness II's start","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t46-h","x":"Requirements The Fremennik Exiles needs 65 Crafting, 60 Slayer, 60 Smithing, 60 Fishing and 55 Runecraft to start, 60 Mining (boostable) later, and The Fremennik Isles, Lunar Diplomacy, Mountain Daughter, Heroes' Quest and their chains. Items: combat gear and a mirror shield, two kegs of beer, a molten glass, 100 astral runes, a pet rock, a fishing rod, the Fremennik shield, ice gloves or smiths gloves (i), a hammer, a glassblowing pipe, three lunar bars (or a pickaxe and three lunar ores) and a seal of passage. The two fights have different death rules. UIM risk The basilisk market fight is instanced and leaves a death outside it, and anything you put on the ground inside is lost, so don't "},{"t":"A Night at the Theatre","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › The Fremennik Exiles, A Night at the Theatre and Monkey Madness II's start","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t47-h","x":"It needs A Taste of Hope and the Myreque chain and Nature Spirit; no skills, 95 combat recommended. Items: an Ivandis or Blisterwood flail, a saw, a ghostspeak amulet (or Morytania legs 2+, which your Morytania legs 3 are) and any axe but the blessed axe. Bring antipoison or anti-venom. The wiki also recommends extra antipoison for Hespori, a dramen staff for the fairy ring and, if you own one, a serpentine helm. Talk to the Mysterious Stranger at the Theatre of Blood entrance in Ver Sinhaza, south-east of Meiyerditch. Go down the stairs north-east of him, kill a vyrewatch (level 105) for a key, unlock the southern gate and open the coffin (take the saw and the flail down with you); bring Ra"},{"t":"Hopespear's Will","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › The Fremennik Exiles, A Night at the Theatre and Monkey Madness II's start","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t48-h","x":"Requirements The miniquest needs 50 Prayer (not boostable), Desert Treasure I, Fairytale II, Land of the Goblins and a started Restless Ghost. Take a ghostspeak amulet (the Morytania legs don't count here), a ring of visibility, a goblin potion, a dramen staff for the fairy ring, food and prayer potions. Leave any follower pet out, because it blocks your entry even if you pick it up. Enter the Goblin Cave just east of the Fishing Guild, head north and then west to the temple guards, drink the goblin potion and go to the crypt. Put on the ghostspeak amulet and ring of visibility only once you're inside, or you'll be thrown out. Talk to Hopespear's ghost in the crypt. Take off everything that "},{"t":"Monkey Madness II to Kruk's Dungeon","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › The Fremennik Exiles, A Night at the Theatre and Monkey Madness II's start","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t49-h","x":"Monkey Madness II needs 69 Slayer, 70 Crafting, 60 Hunter, 55 Agility, 55 Thieving and 60 Firemaking for the balloon, none boostable, plus Enlightened Journey, The Eyes of Glouphrie, Recipe for Disaster's King Awowogei, Monkey Madness I, Troll Stronghold, Watchtower, The Grand Tree, Tree Gnome Village and Death Plateau, and the balloon route to the Gnome Stronghold unlocked (the wiki's requirement to start the quest, so the first steps below open it). Items: a lemon, grapes, a pestle and mortar, a normal log, a light source, the M'speak amulet, a ninja greegree and the translation book. If you lost the amulet or the greegree to an earlier death, get them again before step 7: the translation "},{"t":"Red chinchompas to 92 Ranged, and the Western Provinces hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b8-h","x":"Chinchompas stack, so 20,000 of them are one slot, and throwing them in Kruk's Dungeon is the fastest Ranged in the game. The Western Provinces hard diary sits in the middle of it, because its crystal bow task needs 70 Ranged and its reward unlocks elite void and the crystal halberd you throw the rest with. Gate in 63 Hunter; Monkey Madness II started; a bonecrusher with 24,000+ charges; 900,000 gp for a crystal bow and 750,000 gp for the halberd; the hard diary's levels. Carry in the chinchompa setup in the throwing step: about 20/28. Exit 92 Ranged (or your chosen stop); the Western Provinces hard diary; elite void; the crystal bow and halberd; about 850,000 gp. Carries forward elite void "},{"t":"Catch 20,000 red chinchompas","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Red chinchompas to 92 Ranged, and the Western Provinces hard diary","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t51-h","x":"Catch 20,000 red chinchompas between Tal Teklan and Kastori in Varlamore. The wiki lists 63 Hunter and Eagles' Peak for them and recommends 80+ Hunter, which is why the steps below boost. If that spot is too busy, the second-best red spot is north-east of Prifddinas. UIM risk An alternative is 16,000 black chinchompas in the Wilderness; leave that out, because a Wilderness death hands most of what you carry to the killer. Take box traps (the number you can lay rises with Hunter level, to five at 80) and super hunter potions. Boost with super hunter potions (+6, so 80+ needs a base of 74; your first few hundred catches get you there) and stay at 80+ Hunter for the fifth trap; repotting every "},{"t":"The throwing setup","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Red chinchompas to 92 Ranged, and the Western Provinces hard diary","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t52-h","x":"The setup is ranging potions, a bonecrusher with at least 24,000 charges, the void ranged set (elite once you have it), mixed hide boots, a Ranged ring if you have one (a berserker ring adds nothing to Ranged), the Necklace of Fangs or a charged amulet of glory (an amulet of strength adds nothing to chinchompas), the crystal halberd for specs once you have it, a mixed hide cape, and death charge runes (death, blood, soul) in the rune pouch. In Kruk's Dungeon, use medium fuse, Protect from Melee and Eagle Eye. Medium fuse is most accurate from 4 to 6 squares away and drops to 75% closer or further than that, so stand that far from the pack. One throw rolls against the first monkey, and if it "},{"t":"Throw to 70 Ranged","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Red chinchompas to 92 Ranged, and the Western Provinces hard diary","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t53-h","x":"Throw them in Kruk's Dungeon to 70 Ranged, which the diary's crystal bow task needs; the wiki marks that level as not boostable, so a potion won't stand in for the last level. Done when you are 70 Ranged. Coins: unchanged · Slots: about 20/28 · Requirements: Monkey Madness II at Kruk's Dungeon"},{"t":"The Western Provinces hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Red chinchompas to 92 Ranged, and the Western Provinces hard diary","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t54-h","x":"Buy a crystal bow from Islwyn in Prifddinas (900,000 gp): Chapter 2 had you drop the Roving Elves bow to save a slot, and the Bow of Faerdhinen comes much later. Then complete the Western Provinces hard diary. The tasks: kill an elf with the crystal bow (Roving Elves, 70 Ranged; the Bow of Faerdhinen also counts, and an inactive bow works if you equip it as the elf dies of poison); catch and cook a monkfish in Piscatoris (Swan Song, 62 Fishing and Cooking, a small fishing net; the spots are at the Piscatoris Fishing Colony); complete a veteran Pest Control game (100 combat), which the last block already did; the wiki says the game only counts if you earned commendation points in it, so a gam"},{"t":"Elite void and the crystal halberd","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Red chinchompas to 92 Ranged, and the Western Provinces hard diary","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t55-h","x":"Buy the elite void top and robe at Pest Control (200 points each), now that the hard diary is done. Buy a crystal halberd from Islwyn in Prifddinas or Isafdar (750,000 gp; it needs Roving Elves and the hard diary, and 70 Attack, 35 Strength and 50 Agility to wield). Optionally get an off-task fire cape. Done when you wear elite void and hold the crystal halberd. Coins: about 850,000 gp after the bow and the halberd · Slots: unchanged · Requirements: the Western Provinces hard diary; 70 Attack for the halberd"},{"t":"Throw to 92 Ranged","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Red chinchompas to 92 Ranged, and the Western Provinces hard diary","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t56-h","x":"Come back to Kruk's Dungeon with elite void and the halberd for specs, and throw to 92. Options: Lower targets. Levels 89 and 87 are reasonable stopping points for the corrupted bow's max hits with Eagle Eye, at the cost of a slower Corrupted Gauntlet. Nightmare Zone instead of chinchompas. It has super ranging potions and is safe: elite void, a magic shortbow (i), rune arrows, an amulet of glory and Shayzien boots (5); Hawk Eye, no overhead; a rock cake to 1 Hitpoint with absorptions every 6 to 9 minutes; hard custom rumble (moss giant, sand snake, Count Draynor, King Roald, and the Witch's Experiment, checked with a DPS calculator). Deadeye (optional, not recommended). A zombie axe (it dro"},{"t":"Gem mining, The Red Reef's start and the skiff's camphor upgrades","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b9-h","x":"This block fills the gem bag for Guardians of the Rift, starts The Red Reef, and turns blast-mined adamantite and Great Conch camphor into the skiff's upgrades, everything processed on the spot so nothing waits in a bank you don't have. Gate in the Karamja hard diary and a charged glory for the gem mine; 75 Mining; 52 Sailing and 48 Smithing for The Red Reef; 66 Woodcutting for camphor; about 112,000 gp for camphor planks. Carry in the gem bag and a mining setup; then one build's bars and the plank sack. Exit 75 Mining and a full gem bag; The Red Reef started; 551 adamantite ore and 24 nickel ore smelted, with the copper and lead bought; 1,065 adamant nails; the skiff's adamant keel, camphor"},{"t":"Gems to 75 Mining and the gem bag","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Gem mining, The Red Reef's start and the skiff's camphor upgrades","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t58-h","x":"With the Karamja hard diary done, mine gem rocks until you reach 75 Mining, which the blast mine's runite needs (the nickel needs 74), and keep going until the gem bag is full; you cut the uncut gems later at Guardians of the Rift. You arrive at about 73 Mining, so the first 75 takes about 212,000 XP, roughly 3.5 hours of gems at this level (an estimate from the XP table, not a timed figure). It needs a charged amulet of glory. 3-tick mining is faster, but it is tick manipulation, so it is optional. The long grind to 97 Mining comes later, in 3.2. A UIM can't use the deposit box, but the gem bag holds 60 of each of the five cut types it takes (the wiki's gem rock table has no dragonstones, s"},{"t":"Start The Red Reef","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Gem mining, The Red Reef's start and the skiff's camphor upgrades","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t59-h","x":"Requirements The Red Reef needs 52 Sailing and 48 Smithing (not boostable), Troubled Tortugans and Pandemonium, and the materials step after it needs 75 Mining. The wiki recommends Protect from Missiles, at least 300 hitpoints of repair kits (which the cargo hold stores), and cannons or Ranged or Magic gear for the ship fights, with a combat level of about 65. UIM risk Two UIM warnings from the wiki: the Last Light fight is instanced, so a death leaves your items outside it, and teleporting away after docking at Last Light, or out of the Zenith section, loses your ship at sea with everything in its cargo hold. Charter to the Great Conch (Summer Shore). If the quest won't start right after yo"},{"t":"Mine and smelt the metal","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Gem mining, The Red Reef's start and the skiff's camphor upgrades","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t60-h","x":"Charter to Deepfin Point and mine 24 nickel ore (74 Mining; a boost works, and if you arrive below 74, mine gems until you are there). Buy 48 copper ore and 26 lead ore at the Deepfin Point Ore Exchange, 3 and 38 gp each (about 1,000 gp in all); its lead stock is only 10 at a time, so hop worlds or wait for it to restock. Go back to blast mining (Thirus gives you 40 free dynamite a day now that the Kourend & Kebos hard diary is done, so claim that first) for 551 adamantite ore in total, converting gems into alchs for dynamite money if you need it (cut sapphires, emeralds and rubies, or ruby and diamond bracelets). Keep at least 15 runite ore along the way: the blast mine's runite needs 75 Mi"},{"t":"Camphor planks","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Gem mining, The Red Reef's start and the skiff's camphor upgrades","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t61-h","x":"Take fairy ring CJQ to the Great Conch and chop 82 camphor logs with the log basket open. Don't teleport out to a bank between loads; make the planks on the spot instead, with Plank Make (86 Magic, and a nature rune, two astral runes and 15 earth runes a cast) or at a sawmill, and carry them in the plank sack. Sawmill vouchers (10 for 150 anima-infused bark at a Forestry shop) give one extra plank per log, but nothing in this guide earns that bark, so plan on one log per plank and treat any vouchers you happen to have as a bonus. Make 64 camphor planks, at 1,750 gp each with Plank Make (2,500 gp each at a sawmill), which is about 112,000 gp with Plank Make. The skiff's hull parts take 50 of "},{"t":"Build the skiff upgrades","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Gem mining, The Red Reef's start and the skiff's camphor upgrades","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t62-h","x":"Build, carrying each build's materials only when you go to build it: An adamant keel (skiff): 66 Sailing and 62 Construction, 10 adamant keel parts and 5 lead bars. A camphor hull (skiff): 67 Sailing and 59 Construction, 10 camphor hull parts, 300 adamantite nails, 20 swamp tar and 5 lead bars. A camphor mast and canvas sails (skiff): 68 Sailing (a boost from 67) and 60 Construction, 10 camphor logs, 40 adamantite nails and 5 bolts of canvas from your Chapter 2 hemp. The skiff's camphor cargo hold: 60 Sailing and 53 Construction, 8 camphor planks, 32 adamantite nails and 3 lead bars, which the 1,065 nails already count (the lead bars are the ones you smelted in the mining step). Optional, re"},{"t":"Charting the Sunset, Western and Shrouded oceans, and the sloop's upgrades","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b10-h","x":"Gate in the crew; repair kits in the cargo hold; an antipoison for the Backwater; the Sailing levels for each ocean. Carry in your bow and ammunition for the pirates, food, an antipoison, the spyglass, teleports, the small keys and the drinks you collect (about 20/28), with fish and repair kits in the cargo hold. Exit the Sunset, Western and Shrouded oceans charted; The Red Reef done; the keys and schematics collected; the sloop upgrades and cannonballs held for 3.2; about 739,000 gp. Carries forward the small keys (lockboxes), the sloop's plank list for 3.2. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect them "},{"t":"Crew, cannonballs and drinks","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Charting the Sunset, Western and Shrouded oceans, and the sloop's upgrades","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t64-h","x":"Recruit Cabin Boy Jenkins and Adventurer Ada for the most multiskilling XP while charting. Don't buy the 5,000 mithril cannonballs at Port Roberts yet: at 150 gp each they cost 750,000 gp, which you can't spare before the Gauntlet loot is alched. Port Roberts is a floating platform in the Western Ocean, north-east of Civitas illa Fortis, and it needs 50 Sailing to dock on its western side, which you already have, so the purchase in 3.2 is a short sail. Shoot the pirates with your bow in the meantime, and buy the cannonballs (they stack and the cargo hold takes them) at the start of 3.2's Sailing block. The hold keeps them as one stack, and the wiki lists both the old 2,000 cannonball cap and"},{"t":"The charting route","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Charting the Sunset, Western and Shrouded oceans, and the sloop's upgrades","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t65-h","x":"Each sealed crate needs the crowbar from Prying Times, and you sample its bottle aboard your boat while the boat is not under way. Most bottles give 75 Sailing XP once, and a few destroy courier task cargo, so carry none. The wiki also says you can't boost Sailing to moor at an island you wouldn't normally have the level for. Chart in this order: The Shrouded Ocean, partial, from Corsair Cove (teleport there and recover your boat). Recovering a boat through a shipwright, like using Summon Boat, loses any fish and fish-filled crates in the hold, while repair kits and other items stay, so use up the fish you care about first. In the Simian Sea, dock at the Red Rock and continue The Red Reef un"},{"t":"Finish the Shrouded Ocean and plan the sloop","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Charting the Sunset, Western and Shrouded oceans, and the sloop's upgrades","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t66-h","x":"Requirements Plank Make needs 86 Magic, and each cast also takes 1 nature, 2 astral and 15 earth runes on top of the coin fee. Hold the sloop's upgrades until 3.2: you hold about 739,000 gp, about 350,000 of it spoken for by the Gauntlet's Hespori collections, and the planks cost about 721,000 gp. Once the Blood Moon block's alchs have paid for them, chop another 427 camphor logs in the Sacred Grove, which The Red Reef opens (219 only if you had 204 sawmill vouchers, about 3,060 anima-infused bark, so plan on 427), and make 412 camphor planks (400 for the hull parts, 4 for the helm and 8 for the cargo hold), a plank sack at a time (about 721,000 gp of Plank Make fees at 1,750 gp each). The S"},{"t":"Guardians of the Rift with the gem bag, and the Corrupted Gauntlet","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b11-h","x":"This is the last and longest block of 3.1: about 70 hours of the Corrupted Gauntlet for the Bow of Faerdhinen and crystal armour, broken up by multiskilling Guardians of the Rift with the gems you mined. The Gauntlet suits a UIM only one way: you walk in with nothing, so a death costs only the run. Gate in Song of the Elves; a full gem bag; the Hespori deathbank set up with only what you can afford to lose; the 2.5 million reserve for collection fees. Carry in a pickaxe and chisel at Guardians of the Rift; an empty inventory and nothing worn in the Gauntlet. Exit 6 armour seeds and the enhanced weapon seed; 93 Ranged; crystal armour and the Bow of Faerdhinen (sung or made); the noted loot un"},{"t":"Multiskilling Guardians of the Rift","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Guardians of the Rift with the gem bag, and the Corrupted Gauntlet","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t68-h","x":"Play Guardians of the Rift with the multiskilling method until your gems run out. It still makes combination runes but spends most of the game skilling: Enter the west essence mine only when it opens, and ignore every other chance at essence. The wiki says the portals to the huge guardian remains open roughly every two minutes and stay open for about 25 seconds, so be ready beside one. In the downtime, take uncut gems out of the gem bag and cut them. The bag holds up to 60 of each of the five uncut types and keeps its contents if you die, and when a UIM empties it an interface lets you choose the type and how many to take, so withdraw one type at a time. Drop the cut gems. The deposit pool d"},{"t":"Set up Hespori for the Gauntlet","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Guardians of the Rift with the gem bag, and the Corrupted Gauntlet","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t69-h","x":"Your tools and pouches have nowhere safe to go except a Hespori deathbank, but your coins can wait in Dominic Onion's coffer at the Nightmare Zone (multiples of 1,000 gp). So plan as if your first Gauntlet death wipes the Hespori deathbank, and don't rely on a test to clear it. UIM risk The Gauntlet stores everything you carry in an instanced bank for the length of the run, and an Ultimate Ironman who dies in it loses those items. UIM risk The wiki does not say whether a Gauntlet death counts as an unsafe death for a retrieval-service deathbank; it only says that a Gauntlet death loses what an ultimate ironman holds in the instanced bank, and that an unsafe death deletes what is stored with "},{"t":"Run the Corrupted Gauntlet","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Guardians of the Rift with the gem bag, and the Corrupted Gauntlet","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t70-h","x":"The Gauntlet is entered through the portal in north-west Prifddinas, in the Amlodd district. A teleport crystal drops you in the city centre, south of the Tower of Voices, so expect a run across the city. Restore Prayer at the altar in the Tower of Voices or in the Hefin district before you go in. Each stretch of runs: Do your hourlies first; between runs in the same stretch, skip them. Walk in with an empty inventory and nothing worn. The wiki says everything you hold is stored for the run and any boosts you drank beforehand are removed, so skip the potions. Prepare (7 minutes 30 seconds in the Corrupted Gauntlet). Gather crystal ore, linum tirinum and phren bark (three of each per node, no"},{"t":"The loot, the UIM way","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Guardians of the Rift with the gem bag, and the Corrupted Gauntlet","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t71-h","x":"The reward chest pays resources noted, so a UIM carries them like anyone else. Averages for the grind: Loot Amount What to do with it Crystal shards about 4,540 About 2,450 make a full crystal armour set (300), a sung Bow of Faerdhinen (150) and its corruption (2,000, of which the new bow's charges count 100), plus charges. Trade spare armour seeds for 250 shards each, and turn regular weapon seeds into acorns that grow into crystal trees (up to 28 to 32 shards each). Coins and alchables about 50.7 million gp in all (you realise it in 3.2's Blood Moon block) Includes 500 noted battlestaves (they need charged orbs) and 500 noted diamonds (they need crafting). Make diamond and ruby bracelets a"},{"t":"Crystal armour and the Bow of Faerdhinen","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.1: Slayer and the red prison › Guardians of the Rift with the gem bag, and the Corrupted Gauntlet","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t72-h","x":"Requirements The Bow of Faerdhinen needs 82 Crafting and 82 Smithing (both boostable; 100 shards and the enhanced seed), and its corrupted version 2,000 shards' worth, of which a new bow's 10,000 charges count as 100, so 1,900 more if you corrupt it at once. The bow also needs 80 Ranged and 70 Agility to wield, and a full armour set adds up to 30% accuracy and 15% damage with it. The wiki's levels are 70 Crafting and 70 Smithing for the crystal helm (50 shards, 1 seed), 72 for the legs (100 shards, 2 seeds) and 74 for the body (150 shards, 3 seeds); Conwenna or Reese will make a piece for you for 60 more shards. Make the helm, legs and body at the singing bowl in Prifddinas, or have Conwenna"},{"t":"3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","p":"Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-s5-h","x":"You start 3.2 with about 389,000 gp and realise the Gauntlet loot in the Blood Moon block, which leaves you with about 40.45 million after the UIM gold and the quest cape. It finishes the quest cape, trains Smithing, Sailing, Crafting and Runecraft to their late-game levels, and ends with Construction at 86 and the final house. For a UIM, the quests' deaths and the house are the two things to plan; most of the skilling methods are already UIM methods."},{"t":"The Raiments of the Eye and the colossal pouch","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b12-h","x":"Play Guardians of the Rift until you have the full Raiments of the Eye and the colossal pouch. You have been earning points toward them since 3.1, so this is likely a shorter session than it looks. Multiskill with the gem bag while you have gems; without them, play a mass world with four pouches, making combination runes. Keep using empty cell running. Gate in 27 Runecraft; 1,350 abyssal pearls; the small pouch; 25 Runecraft and 56 Crafting for the colossal pouch; 65 Runecraft and both shield halves for the Ardougne hard diary. Carry in a pickaxe, a chisel, the pouches and the gem bag. Exit the full Raiments of the Eye in the magic wardrobe; the colossal pouch; the Ardougne hard diary if not"},{"t":"Raiments and pearls","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The Raiments of the Eye and the colossal pouch","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t75-h","x":"The Raiments cost 1,350 abyssal pearls in all (400 for the hat, 350 each for the top and bottoms, 250 for the boots) and go in the costume room's magic wardrobe. The Rewards Guardian pays the pearls: a successful roll gives 14 to 16, and the wiki estimates about 630 searches, or about 180 games, for the full set. The pieces are sold at the Temple Supplies shop, each adds 10% bonus runes when you craft and the full set adds another 20% (60% in all), though the bonus runes give no extra Runecraft XP. Done when you own the full Raiments of the Eye."},{"t":"The colossal pouch","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The Raiments of the Eye and the colossal pouch","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t76-h","x":"The colossal pouch is stitched with an abyssal needle from the Rewards Guardian from one each of the small, medium, large and giant pouches. You hold the small pouch, the replacement from the Dark mage in Chapter 2; the medium, large and giant ones come as Rewards Guardian loot while you play, usually in that order because owning the smaller one makes the next size possible, and you need no Runecraft level to receive them (the giant needs 75 to use). Keep each pouch until you have all four; it needs 25 Runecraft and 56 Crafting, holds 40 essence at 85 Runecraft, and is repaired with an abyssal pearl at the Dark Mage, or at Apprentice Cordelia once you have paid 25 abyssal pearls to unlock he"},{"t":"Ardougne hard diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The Raiments of the Eye and the colossal pouch","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t77-h","x":"If you haven't yet, do the Ardougne hard diary at 65 Runecraft (it also needs the shield left half). Done when the Ardougne hard diary is claimed. Coins: about 389,000 gp · Slots: a pickaxe, chisel, the pouches and the gem bag · Requirements: 27 Runecraft; 25 Runecraft and 56 Crafting for the colossal pouch Wiki references Raiments of the Eye Colossal pouch"},{"t":"While Guthix Sleeps, Dragon Slayer II, Vorkath and Monkey Madness II","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b13-h","x":"Three Grandmaster quests and the Vorkath head for Ava's assembler. For a UIM the planning is all about deaths: each fight has its own retrieval rules, and you hold only about 389,000 gp until the Blood Moon block's alchs, so collect Hespori first and carry each fight's setup and nothing else. Gate in 180 quest points and While Guthix Sleeps' levels; 200 quest points, 75 Magic, 70 Smithing, 68 Mining, 62 Crafting, 60 Agility and Thieving, 50 Construction and Hitpoints and 100 Kudos for Dragon Slayer II; the Bow of Faerdhinen; 100,000 gp per retrieval. Carry in each fight's setup only; collect the Hespori deathbank first. Exit While Guthix Sleeps, Dragon Slayer II and Monkey Madness II done; V"},{"t":"While Guthix Sleeps","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › While Guthix Sleeps, Dragon Slayer II, Vorkath and Monkey Madness II","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t79-h","x":"Do While Guthix Sleeps if you haven't already: 180 quest points, 72 Thieving, 67 Magic, 66 Agility, 65 Farming, 65 Herblore and 62 Hunter (none boostable), 49 Firemaking, Warriors' Guild access and a long quest list. Its items include a ring of charos (a) or 500 gp, a knife, a lantern lens, an unpowered orb, a bronze med helm, an iron chainbody, a sapphire lantern, runes for four Astral Contacts and one orb charge, and gear for two combat styles; keep 9 slots free. Its optional tunnel's 100 magic logs are not worth taking now, because the log basket holds only 28; chop the Shades of Mort'ton bloodbark logs when you go for the bloodbark instead. Talk to Ivy Sophista in Taverley to start, then"},{"t":"Dragon Slayer II","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › While Guthix Sleeps, Dragon Slayer II, Vorkath and Monkey Madness II","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t80-h","x":"Dragon Slayer II needs 200 quest points, 75 Magic, 70 Smithing, 68 Mining, 62 Crafting, 60 Agility, 60 Thieving, 50 Construction, 50 Hitpoints (none of these skills is boostable), 100 Kudos and a started pyre-ship Barbarian Training. Its items include a pickaxe, axe, hammer, saw, machete, spade and tinderbox, 8 oak planks, 10 swamp paste and 12+ nails, catspeak and ghostspeak amulets, goutweed, a cut dragonstone, 2 molten glass, a glassblowing pipe, a pestle and mortar, an astral rune, a seal of passage and runes for three Fire Waves or Surges. If you have no goutweed, the wiki suggests stealing one from the Troll Stronghold kitchen rather than farming it. Use the Bow of Faerdhinen against t"},{"t":"Vorkath's head and Ava's assembler","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › While Guthix Sleeps, Dragon Slayer II, Vorkath and Monkey Madness II","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t81-h","x":"Kill Vorkath up to 50 times for his head, in the shield-and-crossbow setup above, and make Ava's assembler: take the head, 75 mithril arrows and your accumulator (or 4,999 gp) to Ava in Draynor Manor. The same Torfinn rule applies, and the bonecrusher handles the bones. Done when you wear Ava's assembler. Coins: about 389,000 gp less retrievals; the Vorkath loot is alched as you go · Slots: your Vorkath setup · Requirements: Dragon Slayer II"},{"t":"Monkey Madness II","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › While Guthix Sleeps, Dragon Slayer II, Vorkath and Monkey Madness II","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t82-h","x":"Finish Monkey Madness II from Kruk's Dungeon. UIM risk Its final fights are in instances, so a death there drops everything on the ground outside the instance, as a deathpile with the one-hour timer, and anything you leave on the ground is lost. In Kruk's Dungeon, take the route that doesn't give a \"feels wrong\" message, and investigate the wall on the path you didn't take before crossing the dodgy ground; the hole it opens near the entrance is your restocking shortcut. The wiki warns that a glitch can trap you between the spinning blade trap and the eastern door. Fight Kruk in his instance. Stand beside a wall so he is diagonal to you, attack when his health bar disappears and step back; ot"},{"t":"Devious Minds, the desert quests and Desert Treasure II","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b14-h","x":"Five quests that end with Desert Treasure II and its three 100,000 XP Prayer lamps. Every boss in them leaves a normal deathpile for a UIM, so each fight is a trip with only its setup. Gate in each quest's requirements as listed; the mithril 2h sword and a non-degraded large or colossal pouch for Devious Minds; Ancient Magicks for Desert Treasure II; the Falador Castle deathpile for Entrana. Carry in each fight's setup only. Exit Devious Minds, Secrets of the North, Beneath Cursed Sands, Into the Tombs and Desert Treasure II done; the ancient icon if you chose it; about 389,000 gp. Carries forward the Desert Treasure II rings and the Phantom Muspah's icon. Deathbank check this block has figh"},{"t":"Devious Minds","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Devious Minds, the desert quests and Desert Treasure II","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t84-h","x":"Requirements Devious Minds needs 50 Runecraft (not boostable), 65 Smithing and 50 Fletching, the mithril 2h sword you smithed in 2.2 (or one from Gaius in Taverley), a bow string and a non-degraded large or colossal pouch. The wiki's UIM warning: the orb is always lost on death, and once it is in the pouch a death loses both, deathpile or deathbank included. So deathpile your gear before you put the orb in the pouch, do that stretch in one go, and if you do lose the orb, the monk at Paterdomus gives you a new one. Runecraft 50 is needed to use the pouch, and a degraded pouch won't work, so repair it at the Dark Mage through Astral Contact first. Talk to the monk outside the Paterdomus temple"},{"t":"Secrets of the North","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Devious Minds, the desert quests and Desert Treasure II","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t85-h","x":"Requirements Secrets of the North needs Devious Minds, 69 Agility, 64 Thieving and 56 Hunter (not boostable), 100 gp and a lockpick (not the strange old lockpick). The Bow of Faerdhinen handles almost everything here. The wiki recommends combat level 85 and an antipoison. Talk to the guard outside the Carnillean mansion in south-west East Ardougne, and update him before you question the Carnillean family, or they refuse to talk. Inside, examine Ceril's body, the broken window and the hidden room behind the false wall. Ask the Khazard barman at the Fight Arena bar about Evelot and follow her trail through the marked barrels, boulders, bushes and stump. Fight Evelot (level 148); every few atta"},{"t":"Beneath Cursed Sands","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Devious Minds, the desert quests and Desert Treasure II","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t86-h","x":"Requirements Beneath Cursed Sands needs 62 Agility, 55 Crafting and 55 Firemaking (not boostable) and Contact!'s chain, with coal, an iron bar and any meat but fish or bird; the wiki recommends 85 combat, heat protection, antipoison and stamina potions. The meat can be raw or cooked, but not fish or raw t-bone steak. The bow works very well against these enemies too. Talk to Jamila at her stall in Sophanem, then to Maisa at her camp east of Sophanem, and inspect the blocked entrance to the Jaltevas Pyramid. Fight the head Menaphite guard without Protect from Melee; it hits for about a third of your Hitpoints. He can't be safespotted, so hit and run around the rocks or bind him. In the Ruins "},{"t":"Into the Tombs","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Devious Minds, the desert quests and Desert Treasure II","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t87-h","x":"Do Into the Tombs, which needs Beneath Cursed Sands and one full Tombs of Amascut run. In the Tombs, with no death invocations on, a death keeps your items and leaves any retrieval service alone. The wiki asks for a full run: free the four lesser gods by beating Akkha, Ba-Ba, Kephri and Zebak, then defeat both Wardens, and it recommends combat level 95. It gives a 50,000 XP lamp for a combat skill of level 60 or more (not Prayer); put it on Strength. Done when Into the Tombs is complete."},{"t":"The Phantom Muspah and the ancient icon","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Devious Minds, the desert quests and Desert Treasure II","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t88-h","x":"Optional, recommended: kill the Phantom Muspah for an ancient icon to upgrade your ancient staff into an ancient sceptre; the wiki gives it a 2 in 100 drop chance. The fight is in an instance reached through a crevice south-west of the Ghorrock Dungeon. Make mithril sapphire bolts (e) and a rune crossbow to drain its shield, as an alternative to Smite between its attacks. A death to it leaves your items outside its lair in the Ghorrock Dungeon. Done when the ancient icon is used, or you skipped it."},{"t":"Desert Treasure II","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Devious Minds, the desert quests and Desert Treasure II","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t89-h","x":"Requirements Desert Treasure II needs 75 Firemaking, 75 Magic, 70 Thieving, 62 Herblore, 60 Runecraft and 60 Construction, The Garden of Death, His Faithful Servants and a long quest list, on Ancient Magicks with runes for Blood, Ice, Smoke and Shadow Burst, a ring of visibility and a facemask or Slayer helmet. The Ancient Pyramid altar, which the Pharaoh's sceptre's Jaldraocht teleport reaches, switches you to Ancient Magicks, and the Gauntlet's blood runes cover Blood Burst. The wiki's list also names 8 death, 16 chaos, 2 fire, 3 air, 4 water, 2 soul and 2 blood runes, and you get the tinderbox, pestle and mortar and pickaxe during the quest. Keep two free slots, and more for the Kasonde d"},{"t":"The Blood Moon Rises, the quest cape and UIM gold to 86 Smithing","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b15-h","x":"Gate in The Blood Moon Rises' levels and quests; every quest for the cape, including Meat and Greet and Mudfoot's Big Adventure; the Gauntlet loot noted; charged orbs; about 10.5 million gp of UIM gold ore. Carry in the UIM gold setup; the loot a load at a time. Exit the quest cape; 86 Smithing; the Gauntlet loot alched; the Lumbridge elite diary when your levels allow; about 40,450,000 gp. Carries forward 15 runite bars, the rest of the stack for the Sailing and house blocks. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect them before you start: an unsafe death here deletes them."},{"t":"The Blood Moon Rises","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The Blood Moon Rises, the quest cape and UIM gold to 86 Smithing","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t91-h","x":"Requirements The Blood Moon Rises: 74 Slayer (not boostable), 74 Woodcutting, 72 Smithing, 72 Cooking, 70 Fletching, 66 Mining, 65 Hunter, 64 Crafting, 64 Herblore and 57 Magic, plus A Night at the Theatre, Sins of the Father and the Myreque chain. Start and complete The Blood Moon Rises, its tome of experience (six uses of 30,000 XP in a skill above 70) on Herblore. It is challenging, but the boss fights have infinite resets with free, overpowered supplies. The tome goes on Herblore for a reason: the Kandarin elite diary needs 86 Herblore and the ornate rejuvenation pool 87, both further on in this chapter. Bring a Blisterwood flail (or 40,000 gp for one), the vyre noble clothing from the c"},{"t":"The quest cape","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The Blood Moon Rises, the quest cape and UIM gold to 86 Smithing","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t92-h","x":"Requirements The quest cape needs every quest: the wiki lists 191 quests worth 354 quest points as of 22 November 2026, so check the count in your quest list before you buy the cape. November 2026's Quest Month added six of them; this guide does The Writing's on the Wall (Kourend, 2.1), The Birds and the Wasps (Varrock, 2.1), A Shell of a Friend (Morytania, 2.1), A New Leaf (the Tithe Farm block, 2.2) and Rag and Bone Man III (the cave horror block, 3.1), and the sixth is Mudfoot's Big Adventure below. The Graveyard, the Fremennik sequel, is scheduled for 25 November 2026 with 3 quest points, 65 Sailing, 65 Agility, 56 Woodcutting and 54 Fletching; if it is out when you get here, do it too. "},{"t":"UIM gold to 86 Smithing","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The Blood Moon Rises, the quest cape and UIM gold to 86 Smithing","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t93-h","x":"Once the loot below is alched, use the Corrupted Gauntlet money to train Smithing to 86 with UIM gold, the wiki's UIM gold method: about 42,900 gold ores for 86 (2,501,514 XP from your 74 Smithing, less 80,000 from Dragon Slayer II, 5,000 from The Red Reef and 6,500 from Devious Minds, at 56.2 XP each), which the diaries need. The wiki puts that method at about 4.25 to 4.5 coins per XP (the wiki's 4 coins per XP for the ore works out at roughly 225 gp each, and the Blast Furnace coffer drains while you work), so 42,900 ores cost about 10.5 million gp; stopping at 83 (about 26,400 ores) costs about 6.5 million. The method is the wiki's Blast Furnace dropping routine, and it uses kit you alrea"},{"t":"Lumbridge elite diary","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The Blood Moon Rises, the quest cape and UIM gold to 86 Smithing","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t94-h","x":"Requirements Lumbridge elite diary: every quest, 88 Smithing (boost from 86, or +5 from 83), 78 Thieving, 76 Runecraft, 75 Firemaking, Magic and Woodcutting, 74 Slayer, 72 Mining and Cooking, 70 in Strength, Agility, Herblore, Ranged, Crafting, Fletching, Farming, Construction and Hunter, 65 Defence, 62 Fishing, 52 Prayer and 62 Sailing, with the Bones to Peaches spell (the 76 Runecraft is 57 with three pieces of the Raiments of the Eye). Complete the Lumbridge elite diary when you can. The diary waits behind the cape because one of its six tasks is the quest cape emote in the Wise Old Man's house. The others are in Dorgesh-Kaan (a rich chest at 78 Thieving with a lockpick, and a pylon grapp"},{"t":"Finishing the Gauntlet loot","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The Blood Moon Rises, the quest cape and UIM gold to 86 Smithing","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t95-h","x":"While you are at the furnaces, finish the Gauntlet loot: turn your diamonds (and rubies, if you like) into bracelets and alch them, keeping diamonds back for The Fractured Archive's Ascension crossbows if you want; charge enough unpowered orbs to match your battlestaves (about 500 on the averages), attach them and alch the staves, unnoting the staves at a bank booth a load at a time. Don't make air battlestaves: the air obelisk is in the Wilderness north of Edgeville. A UIM can make water battlestaves instead: the Obelisk of Water, on the island off Catherby, is outside the Wilderness. Reach it by the ladder near the black dragons in Taverley Dungeon, past the dusty key gate from Chapter 2 ("},{"t":"Optional extras, and if the Gauntlet loot comes in short","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The Blood Moon Rises, the quest cape and UIM gold to 86 Smithing","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t96-h","x":"Optional extras: the Ardougne elite diary's \"rune crossbow from scratch\" task, and the rest of that diary if you have the stats: 90 Agility, 91 Smithing, 91 Cooking, 94 Magic, 85 Farming, 82 Thieving, 81 Fishing and 69 Fletching, Desert Treasure I and Haunted Mine among its quests, and 800,000 Nightmare Zone points (400,000 with the hard Combat Achievements). It also needs an imbued salve amulet from Nightmare Zone, and you can boost Ice Barrage at Castle Wars from 85 with a Castle Wars brew; force spawning marks of grace while you process resources, for stamina potions; the dropping version of UIM gold doesn't need any. Coins: about 40,450,000 gp: the 389,000 gp you hold, plus the Gauntlet "},{"t":"Sailing to 76 and 78: bounty tasks, the Gwenith Glide and the Northern Ocean","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b16-h","x":"Gate in the stack restored by the Gauntlet loot; 72 Sailing (not boostable) for Sunbleak Island and the Gwenith Glide; 73 and 67 for the extractors; 76 to dock at Buccaneers' Haven; 78 and 72 (boostable) for the braziers; 89 Smithing (boost) for rune nails; Making Friends with My Arm for the salts. Carry in the Bow of Faerdhinen setup, food and prayer potions, teleports, the Heart of Ithell, the next build's materials only and the bounty parts (about 24/28); repair kits, cannonballs and fish in the cargo hold. Exit a base 76 Sailing (78 with a boost for the braziers); the sloop upgrades; crystal extractors and eternal braziers on both ships; the Northern Ocean charted; 80 Woodcutting; about "},{"t":"Bounty tasks","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Sailing to 76 and 78: bounty tasks, the Gwenith Glide and the Northern Ocean","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t98-h","x":"The Gauntlet has paid for the purchases this chapter held back, so make them first: build the sloop's upgrades from the list in the Charting block (about 721,000 gp of Plank Make fees for the 412 camphor planks), and buy the 5,000 mithril cannonballs at Port Roberts for 150 gp each (750,000 gp). Then swap the sloop's kraken ink stout keg for perildance bitter. Then collect port bounty tasks. Each board always offers one bounty, and you can hold three port tasks from 30 Sailing, four from 56 and five from 84. A bounty checks only your Sailing level, which boosts don't raise. Two tasks for the same creature can be held together only if they want different parts, and the second starts dropping "},{"t":"The Gwenith Glide and the ship upgrades","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Sailing to 76 and 78: bounty tasks, the Gwenith Glide and the Northern Ocean","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t99-h","x":"Requirements 72 Sailing that is not boosted, Regicide done and a skiff with an adamant keel or better, with no crew or other player aboard. Do the Woodcutting and Sunbleak Island part below first: the crystal extractors and eternal braziers need its 20 ironwood planks. When the bounties are done, or you reach 72 Sailing another way, take the skiff to the Gwenith Glide and complete at least up to the shark rank, which unlocks the Heart of Ithell, and reach 75 Sailing (1,210,421 XP), whichever comes later. The ranks are swordfish, shark and marlin, and the shark rank (3:42.00 or better) pays the Heart of Ithell. If resonance crystals crystallise your helm, click it three times to clear them. I"},{"t":"Chart the Northern Ocean and build the eternal braziers","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Sailing to 76 and 78: bounty tasks, the Gwenith Glide and the Northern Ocean","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t100-h","x":"Boosting where needed, chart the Northern Ocean in full from Rellekka: first the pink leg by raft, then the red one by skiff. The wiki's docking levels there are Rellekka 62, Etceteria 65, Lunar Isle 76, Weiss 80 (Making Friends with My Arm), Brittle Isle 81 and Grimstone 87, and the wiki says docking can't be boosted. The eternal brazier. The eternal brazier is what lets you sail its icy seas safely, and its schematic is in a lockbox on Buccaneers' Haven (opened with the small key from the Tear of the Soul), where docking needs a base 76 Sailing; the brazier itself needs 78, which boosts can cover, so keep charting, harvesting wind motes and doing bounties until you have the base 76 and a w"},{"t":"Finishing the charting","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Sailing to 76 and 78: bounty tasks, the Gwenith Glide and the Northern Ocean","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t101-h","x":"That completes your charting; collect the XP bonuses and the Horizon's lure from Chartin' Charles McAtless, and buy 50 of the drink for a keg on each ship. Drink the bottle of fishier bladderier stout soon after getting it (complete the meteorologist first). It puts you in an instanced troll arena with three trolls (fighting them is optional; you can leave and appear in the Rellekka Longhall) and leaves the ship docked at Rellekka, which needs 62 Sailing and The Fremennik Trials; then carry on. At Buccaneers' Haven, also take the small key for the dragon cannon schematic (dig it up with a spade from a tool leprechaun in the Buccaneers' Laboratory, on the red ball in the north-western prison "},{"t":"Woodcutting to 80 and Sunbleak Island","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Sailing to 76 and 78: bounty tasks, the Gwenith Glide and the Northern Ocean","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t102-h","x":"Requirements Sunbleak Island needs a base 72 Sailing (it can't be boosted) to moor and the adamant helm you built to cross its tangled kelp, so finish enough bounty tasks to be at 72 first. Train Woodcutting to 80 (bloodwoods, teaks or sulliusceps), then go to Sunbleak Island for the dragon helm schematic. The island is south-east of Deepfin Point. The schematic is in a lockbox west of the cave entrance that opens with the small key from Laguna Aurorae, so keep that key. The 14 ironwood trees need 80 Woodcutting. A UIM can't bank, so skip the bank chest there and save the magic stone it takes. Ironwood trees there are good AFK Woodcutting: take Plank Make and make enough logs into 20 ironwoo"},{"t":"The fire cape and a dragon pickaxe","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b17-h","x":"Gate in your stats; a setup you can afford to lose at the Kalphite Queen. Carry in each fight's setup. Exit the fire cape and a dragon pickaxe; about 35,010,000 gp. Carries forward nothing new. Deathbank check this block has fights where a death is unsafe. If Hespori or another retrieval service holds your items, collect them before you start: an unsafe death here deletes them."},{"t":"The fire cape","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The fire cape and a dragon pickaxe","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t104-h","x":"Get a fire cape off task if you don't have one. The Fight Caves are a safe minigame, so a death costs nothing but the attempt. They are inside the Karamja volcano at Mor Ul Rek: take the BLP fairy ring and run north, and you fight 63 waves alone. A death returns you outside with your gear and stats restored. Turn off auto retaliate, which can pull you out of a safespot. On wave 62 find the orange Ket-Zek early, because Jad appears where it spawns next round, and start wave 63 with Protect from Missiles on. Jad's foot stomp is his ranged attack and the rear-up his magic, so switch during the animation, before the projectile leaves. At half health Yt-HurKot healers appear; you needn't kill the"},{"t":"The dragon pickaxe","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › The fire cape and a dragon pickaxe","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t105-h","x":"Requirements 60 Attack to wield and 61 Mining to use. Then get a dragon pickaxe. The options are Artio, Spindel and Vet'ion if you plan a Voidwaker later, or the chaos elemental with a Bow of Faerdhinen; all of them are in the Wilderness, where a death hands your setup to whoever kills you. The Kalphite Queen instead. Use the Kalphite Queen instead: it drops the pickaxe at 1/400. Her lair is south-west of Shantay Pass and you need two ropes: one is used up entering the dungeon and the other to reach the lower level, and the hard Desert diary makes the ropes permanent. The wiki says she has protection prayers up, against Magic and Missiles in her first form and Melee in her second, so bring t"},{"t":"Marks of grace, Herblore and the Falador and Kandarin elite diaries","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b18-h","x":"Gate in 90 Agility for the Ardougne rooftops; the elite diaries' levels. Carry in the herb sack and potion supplies. Exit marks of grace or amylase crystals; the Falador and Kandarin elite diaries if your levels allow; about 35,010,000 gp. Carries forward marks and amylase crystals."},{"t":"Herblore and marks of grace","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Marks of grace, Herblore and the Falador and Kandarin elite diaries","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t107-h","x":"Herblore has its own block later in this chapter (Herblore to 84 with Mastering Mixology), so here you only force-spawn marks of grace in Ardougne: every 3 to 9.5 minutes (lower is better, but not too quick), do exactly one lap of the Ardougne rooftop course, then do something else. After a mark spawns, no other can spawn for 3 minutes (half the time 2 with the elite Ardougne diary), so a quicker lap is wasted. A mark lasts 10 minutes and Ardougne has one mark tile, so a new mark stacks on the old one and resets its timer, which pauses while you are logged out; a mark spawns at the end of the lap about two times in three (about 75% with the elite Ardougne diary), and you pick it up on the ne"},{"t":"Falador and Kandarin elite diaries","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Marks of grace, Herblore and the Falador and Kandarin elite diaries","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t108-h","x":"Then complete the remaining Falador and Kandarin elite diary tasks if your levels allow. From the wiki: the Falador elite needs 80 Agility, 81 Herblore, 88 Runecraft (55 with the full Raiments of the Eye), 91 Farming and 75 Woodcutting, the White Knight Master rank, and one of all quests, all music tracks or a 99 in any skill. The wiki also wants Warriors' Guild access (130 combined Attack and Strength), part of Ratcatchers, a Giant Mole kill and a prospector helmet from the Motherlode Mine, and it puts the master rank at a Black Knight kill score of 1,300, so check that early. The six tasks are 252 air runes crafted at once with no extracts from at least 28 essence; a white two-handed sword"},{"t":"Sand, Crafting to 93 and Thieving to 91","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b19-h","x":"This block finishes Crafting and takes Thieving to 91 for the second sceptre. It suits a UIM well, because the Desert Quarry's grinder keeps your sand for you: it is the closest thing to a bank this guide uses. Gate in 35 Mining; 77 Magic; bucket packs deposited with Drew; about 3,700,000 gp; astral runes. Carry in a cast's sand and seaweed or soda ash, plus a pickaxe. Exit 93 Crafting (or 99); 91 Thieving; about 31,310,000 gp. Carries forward the sand in Drew's grinder."},{"t":"Fill the grinder with buckets and sand","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Sand, Crafting to 93 and Thieving to 91","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t110-h","x":"The grinder in the Desert Quarry keeps the sand from your sandstone, so it is your sand storage. Count what you need first: by the wiki's rates a bucket of sand is worth about 78 Crafting XP with soda ash (10 for the cast and 1.3 molten glass at 52.5 each) or about 96 with giant seaweed, so 93 Crafting from the 80 you start with plus the Gauntlet's 506,000 XP takes roughly 60,000 sand (49,000 with seaweed), and 99 roughly 135,000. Sandstone gives 1 to 8 sand a piece, depending on its size. By the wiki's table a 1 kg piece gives 1, a 2 kg piece 2, a 5 kg piece 4 and a 10 kg piece 8. The rocks stand just east of the grinder, and the quarry is in desert heat, so bring waterskins, a circlet of w"},{"t":"Astral runes for Superglass Make","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Sand, Crafting to 93 and Thieving to 91","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t111-h","x":"Each cast takes 2 astral runes, about 9,000 in all. Craft them at the Astral Altar on Lunar Isle from pure essence (40 Runecraft; one per essence, two from 82) or buy 250 at a time from Baba Yaga. Done when you hold about 9,000 astral runes."},{"t":"Superglass and arteglass to 93 Crafting and 91 Thieving","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Sand, Crafting to 93 and Thieving to 91","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t112-h","x":"Take sand from Drew, who hands it back noted at 50 gp a bucket. Carry the notes to a bank booth (Nardah's is the usual one) and unnote one cast's worth at a time. Cast Superglass Make there with soda ash from the charter traders, or giant seaweed from your Fossil Island patches; seaweed doesn't stack, so harvest it and use it straight away. It is a Lunar spell, so be on the Lunar spellbook. Use 3 giant seaweed with 18 sand, which beats 2 with 12, and pick up the extra glass that falls to the floor, because the best yield, about 1.6 glass a sand, needs it. Blow the glass at once and drop the products, or blow it between artefacts in Port Piscarilius, as in 3.1, until you are 91 Thieving for t"},{"t":"Runecraft to 90 or 95","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b20-h","x":"Optional, recommended: train Runecraft now, to 90 or 95, for the wrath runes that Offering spells use during Slayer and for the 6,000 blood and soul runes the house needs. Multiskilling ZMI with daeyalt essence is the common fast method; with Noranna's noted essence a UIM can run it too, unnoting a load at a bank booth each trip, but the wiki's UIM route below needs no essence storage at all. Gate in the Raiments of the Eye; 77 Runecraft for blood runes, 90 for soul; 38 Mining and 38 Crafting for dense essence. Carry in a pickaxe, a chisel and the fragments. Exit 90 or 95 Runecraft; 6,000+ blood and soul runes for the house; about 31,310,000 gp. Carries forward blood and soul runes (the dark"},{"t":"Guardians of the Rift to 77","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Runecraft to 90 or 95","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t114-h","x":"Play Guardians of the Rift with the full Raiments of the Eye on, as in 3.1, until 77 Runecraft. Done when you are 77 Runecraft."},{"t":"Blood runes to 90","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Runecraft to 90 or 95","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t115-h","x":"Arceuus runecrafting needs no essence storage, so a UIM can run it indefinitely. The loop is: mine a full inventory of dense essence, convert it at the Dark Altar, run back chiselling the blocks into fragments, do a second inventory the same way, then craft at the altar. The Blood Altar, south of the Dark Altar, needs 77 Runecraft and no quest. The wiki puts blood runes at about 37,000 XP an hour; they are slower than ZMI but very profitable. Mine dense essence blocks at the Arceuus essence mine (38 Mining). Take them to the Dark Altar, north-west of the mines, which turns every dense block in your inventory into a dark essence block one for one (it drains a Prayer point per block but works "},{"t":"Soul runes to 95 (optional)","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Runecraft to 90 or 95","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t116-h","x":"From 90, do the same loop at the Soul Altar, about 45,000 XP an hour, until you hold at least 6,000 soul runes, and on to 95 if you want wrath runes. Wrath runes come from Guardians of the Rift's wrath altar at 95, once Dragon Slayer II is done. Blow glass or fletch in your downtime. Ali's Discount Wares in Al Kharid buys runes at a fixed 50% of their price (nature 90, law 120, death 90, blood 200, soul 150, cosmic 25 gp each), so runes you won't use are a coin reserve. You can also sell chaos runes for tokkul at TzHaar-Mej-Roh to buy onyx bolt tips and uncut gems (this needs a fire cape), and keep whatever else you'll use yourself. The Tombs of Amascut are safe for a UIM with no death invoc"},{"t":"Mining to 97 with gem rocks","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b21-h","x":"The gem step in 3.1 only took you to 75. This block finishes the skill the same way, with the charged glory and the Shilo Village rocks, and it is the longest single grind this chapter adds. You arrive at roughly 80 Mining, since the sand block's sandstone and the blast mining already gave you about 800,000 XP (an estimate; check your own level), and about 8.7 million XP lies between there and 97. Decide where you stop: 90 is about 2.8 million XP from 82, about 40 hours. Gate in the Karamja hard diary and a charged amulet of glory; 75 Mining; the sand block and the Arceuus runes done, which is where most of your XP above 75 came from. Carry in a pickaxe, the charged glory and the gem bag. Ex"},{"t":"Gem rocks from 80 to 97","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Mining to 97 with gem rocks","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t118-h","x":"Wear the charged glory and mine the underground Shilo Village gem rocks (the medium Karamja diary opens the 48-rock mine, and the Karamja gloves 3 teleport you in). A gem is 65 XP, and the wiki's rate for plain mining is about 58,000 XP an hour at 70 and 75,000 at 99, which averages about 70,000 on the way up. At 3-tick the wiki puts it at 105,000 to 110,000 an hour, and 3t4g granite in the Desert Quarry at 109,000 to 126,000. Both need tick manipulation, so they are optional speed-ups: about 125 hours without them, about 75 with them. The glory raises your success rate (from about 28% to 82% at 99), and mining does not use up its charges. The rocks give no dragonstones: the wiki's table is "},{"t":"The second Pharaoh's sceptre","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b22-h","x":"Requirements Room 7 needs 81 Thieving and room 8 needs 91, and neither can be boosted. If you only have one sceptre, do Pyramid Plunder for a second, ideally at 91 Thieving or later. That is why you need two: the occult altar uses one up while the first keeps its teleports. The wiki places a death's gravestone exactly where you died inside the pyramid; for you that spot holds your deathpile, so you go back into the pyramid for it within your 60 minutes. The sceptre drops at about 1 in 650 per chest or sarcophagus in rooms 7 and 8 and throws you out when it appears. What changes from last time: Gate in 91 Thieving recommended; the first sceptre. Carry in energy or stamina potions and food. Ex"},{"t":"Thieving to 99","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b23-h","x":"The second sceptre leaves you at about 93 Thieving, so this block takes the last six levels: blackjacking to 94, then pickpocketing the Master Farmers in Hosidius, whose seed drops feed the Herblore block that follows. All yields here are the wiki's figures and need a recount in your own game. Gate in the second sceptre; 38 Thieving for the Master Farmers (94 and the hard Ardougne diary for no failures); 45 Thieving and The Feud for blackjacking; the rogue equipment (50 Agility and 50 Thieving to wear). Carry in Saradomin brews or wine for the thugs, a free slot and the rogue outfit worn. Exit 99 Thieving; the seed box holding the Master Farmer seeds; about 31,810,000 gp. Carries forward the"},{"t":"The rogue outfit","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Thieving to 99","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t121-h","x":"Rogue equipment comes from the wall safes at the end of the Rogues' Den maze and needs 50 Agility and 50 Thieving to wear. It raises the chance of double pickpocket loot (the full set is the strongest), and the guide's 200,000 gp an hour for blackjacking assumes it. The wiki's page does not say outright that the bonus applies to knocked-out thugs, so treat the coin figure as an estimate. Done when you hold all five pieces."},{"t":"Blackjack to 94","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Thieving to 99","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t122-h","x":"Blackjack the Menaphite thugs in southern Pollnivneach, as in Chapter 2: lure one to the southern house next to the bar, knock it out and pickpocket twice. The wiki puts the XP at about 255,000 to 265,000 an hour with Saradomin brews or wine, and the coins at about 200,000 gp an hour in the full outfit. Keep the inventory nearly full, because a full inventory stops coin pouches reaching you. About 2.9 hours takes you from 93 to 94 and earns about 580,000 gp, so I round the coin line down to 500,000 gp to stay conservative. Done when you are 94 Thieving."},{"t":"Master Farmers to 99","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Thieving to 99","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t123-h","x":"Pickpocket the Master Farmers in Hosidius with the rogue outfit on. The wiki's figure is about 115,000 XP an hour at full success, so 94 to 99 (about 5.1 million XP) takes about 44 hours. The seeds are why: the wiki's UIM page gives up to about 60 ranarr-or-better seeds an hour at maximum efficiency, but its own per-seed rarities do not agree with that, so count what you really get in the first hour and plan the Herblore block from that count. Put every seed in your seed box, drop the allotment, hop and flower seeds you will not plant, and keep a slot free, because a full inventory blocks the pickpocket. If you would rather have coins than seeds, blackjack all the way instead: about 260,000 "},{"t":"Herblore to 84 with Mastering Mixology","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b24-h","x":"The lamps and quests leave you at about 73 Herblore, and the potions the chapter needs only get to 84 if you train the skill on purpose. A UIM has no bank for herbs and few secondaries, so this block uses the one method that needs no secondaries at all: Mastering Mixology. Gate in 60 Herblore (not boostable) and Children of the Sun for Mixology; the seed stock from the Thieving block; the herb sack. Carry in the herb sack, the seed box, a spade and a seed dibber. Exit 84 Herblore; about 31,810,000 gp. Carries forward the herb runs, which fit between Mahogany Homes contracts in the next block."},{"t":"Herb runs","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Herblore to 84 with Mastering Mixology","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t125-h","x":"Plant every herb patch you can reach with the best seeds in the box, with ultracompost. The wiki's average is about 8.8 herbs a seed, so a ten-patch run is about 88 herbs, and each patch takes about 80 minutes to grow. Put every herb in the herb sack as you pick it. Farming contracts at the Guild add seed packs (about ten herb seeds each, mostly mid-level types), and the Slayer herbs the chapter already collects go into the same sack. If you made the 1.9 million XP between 73 and 84 as ordinary potions it would take about 12,000 herbs of about 160 XP each, roughly 130 full runs, which is why Mixology is the method here; the herbs it uses are the open question below."},{"t":"Mastering Mixology","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Herblore to 84 with Mastering Mixology","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t126-h","x":"Go to the Mastering Mixology facility and bring clean, unnoted herbs. Refine them into the three pastes at the machines (the hopper keeps up to 3,000 of each paste, which for you is a paste store between visits), then fill the potion orders. The wiki gives about 45,000 Herblore XP an hour for passive potion play and about 70,000 with every speed-up; each ordered potion is worth 190 to 365 XP depending on its level, and unordered potions about a third of that. At about 55,000 an hour, 73 to 84 (about 1.9 million XP) is about 35 hours. What the wiki does not give is how many herbs an hour that costs: passive refining alone eats about 2,750 herbs an hour for only 16,500 XP, so the herb bill cou"},{"t":"The potions the chapter needs","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Herblore to 84 with Mastering Mixology","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t127-h","x":"Make the pool's ten stamina (4), ten prayer (4) and ten super restore (4) potions the normal way, from the marks or amylase crystals and the herbs in the sack. Decant spare potions at Bob Barter in the Grand Exchange, where they come back noted; unnote them at a bank booth before you drink or build. Nothing in this guide buys potions, so make only what a trip needs. The ornate pool's 87 Herblore for the anti-venom is boostable, so you don't train for it: steal a golovanova fruit top from a Hosidius fruit stall and bake a botanical pie as in Chapter 1 (52 Cooking), eat a half (+4 Herblore, 84 to 88) and make the ten anti-venom (4) from antidote++ and Zulrah scales straight away, before the bo"},{"t":"Construction to 86 and the finished house","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b25-h","x":"Use Mahogany Homes Expert contracts again, chopping and planking the mahogany yourself as in 3.1. It is a long grind, but it needs far fewer planks than building furniture for the same XP. For a UIM this is the house the whole guide has been building toward: the ornate jewellery box and the fairy ring replace most carried teleports, the ornate pool restores you between trips, the occult altar swaps every spellbook, and the costume room's final tiers hold almost every set you own. Gate in the Mahogany Homes kit; about 6.1 million gp of plank fees and about 2.5 million gp of builds; 10,000 astral runes in your inventory for the occult altar, on top of about 11,600 used up by Plank Make; 87 Her"},{"t":"Mahogany Homes to 86","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Construction to 86 and the finished house","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t129-h","x":"Aim for 86, not 83. Most of the pieces below sit above 83: the wiki puts the ornate jewellery box at 91, the ornate rejuvenation pool and the occult altar at 90, the marble cape rack at 90, the fairy ring at 85 (the crystal saw does not apply to it) and the mahogany treasure chest at 84. From 83 they need +7 or +8, which only a +4 or +5 spicy stew (random from −5 to +5) plus the crystal saw gives. At 86, tea (+2) and the saw (+3) reach 91, and every piece builds without luck. The saw is destroyed by a death and has only 28 charges, so if the Entrana deaths or the builds have used it up, ask Brimstail in the Tree Gnome Stronghold for a new seed (free) and sing it at his bowl before you build."},{"t":"The jewellery boxes, cape rack, treasure chest and wardrobe","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Construction to 86 and the finished house","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t130-h","x":"Gather each piece's items right before building it, and drink tea first. You make the tea in your own kitchen (20 Cooking, a stove, a larder, a sink and teak shelves): a porcelain cup gives +2 and a trimmed cup on the second teak shelves (67 Construction) gives +3. Leaving the house removes all tea items, so drink it and build before you walk out. Every piece needs a hammer and a saw in your inventory, and jewellery must be unnoted. Upgrade the basic jewellery box to a fancy jewellery box (86 Construction; a gold leaf, 5 combat bracelets (4) and 5 skills necklaces (4)). Upgrade it to an ornate jewellery box (91 Construction; 2 gold leaves, 8 amulets of glory and 8 rings of wealth; the box it"},{"t":"The fairy ring","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Construction to 86 and the finished house","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t131-h","x":"Buy a second superior garden and build a fairy ring in it (85 Construction, Fairytale II; the crystal saw doesn't count), with 10 mushrooms and a fairy enchantment. The build also needs a watering can with at least one dose in your inventory, and the mushrooms must be unnoted. Fairy Fixit provides the enchantment after Fairytale II. Tea works here, and a trimmed cup (+3) gets you in from 82. Done when the fairy ring is built."},{"t":"The ornate rejuvenation pool","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Construction to 86 and the finished house","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t132-h","x":"Requirements The ornate pool needs 87 Herblore for the anti-venom, which the wiki marks boostable for ironmen: the botanical pie from the Herblore block (+4 from 84) covers it, with the Zulrah scales and antidote++ the anti-venom takes. 3.1 left the pool for here, so build the whole chain from restoration to ornate: 5 limestone bricks, 5 buckets of water, 1,000 soul runes, 1,000 body runes, 1,000 blood runes, 10 stamina potions (4), 10 prayer potions (4), 10 super restores (4), 10 anti-venom (4), 2 marble blocks and the 5 gold leaves the pieces take. Leave the pool for after the guide only if you can't get the scales. The wiki says every material must be unnoted, which suits you since you ma"},{"t":"The dark altar, then the occult altar","p":"Chapter 3 › 3.2: Quest cape, quality of life › Construction to 86 and the finished house","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-t133-h","x":"Build the dark altar (80 Construction): 10 limestone bricks, a magic stone (975,000 gp at the Keldagrim stonemason), 5,000 blood runes, 5,000 soul runes and an Arceuus signet, free from Tyss. With the pool that is 6,000 blood and 6,000 soul runes, which the Arceuus runecrafting left you. Upgrade it to the occult altar (90 Construction), which the wiki says is only made by upgrading an altar like that. It is built in the altar space of the house's Achievement Gallery, so keep the dark altar standing until you have every item. It needs a hammer and a saw in your inventory, and the crystal saw's boost counts. It uses up an uncharged Pharaoh's sceptre (the reason for the second one), an ancient "},{"t":"End of Chapter 3","p":"Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-s6-h","x":"You finish with the quest cape, 100+ combat, the Bow of Faerdhinen and crystal armour, 86 Construction with the ornate house, and a total level near 2,118, and about 22 million gp in hand (the coin chain is in the second table below). End-of-guide stats: Skill Level Notes Attack / Strength / Defence 78 / 88 / 76 Hitpoints / Ranged / Prayer 87 / 93 / 76+ Magic / Runecraft 96 / 90 to 95 Runecraft depends on how far you take the Arceuus runes Construction / Agility 86 / 98 86 so every house piece builds with tea and the crystal saw Herblore / Thieving about 84 / 99 Herblore 84 with Mixology; the ornate pool's 87 is reached with a botanical pie (+4) Crafting / Fletching 93 / 99 Slayer / Hunter 7"},{"t":"Where things live at the end of Chapter 3","p":"Chapter 3 › End of Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b26-h","x":"Storage What it holds Costume room (mahogany armour case and fancy dress box, marble cape rack, gilded magic wardrobe, mahogany treasure chest, toy box) Quest and minigame sets, capes, magic sets (and the graceful outfit whenever you aren't wearing it), costumes and clue items Ornate jewellery box, fairy ring, portal and altars in the house Most teleports and every spellbook Skiff and sloop cargo holds Kept: repair kits, cannonballs, charting supplies, cider, whirlpool surprises, fish offcuts, empty crates, tools and bait. Lost when the ship is summoned, quick-transported or recovered: salvage, fish, bounty items and courier crates. No noted items Kegs Perildance bitter, whirlpool surprise a"},{"t":"Verification list","p":"Chapter 3 › End of Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b27-h","x":"These claims were checked on the wiki or in game: Mahogany Homes' Expert tier (70, mahogany planks, Hosidius among the towns), the mahogany trees north of the Farming Guild, Tiadeche selling karambwans for coins, the Desert Quarry grinder keeping your sand (returned noted at 50 gp a bucket), the Kalphite Queen's dragon pickaxe (1/400; a death in the Ironman instance leaves your items outside it, by the wiki's instance death rule), the death rules of A Night at the Theatre, Monkey Madness II, Desert Treasure II and the Phantom Muspah, Zulrah's free retrieval for a UIM, the armour case storing void, the water and air battlestaff values, and the Construction levels for the house pieces. A secon"},{"t":"After the guide","p":"Chapter 3 › End of Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b28-h","x":"Chapter 4 continues from here to the max cape, one skill block at a time in the same route format, with a fast track and an easier option for every block."},{"t":"Changelog","p":"Chapter 3 › End of Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b29-h","x":"6 November 2026: first full version of Chapters 1 to 3. 11 November 2026: rewritten in the route-card format (Gate in, Carry in, Exit, Carries forward, Done when); a full audit of all three chapters against the wiki; the corrections from two independent audits (death rules, raw fish in deathpiles, the Kalphite Queen instance, Daeyalt essence, tick manipulation made optional, kudos, the Fractured Archive's Pete Kayer rule); Deathbank check lines on every block with unsafe fights; If it doesn't drop lines for the long drop grinds. 13 November 2026: Chapter 3 rewritten step by step to the depth of Chapters 1 and 2: numbered walkthroughs for The Final Dawn, Fallen From Grace, The Fremennik Exile"},{"t":"Sources","p":"Chapter 3 › End of Chapter 3","u":"chapter-3.html#ch3-b30-h","x":"Wiki pages used for this chapter's UIM changes include Item Retrieval Service, Torfinn, Tombs of Amascut, Bottle of banker's draught, Ultimate Ironman Guide/Runecraft, Blood rune, Ultimate Ironman Guide/Construction, Battlestaff (the Gauntlet's noted rewards) and Items Kept on Death. Also checked for this chapter: Mahogany Homes, Mahogany tree, Tiadeche's Karambwan Stall, Kalphite Queen, Armour case space, Void Knight equipment, Jewellery box space, Basic jewellery box, Ornate jewellery box, Rejuvenation pool, Dark altar (Construction), Costume room, Cape rack space, Obelisk of Water, Water battlestaff and Air battlestaff. Quest, diary and activity pages checked in the audit: The Final Dawn,"},{"t":"Where Chapter 3 left you","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s1-h","x":"You start with the quest cape, about 22.2 million gp, 86 Construction with the ornate house, the Bow of Faerdhinen and crystal armour, and a total level near 2,118. Your stats are the end-of-Chapter-3 stats: 78 Attack, 88 Strength, 76 Defence, 87 Hitpoints, 93 Ranged, 76 Prayer, 96 Magic, 90 to 95 Runecraft, 86 Construction, 98 Agility, about 84 Herblore, 99 Thieving, 93 Crafting, 99 Fletching, 76 Slayer, 91 Hunter, 97 Mining, 86 Smithing, 99 Fishing, 81 Cooking, 89 Firemaking, 80 or more Woodcutting, 96 Farming and 78 Sailing. Your long-term items are where Chapter 3's \"Where things live at the end of Chapter 3\" table puts them: sets, capes and clue items in the costume room, teleports in t"},{"t":"What changes for a UIM in Chapter 4","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s2-h","x":"The blocks are skills, not unlocks. The quest cape is done, so nothing gates the order any more except supplies and money. Each block has one active skill and the daily runs alongside it: tree, fruit tree and hardwood runs, a hard contract from Jane, the herb runs and the bird houses. The order follows the supplies. The first blocks make what the last ones spend: the Sepulchre and Slayer pay coins, Runecraft stocks the barrage runes, and the herb runs and Slayer drops stock Herblore. Smithing, Construction and Prayer, the most expensive 99s, come last. Stockpiles are notes. A UIM can't bank a stockpile, but notes take one slot a type. Use your grimy herbs on the tool leprechaun to note them "},{"t":"Chapter 4 at a glance","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s3-h","x":"Section Skills Main method UIM handling 4.1 Two short 99s Agility 98 → 99, Mining 97 → 99 The Hallowed Sepulchre's floor 5; gem rocks at Shilo Village The daily runs start; herbs noted for 4.7 4.2 Runecraft 90 → 99 Guardians of the Rift; Arceuus blood and soul runes The barrage rune stock for 4.3 and 4.5 4.3 Slayer I Slayer 76 → 90, Magic 96 → 99, Ranged 93 → 99 Barrage on multi-combat tasks; the Bow of Faerdhinen elsewhere Farming reaches 99 on the daily runs; the bonecrusher and ash sanctifier add Prayer XP 4.4 Sailing 78 → 99 The Barracuda Trials Independent of the rest; can move 4.5 Slayer II Slayer 90 → 99, Attack, Strength, Defence and Hitpoints to 99 Melee and barrage tasks from the h"},{"t":"The starting point","p":"Chapter 4 › Chapter 4 at a glance","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b1-h","x":"Skill Level XP to 99 Block Attack 78 11,405,231 4.5 Strength 88 8,648,655 4.5 Defence 76 11,697,988 4.5 Hitpoints 87 9,062,137 4.5 Ranged 93 5,838,802 4.3 Prayer 76 11,697,988 4.8 Magic 96 3,349,854 4.3 Runecraft 90 7,688,099 4.2 Construction 86 9,436,639 4.8 Agility 98 1,228,825 4.1 Herblore 84 10,083,058 4.7 Crafting 93 5,838,802 4.6 Slayer 76 11,697,988 4.3 and 4.5 Hunter 91 7,131,600 4.6 Mining 97 2,341,802 4.1 Smithing 86 9,436,639 4.8 Cooking 81 10,841,613 4.6 Firemaking 89 8,192,136 4.6 Woodcutting 80 11,048,363 4.6 Farming 96 3,349,854 Daily runs, 4.1 to 4.3 Sailing 78 11,405,231 4.4 Thieving, Fletching, Fishing 99 0 Done Runecraft is counted from 90; if Chapter 3 took you further, 4"},{"t":"4.1: Two short 99s","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s4-h","x":"Section 4.1 finishes the two skills closest to 99, Agility and Mining, in about 35 hours, and starts the daily runs that carry Farming to 99 by the end of 4.3. It comes first for two reasons. The Sepulchre's coffins pay coins that the expensive last block spends. And the daily runs need weeks of real time, so they should start as early as possible. The daily runs, from here to the end of 4.3. Every day you play, do the tree, fruit tree and hardwood runs, take one hard contract from Jane at the Farming Guild and do the bird houses, as Chapter 2 set them up. Do the herb runs too, but stop putting the herbs into potions: use each run's grimy herbs on the tool leprechaun to note them and keep th"},{"t":"Agility to 99 in the Sepulchre","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.1: Two short 99s","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b2-h","x":"Gate in 98 Agility; the hallowed hammer, focus and ring from Chapter 2; 87 Agility for floor 5 and 84 Thieving for the Grand Hallowed Coffin, both already met. Carry in a Saradomin item for the obelisks, the ring of endurance if Chapter 2's runs gave you one, high alchemy runes and something to alch; about 10/28. Exit 99 Agility and the Agility cape; about 22 million gp in the coin line, plus the coffin loot it doesn't count. Carries forward the coffin loot; spare hallowed marks. The wiki gives 98,500 XP an hour on floor 5 when you loot only the Grand Hallowed Coffin, and 90,000 an hour when you also loot the floor's other coffins. The 1,228,825 XP from 98 to 99 is about 12.5 hours the first"},{"t":"Before the first run","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.1: Two short 99s › Agility to 99 in the Sepulchre","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-t7-h","x":"Wear a Saradomin item. Anything from the hallowed shop counts, and without one the obelisks don't restore your run energy; a god item of another faction drains it. Carry two or three stamina potions. If you have the ring of endurance, wear it: each dose you drink with it on uses a charge and lasts twice as long, and with 500 or more charges it also cuts run energy drain by 15%. It doesn't replace the potions; it makes them go further. Keep a few hallowed tokens. Each adds a minute to the timer, which saves a bad floor 5. Put the alch runes in the rune pouch and the alchables in one stack. Done when you stand in the Darkmeyer lobby with the kit above."},{"t":"Run floor 5 to 99","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.1: Two short 99s › Agility to 99 in the Sepulchre","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-t8-h","x":"Take the runs from Darkmeyer as in Chapter 2. Clear floors 1 to 4 without looting anything and take the stairs down; the timer starts at 2 minutes on floor 1 and gains 2 more for each floor, so you reach floor 5 with about ten minutes if you waste none. On floor 5, clear the obstacles and loot only the Grand Hallowed Coffin. Leave the floor's bridge, grapple and enchantment loot. If a run goes wrong, leave by an obelisk instead of finishing it slowly: the XP for the floors you completed is already yours. Alch as you move. The Magic XP counts toward 4.3. Spend the marks on hallowed crystal shards, which teleport you to the lobby, or on loot sacks. At 99, buy the Agility cape from Cap'n Izzy N"},{"t":"Mining to 99 with gem rocks","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.1: Two short 99s","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b3-h","x":"Gate in 97 Mining; the charged amulet of glory, the gem bag and the underground Shilo Village mine from Chapter 3. Carry in a pickaxe, the charged glory, the gem bag, a chisel, a knife and one teak log, with spare teak logs in the log basket. Exit 99 Mining and the Mining cape; about 460,000 Crafting XP from the gems; about 21.9 million gp. Carries forward the gem bag. The 2,341,802 XP from 97 to 99 is the same method as Chapter 3's last Mining block. Its figures are 65 XP a gem rock and, from the wiki, about 75,000 XP an hour near 99 with plain mining and 105,000 to 110,000 an hour with 3-tick mining. That makes about 22 hours with 3-tick and about 31 hours without it. It is about 36,000 ge"},{"t":"Set up 3-tick mining","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.1: Two short 99s › Mining to 99 with gem rocks","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-t10-h","x":"3-tick mining replaces the pickaxe's own timing with a three-tick action that you start on the same tick as you move to the next rock. The wiki lists several actions that do it; a UIM already carries the parts for one of them: a knife used on a single teak or mahogany log, with spares in the log basket in case a mistake uses one up; or a clean herb (guam to irit) used on swamp tar, with a pestle and mortar. Keep only one of the processable item in your inventory, because two open a Make-X window that wastes the tick. If 3-tick is new to you, practise it for ten minutes before you count the hours. Done when you can hold the 3-tick rhythm for a few minutes without a miss."},{"t":"Gem rocks from 97 to 99","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.1: Two short 99s › Mining to 99 with gem rocks","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-t11-h","x":"Wear the charged glory, open the gem bag and mine the 48 underground gem rocks at Shilo Village (the Karamja gloves 3 teleport you in). Mine with the 3-tick action between rocks; it is this block's main method because it saves about nine hours. Drop the opals, jade and red topaz as they come: they are 105 of every 128 gems. When the bag's sapphires, emeralds, rubies or diamonds reach 60, take one type out and cut it with the chisel. Over the block that is about 2,500 sapphires, 1,400 emeralds, 1,400 rubies and 1,100 diamonds, about 460,000 Crafting XP at 50, 67.5, 85 and 107.5 XP a gem. Drop the cut gems; nothing here is sold. At 99, buy the Mining cape from Gadrin in the Mining Guild and ha"},{"t":"4.2: Runecraft","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s5-h","x":"Section 4.2 takes Runecraft from 90 to 99 and fills the rune stock that the barrage in 4.3 and 4.5 burns. It is about 125 hours, most of it at Guardians of the Rift, the method Chapter 3 used, which supplies its own essence and so needs no storage. It comes before the Slayer blocks because every Ice Barrage costs 6 water, 2 blood and 4 death runes, and blood runes are the one part of that you can only make yourself. How many runes. The barrage's real cost depends on how many monsters each cast hits, so this is a planning figure. A cast gives 52 base Magic XP plus 2 XP per point of damage; if a cast on a good barrage task averages about 60 damage across the monsters it hits, it is worth about"},{"t":"Guardians of the Rift to 99","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.2: Runecraft","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b4-h","x":"Gate in 90 Runecraft; the Raiments of the Eye and the colossal pouch from Chapter 3; Mourning's End Part II and Sins of the Father for the death and blood portals. Carry in a pickaxe, a chisel, the colossal pouch and the rune pouch; the Raiments worn. Exit 99 Runecraft and the Runecraft cape; the death and blood runes crafted on the way, counted against the 80,000 and 40,000 above; about 21.8 million gp. Carries forward the death and blood runes. The wiki gives 65,000 Runecraft XP an hour at Guardians of the Rift from 85 to 98, and 70,000 at 99. The full Raiments of the Eye add 10% more runes a piece and a 20% set bonus. Keep the death and blood runes you craft in the minigame, as Chapter 3 "},{"t":"Blood runes for the barrage","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.2: Runecraft","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b5-h","x":"Gate in 77 Runecraft; 38 Mining and 38 Crafting for dense essence. Carry in a pickaxe and a chisel; the Raiments worn. Exit about 40,000 blood runes in stock. Carries forward the blood runes. This is Chapter 3's Arceuus loop: mine dense essence, turn it into dark essence blocks at the Dark Altar, chisel them into fragments and bind them at the Blood Altar. The wiki's figure with the full Raiments is about 2,350 blood runes an hour, so 40,000 is about 17 hours, at the roughly 37,000 Runecraft XP an hour Chapter 3 gives for the loop. Those hours count toward 99, so they shorten the Guardians of the Rift block by about as much XP. Mine a full inventory of dense essence at the Arceuus essence mi"},{"t":"4.3: Slayer I, Magic and Ranged","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s6-h","x":"Section 4.3 takes Slayer from 76 to 90 and, on the way, Magic and Ranged to 99. That is about 4.0 million Slayer XP, plus the 3.35 million Magic and 5.84 million Ranged XP that ride on it. Barrage tasks train Magic, the other tasks train Ranged with the Bow of Faerdhinen, and once Ranged is 99 those tasks switch to melee, which counts toward 4.5. Farming reaches 99 on the daily runs during this section, and the bonecrusher and the ash sanctifier turn the bones and ashes you would drop into Prayer XP. The wiki gives no overall Slayer rate to plan by, so time your first ten tasks and plan the rest of the section from your own figure."},{"t":"The Slayer setup for Chapter 4","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.3: Slayer I, Magic and Ranged","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b6-h","x":"Gate in 76 Slayer and 100+ combat from Chapter 3; the Slayer helmet Chapter 3 made from the black mask; the bonecrusher; Arclight; the ancient staff (or the ancient sceptre, if the Phantom Muspah gave you the icon); the Bow of Faerdhinen and crystal armour; the rune stock from 4.2; the occult altar at home. Carry in the task's setup only. Exit a Slayer routine that runs to the end of 4.5. Carries forward the ash sanctifier and its charges."},{"t":"The master and the points","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.3: Slayer I, Magic and Ranged › The Slayer setup for Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-t17-h","x":"The wiki names Duradel, in Shilo Village, as the master for the fastest XP. He needs 100 combat and 50 Slayer, which Chapter 3 gave you, and pays 15 points a task. Konar pays more points (18, about 20 with the elite Kourend & Kebos diary) but sets the location; take a Konar task only when you want the points, for example to skip a run of bad Duradel tasks. Spend points on skipping tasks you do slowly, and block the worst ones: you get one block slot for every 50 quest points, and one more for the elite Lumbridge & Draynor diary. Done when your tasks come from Duradel."},{"t":"The ash sanctifier","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.3: Slayer I, Magic and Ranged › The Slayer setup for Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-t18-h","x":"Chapter 3 completed the hard Kourend & Kebos diary, so claim the ash sanctifier from Tyss at the Dark Altar if you haven't. With charges and in your inventory it purifies the demonic ashes that demons drop, for half the Prayer XP of scattering them. It is charged with death runes, 10 charges a rune, so its charges come out of the same death rune stock as the barrage; keep a few thousand charges and recount the stock when you do. With the bonecrusher from Chapter 3 doing the same for bones, every task now pays some Prayer XP without a slot. Done when the sanctifier is in your Slayer kit with charges."},{"t":"The trip routine","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.3: Slayer I, Magic and Ranged › The Slayer setup for Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-t19-h","x":"Use Chapter 3's routine on every task: collect any deathbank first, keep unused sets in the costume room, carry only the task's setup (gear, food, potions, the rune pouch, the herb sack, the bonecrusher and the sanctifier), alch as you go, and go straight back for a deathpile before you do anything else. Swap spellbooks at the occult altar in your house: Ancient Magicks for barrage tasks, the standard book for alching and teleports. Done when you follow the routine on every task. Coins: about 21.8 million gp · Slots: the task's setup · Requirements: 100 combat and 50 Slayer for Duradel; the hard Kourend & Kebos diary for the ash sanctifier Wiki references Slayer training Duradel Ash sanctifi"},{"t":"Barrage tasks: Magic to 99","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.3: Slayer I, Magic and Ranged","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b7-h","x":"Gate in 94 Magic for Ice Barrage, which your 96 already covers; Desert Treasure I for Ancient Magicks; the rune stock from 4.2. Carry in the ancient staff or sceptre, the Slayer helmet, Prayer-bonus gear, prayer potions, the rune pouch with blood and death runes and a water rune stack (or a water staff, which removes the water runes); about 20/28. Exit 99 Magic and the Magic cape. Carries forward the barrage routine, now on defensive for 4.5. Every multi-combat task is a barrage task. The Catacombs of Kourend are the usual place: the wiki says barrage tasks are done in multi-combat areas like the catacombs, where you stack the monsters and hit them all at once. Chapter 3's list holds: warped"},{"t":"Bow tasks: Ranged to 99, then melee","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.3: Slayer I, Magic and Ranged","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b8-h","x":"Gate in 80 Ranged and 70 Agility for the Bow of Faerdhinen, met in Chapter 3. Carry in the Bow of Faerdhinen and crystal armour, the Slayer helmet, ranging and prayer potions, food; about 20/28. Exit 99 Ranged and the Ranged cape; 90 Slayer by the end of the section. Carries forward the melee routine for 4.5. The 5.84 million Ranged XP from 93 to 99 is about 1.46 million points of damage at 4 Ranged XP a point, so it takes a little over a third of this section's 4.0 million Slayer XP. Use the bow on every task you don't barrage: it needs no ammunition, which is the UIM reason it beats a crossbow here. On each non-barrage task, use the Bow of Faerdhinen on rapid, with Protect from Melee where"},{"t":"Farming to 99 on the daily runs","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.3: Slayer I, Magic and Ranged","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b9-h","x":"Gate in the daily runs started in 4.1. Carry in the farm run kit, between Slayer tasks. Exit 99 Farming and the Farming cape; the noted herbs and the seeds kept for 4.7. Carries forward the noted herbs; the herb runs, which go on to the end of 4.6. Keep the runs going between tasks. Farming needs 3.35 million XP from 96, and the tree, fruit tree and hardwood runs with Jane's hard contracts bring most of it; trees take most of a day to grow, so the pace is set by how many days you play, not how long. If Farming is short of 99 when 4.3 ends, keep the runs going into 4.4: nothing later depends on it except the cape. At 99, buy the Farming cape and hang it in the cape rack. Keep the herb runs go"},{"t":"4.4: Sailing","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s7-h","x":"Section 4.4 takes Sailing from 78 to 99, about 11.4 million XP, on the Gwenith Glide's marlin rank. It depends on nothing before it and nothing after it needs it, so it sits between the two Slayer sections as a change of pace; move it anywhere you like. The daily runs go on alongside it."},{"t":"The Gwenith Glide to 99","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.4: Sailing","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b10-h","x":"Gate in 78 Sailing (72 unboosted is the trial's own requirement); Regicide; the shark rank completed in Chapter 3, which opens the marlin rank; the skiff with an adamant or better keel, a wind or gale catcher and the crystal extractor beside the helm, all from Chapter 3. Carry in food or a regen bracelet for the resonance crystal damage, and nothing you can't afford to leave in a deathpile; no crew on the skiff. Exit 99 Sailing and the Sailing cape; a stack of crystal shards from the extractor. Carries forward the crystal shards. The wiki's rates for the Gwenith Glide are 113,538 XP an hour at the swordfish rank, 144,543 at shark and 184,369 at marlin, or 198,119 at marlin with a crystal ext"},{"t":"Run the marlin rank","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.4: Sailing › The Gwenith Glide to 99","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-t25-h","x":"Dismiss any crew first: the trial won't start with a crewmate or another player aboard. Gwyna can dismiss them, and the Crew Registrar reassigns them afterwards. Keep the sails trimmed with crystal motes for the whole run; without a full catcher you can't beat the rank's time. Collect every floating crate of lost supplies; the trial won't finish without them. Pass through the portals to imbue the Crystals of Ithell, which the finish needs. When a resonance crystal hits, click the helm three times to clear it. The wiki says dodging them usually isn't worth the time, because early breaks do one damage each; eat when the damage builds. At 99, buy the Sailing cape and hang it in the cape rack. O"},{"t":"4.5: Slayer II and the combat 99s","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s8-h","x":"Section 4.5 is the longest of the chapter: Slayer from 90 to 99, about 7.7 million Slayer XP, with Attack, Strength, Defence and Hitpoints taken to 99 by the same tasks. It ends with a count of your coins against what 4.6 and 4.8 will spend, because the Slayer loot of 4.3 and 4.5 is what pays for them."},{"t":"Slayer 90 to 99, with melee and defensive barrage","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.5: Slayer II and the combat 99s","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b11-h","x":"Gate in 90 Slayer; 99 Magic and Ranged; the Slayer routine from 4.3; your Chapter 3 melee setup with Hallowfell and Arclight, Piety and the fire cape. Carry in the task's setup only. Exit 99 Slayer, Attack, Strength, Defence and Hitpoints, and their five capes. Carries forward the Slayer loot and any noted drops for 4.8. Every point of damage on a melee task gives 4 XP in the style you choose and 1.33 Hitpoints XP; every point on a defensive barrage task gives 1 Defence XP, 1.33 Magic XP and 1.33 Hitpoints XP. Slayer XP is the hitpoints of what you kill, so the 7.7 million Slayer XP of this section is about 30.8 million melee XP if every task were melee, and about 10.2 million Hitpoints XP w"},{"t":"Set the styles","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.5: Slayer II and the combat 99s › Slayer 90 to 99, with melee and defensive barrage","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-t28-h","x":"Do the barrage tasks on defensive, as 4.3 left them: they are your cheapest Defence. On melee tasks, train Attack first and then Strength, each on its own style, so that every melee point goes where it is needed. Leave Defence to the barrage tasks for now. At 95 Slayer, check the three: add up the XP each still needs, and compare it with four times the Slayer XP left to 99 (about 4.3 million at 95, so about 17 million melee XP). If Defence is the one behind, move the melee tasks to defensive. New tasks open on the way: smoke devils at 93 Slayer are a barrage task (they have Magic defence, so the wiki suggests Magic accuracy against them); the Alchemical Hydra at 95 is optional. At each 99, b"},{"t":"The coin check before the last blocks","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.5: Slayer II and the combat 99s","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b12-h","x":"Gate in the end of the Slayer tasks. Carry in nothing. Exit a coin figure for 4.6 and 4.8, and a plan to close the gap if there is one. Carries forward the coins. This chapter's coin lines only subtract, because the Sepulchre's grand coffins and the Slayer drops vary too much to plan by. Now count what they actually gave you: your coin stack plus the Nightmare Zone and Last Man Standing coffers. Then compare it with what 4.6 and 4.8 will spend, which is more than the rest of the chapter together. Each block prices its part in full; these are the planning figures: What 4.6 and 4.8 buy Planning figure How it is worked out Raw karambwans for Cooking 81 to 99 (4.6) About 6.6 million gp About 57,"},{"t":"4.6: Skilling","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s9-h","x":"Section 4.6 takes five skills to 99: Hunter, Woodcutting, Firemaking, Cooking and Crafting, about 42.6 million XP after the gems of 4.1. None of them risks your items, and only Cooking and Crafting cost much, about 6.6 and 3.3 million gp. The order inside the section doesn't matter; the one link is that Wintertodt's Reward Cart, searched at your current levels, is a good source of the herbs 4.7 needs. The herb runs go on through this section."},{"t":"Hunter to 99 with Hunters' Rumours","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.6: Skilling","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b13-h","x":"Gate in 91 Hunter and At First Light for master rumours. Carry in the Huntsman's kit and each rumour's traps; teleports. Exit 99 Hunter and the Hunter cape. Carries forward nothing. The wiki gives about 195,000 XP an hour from master rumours at 91 and about 250,000 at 99, with an experience-focused block list, the full guild hunter outfit and good teleports. The 7,131,600 XP from 91 is about 32 hours. Take rumours from the master hunter, block the slow ones, and wear more of the guild hunter outfit as the rumours pay for it. Keep the bird houses going between rumours. Easier option. Bird houses alone: the wiki calls them viable up to 99 if you don't need the levels quickly. Redwood houses ne"},{"t":"Woodcutting to 99 with teaks","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.6: Skilling","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b14-h","x":"Gate in 80 Woodcutting; Bone Voyage for Fossil Island. Carry in your best axe, the forestry kit and the 1.5-tick items; nothing else. Exit 99 Woodcutting and the Woodcutting cape. Carries forward nothing; the logs are dropped. Teaks on Fossil Island with 1.5-tick woodcutting are the wiki's fastest method here: 208,000 XP an hour at 80 and 235,000 at 99, about 50 hours for the 11,048,363 XP. Drop every log: the wiki's rates assume it, and a UIM can't keep 10,000 teak logs anyway (the tool leprechaun won't note them). If 1.5-tick is too intense, 2-tick teaks on Ape Atoll, the Isle of Souls or in Prifddinas give 186,000 to 215,000. Easier option. Forestry events on ironwoods or yews (70,000 to "},{"t":"Firemaking to 99 at Wintertodt","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.6: Skilling","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b15-h","x":"Gate in 89 Firemaking; the four warm items and the Wintertodt kit from Chapter 1. Carry in a hammer, a knife, a tinderbox and the rejuvenation potions the camp gives you; about 10/28. Exit 99 Firemaking and the Firemaking cape; a full Reward Cart to search. Carries forward the noted herbs from the cart, for 4.7. The wiki gives 290,000 Firemaking XP an hour at 90 and 320,000 at 99 at Wintertodt, on a busy official world where games last about four minutes. The 8,192,136 XP from 89 is about 27 hours. You play it as in Chapter 1, but now every game also gives a little Woodcutting XP and stacks more rolls in the Reward Cart. Play on the wiki's official Wintertodt worlds, scoring at least 500 poi"},{"t":"Cooking to 99 with karambwans","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.6: Skilling","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b16-h","x":"Gate in 81 Cooking; Tai Bwo Wannai Trio, which you finished in Chapter 2. Carry in coins, a tinderbox and logs for the fire; the fish barrel if you have one. Exit 99 Cooking and the Cooking cape. Carries forward nothing. Karambwans give 190 Cooking XP each, so the 10,841,613 XP from 81 is about 57,000 karambwans. The cooking is fast (the wiki gives 273,000 XP an hour AFK at 99 and up to 950,000 with 1-tick cooking), so the limit is the raw fish. Tiadeche's Karambwan Stall in Tai Bwo Wannai sells them at 110 gp, 10 in stock and one back every 6 seconds, with the price rising 1% for each one you buy from a full stock, so about 115 gp a fish on average. That makes the supply about 6.6 million g"},{"t":"Crafting to 99 with Superglass Make and light orbs","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.6: Skilling","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b17-h","x":"Gate in 93 Crafting; 77 Magic and Lunar Diplomacy for Superglass Make; 87 Crafting for light orbs; the Desert Quarry grinder from Chapter 3. Carry in one cast's sand and soda ash or giant seaweed, a glassblowing pipe, the rune pouch with astral, air and fire runes, and a pickaxe for the sandstone. Exit 99 Crafting and the Crafting cape. Carries forward nothing. This is Chapter 3's loop with one change: blow every molten glass into an empty light orb (87 Crafting, 70 XP) instead of an unpowered orb. A bucket of sand is then worth about 101 Crafting XP with soda ash (10 for the cast and about 1.3 glass at 70 each), or about 122 with giant seaweed. After the 4.1 gems, Crafting needs about 5.4 m"},{"t":"4.7: Herblore","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s10-h","x":"Section 4.7 takes Herblore from 84 to 99, about 10.1 million XP, and for a UIM it is a supply problem more than a training one. At Chapter 3's figure of about 160 XP a herb for an ordinary potion (cleaning included), 99 is about 63,000 herbs. A ten-patch herb run gives about 88, so that is the equivalent of about 700 runs, which is why every block since 4.1 has noted its herbs for this one."},{"t":"Count the herbs first","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.7: Herblore","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b18-h","x":"Gate in the noted herbs from 4.1 to 4.6, the Reward Cart's herbs from 4.6 and the herb sack. Carry in your herb notes. Exit a count of herbs, and of the XP they can cover. Carries forward the plan for the rest of 4.7. Add up your noted herbs and the herb sack. Multiply by 160: that is roughly how much XP the stock covers. If it covers 10.1 million, make potions as below and finish 4.7 in one go. If it doesn't, start 4.8 anyway and keep the herb runs going between 4.8's sessions. Return to 4.7 whenever the notes have grown, and finish it last if you have to. Done when you know whether your herbs cover 99."},{"t":"Potions to 99","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.7: Herblore","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b19-h","x":"Gate in 84 Herblore; the herb notes; vial of water packs; each potion's secondary. Carry in one batch: 8 unnoted herbs, 8 vials of water and 8 secondaries, plus the herb, vial and secondary notes; 27/28, or 28/28 with a pestle and mortar if the secondary needs crushing. Exit 99 Herblore and the Herblore cape. Carries forward the potions you want for later trips, decanted and noted. Vials of water come noted in packs: Jatix's Herblore Shop in Taverley sells the water-filled vial pack, 100 noted vials of water, for 201 gp, 750 in stock. About 630 packs cover 63,000 potions for about 127,000 gp, so buy them a few hundred at a time and unnote the vials with your herbs. Unnote one batch at a bank"},{"t":"4.8: The last three","p":"Chapter 4","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-s11-h","x":"Section 4.8 finishes the three most expensive skills: Construction, Prayer and Smithing, each 9 to 12 million XP. Do them in that order. Construction first, while the 4.5 count is fresh, because it is the biggest bill after Smithing and the one with a cheaper fallback (teak) if the coins are short; its cape's house teleports also serve the Prayer block's easier option. Prayer next; Smithing last, because it is nothing but coins turned into XP, so it can wait for whatever money the other two leave."},{"t":"Construction to 99 with Mahogany Homes","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.8: The last three","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b20-h","x":"Gate in 86 Construction; the plank sack and log basket; 86 Magic for Plank Make; the coins from the 4.5 count. Carry in the plank sack full of mahogany planks, a hammer, a saw and a few steel bars; the log basket when you chop. Exit 99 Construction and the Construction cape. Carries forward the Construction cape's house teleports, for the Prayer block. This is Chapter 3's loop to the end: Expert contracts, with the mahogany chopped and planked yourself, because the contract completion bonus makes Mahogany Homes far cheaper in planks than building furniture. Chapter 3's figures are about 4,400 XP and 13 planks a contract, about 338 XP a plank, so the 9,436,639 XP from 86 is about 27,900 mahog"},{"t":"Prayer to 99","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.8: The last three","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b21-h","x":"Gate in Prayer where 4.3 and 4.5 left it; 92 Magic and A Kingdom Divided for Sinister Offering; wrath runes (95 Runecraft at Guardians of the Rift) and blood runes; Dragon Slayer II for the Myths' Guild part of the Corsair Cove Dungeon; the Construction cape, for the easier option. Carry in your dragon setup with antifire potions, the rune pouch with wrath and blood runes, and space for the bones. Exit 99 Prayer and the Prayer cape. Carries forward nothing. The wiki's UIM Prayer page puts the green dragons in the Corsair Cove Dungeon under the Myths' Guild as the method that keeps you out of the Wilderness. You offer the bones on the spot with Sinister Offering, an Arceuus spell that takes u"},{"t":"Smithing to 99 with UIM gold","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.8: The last three","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b22-h","x":"Gate in 86 Smithing; the goldsmith gauntlets and ice gloves; the rest of the coins. Carry in the UIM gold setup from Chapter 3: coins, the gauntlets and the ice gloves. Exit 99 Smithing and the Smithing cape. Carries forward nothing. The same Blast Furnace dropping routine Chapter 3 used to reach 86: buy gold ore from Ordan, load it wearing the goldsmith gauntlets (56.2 XP a bar instead of 22.5), take the bars with the ice gloves and drop them. Chapter 3 put the method at about 4.25 to 4.5 coins per XP with the coffer's drain, so the 9,436,639 XP from 86 costs about 40 to 42.5 million gp, about 168,000 ores. There is no cheaper Smithing route: every method turns bars or ore into XP. If the c"},{"t":"The max cape","p":"Chapter 4 › 4.8: The last three","u":"chapter-4.html#ch4-b23-h","x":"With the last 99, buy the max cape from Mac, on his island west of the Warriors' Guild: 2,376,000 gp (99,000 a skill), with the max hood. Reaching him needs a pickaxe and an axe, and the 99s you now have. Every block of this chapter, and of the three chapters before it, is done. Done when you wear the max cape. Coins: less 2,376,000 gp · Slots: a pickaxe and an axe · Requirements: 99 in all 24 skills Wiki references Max cape"}];